\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate calls on supreme court chief justice to investigate \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18gift\u8217\'20\'19 trips \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Kari Paul (now) and Chris Stein in Washington (earlier) \par \uc2 4,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par 22:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judiciary committee will review supreme court justice\u8217\'20\'19s undeclared luxury travel with Republican mega-donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Kari Paul here, signing off for the day. Here is the news you need to know from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s gun violence epidemic continues, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6434231b8f08547fbc668643#block-6434231b8f08547fbc668643"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five people killed}}}\uc2  in a mass shooting at a bank building in Louisville, Kentucky this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tennessee Republicans have managed to oust from the state House of Representatives two Black Democratic lawmakers who staged a noisy protest in favor of gun control after a mass shooting in Nashville. One was reappointed back to his seat in a vote today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-643412eb8f08495ac86cb4b8#block-643412eb8f08495ac86cb4b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will run for re-election}}}\uc2 , but plans to make a formal announcement in the future, he said in a surprising, offhand remark at the annual White House Easter egg roll.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-643433c68f08156fb81ec80b#block-643433c68f08156fb81ec80b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suing}}}\uc2  to stop his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  from talking to a grand jury investigating the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace, a Republican lawmaker in the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , says the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64341dcb8f08547fbc66860f#block-64341dcb8f08547fbc66860f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should ignore}}}\uc2  a conservative federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling suspending the certification of one of the drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 However the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-6434601a8f08156fb81ec949#block-6434601a8f08156fb81ec949"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  it has no intention of ignoring the ruling, but the justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-6434569a8f08547fbc668836#block-6434569a8f08547fbc668836"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has appealed it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fallout continues after a \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report revealed supreme court chief justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  accepted a number of luxury gifts from a Republican donor \u8211\'20\'13 Senate Democrats have promised to hold a hearing on and demand investigation into whether Thomas broke disclosure rules, and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  wants him impeached\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Expelled representative Justin Jones reinstated to the Tennessee House of Representatives in unanimous vote\par \par \uc2 In a vote of 36-0 the Metro Nashville council voted to reinstate Justin Jones to the Tennessee house of representatives following his removal over gun control demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 enltrNashville Council votes to reinstate Justin Jones 36-0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cOueZkbtmy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cOueZkbtmy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1645542902855000065?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Jones was one of two Democratic lawmakers expelled from Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s GOP-dominated house of representatives in retaliation for their role in a gun control demonstration after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killings}}}\uc2  at a Nashville elementary school.\par \par \uc2 Expelling members of state legislature is rare and generally reserved as a punishment for lawmakers accused of serious misconduct. Both expelled representatives are Black, and Jones condemned the action as \u8220\'20\'1Copenly racist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The banishment resulted in thousands flocking to the state capitol to protest and a public condemnation from president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who called the expulsions \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking, undemocratic and without precedent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThree kids and three officials gunned down in yet another mass shooting,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1644100520636739586"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd what are GOP officials focused on? Punishing lawmakers who joined thousands of peaceful protesters calling for action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There has not yet been a vote on Justin Pearson, the other representative expelled over the protest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate calls for investigation of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\par \par \uc2 More details are emerging about the Senate judiciary committee\u8217\'20\'19s calls to investigate supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  over potential violations of donor disclosure rules.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators on Monday urged US chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to investigate luxury trips Thomas took that were paid for by a Republican donor \u8211\'20\'13 conduct they deemed inconsistent with ethical standards for \u8220\'20\'1Cany person in a position of public trust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The full letter is here:\par \par \uc2 enltrAll Democrats on the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  are calling on Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to investigate a report last week that detailed how Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  accepted hundreds of thousands of dollars in luxury trips from a Dallas-based GOP donor that weren't reported. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/29EAx72MMk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/29EAx72MMk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laura Litvan (@LauraLitvan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LauraLitvan/status/1645530373290442753?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Chairman \uc2 Richard Durbin\uc2  and the panel\u8217\'20\'19s 10 other Democratic members wrote in a letter to Roberts that the committee will hold a hearing in the coming days focusing on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need to restore confidence in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ethical standards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if the court does not resolve this issue on its own, the committee will consider legislation to resolve it\u8221\'20\'1D, they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CBut you do not need to wait for Congress to act to undertake your own investigation into the reported conduct and to ensure that it cannot happen again. We urge you to do so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report revealed Thomas accepted a number of trips and gifts from Republican businessman \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2  over decades, though Crow claims he had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever sought to influence Justice Thomas on any legal or political issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In their letter, senators told Roberts that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou have a role to play as well, both in investigating how such conduct could take place at the court under your watch, and in ensuring that such conduct does not happen again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe report describes conduct by a sitting justice that he did not disclose to the public and that is plainly inconsistent with the ethical standards the American people expect of any person in a position of public trust,\u8221\'20\'1D the senators wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  wants \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  impeached\par \par \uc2 Democratic US representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said on Sunday she wants \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  impeached over his trips with a Republican mega-donor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the House\u8217\'20\'19s responsibility to pursue that investigation in the form of impeachment,\u8221\'20\'1D she told CNN in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Her comments to CNN echo statements {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made last week}}}\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2  revealed Thomas may have violated financial disclosure rules over his relationship with property billionaire \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report showed Thomas accepted expensive trips from Crow over decades despite federal law requiring the disclosure of most gifts.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez acknowledged it was unlikely the Republican majority in the House of Representatives would want to take action against the conservative justice.\par \par \uc2 Thomas has defended the trips, saying in a statement on Friday that he had been advised he was not required to report that type of \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal hospitality\u8221\'20\'1D, and that he would now follow new rules brought in by the judicial conference responsible for financial disclosure requirements for the entire federal judiciary.\par \par \uc2 Crow told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  he had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever sought to influence Justice Thomas on any legal or political issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, Kari Paul here on the west coast taking over the blog for a bit. Stay tuned for more updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate to hold hearing on supreme court justice's trips, demand investigation\par \par \uc2 The Senate judiciary committee will hold a hearing on conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s travel with Republican mega-donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 , and has demanded chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  investigate his activities, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear when the hearing would take place. On Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica reported}}}\uc2  that Thomas had for years accepted flights on private jets and stays in exclusive resorts from Crow, who is linked to a number of conservative causes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  has a message for the House Republicans who plan to hold a committee hearing in New York City next week to address the issue of crime: go somewhere else.\par \par \uc2 In particular, he questions why Jim Jordan, chair of the judiciary committee that\u8217\'20\'19s holding the hearing, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t convene lawmakers in one of the Ohio cities near his district where the murder rate is higher:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kQIlFMsC6X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kQIlFMsC6X}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YNq0I2bjas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YNq0I2bjas}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  (@ManhattanDA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ManhattanDA/status/1645501803323170841?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This all has to do with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whom Bragg has indicted for allegedly falsifying business records. Republicans such as Jordan have hit back at the prosecutor, saying he should be more concerned with crime in his own district.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 At her briefing today, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said the Texas federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling suspending mifepristone was part of the Republican campaign to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, the Hill reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  on Texas decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill: \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat we're seeing currently right now is part of the plan, it's part of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve been hearing from extreme MAGA Republicans\u8230\'20\'26 who say they want a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AlexGangitano (@AlexGangitano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexGangitano/status/1645502313354731520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 However, she said the Biden administrations wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t follow the advice of some Democrats, such as progressive \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , to ignore the ruling, according to Semafor:\par \par \uc2 enltrKarine Jean-Pierre says it would set a "dangerous precedent" for the admin to disregard a binding court decision, in response to Q on AOC's call for the admin to ignore ruling on mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Chalfant (@mchalfant16) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mchalfant16/status/1645503240925052930?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 250 pharmaceutical industry leaders have released an open letter decrying the Texas federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling suspending authorization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone:\par \par \uc2 The decision ignores decades of scientific evidence and legal precedent. Judge Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s act of judicial interference has set a precedent for diminishing \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority over drug approvals, and in so doing, creates uncertainty for the entire biopharma industry. As an industry we count on the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s autonomy and authority to bring new medicines to patients under a reliable regulatory process for drug evaluation and approval. Adding regulatory uncertainty to the already inherently risky work of discovering and developing new medicines will likely have the effect of reducing incentives for investment, endangering the innovation that characterizes our industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the signatories on the letter is \uc2 Albert Bourla\uc2 , CEO of \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 , as well as officials from major drugmakers like Merck and \uc2 Biogen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read the letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docsend.com/view/2ahvmwy8djzxax3g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department appeals ruling suspending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has filed an appeal against a federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling last week that suspended the approval of one of the drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/justice-dept-asks-court-delay-abortion-medication-decision-rcna78978"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its appeal, the justice department said the ruling by Matthew Kacsmaryk, a conservative judge appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and seated in Amarillo, Texas, \u8220\'20\'1Cupended decades of reliance by blocking \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone and depriving patients of access to this safe and effective treatment, based on the court\u8217\'20\'19s own misguided assessment of the drug\u8217\'20\'19s safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The department called the ruling, which is to go into effect Friday and could mean mifepristone is taken off pharmacy shelves nationwide, \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary and unprecedented.\u8221\'20\'1D If the fifth circuit court of appeals does not grant the stay, the justice department may decide to appeal to the supreme court, NBC reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden attacks Republicans after Louisville shooting\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a statement of condolence following the mass shooting that left five people dead in Louisville, Kentucky, while attacking Republicans for passing what he called \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous bills\u8221\'20\'1D that make gun violence worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many more Americans must die before Republicans in Congress will act to protect our communities? It\u8217\'20\'19s long past time that we require safe storage of firearms. Require background checks for all gun sales. Eliminate gun manufacturers\u8217\'20\'19 immunity from liability. We can and must do these things now,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/04/10/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-shooting-in-louisville-kentucky/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his statement}}}\uc2  in full:\par \par \uc2 Once again, our nation is in mourning after a senseless act of gun violence. Jill and I are praying for those killed and injured in the tragic shooting in Louisville, and for the survivors who will carry grief and trauma for the rest of their lives. We are grateful to the Louisville Metropolitan Police Department officers who quickly and courageously stepped into the line of fire to save others.\par \par \uc2 How many more Americans must die before Republicans in Congress will act to protect our communities? It\u8217\'20\'19s long past time that we require safe storage of firearms. Require background checks for all gun sales. Eliminate gun manufacturers\u8217\'20\'19 immunity from liability. We can and must do these things now. A strong majority of Americans want lawmakers to act on commonsense gun safety reforms. Instead, from Florida to North Carolina to the \uc2 U.S. House of Representatives\uc2 , we\u8217\'20\'19ve watched Republican officials double down on dangerous bills that make our schools, places of worship, and communities less safe. It\u8217\'20\'19s unconscionable, it\u8217\'20\'19s reckless, and too many Americans are paying with their lives.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Connecticut US senator Richard Blumenthal said Sunday that he had surgery aimed at repairing a broken leg that he suffered at a parade celebrating a national championship won by his state\u8217\'20\'19s flagship university.\par \par \uc2 Blumenthal, a 77-year-old Democrat, told the local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://connecticut.news12.com/sen-blumenthal-fractures-femur-at-uconn-parade-will-undergo-surgery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 News 12 station}}}\uc2  that someone fell on him after tripping while they were at Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s parade honoring the \uc2 University of Connecticut\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s men\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team, which won its first-ever national championship on 3 April.\par \par \uc2 He then said Sunday on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that he had surgery to help heal a break to one of his upper femurs, calling the procedure \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely successful\u8221\'20\'1D and saying his medical caretakers had been \u8220\'20\'1Cmagnificent\u8221\'20\'1D. Blumenthal also said he had already started his physical therapy and planned to be back at work in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital in the middle of April, when Congress is set to resume its legislative session after a break.\par \par \uc2 enltrSecond, a quick update: I just got out of surgery to repair the minor fracture to my upper femur. The surgery was completely successful and the staff, docs, and everyone here at Stamford Hospital has been magnificent.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Blumenthal (@SenBlumenthal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBlumenthal/status/1645209334471589891?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Connecticut\u8217\'20\'19s other Democratic senator, \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , said Blumenthal managed to finish the parade before going to the hospital after fracturing his leg. \u8220\'20\'1CHe \u8230\'20\'26 dusted himself off and FINISHED THE PARADE,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy wrote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisMurphyCT/status/1644875301539790849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1644875301539790849%7Ctwgr%5E999bc862b30a4ff8dac13964bb8c4a2a92015bd1%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fiframe.nbcnews.com%2FODVi0UE%3F_showcaption%3Dtrueapp%3D1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CMost Dick Blumenthal thing ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blumental is in his third term in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  after first being elected to the chamber in 2010.\par \par \uc2 He wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful to everyone who has called, texted or tweeted \u8230\'20\'26 well wishes\u8221\'20\'1D since news of his leg fracture spread across social media, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt means so much to me and my family \u8211\'20\'13 thank you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the only former American president ever to be indicted, but the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that he now thinks the charges could be useful in his quest to return to the White House:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared angry and shaken during his arraignment in Manhattan criminal court on Tuesday, but he had brushed off the moment by the weekend, contending that the indictment and other legal troubles would carry him to the 2024 Republican nomination, people close to him said.\par \par \uc2 With his status as a criminal defendant subjecting him to the strictures of the judicial process, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president}}}\uc2  is playing an increasingly high-stakes game to inextricably tie his legal strategy to his political gameplan as he seeks to recapture the Oval Office next year.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wager is that using his legal troubles as a campaign issue will harden support from his base and Republican elected officials, and that support could undercut or falsely delegitimize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/08/donald-trump-legal-troubles-new-york-georgia-reelection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecutions in Georgia or by the US justice department}}}\uc2  in other criminal investigations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/trump-indictments-2024-republican-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump bets indictments could make him 2024 Republican nominee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s gun violence epidemic continues, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6434231b8f08547fbc668643#block-6434231b8f08547fbc668643"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five people killed}}}\uc2  in a mass shooting at a bank building in Louisville, Kentucky this morning. Meanwhile, Tennessee Republicans have managed to oust from the state House of Representatives two Black Democratic lawmakers who staged a noisy protest in favor of gun control after a mass shooting in Nashville \u8211\'20\'13 but local officials may reappoint them back to their seats, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-6434026c8f08547fbc6684c2#block-6434026c8f08547fbc6684c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one being voted on}}}\uc2  as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-643412eb8f08495ac86cb4b8#block-643412eb8f08495ac86cb4b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will run for re-election}}}\uc2 , but plans to make a formal announcement in the future, he said in a surprising, offhand remark at the annual White House Easter egg roll.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-643433c68f08156fb81ec80b#block-643433c68f08156fb81ec80b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suing}}}\uc2  to stop his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  from talking to a grand jury investigating the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace, a Republican lawmaker in the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , says the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/10/abortion-pill-ruling-trump-tennessee-democrats-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64341dcb8f08547fbc66860f#block-64341dcb8f08547fbc66860f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should ignore}}}\uc2  a conservative federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling suspending the certification of one of the drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  said he lost two friends in the shooting in downtown Louisville today.\par \par \uc2 Beshear and lieutenant governor Jacqueline Coleman are the only Democrats elected statewide in the otherwise overwhelmingly red state. Last month, Beshear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wtvq.com/bill-to-make-ky-a-second-amendment-sanctuary-becomes-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took no action}}}\uc2  on a Republican-backed bill that would make Kentucky a \u8220\'20\'1CSecond Amendment Sanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D where police are banned from enforcing federal gun legislation, allowing it to become law, according to WTVQ.\par \par \uc2 Here are his comments, courtesy of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrKentucky Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  (D) said two of his close friends were killed in the shooting and another was injured. The shooter had a connection to the downtown Louisville bank targeted in Monday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting, authorities said during a news conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a very close friend\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X17XagqiO1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X17XagqiO1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  (@washingtonpost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/washingtonpost/status/1645460457728225282?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ranks of disaffected Trump administration officials are deep, and include people who were once in positions of great power. Among them is \uc2 William Barr\uc2 , his former attorney general. Over the weekend, Barr predicted that the former president would be in deep trouble over the January 6 insurrection and the classified documents scandal, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chas a penchant for engaging in reckless and self-destructive behavior\u8221\'20\'1D and is facing a serious threat of a federal indictment over his handling of classified documents and his supporters\u8217\'20\'19 deadly January 6 attack on the US Capitol, his former attorney general \uc2 William Barr\uc2  said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s dug himself a hole on the documents, and also on the January 6 stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D Barr said of the former president during an interview on ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was reckless behavior that was destined to end up being investigated. So it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t surprise me that he has all these legal problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A US justice department special counsel, Jack Smith, is investigating whether Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/04/02/trump-mar-a-lago-obstruction-classified/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obstructed an inquiry}}}\uc2  into his handling of classified documents at the Mar-a-Lago estate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/trump-william-barr-classified-documents-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump \u8216\'20\'18dug himself a hole\u8217\'20\'19 on classified documents and role in January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 Barr}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is trying to prevent his former vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , from testifying to the grand jury investigating the January 6 insurrection, NBC News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has filed an appeal seeking to block \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  from testifying before a federal grand jury hearing evidence related to Jan 6, a source confirms to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LauraAJarrett?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LauraAJarrett}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GaryGrumbach?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GaryGrumbach}}}\uc2  spotted Trump lawyer Evan Corcoran at the DC federal courthouse this morning\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Barnes (@dnlbrns) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dnlbrns/status/1645456851302072322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPence chose not to appeal the district judge's order to testify after he won a narrow victory on speech & debate grounds, but Trump can still appeal on executive privilege grounds\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Barnes (@dnlbrns) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dnlbrns/status/1645457275283202054?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/mike-pence-testify-justice-department-grand-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided to drop}}}\uc2  his legal challenge to the subpoena from special counsel Jack Smith, who is investigating the insurrection at the Capitol in addition to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election and the classified documents discovered at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer elaborated on their strategy to derail the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  with the latest:\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  launches verbal attacks against the prosecutor and judge overseeing his criminal charges in connection with hush money payments to the adult film star Stormy Daniels, an attorney for the former US president has said his main focus is on legal maneuvers aiming to get the case dismissed long before a trial jury is ever seated.\par \par \uc2 Jim Trusty appeared on Sunday on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/week-transcript-4-09-23-bill-barr-jim/story?id=98451968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week}}}\uc2  and argued that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot to play with\u8221\'20\'1D when examining whether New York state prosecutors waited too long to secure an indictment against Trump and if the ex-president intended to commit any crimes with the payments at the center of the case.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/09/trump-indictment-women-stormy-daniels-karen-mcdougal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The payments}}}\uc2  were made at the height of the 2016 White House race which Trump won, and Trusty also reiterated questions that his side has previously asked about whether the office of the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , should be able to apply \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal election law into a New York case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/trump-lawyer-jim-trusty-defense-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lawyer says he aims to get hush money case dismissed before trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican House speaker Cameron Sexton will not try to stop ousted Democrats Justin Jones and Justin Pearson from returning to their seats, should they be reappointed.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to local broadcaster WKRN, who received a statement from Sexton\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Press Sec. for Speaker Cameron Sexton tells me Justin Jones and Justin Pearson will be sat, if the county commissions vote for it.\par \par \uc2 Statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe two governing bodies will make the decision as to who they want to appoint to these seats\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WKRN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WKRN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TNLeg23?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TNLeg23}}}\par \par \uc2 1/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris O\u8217\'20\'19Brien (@THEChrisOB) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/THEChrisOB/status/1645439751359545344?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8230\'20\'26Those two individuals will be seated as representatives as the constitution requires.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WKRN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WKRN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TNLeg23?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TNLeg23}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris O\u8217\'20\'19Brien (@THEChrisOB) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/THEChrisOB/status/1645439753615974400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has (basically) declared his re-election intentions, let\u8217\'20\'19s check in on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his freshly indicted opponent who remains the most popular man among Republican candidates.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110175037026906627"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post on his Truth Social account}}}\uc2  this morning, Trump encouraged Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is widely expected to throw his hat into the 2024 primary field for the GOP nomination, not to run. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the former president\u8217\'20\'19s argument:\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is a young man who is not doing well against me in the polls, to put it mildly. I believe that if he decides to run for President, which will only hurt and somewhat divide the Republican Party, he will lose the cherished and massive MAGA vote, and never be able to successfully run for office again. If he remains Governor, which is what Florida voters assumed, it would be a whole different story\u8230\'20\'26.JUST SAYIN\u8217\'20\'19 - But who knows?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Five dead in Louisville mass shooting\par \par \uc2 Five people have been killed in a mass shooting at a bank building in downtown Louisville, the city\u8217\'20\'19s police department confirms:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe lone shooter is deceased\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 LMPD (@LMPD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LMPD/status/1645435996824010754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTotal deceased is 5. At least 6 more were transported to UL hospital.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 LMPD (@LMPD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LMPD/status/1645436161937092609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been informed of the shooting:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden has been informed of the shooting in Louisville, Kentucky, a White House official tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDiamond1?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JDiamond1}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6c5f15mvq1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6c5f15mvq1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Priscilla Alvarez (@priscialva) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/priscialva/status/1645438912670646272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Follow the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s story for the latest:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/louisville-active-shooting-attack-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Multiple casualties\u8217\'20\'19 in downtown Louisville shooting attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republican Nancy Mace told CNN she also thinks the Biden administration should ignore the ruling from a conservative federal judge ruling that could cut off access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of that interview:\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NancyMace?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NancyMace}}}\uc2  says she believes the \uc2 FDA\uc2  should ignore the Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved drug. Whether you agree with its usage or not, that's not your decision. That is the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wGJBunurcL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wGJBunurcL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1645396103712391170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 While Mace says she opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she has also in the past rejected some of the more extreme proposals from her fellow Republicans aimed at curtailing access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are furious after a conservative federal judge revoked the authorization of one of two drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with some saying the Biden administration should ignore the ruling entirely. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  with the latest:\par \par \uc2 The New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said on Sunday there was \u8220\'20\'1Can extraordinary amount of precedent\u8221\'20\'1D for the Joe Biden White House to ignore a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk#:~:text=A%20federal%20judge%20in%20Texas,brought%20by%20anti%2Dabortion%20activists."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Friday court ruling}}}\uc2  suspending federal approval of a drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those remarks from the Democratic US House member quickly prompted a threat by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  Republican congressman Tony Gonzales to defund certain programs under the federal agency which oversees medication approvals if Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration did as Ocasio-Cortez suggested.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has already said it plans to appeal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Friday ruling}}}\uc2  from Texas-based federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a conservative appointed by the Donald Trump White House, that blocked the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approval of the drug mifepristone. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the drug in 2000, a move that is now being challenged by the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a conservative Christian legal group.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/09/aoc-urges-biden-ignore-texas-abortion-pills-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC urges Biden to ignore Texas ruling suspending approval of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  low-key announces re-election campaign\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  confirmed today that he will stand for a second term in the White House, but will make a former announcement later on.\par \par \uc2 The comment came in an interview with television personality Al Roker during today\u8217\'20\'19s Easter Egg Roll at the White House. After some banter between the two men about whether Biden would be hosting the annual tradition beyond 2024, Roker pressed the president to clarify his intentions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m planning on running, Al, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not ready to announce it yet,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the clip below:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: TODAY\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alroker?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @alroker}}}\uc2  asks President Biden about his possible Presidential run in 2024. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3OELi0yJmK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3OELi0yJmK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TODAY (@TODAYshow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TODAYshow/status/1645400548709892096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Expulsion vote could come back to haunt Tennessee GOP\par \par \uc2 Officially, Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party is defending the vote by its lawmakers to oust two Democrats from the state house of representatives after they staged a noisy protest in favor of gun control legislation. Here\u8217\'20\'19s their statement from Thursday, when the expulsion occurred:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rO5QNTRMYN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rO5QNTRMYN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TN House Republicans (@tnhousegop) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tnhousegop/status/1644175765859180544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And yet, there are signs from within the party that the banishment wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the best idea, despite the fact that Tennessee is an overwhelmingly red state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf my job, along with other members of the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , is to protect the brand of the Republican Party, this didn\u8217\'20\'19t help,\u8221\'20\'1D Oscar Brock, a Republican National Committeeman from Tennessee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/08/us/politics/protests-trump-tennessee-chicago-wisconsin.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve energized young voters against us. Worse than squandering support, you\u8217\'20\'19ve made enemies where we didn\u8217\'20\'19t need them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 Even in Tennessee, we have swing districts in the State House and Senate and if you\u8217\'20\'19ve angered tens of thousands of students and presumably their parents, you could theoretically expose yourself to a united front.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The GOP is already reeling nationally as it feels the consequences of its enthusiastic support for the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade. Last week, a conservative candidate lost the race for a crucial Wisconsin supreme court seat, which could set the stage for Democrats to undo the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s gerrymandered legislative maps and its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 As for the two Black Democrats ousted from the Tennessee House last week, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson, they seem set to be reappointed to their seats by the local councils in their constituencies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ousted Tennessee Democrat may head back to statehouse after vote today\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Republicans in Tennessee last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/tennessee-gun-control-protest-house-expel-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed}}}\uc2  two Black Democratic lawmakers who staged a noisy protest in favor of gun regulations on the floor of the state house of representatives, but they may not be gone for long. The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tennessee-expulsion-democracy-election-nashville-60e64c8c972d48cce64992b9e1f8f04c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that Nashville\u8217\'20\'19s metro council will today vote to send one of the now-former lawmakers right back to his seat, while the Shelby county commission could do the same for the other legislator on Wednesday. We\u8217\'20\'19ll then see what the state GOP thinks of this.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill access{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-explainer-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears imperiled}}}\uc2  after a Friday evening ruling from a conservative Texas federal judge revoked the approval of one of two pills used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though another judge in Washington state simultaneously ordered the pills remain available.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans remain very, very mad at Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  for indicting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1645404735510282241"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have just announced}}}\uc2  a hearing featuring \u8220\'20\'1Cvictims of violent crime in Manhattan\u8221\'20\'1D for next Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  briefs reporters at 2pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230410ej4a001ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
