\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What next?\u8217\'20\'19 Schumer lambasts Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 808 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par 15:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats including Senate majority leader warn of \u8216\'20\'18dangerous new precedent\u8217\'20\'19 set by ruling and vow to fight it\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers are doubling down on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/08/abortion-pill-mifepristone-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outrage}}}\uc2  against Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that threatens access to a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, saying the ruling sets a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous new precedent\u8221\'20\'1D that could harm future medications approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake, the decision could throw our country into chaos,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  on a call with reporters on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have completely eviscerated the \uc2 FDA\uc2  as we know it and threatened the ability of any drug on the market to avoid being prohibited.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat could come next if some fringe radical group brings a lawsuit? Cancer drugs? Insulin? Mental health treatment?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone was approved for use by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2000 and, along with a second drug called misoprostol, is the most common method for terminating a pregnancy in the US. More than half of women in the country who get abortions use the two medications.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk of Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone in a lawsuit that challenges the drug\u8217\'20\'19s initial approval. Kacsmaryk gave the \uc2 FDA\uc2  a week to appeal his ruling.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a federal court in Washington state handed down a conflicting ruling that orders the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to not take any action that affects the drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability.\par \par \uc2 The president and chief executive officer of the Center for Reproductive Rights, Nancy Northrup, told reporters the Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision could have a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating impact\u8221\'20\'1D if it goes into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf allowed to stand, it would remove mifepristone from the market in states where it\u8217\'20\'19s legal and exposes the lie\u8221\'20\'1D that states would get to decide their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights through their Dobbs decision last year, Northrup said. She added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt threatens the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority over its entire drug approval process, which could severely limit the development of new drugs overall and have far-reaching repercussions on patients\u8217\'20\'19 access to \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medications.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Northrup emphasized that the medication is a safe and effective means of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the drug is on the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s list of essential medicines. She also said the appeal could end up in the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  within a week, if the litigation from the 2021 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 which was quickly taken up by the court \u8211\'20\'13 is any indication.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s entirely possible, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers across the country are preparing and being advised on what to do if this actually goes into effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Northrup said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats on Saturday said they support the appeal that the US justice department on Friday indicated it would file, seeking a halt to Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision. And the party is still working to get the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act passed. The legislation, introduced late last month, seeks to protect abortions on a federal measure but lacks the Republican support needed to pass.\par \par \uc2 A Democratic senator from Washington, \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , said Democrats would \u8220\'20\'1Cput Republicans on the record every way we can so the American people know exactly who is responsible for this chaos\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will have this debate out in the public for everyone to see,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Schumer said that Republicans have likely mostly been silent on the ruling because \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re afraid to speak out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is outrageous. They are letting the \u8230\'20\'26 extreme wing of their party \u8230\'20\'26 run the whole show,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have an obligation to speak out or they are complicit in taking away mifepristone for tens of millions of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beyond the justice department appeal, it is unclear what other course of action Democrats are planning to take to combat the ruling. Schumer and Murray were asked by a reporter if there is any possibility that the federal government could take similar action to Washington state, where governor \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2  announced on Tuesday that his administration would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/04/1167867948/washington-state-stockpiles-thousands-of-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stockpile}}}\uc2  thousands of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills for his constituents in anticipation of it becoming difficult to access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur very first action is to make sure that this does not go into effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray said. \u8220\'20\'1COur most important task is to have this appealed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also on Saturday, more than 40 House Democrats sent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSummerLee/status/1644724038684622852?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  calling on the president to \u8220\'20\'1Cuse all the tools at your disposal to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The representatives said that in addition to legal action against the ruling, the White House should defend the authority of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and meet with the pharmaceutical industry to \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss possible ramifications of an unfavorable decision regarding market access to medication abortions and the implications it will have on the [\uc2 FDA\uc2 ] drug review process at large\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230408ej480028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
