\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Democrats condemn judge\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18draconian\u8217\'20\'19 decision threatening  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drug\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 1,057 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par 15:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Party members call on Biden to do more to protect reproductive rights amid conflicting judicial rulings on mifepristone\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  angrily denounced as \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdraconian\u8221\'20\'1D a decision by a Texas judge that threatens access to a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, while demanding the Joe Biden White House do more to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Nearly a quarter-century after the Food and Drug Administration approved the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, the federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to invalidate the agency\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2 , handing down an unprecedented order that \u8211\'20\'13 if upheld \u8211\'20\'13 would severely restrict access to one of the most commonly used methods of terminating a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In a dueling court ruling, handed down moments after, a judge in Washington state contradicted the Texas decision, ordering the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to maintain the \u8220\'20\'1Cstatus quo\u8221\'20\'1D availability of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 With the future of access to medication {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in potential jeopardy, even in states where the procedure remains legal, Democrats, reproductive rights advocates and providers vowed to keep fighting to protect the drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden}}}\uc2  called the ruling the \u8220\'20\'1Cnext big step toward the national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Republican elected officials have vowed to make law in America\u8221\'20\'1D and pledged to fight Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision. On Friday night, the justice department gave notice that it would appeal the Texas ruling and said it was reviewing the Washington decision.\par \par \uc2 The conflicting court orders left much uncertainty about the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, probably elevating the issue to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . With little faith in a majority conservative court that overturned Roe v Wade, Democrats are urging the administration to act more aggressively.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIgnore this ruling,\u8221\'20\'1D the US senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , a Democrat of Oregon, said, arguing that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has the authority to disregard the decision by Kacsmaryk, who was appointed to the federal bench by the Donald Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 Wyden added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2 , doctors, and pharmacies can and must go about their jobs like nothing has changed and keep mifepristone accessible to women across America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is the first pill in a two-drug medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen, which is approved for use through the 10th week of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than half}}}\uc2  of abortions in the US rely on the medication, and the Texas decision, if allowed to stand, would have severe ramifications for access.\par \par \uc2 The president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group All* Above All, Morgan Hopkins, said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration must \u8220\'20\'1Cact immediately to ensure medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care remains available, without interference from politicians or judges\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court eliminated the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , administration officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have moved}}}\uc2  to expand access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication and protect patients seeking care who travel to states where the procedure is legal. But the White House has so far resisted calls from reproductive rights advocates to declare a public health emergency for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden has insisted, as he did again on Friday, that the \u8220\'20\'1Conly way to stop those who are committed to taking away women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D is to elect candidates who will codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into federal law.\par \par \uc2 The Texas ruling comes days after a liberal judge won a commanding victory to serve on the Wisconsin supreme court in a contest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results-janet-protasiewicz-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that underscored the enduring potency of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  politics}}}\uc2 . The judge, Janet Protasiewicz, had effectively promised voters that if they elected her, flipping the ideological balance of the court from conservative to liberal, the new majority would overturn Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Successive victories in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights from Kansas to Michigan have galvanized Democrats, who say the issue was key to their unexpectedly strong showing in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. The party plans to continue harnessing voter anger over the loss of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in upcoming elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican party is playing with fire,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cecile Richards, a former president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  who is now a co-chair at American Bridge 21st Century, a Democratic organization. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have put their rightwing politics ahead of the health and wellbeing of American women. They are trying to strip Americans of our basic rights to control our bodies and our futures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler, president of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, said the group was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking overtime to replace Republicans up and down the ballot with Democratic pro-choice women who are committed to protecting our reproductive freedoms no matter what\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democrats were quick to cast the decision by Kacsmaryk, who had written critically of the Roe precedent, as part of a broader effort by conservatives to erode women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is bullshit,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mobile.twitter.com/CortezMasto/status/1644477999851397120"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , a Democrat of Nevada who narrowly won re-election last year after making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a central issue of her campaign.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Connecticut senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  added in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow rightwing judges to ignore the science, and put the health, safety, and autonomy of millions of women at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And Congressman \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the US House Democratic leader, said Republican efforts to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care were \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democraticleader.house.gov/media/press-releases/leader-jeffries-statement-district-court-decision-suspend-fda-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a malignant tumor}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D spreading across the US.\par \par \uc2 Yet despite their fury, congressional Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oregoncapitalchronicle.com/2023/04/06/as-future-of-abortion-pill-is-weighed-democrats-in-congress-see-little-they-can-do/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see few legislative options}}}\uc2 . With Republicans in control of the House, and Senate Democrats unable to eliminate the 60-vote legislative filibuster, efforts to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access are all but certain to fall short.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  of New York, said his caucus was \u8220\'20\'1Crelentlessly working to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose from this extreme \u8230\'20\'26 Republican agenda\u8221\'20\'1D and recommitted to passing the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, legislation that seeks to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in federal law. But the measure lacks enough support to overcome the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 In response to the Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, a number of Democrats renewed calls to eliminate the filibuster in the Senate, though they do not have enough support among their caucus to do so.\par \par \uc2 Some prominent conservatives celebrated Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision. For instance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CLife won again today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But some top Republicans, including Trump, the leading contender for the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, were silent late on Friday, reflecting a growing unease within the party about the political risks of overreaching on one of the most emotionally charged issues in American politics.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230408ej48001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
