\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unborn human\u8217\'20\'19: the anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rhetoric of Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 911 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk issued a ruling on Friday aiming to suspend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone\par \par \uc2 Texas-based federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk on Friday issued a ruling aiming to suspend the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug approved for use 23 years ago that has been consistently found to be safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 It is widely believed that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups who brought the case challenging the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authorization of the drug did so in Amarillo, Texas, so that it would be certain to land on the desk of this particular judge. Kacsmaryk, who was appointed by Donald Trump, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known for disregarding precedent}}}\uc2  and for weighing in on the far-right side of culture war issues.\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s 67-page {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067.137.0_8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a preliminary ruling that will be appealed and is likely to wind its way up to the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 makes plain that the strategy paid off. His decision employs the same rhetoric that has been deliberately seeded over decades by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. Some examples are below.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unborn child\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In the very first footnote to the decision, Kacsmaryk sets the tone for the opinion, explaining he why he will use \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn human\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D throughout his ruling:\par \par \uc2 Jurists often use the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfetus\u8221\'20\'1D to inaccurately identify unborn humans in unscientific ways. The word \u8220\'20\'1Cfetus\u8221\'20\'1D refers to a specific gestational stage of development, as opposed to the zygote, blastocyst, or embryo stages \u8230\'20\'26 Because other jurists use the terms \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn human\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D interchangeably, and because both terms are inclusive of the multiple gestational stages relevant to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  Approval, 2016 Changes, and 2021 Changes, this Court uses \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn human\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D terminology throughout this Order, as appropriate.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18To kill the unborn human\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, the drug at the center of the case, works by blocking progesterone, a hormone required for a pregnancy to develop. It is approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to be taken up until 10 weeks of pregnancy and is generally used in conjunction with misoprostol, which causes the uterus to contract. This is how Kacsmaryk describes this two-pill regimen, which together account for more than half the abortions in the US:\par \par \uc2 Because mifepristone alone will not always complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 FDA\uc2  mandates a two-step drug regimen: mifepristone to kill the unborn human, followed by misoprostol to induce cramping and contractions to expel the unborn human from the mother\u8217\'20\'19s womb.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Shame, regret, anxiety, depression\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is known to champion the idea that people who have abortions come to be plagued by regret \u8211\'20\'13 an idea promoted by former supreme court justice \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2  in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supct/html/05-380.ZO.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2007 decision}}}\uc2 , even as he admitted there\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cno reliable data to measure the phenomenon\u8221\'20\'1D. But reliable data finally came in 2020, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ucsf.edu/news/2020/01/416421/five-years-after-abortion-nearly-all-women-say-it-was-right-decision-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark Turnaway Study}}}\uc2 , which spent five years following nearly 1,000 women who sought abortions. The study found that 95% of women who had abortions reported five years later that it had been the right decision for them.\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk, however, writes:\par \par \uc2 Women who have aborted a child \u8211\'20\'13 especially through chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs that necessitate the woman seeing her aborted child once it passes \u8211\'20\'13 often experience shame, regret, anxiety, depression, drug abuse\par \par \uc2 and suicidal thoughts because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Fetal personhood\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk also writes that any consideration of alleged damage caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill should extend to the fetus. This is a nod to the radical idea of \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that embryos and fetuses are people entitled to the full protection of the US constitution. That argument presumes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be murder, and were it to take hold in the legal system, could lead to a national ban on the procedure. Invoking the name of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision which eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, he writes:\par \par \uc2 Parenthetically, said \u8220\'20\'1Cindividual justice\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cirreparable injury\u8221\'20\'1D analysis also arguably applies to the unborn humans extinguished by mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 especially in the post-Dobbs era.\par \par \uc2 Comstock Act\par \par \uc2 The groups that brought the case ruled on by Kacsmaryk aim to revive a long dormant, 150-year-old anti-obscenity law called the Comstock Act, which prohibited sending abortifacients in the mail. Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision indeed revives that law \u8211\'20\'13 and some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mobile.twitter.com/maryrziegler/status/1644508131832233985"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts fear his logic}}}\uc2  could extend to more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  methods and even lead to a national ban.\par \par \uc2 This purported \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus view\u8221\'20\'1D is that the Comstock Act does not prohibit the mailing of items designed to produce abortions \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere the sender does not intend them to be used unlawfully\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Id. This argument is unpersuasive for several reasons \u8230\'20\'26 In any case, the Comstock Act plainly forecloses mail-order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the present \u8230\'20\'26 the law is plain.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as eugenics\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk also quotes conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , who has linked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2019/05/28/politics/clarence-thomas-eugenics-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to eugenics}}}\uc2 , the belief in selective breeding to produce a superior society. In rejecting research pointing to worse psychosocial and financial outcomes for children of people denied abortions, he also seems to draw a line between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the worst atrocities of the last century:\par \par \uc2 (\u8220\'20\'1C[A]bortion has proved to be a disturbingly effective tool for implementing the discriminatory preferences that undergird eugenics.\u8221\'20\'1D)\par \par \uc2 Though eugenics were once fashionable in the Commanding Heights and High Court, they hold less purchase after the conflict, carnage\par \par \uc2 and casualties of the last century revealed the bloody consequences of Social Darwinism practiced by would-be \u220\'00\'DCbermenschen.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230408ej48001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
