\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meets with Nashville lawmakers after Democrats expelled over anti-gun protests \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (now), Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 6,049 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par 00:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president visiting lawmakers at \uc2 Fisk University\uc2  as Republican-controlled house\u8217\'20\'19s move condemned as racistSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Evening Summary\par \par \uc2 After an intense week of news, I am signing off of the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live blog. Here are some of the biggest things to happen today. Thanks for joining us, and we wish everyone a peaceful holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Trump-appointed federal judge in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  has ordered a hold on the US approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, one of the two drugs commonly used for medication abortions, in a closely watched case brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke at \uc2 Fisk University\uc2  in Nashville to show support for the two Black lawmakers who were ousted following an anti-gun protest on the statehouse floor. During the last-minute visit, Harris reaffirmed the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s consistent calls for Congress to impose a ban on assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , the Arizona senator who flipped from the Democratic party to become an independent in December, is planning to defend her seat next year, the Wall Street Journal reported, setting up a three-way contest in the highly competitive state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended himself}}}\uc2  after reports he accepted decades of undeclared hospitality from a Republican mega-donor. Thomas, a staunch conservative, says he didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe he was required to disclose it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/supreme-court-west-virginia-bid-trans-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a proposal }}}\uc2  that would forbid schools and colleges across the US from enacting outright bans on transgender athletes competing in sports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US officials say they suspect Russia is behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/pentagon-investigates-reported-leak-of-top-secret-ukraine-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaking and posting on social media}}}\uc2  of top secret documents, including an assessment of the country\u8217\'20\'19s progress in its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Kansas voted to ban gender-affirming medical care for transgender youth, but the bill is likely to be vetoed by Democratic governor \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 A Trump-appointed federal judge in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  has ordered a hold on the US approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, one of the two drugs commonly used for medication abortions, in a closely watched case brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Matthew J Kacsmaryk signed an injunction directing the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) \uc2 to stay mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval while a lawsuit challenging the safety and approval of the drug continues. The immediate impact of the ruling was not clear, including how quickly access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill might be curtailed.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on the ruling, Senator Elizabeth Warren called on \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to swiftly appeal the decision:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of today\u8217\'20\'19s lawless ruling by an extremist Republican judge, women across the country could lose access to a safe and legal medication they\u8217\'20\'19ve relied on for decades. Attorney General Garland should quickly appeal this decision in order to preserve access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and I urge the Biden administration to use every legal and regulatory tool in its power to keep this drug available.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The case against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was brought by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), a Christian conservative legal advocacy group, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/Alliance-for-Hippocratic-Medicine-v-FDA-2022-11-18-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing that}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2  exceeded its regulatory authority when it approved mifepristone more than two decades ago, in 2000.\par \par \uc2 In the complaint, the group argues that the drug puts the health of women and girls at risk and invoked a 19th-century law that made it illegal to send \u8220\'20\'1Cobscene, lewd or lascivious\u8221\'20\'1D items through the mail, including pornography and abortifacients.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 While speaking at \uc2 Fisk University\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reaffirmed the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s consistent calls for Congress to impose a ban on assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 Her visit to the HBCU comes on the heels of the expulsion of Justin Pearson and Justin Jones, Democratic state lawmakers who held a protest on the Tennessee statehouse floor while it was in session. The protest was meant to draw attention to the 27 March killing of three students and three school staff at a Christian school in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CAssault weapons. These are weapons of war. These are weapons that are designed to kill a lot of people quickly. They have no place on the streets of a civil society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Becca Andrews (@kbeccaandrews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kbeccaandrews/status/1644474333601964036?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and the three Tennessee lawmakers at the center of an unprecedented expulsion effort are gathered at a chapel on the campus of Fisk, a historically Black university in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meets with Gloria Johnson, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson at \uc2 Fisk University\uc2 . Photograph: Andrew Nelles/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is currently meeting with the Democratic lawmakers of Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s statehouse at \uc2 Fisk University\uc2 , the alma mater of Justin Jones, who alongside Justin Pearson, was expelled from the state legislature yesterday.\par \par \uc2 After meeting with officials, Harris will address the hundreds of people gathered at the Fisk memorial chapel. The vice-president is expected to voice her support of Jones, Pearson and Gloria Johnson (the sole legislator to keep her seat) and renew the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s call for an assault weapons ban, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 Becca Andrews is in the chapel and we\u8217\'20\'19ll be sharing her dispatches on the blog.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s feeling even more like a church service in here. Lots of call and response, lots of amens, go on\u8217\'20\'19s, that\u8217\'20\'19s right\u8217\'20\'19s. There is love and passion in this sanctuary.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Becca Andrews (@kbeccaandrews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kbeccaandrews/status/1644462202722607105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are keeping an eye on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s last-minute trip to Tennessee following the expulsion of two Black lawmakers via Becca Andrews, a reporter based in Nashville. She is sitting in what appears to be a church sanctuary awaiting Harris\u8217\'20\'19s arrival.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m covering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s appearance to support the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Tennessee3?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Tennessee3}}}\uc2  in Nashville today for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @guardian}}}\uc2 . Follow along here! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iqOTpml3Yr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iqOTpml3Yr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Becca Andrews (@kbeccaandrews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kbeccaandrews/status/1644449691491262464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two Black parents, their midwife and other supporters are calling on Dallas child protective services to return an infant who advocates say was \u8220\'20\'1Ckidnapped\u8221\'20\'1D because the couple chose to use a midwife and treat their child\u8217\'20\'19s jaundice at home instead of at a hospital, Jezebel reports.\par \par \uc2 Rodney and Temecia Jackson of Dallas say that police came to their home late last month to tell them that they had to turn their daughter Mila over based on a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s report. They refused, and days later police returned, arrested Rodney, and used his key to enter the home and take the infant from Temecia.\par \par \uc2 I felt like they had stolen my baby, as I\u8217\'20\'19d had a home birth. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know where to turn,\u8221\'20\'1D Temecia said.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the latest examples of what advocates describe as a historical pattern of US child welfare services dividing poor, Black and Indigenous families in particular on the grounds of alleged neglect and abuse. As my colleague Edwin Rios reported in March, Bianca Clayborne and Deonte Williams\u8217\'20\'19s five children were taken into the state of Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s custody after Williams was arrested during a traffic stop.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s department of children\u8217\'20\'19s services ultimately alleged that Clayborne and Williams\u8217\'20\'19s children were being abused to obtain an emergency order to take them away.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Edwin\u8217\'20\'19s coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/18/police-stopped-a-couple-in-tennessee-then-they-took-their-children-away"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And the Jezebel article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/black-couple-says-texas-authorities-seized-their-newbor-1850309498"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon, I\u8217\'20\'19m Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, taking over the blog from the west coast.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Martin Pengelly reported on \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  investigation that found that the supreme court justice has long accepted expensive gifts, including yacht trips and luxury resort stays, from Republican mega-donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thomas says that he was advised early on in his tenure that this \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal hospitality from close personal friends\u8221\'20\'1D did not need to be disclosed.\par \par \uc2 But a rule change last month now requires gifts like rides on private jets to be reported. Thomas says he will follow the updated guidance in the future.\par \par \uc2 Following the \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report, the justice has been lambasted by Democratic officials including \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , who said: \u8220\'20\'1CThomas must be impeached,\u8221\'20\'1D as the court was becoming known for \u8220\'20\'1Crank corruption, erosion of democracy and the stripping of human rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of Martin\u8217\'20\'19s story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , the enigmatic Arizona senator who stunned colleagues by announcing she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/09/kyrsten-sinema-independent-days-after-democrats-secure-senate-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flipping to become an independent}}}\uc2  after Democrats retained control of the chamber in December, plans to defend her seat, according to the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kyrsten-sinema-is-preparing-for-a-2024-re-election-campaign-23edb2fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on Friday}}}\uc2  that Sinema is \u8220\'20\'1Cpreparing for a re-election campaign, setting the stage for what could be an unpredictable three-way contest\u8221\'20\'1D next year in the key swing state.\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 . Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 The article said Sinema met with staff at a retreat in Phoenix earlier this week to begin laying the groundwork for her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Along with West Virginia Democrat and centrist senator Joe Manchin, Sinema was a holdout on several key elements of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legislative agenda during the first two years of his administration, though she still caucuses with, and usually votes in tandem with Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court sided with the justice department on Friday in a case that could have upended hundreds of charges brought in the January 6 Capitol riot, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The decision, however, leaves open the possibility of further challenges to the charge of obstruction of Congress, which has been brought against more than 300 defendants in the massive federal prosecutions following the deadly violence, the agency says.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: THREAD: This is significant. The appellate court has REVERSED judge Nichols ruling that 18 USC 1512(c)(2) Obstructing an Official Proceeding doesn\u8217\'20\'19t apply to January 6. 1/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mueller, She Wrote (@MuellerSheWrote) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MuellerSheWrote/status/1644354677704904705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In a 2-1 ruling, a three judge panel of the US court of appeals for the District of Columbia circuit said a lower court judge was wrong in dismissing the charge in three cases in which the judge concluded it didn\u8217\'20\'19t cover the defendants\u8217\'20\'19 conduct. Those defendants may ask the full appeals court or the supreme court to review the decision.\par \par \uc2 The charge of obstruction of an official proceeding, which carries a prison term of up to 20 years, is among the most widely used felony charges in the January 6 cases. It has been brought against extremists accused of plotting to stop the transfer of presidential power from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as well as in dozens of less serious cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spared Tennessee lawmaker: Republicans 'talked down' to Black colleagues\par \par \uc2 Gloria Johnson, the Tennessee Democratic house lawmaker spared from expulsion as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Black colleagues were booted}}}\uc2 , is accusing Republicans of conducting effectively a sham trial.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has just been speaking on CNN, where she said she was subjected to a markedly different tone during questioning than that directed at her ousted Black colleagues Justin Jones and Justin Pearson :\par \par \uc2 Gloria Johnson with Justin Jones. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Justin Jones, whose resolution went before mine, made such a beautiful defense. I was like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh my goodness, I could never be that eloquent and articulate\u8217\'20\'19. [He is] a powerful speaker, and Justin Pearson after that.\par \par \uc2 But when you heard the tone of the questioning in there, on how they were questioned, and how I was questioned, it was clear what that was about.\par \par \uc2 They were talking down, they were rude. It was like they were prosecutors, but then they didn\u8217\'20\'19t allow us to build a defense. They allowed themselves to bring video but we were told we could not bring video.\par \par \uc2 They were dishonest throughout the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Johnson took issue with a statement from Republican caucus chair Jeremy Faison, who said the trio might have been spared an expulsion vote of they had apologized for taking part in a protest on the House floor for gun reforms:\par \par \uc2 They can say that now. But that certainly wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the tone of the questioning.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Justinjpearson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Justinjpearson}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CYou all heard that. How many of you would want to be spoken to that way?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pearson responds to Rep. Farmer\u8217\'20\'19s belittling, disrespectful rant. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TennesseeThree?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TennesseeThree}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5uWznU7atq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5uWznU7atq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Tennessee Holler (@TheTNHoller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheTNHoller/status/1644113522807152640?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Regarding meeting vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  later, Johnson said she would be raising the immediate need for firearms reforms following last week\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting at Nashville\u8217\'20\'19s Covenant school that left six dead:\par \par \uc2 I just want to talk about the immediacy of getting solutions for gun violence. I\u8217\'20\'19m so very proud of this young generation who are organizing and fighting and working so hard, showing up and speaking up at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a rare day on the politics blog when we get to the afternoon without a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -related post. My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/kari-paul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Paul}}}\uc2  has this look at an interview given by adult movie actress Stormy Daniels, and the hush-money payment made by the former president that led to this week\u8217\'20\'19s criminal charges against him:\par \par \uc2 In her first major interview since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s indictment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2  has said that while she wants the former president to be \u8220\'20\'1Cheld accountable\u8221\'20\'1D she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe he should go to prison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that his crimes against me are worthy of incarceration. I feel like the other things that he has done, if he is found guilty, absolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D Daniels, 44, said in an interview with Fox Nation\u8217\'20\'19s Piers Morgan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/piersmorgan/status/1644080931215671296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Stormy Daniels. Photograph: Robyn Beck/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Daniels sat down with Morgan for a 1.5 hour interview, which she called her most extensive yet. She thanked people for \u8220\'20\'1Clove and support\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StormyDaniels/status/1644081842482745344"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a tweet}}}\uc2 , saying that the segment \u8220\'20\'1Claid to rest a lot of misinformation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked by Morgan how it felt to see Trump appear in court, Daniels said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI thought he was going to get away with not being accountable,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe king has been dethroned \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s no longer untouchable,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody should be untouchable, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter what your job description is \u8211\'20\'13 whether you\u8217\'20\'19re the president \u8211\'20\'13 you should be held responsible for your actions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Daniels, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/stormy-daniels-piers-morgan-uncensored-interview-security-issues-1235570481/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postponed the original timing}}}\uc2  of her interview with Morgan last week citing \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity concerns\u8221\'20\'1D, said she was also regularly receiving threats. She told Morgan that one in 10 messages she gets now are death threats, and that the tone has become increasingly violent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like a suicide bomber,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the depths of their soul, they feel like they\u8217\'20\'19re doing the right thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/stormy-daniels-interview-donald-trump-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The king has been dethroned\u8217\'20\'19: Stormy Daniels speaks on Trump indictment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate leaders partner for detained journalist's release\par \par \uc2 A rare joint statement from Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and his Republican counterpart \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is calling on Russia to release an American Wall Street Journal reporter who was arrested last week.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in Moscow have charged \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  with espionage, Reuters reported on Friday, citing the Interfax news agency. The 31-year-old journalist was detained last month during a reporting trip to the city of Yekaterinburg, and faces up to 20 years in prison if convicted.\par \par \uc2 According to the news agency, Gershkovich pleaded not guilty during a court hearing on Friday.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe demand the baseless, fabricated charges against \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  be dropped and he be immediately released by the Russian government.\par \par \uc2 Let there be no mistake: journalism is not a crime. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dK9CMrps4z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dK9CMrps4z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1644352425480814596?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In their statement, the senate leaders insisted \u8220\'20\'1Cjournalism is not a crime\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 We strongly condemn the wrongful detention of US citizen and Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , and demand the immediate release of this internationally known and respected independent journalist.\par \par \uc2 Russian authorities have failed to present any credible evidence to justify their fabricated charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Black Democratic party legislators in Tennessee are appealing to Republicans to hold talks with them over the shock expulsion of two state lawmakers last night because they joined a public demonstration in the legislative chamber demanding greater gun safety after yet another school shooting.\par \par \uc2 Amid news that US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is hastily arranging to visit Tennessee later today and meet with the ousted lawmakers, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson, the Tennessee Black caucus of state legislators spoke outside the state capitol a little earlier.\par \par \uc2 Representative Sam McKenzie of Knoxville, chairman of the Tennessee Black caucus, called almost unprecedented ousting of the lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Can injustice\u8221\'20\'1D, local media {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbir.com/article/news/politics/black-caucus-tennessee-three-house-expulsions-racism/51-a529385a-de28-4939-9155-7a4493f0500a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world saw the optics. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have to say a word about the fact that our two young African American brothers were unfairly prosecuted with information... evidence introduced inappropriately, but they handled themselves like true champions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 State representative Sam McKenzie of the Tennessee Black caucus of state legislators responds to questions during a press conference outside the state capitol today. Photograph: George Walker IV/AP\par \par \uc2 The two lawmakers, and Democratic state representative Gloria Johnson, are now known as the Tennessee Three. Johnson narrowly survived a vote to expel her. The two men are in their twenties. Johnson is white and in her sixties. \u8220\'20\'1CI made it through, and these two young men did not make it through,\u8221\'20\'1D she said earlier today, and it was reported that she agreed when asked if her being white played a part in her not being expelled from the legislature.\par \par \uc2 Nashville representative Vincent Dixie said: \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome to Tennessee, where there\u8217\'20\'19s a pattern of racism that has permeated these halls that we walked through that were supposed to make laws for everyone here in Tennessee.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is watching. And what are we going to do now? Is it gonna be business as usual? \u8216\'20\'18Well, it happened to two Black men. Oh, well. Let\u8217\'20\'19s move on.\u8217\'20\'19 Or are we going to actually do something about it?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbir.com/article/news/politics/black-caucus-tennessee-three-house-expulsions-racism/51-a529385a-de28-4939-9155-7a4493f0500a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WBIR.com reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-president to visit Tennessee after lawmakers kicked out\par \par \uc2 US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  plans to travel to Nashville, Tennessee, today after the Republicans controlling the state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expelled two}}}\uc2  young Black lawmakers last night for joining public protests demanding greater gun safety in the wake of a mass shooting at an elementary school in the city.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a tweet from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Kirsten Allen.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW >> Today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  will travel to Nashville, TN. There she will meet with state lawmakers as well as young leaders who continue to demand action on common sense gun reform. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kMeaAAF1UI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kMeaAAF1UI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kirsten Allen (@KirstenAllen46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KirstenAllen46/status/1644382413231882241?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris will meet with the two lawmakers, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson, and a third Democratic lawmaker, Gloria Johnson, who is white and narrowly avoided being expelled.\par \par \uc2 The move has been condemned as racist, anti-democratic and not in the interests of protecting children\u8217\'20\'19s safety from gun violence and school shootings, critics say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime on Friday, and we\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to hear from Democrats in Tennessee how they intend to respond to the vote by Republicans to expel two young Black Democrats from the state\u8217\'20\'19s House after they led a protest calling for gun reforms.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of outrage}}}\uc2  followed Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s move. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  blasted the move \u8220\'20\'1Cundemocratic\u8221\'20\'1D while the ACLU of Tennessee, and Martin Luther King III, son of the civil rights pioneer, suggested racism was behind the action.\par \par \uc2 Both point out that the two expelled lawmakers are Black, while a third Democrat involved in the protest, who won enough support to survive the vote to oust her, is white.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defending himself}}}\uc2  after reports he accepted decades or undeclared hospitality from a Republican mega-donor. Thomas, a staunch conservative, says he didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe he was required to disclose it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/supreme-court-west-virginia-bid-trans-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a proposal }}}\uc2  that would forbid schools and colleges across the US from enacting outright bans on transgender athletes competing in sports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US officials say they suspect Russia is behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/pentagon-investigates-reported-leak-of-top-secret-ukraine-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaking and posting on social media}}}\uc2  of top secret documents, including an assessment of the country\u8217\'20\'19s progress in its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Kansas voted to ban gender-affirming medical care for transgender youth, but the bill is likely to be vetoed by Democratic governor \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more to come this afternoon, please stick with us.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 US officials say they know who\u8217\'20\'19s behind the leak and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/pentagon-investigates-reported-leak-of-top-secret-ukraine-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posting on social media of classified documents}}}\uc2  offering their assessment of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s progress in the war in Ukraine: it\u8217\'20\'19s Russia.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported on Friday that three US officials, speaking anonymously, told the news agency that the documents also appear to have been altered to lower the number of casualties suffered by Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 The military documents offer a partial, month-old snapshot of the war, they said, adding that their assessment that Russia, or pro-Russian elements, were behind the leak was informal, and separate to an official investigation into what happened.\par \par \uc2 The three declined to discuss the documents in detail, the agency said, and the Kremlin and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Washington did not immediately respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Lorenzo Tondo reported on Friday that the Pentagon is investigating the security breach in which classified war documents detailing secret American and Nato plans for supplying aid to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  before its prospective offensive against Russia were leaked to Telegram and Twitter.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/pentagon-investigates-reported-leak-of-top-secret-ukraine-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pentagon investigates reported leak of top-secret Ukraine documents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Tennessee chapter of the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) \uc2 has added its voice to the furor over the expulsion of two Democratic Black state lawmakers by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Kathy Sinback, the chapter\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, attacks the racial overtones of what she calls a \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful\u8221\'20\'1D move:\par \par \uc2 Over the course of this legislative session, the Tennessee general assembly has systematically eroded the rights of some of the most vulnerable communities in our state. These expelled lawmakers represent over 136,000 people \u8211\'20\'13 predominantly people of color \u8211\'20\'13 in districts across the state, and this expulsion strips these voters of their representation.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Rep. Justin Jones and Rep. Justin Pearson have been expelled from our state legislature, an extreme measure that undermines democracy while disenfranchising & silencing the voices of marginalized communities.\par \par \uc2 Our statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XDHWrDIOZE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XDHWrDIOZE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU of Tennessee (@aclutn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aclutn/status/1644149231408541696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, only a small minority of Tennessee legislators are people of color. Not only is this targeted expulsion of two Black legislators without due process an extreme measure that undermines democracy, it raises questions about the disparate treatment of Black representatives, while continuing the shameful legacy of disenfranchising and silencing the voices of marginalized communities and the Black lawmakers they elect.\par \par \uc2 This unprecedented, authoritarian effort to silence opposition sets a dangerous precedent that could threaten democracy in statehouses across the country. We will continue to fight for a state where all Tennesseans have a voice and are treated justly and equitably.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleagues on the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s video production team have compiled this rather excellent look at the expulsion of two Black Democratic lawmakers by Republicans in Tennessee, noting such \u8220\'20\'1Cbanishments\u8221\'20\'1D have taken place only a handful of times since the American civil war.\par \par \uc2 The episode has ignited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furious backlash}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  downwards, and features elements of racism, Republicans standing in the way of gun reforms, and an assault of democracy.\par \par \uc2 The video is well worth a look. You can watch it here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  defends undeclared hospitality\par \par \uc2 Embattled supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  says he believed the decades of lavish hospitality he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received from a Republican mega-donor}}}\uc2  did not need to be disclosed.\par \par \uc2 The statement from the conservative justice released on Friday is his first response to the bombshell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusations by ProPublica}}}\uc2  the day before that he took travel on yachts and jets, and other gifts funded by the property billionaire \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 , but did not declare them.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Democrats are calling for Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment.\par \par \uc2 In the lengthy statement, a rare move for a sitting supreme court justice, Thomas says, in part:\par \par \uc2 Early in my tenure at the Court, I sought guidance from my colleagues and others in the judiciary, and was advised that this sort of personal hospitality from close personal friends, who did not have business before the Court, was not reportable.\par \par \uc2 I have endeavored to follow that counsel throughout my tenure, and have always sought to comply with the disclosure guidelines.\par \par \uc2 Thomas says he will comply with tweaks made to disclosure rules for all justices and federal judges last month that require personal hospitality to be declared.\par \par \uc2 In his own statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawandcrime.com/supreme-court/justice-thomas-accused-of-breaking-the-law-by-going-on-secret-superyacht-trips-and-his-billionaire-pal-had-a-telling-response/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by Law and Crime}}}\uc2 , Crow insisted he and his wife Kathy were \u8220\'20\'1Cdear friends\u8221\'20\'1D with Thomas and his wife Ginni, and \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have never sought to influence Justice Thomas on any legal or political issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas faces impeachment calls after reports of undisclosed gifts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Kansas on Friday voted to ban gender-affirming medical care for transgender youth, but the bill is likely to be vetoed by Democratic governor \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Kansas house {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kslegislature.org/li/b2023_24/measures/vote_view/je_20230407023107_767743/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted 70-52}}}\uc2  to pass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kslegislature.org/li/b2023_24/measures/documents/ccrb_sb26_02_040623.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bill}}}\uc2  requiring the state\u8217\'20\'19s medical board to revoke the licenses of doctors who provide such care, followed by a 23-12 vote in the senate that sent the measure to Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s desk, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Kansas governor \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2 . Photograph: John Hanna/AP\par \par \uc2 Kelly promised LGBTQ+ youth during a statehouse lobbying day last month that she would protect their rights and reject any measure \u8220\'20\'1Cthat aims to harm or discriminate against you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the bill do not have a two-thirds majority in either chambers needed to override any veto, the AP said.\par \par \uc2 There seems to be enough support, however, for overriding Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s expected veto of a transgender bathroom bill that passed the legislature by larger margins.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/kansas-republicans-majority-governor-veto-trans-bathroom-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas Republicans set to override governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto of trans bathroom bill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House moves to strengthen transgender protections\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  has released a proposal that would forbid schools and colleges across the US from enacting outright bans on transgender athletes competing in sports.\par \par \uc2 But teams could create some limits in certain cases \u8211\'20\'13 for example, to ensure fairness, according to the proposal, which did not go into extensive detail about the term.\par \par \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s education secretary. Photograph: Mike Theiler/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 If finalized, the proposal would become enshrined as a provision of Title IX, the federal nondiscrimination requirement in education at institutions that receive federal funding. It must undergo a lengthy approval process, however, and is almost certain to face challenges from opponents.\par \par \uc2 It comes as a slew of Republican-controlled states nationwide enact legislation banning or restricting transgender athletes taking part in sports in educational settings, and new anti-trans laws in general.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  refused to let {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  enforce a state law banning trans athletes from female sports teams at public schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery student should be able to have the full experience of attending school in America, including participating in athletics, free from discrimination,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s education secretary, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/supreme-court-west-virginia-bid-trans-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden proposal forbids US schools from outright bans on transgender athletes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a selection of Twitter reactions to the expulsion by Tennessee Republicans of two Black Democratic lawmakers for joining a protest for stronger gun laws.\par \par \uc2 The overriding theme seems to be that it\u8217\'20\'19s a fight for democracy that\u8217\'20\'19s just beginning, and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s young people will be leading the charge.\par \par \uc2 From Democratic New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublicans may think they won today in Tennessee, but their fascism is only further radicalizing and awakening an earthquake of young people, both in the South and across the nation.\par \par \uc2 If you thought youth organizing was strong, just wait for what\u8217\'20\'19s coming. Gen Z don\u8217\'20\'19t play {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gPwoFI7uib"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gPwoFI7uib}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1644116250497253376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 From NBC News and MSNBC legal analyst Glenn Kirschner :\par \par \uc2 enltrThe naked racism of those Republican legislators in Tennessee should serve as a stark reminder that American apartheid endures. This is OUR struggle. All of us. There is no justice if there\u8217\'20\'19s not equal justice. And yes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/JusticeMatters?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #JusticeMatters}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rsyEgv5ZdB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rsyEgv5ZdB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Glenn Kirschner (@glennkirschner2) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/glennkirschner2/status/1644319280425492481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 From Mallory McMorrow, Democratic Michigan state senator and gun reform advocate:\par \par \uc2 enltrTennessee Republicans thought they could silence three House Reps just because they spoke out of turn to recognize Tennesseans demanding action on gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Today, they expelled two young Black men from office.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 and they handed them a national stage.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s. Go. ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ulqVxaE4Br"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ulqVxaE4Br}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mallory McMorrow (@MalloryMcMorrow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MalloryMcMorrow/status/1644155897063645186?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 From Joe Walsh, former Republican congressman, now a political analyst:\par \par \uc2 enltrTennessee Republicans just fucked up. Big time. And like every other cruel, intolerant, bigoted, authoritarian, & anti-democratic Republican fuck up of the past 7 yrs, this fuck up will hurt them politically. It will continue the shrinking of & ultimate demise of my former party.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Walsh (@WalshFreedom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WalshFreedom/status/1644147745735815168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrTennessee:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou ban books, you ban drag\u8212\'20\'14 kids are still in body bags.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SmRJDjATU3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SmRJDjATU3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1644142055390674947?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And finally, for now, the Tennessee house Republicans, who insist they were \u8220\'20\'1Cobliged\u8221\'20\'1D to take action because the two expelled Democrats were \u8220\'20\'1Cdisrespectful\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rO5QNTRMYN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rO5QNTRMYN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TN House Republicans (@tnhousegop) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tnhousegop/status/1644175765859180544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Tennessee are planning to reveal their next moves later on Friday in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D expulsion}}}\uc2  by Republicans from the state house of two Black lawmakers for taking part in a protest for tighter gun laws.\par \par \uc2 It comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and others weigh in on the \u8220\'20\'1Cundemocratic\u8221\'20\'1D actions of the Republicans in booting two of three Democrats who joined the protest that followed last week\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covenant school shooting}}}\uc2  in Nashville that killed six, including three nine-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 The two politicians ousted for a \u8220\'20\'1Cbreach of decorum\u8221\'20\'1D, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson, are Black. A third Democrat, Gloria Johnson, who survived the expulsion vote, is white.\par \par \uc2 The president, in a statement released last night, condemned Republicans for playing politics, and not focusing on \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense gun safety reforms\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s expulsion of lawmakers who engaged in peaceful protest is shocking, undemocratic and without precedent. Rather than debating the merits of the issue, these Republican lawmakers have chosen to punish, silence and expel duly-elected representatives of the people of Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 This morning, Martin Luther King III, son of the famed civil rights leader, praised the two expelled politicians and launched an attack on the \u8220\'20\'1Cunconscionable\u8221\'20\'1D actions by the majority party for ignoring gun reform. On CNN he said:\par \par \uc2 Martin Luther King III. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Our nation refuses to deal with this issue. I\u8217\'20\'19m so excited that these young men are fighting for democracy.\par \par \uc2 We had an assault ban until 2014, it\u8217\'20\'19s very sad. [But] people can stand up and things can change, my father and mother taught us that.\par \par \uc2 The episode, he said, made it \u8220\'20\'1Ccrystal clear\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cracism is still very real\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to eradicate this evil. My dad used to say darkness cannot put out darkness, only light can do that.\par \par \uc2 It just goes to show how sad and tragic and divisive, and how awful racism is. We are better than that. We have got to change this behavior.\par \par \uc2 Jones, in comments on Thursday, said the nation was watching. \u8220\'20\'1CThey think this issue is over. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see you on Monday,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, referring to more protests likely to draw thousands to Nashville.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to learn what moves the Democrats might make. There will almost certainly be special elections, in which Jones and Pearson, who represent about 130,000 constituents between them, will be eligible to run. And they could be reinstated meanwhile by their county commissions.\par \par \uc2 Read the latest on this story here from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Nina Lakhani :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/tennessee-republicans-racism-democrats-expelled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee Republicans accused of \u8216\'20\'18overt racism\u8217\'20\'19 after Democratic duo\u8217\'20\'19s expulsion}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 A Good Friday good morning to our US politics blog readers! There\u8217\'20\'19s more than a whiff of racism hanging over the Tennessee state house this morning, where Republican lawmakers on Thursday expelled two of three Democrats who took part in a rowdy gun control protest on the chamber floor.\par \par \uc2 Those ousted are Black, while the third, who survived the expulsion vote, is white. Their perceived crime was \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking decorum\u8221\'20\'1D for joining constituents demanding tighter gun laws in the wake of last week\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covenant school shooting}}}\uc2  in Nashville that killed six, including three nine-year-olds.\par \par \uc2 Reaction to the expulsions has been swift as observers mull elements of racism, gun rights and an attack on democracy. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called it \u8220\'20\'1Cundemocratic\u8221\'20\'1D, while Martin Luther King III said on CNN Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CRacism is still very real \u8230\'20\'26 we have got to eradicate this evil.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more coming up. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is facing calls for his impeachment after it was revealed he accepted undeclared luxury gifts from a Republican mega-donor for more than two decades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stormy Daniels, the adult movie actress paid off by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to keep quiet about an encounter before the 2016 election, says in a new interview the former president has been \u8220\'20\'1Cdethroned\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump appeared in court this week charged with falsifying business records relate to the pay-off.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats in North Carolina are fuming over the defection of a lawmaker, giving Republicans a veto-proof supermajority in the state house for critical issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voting rights and gun controls.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden received good economic news on Friday with figures showing unemployment in the US down to 3.5%, and 236,000 jobs added in March.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate and House lawmakers are on their Easter break, and neither Biden nor vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have any public events scheduled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230407ej47001h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
