\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  funds cautiously resume services following legal reprieve\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,056 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 April 2023\par 14:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Groups had stopped work funding out-of-state travel for abortions due to threats from Republican attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/scotus-roe-wade-decision-what-happens-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last June, Kamyon Conner sat at her desk and sobbed.\par \par \uc2 As executive director of the Texas Equal Access Fund \u8211\'20\'13 a non-profit based in north Texas that helps patients pay for their abortions \u8211\'20\'13 Conner was forced to shut off the group\u8217\'20\'19s hotline for the first time in its nearly 20-year history. That meant cutting off a critical avenue for hundreds of largely low-income people of color to afford essential out-of-state care.\par \par \uc2 With Roe overturned, Texans \u8211\'20\'13 already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/03/texas-abortion-ban-six-months-grave-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 living under a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 still had two months until a full {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/us-abortion-trigger-bans-laws-tennessee-texas-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D ban}}}\uc2  would be enacted. However, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/executive-management/Post-Roe%20Advisory%20(updated%20draft%2006.21.2022)%20(1).pdf?utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_name=&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a notice}}}\uc2  that day, encouraging local district attorneys to immediately pursue criminal charges against anyone who helps people obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . All 10 Texas funds quickly ceased \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support services out of fear of jail time for themselves, their clients and their supporters.\par \par \uc2 Now, after nearly nine months of pause, organizations like the Texas Equal Access Fund are finally resuming services \u8211\'20\'13 with caution.\par \par \uc2 This comes after US district court judge \uc2 Robert Pitman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/02/24/texas-abortion-funds-ruling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted a preliminary injunction}}}\uc2  in February that prevents a handful of district attorneys from prosecuting organizations that help Texans with out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, in response to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.classaction.org/media/fund-texas-choice-et-al-v-paxton-et-al.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 class-action lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed by eight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds. The funds hope Pitman issues permanent protection in the coming months and also expands his ruling to cover all of the district attorneys in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Largely grassroots non-profits, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds assist low-income residents with financing either \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures directly or practical support services like travel to clinics, hotel stays, gas, air fare and childcare. For nearly 30 years, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds have played an instrumental role all over the country in connecting the most vulnerable people with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, a role that is only escalating in importance as more states move to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the post-Roe world. Donations to funds around the country soared after the Dobbs decision that toppled Roe: in the five months after the ruling, the National Network of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds (NNAF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6242277/abortion-funds-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  raised more than $8m}}}\uc2 , compared with less than $2m in individual donations in all of 2020.\par \par \uc2 Texas \u8211\'20\'13 the largest state in the US to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care \u8211\'20\'13 is home to more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds than any other state, comprising more than 10% of funds nationally, says Oriaku Njoku, executive director of the NNAF. Texans must travel at least 515 miles to the nearest out-of-state clinic for care, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/texas/abortion-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The number of residents who were not able to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through Texas funds during the prolonged pause in operations is probably in the thousands. Even before shutting down the helpline, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds like Texas Equal Access often could not meet the high demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  aid in Texas: it was able to fund, for example, less than one-third of the 5,000 people who requested help in 2021. Of the roughly 4,000 calls the Lilith Fund, an Austin-based group, received in 2020, it was only able to fund about 1,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was heartbreaking knowing we couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help our callers \u8211\'20\'13 these are some of the most marginalized people in the state that have the most pressing need for support,\u8221\'20\'1D says Conner, who has worked at the Texas Equal Access Fund since 2006. \u8220\'20\'1CSome have undoubtedly been forced to give birth against their will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fund Texas Choice, which offers travel assistance, resumed \u8220\'20\'1Climited\u8221\'20\'1D services in early March, while the Texas Equal Access Fund started back up last week. The Lilith Fund announced it would finally restart its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are overjoyed to be able to fund abortions for Texans again,\u8221\'20\'1D says Neesha Dav\u233\'00\'E9, interim executive director of the Lilith Fund. \u8220\'20\'1CEven though no one should have to leave home for healthcare, it means everything to us to support Texans who have been forced to travel to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s threats against the funds are part of a broader campaign by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in the state.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/press-releases/aclu-sues-seven-texas-cities-over-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deemed \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal\u8221\'20\'1D organizations}}}\uc2  in local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  ordinances proliferating in Texas. Last year, the funds received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/03/29/abortion-funds-defamation-briscoe-cain/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cease-and-desist letters}}}\uc2  from an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmaker and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2022/05/roe-v-wade-abortion-funds.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced}}}\uc2  the threat of legal action from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates that alleged the organizations \u8220\'20\'1Caided and abetted\u8221\'20\'1D prohibited abortions.\par \par \uc2 Not all funds have resumed services, including the Frontera Fund, which assists those living on the US-Mexico border \u8211\'20\'13 mainly Latino and undocumented people who experience the longest travel times to clinics and already face logistical barriers due to immigration status. The same goes for Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Due Process, which helps teenagers obtain a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without parental consent.\par \par \uc2 Both funds have yet to resume services, attributing their caution to the particular vulnerability of their clients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been struggling with so much fear, anxiety and frustration for our staff and for our clients,\u8221\'20\'1D says Nan Kirkpatrick of Jane\u8217\'20\'19s Due Process.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated legislature currently in session could make the funds\u8217\'20\'19 recent court victory short-lived.\par \par \uc2 Among many pieces of legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=HB2690"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one bill}}}\uc2  seeks to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds by making it a felony for any Texan to pay for any portion of the cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 even if the procedure occurs in a state in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal \u8211\'20\'13 and forces internet service providers to block websites affiliated with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund. It also grants the attorney general the power to prosecute violations of the law if a local prosecutor declines to pursue charges. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=SB20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another bill}}}\uc2  would remove district attorneys who decline to prosecute violations of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, a direct rebuke to the swell of progressive DAs who have said they will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/29/1108513274/a-district-attorney-in-texas-says-he-wont-prosecute-abortion-crimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not prosecute}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related crimes. The legislative session ends on 29 May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been threatened time and time again by extremists,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dav\u233\'00\'E9. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s exhausting and frustrating, but we will continue to be resilient and fight back against unfair laws to ensure we are still here to help people access the care they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230406ej46000xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
