\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will comply with subpoena to testify before January 6 grand jury \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington and Martin Belam \par \uc2 8,222 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2023\par 20:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former vice-president will not fight a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order compelling him to appear before a special grand jury\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 End of day summary\par \par \uc2 It was a lively day in Washington with developments on several fronts this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , will not fight a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order compelling him to appear before a special grand jury hearing testimony in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 King Charles invited Biden to the United Kingdom for an official state visit and the US president accepted, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters. She offered no timeline for when the visit would take place.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  on Wednesday signed the repeal of a dormant 1931 law that the banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and criminalized providers who performed them.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Kevin McCarthy met Taiwanese president \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2  -wen in California today, becoming the most senior US figure to meet a Taiwanese leader on US soil since 1979, despite threats of retaliation from China, which claims self-ruled Taiwan as its own.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Mexican president, \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  , has weighed in to say he does not agree with the criminal charges brought against former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the US, calling the case political, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reflecting on his day in court, Trump said he sees a silver lining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs much as I can enjoy a day like Tuesday,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president wrote, denouncing liberals as \u8220\'20\'1CRadical Left Lunatics\u8221\'20\'1D and insisting there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno crime\u8221\'20\'1D committed, \u8220\'20\'1Cit was an unbelievable experience, perhaps the Best Day in History for somebody who had just suffered Unjustifiable Indictment!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a burst of posts on his social media platform, Truth Social, Trump shared polling, promoted by conservative outlets, that showed him stretching his lead over the nominal Republican presidential field.\par \par \uc2 While Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment have appeared to rally Republican voters to his side, polling also shows that a majority of Americans agree with indictment, suggesting his legal woes could hinder him with the broader electorate.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CMy Poll Numbers have never been better, almost $10 Million was raised for the Campaign and, the day was capped off with a very important Speech. If we don\u8217\'20\'19t stop the Radical Left, America is DEAD!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/trump-vents-grievances-against-criminal-charges-from-the-safety-of-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump attacks hush money case in grievance-filled Mar-a-Lago speech }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nevada senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  , a Democrat, will seek re-election, an expected but nevertheless welcome announcement for the party facing a tough electoral map in 2024.\par \par \uc2 enltrI ran for office to solve problems, fight for hardworking Nevada families, and make a real difference in people\u8217\'20\'19s lives.\par \par \uc2 Our work in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  is just getting started \u8212\'20\'14 that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m officially launching my re-election campaign today! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rKv62KfqqQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rKv62KfqqQ }}}\uc2  is just getting started \u8212\'20\'14 that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m officially launching my re-election campaign today!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  (@RosenforNevada) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RosenforNevada/status/1643577904154943490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@RosenforNevada)\par \par \uc2 The Silver State has proved to be one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most competitive battlegrounds. In 2022, Democratic incumbent \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  narrowly eked out a victory against her Republican opponent, while the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor lost re-election to the Trump-backed Joe Lombardo.\par \par \uc2 Next year Senate Democrats are defending seats in a handful of states Trump won as well as a number of swing states. This comes after they expanded their narrow majority to 51 in 2022 by flipping a seat Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s launch video emphasizes her biography, her support for the infrastructure law and legislation reducing the cost of prescription drug prices, and her focus on issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and climate change.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican-led legislatures around the country are considering \u8211\'20\'13 and passing \u8211\'20\'13 new laws to control the lives of trans youth \u8211\'20\'13 from the care they can seek, to the sports\u8217\'20\'19 team they can play on and the school bathrooms they can use.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whas11.com/article/news/local/indiana/indiana-governor-ban-gender-affirming-care-transgender-trans/417-320af05c-22bf-43f2-a60b-7908b8f79999"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law }}}\uc2  a measure banning all gender-affirming care for minors, after telling reporters the bill sent to his desk was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/indiana-trans-heath-care-ban-d4690b52eebc1067dc1a64f43f99ce11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cclear as mud\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 . With his signature, Indiana joins at least 12 other states that have enacted similar bans or restrictions on such care.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of such legislation say the care, which includes hormone therapy and puberty blockers endorsed by top medical associations, are safe, largely reversible and can be life-saving for trans youth.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Kansas, meanwhile, overrode the Democratic governor, Laura Kelly \u8217\'20\'19s veto of a bill banning transgender athletes from participating in girl\u8217\'20\'19s and women\u8217\'20\'19s sports from kindergarten through college, per the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 It follows a measure approved by Kansas lawmakers on Tuesday that critics say is among the most restrictive in the nation. The bill, which Kelly is expected to veto, would prevent trans people from using public restrooms, locker rooms and other facilities that do not align with the gender on their birth certificate. It would also prevent them from changing their name or gender on their driver\u8217\'20\'19s license.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence won\u8217\'20\'19t fight order compelling grand jury testimony\par \par \uc2 Former Vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , will not fight a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order compelling him to appear before a special grand jury hearing testimony in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-president Pence will not appeal the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and will comply with the subpoena as required by law,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesman for Pence said.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Former VP \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will not appeal order compelling to testify in criminal investigation into Jan. 6 Capitol attack, per spokesman: \u8220\'20\'1CVice President Pence will not appeal the Judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and will comply with the subpoena as required by law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1643687430288023557?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark and historic ruling affirmed for the first time in history that the speech or debate clause extends to the vice-president,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CHaving vindicated that principle of the constitution, VP Pence will not appeal the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and will comply with the subpoena.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president and the first lady are \u8220\'20\'1Cvery much looking forward\u8221\'20\'1D to welcoming LSU Tigers basketball team to the White House after they defeated the Iowa Hawkeyes to win their first \uc2 NCAA\uc2  championship, Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 But it appears unclear whether the team, or its star player, Angel Reese, is planning to attend after a verbal flap by the first lady, who attended the championship game, suggested both teams be invited to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Traditionally, only the champions are invited. Reese called the remark a \u8220\'20\'1CJOKE\u8221\'20\'1D on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  . The White House attempted to walk back the comment, saying Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Cintended to applaud the historic game and all women athletes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe looks forward to celebrating the LSU Tigers on their championship win at the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_r_Z8-FgO5A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 podcast }}}\uc2  interview, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/05/sport/angel-reese-white-house-jill-biden-intl-spt/index.html?utm_content=2023-04-05T17%3A45%3A04&utm_medium=social&utm_term=link&utm_source=twCNN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN,  }}}\uc2  Reese told the hosts that she did not accept Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Capology\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t go back on certain things that you say \u8230\'20\'26 They can have that spotlight. We\u8217\'20\'19ll go to the Obamas.\u8217\'20\'19 We\u8217\'20\'19ll go see Michelle. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see Barack,\u8221\'20\'1D the star said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden accepted King Charles' invitation for an official state visit\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said King Charles invited Biden to the United Kingdom for an official state visit and he accepted. The king extended the invitation during a recent call with the president, which Jean Pierre described as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery friendly\u8221\'20\'1D. She offered no timeline for when the visit would take place.\par \par \uc2 Biden is not planning to attend King Charles\u8217\'20\'19 coronation next month in keeping with past precedent. The US delegation will be lead instead by the first lady, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 Pressed repeatedly on why Biden wasn\u8217\'20\'19t attending, Jean-Pierre insisted that the British people should not see the decision as a \u8220\'20\'1Csnub.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will leave it at that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not a snub.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On whether he would meet with the king during his visit to the UK and Ireland next week, Jean-Pierre said to stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press briefing begins\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is at the podium this afternoon answering reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions on a range of subjects. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick rat-a-tat.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 She declined to offer a timeline of when the White House would release a comprehensive strategy for combatting antisemitism, as Biden announced in a CNN op-ed this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 She would not comment on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment, citing the White House\u8217\'20\'19s position that it does not comment on ongoing legal cases. However, she did in general terms say that the White House and the president condemns \u8220\'20\'1Cany type of attacks on any judge or our judicial system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden was briefed by senior advisers about the charges against Trump, Jean-Pierre said, insisting his focus was not on the former president. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not focused on this indictment,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with the Taiwanese president, Jean Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no reason for Beijing to turn this transit into something that is used as a pretext to overreact \u8230\'20\'26 We just do not see, there should not be a reason, for the PCR to overreact here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 She would not say whether Biden planned to take family members with him on what he views as a return to his ancestral home. She said he would use his family\u8217\'20\'19s history and Irish roots to tell a broader story about Irish immigrants influence on the nation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor repeals state's 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  on Wednesday signed the repeal of a 1931 law that the banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and criminalized providers who performed them.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, we are repealing Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s extreme 1931 law that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and criminalized nurses and doctors for doing their jobs.\par \par \uc2 This is long overdue. ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PCOqJhTtb4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PCOqJhTtb4 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  (@GovWhitmer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovWhitmer/status/1643650449017282561?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@GovWhitmer)\par \par \uc2 A backlash to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s to overturn the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped power Whitmer and a slate of Democratic candidates to victory in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Voters overwhelmingly approved a citizen-led initiative to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, which rendered the 1931 law unconstitutional. However, if at some point in the future, voters were to gather enough signatures to amend the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right, the 1931 ban would then have been enforceable.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer\u8217\'20\'19s signature eliminated that possibility entirely, erasing the nearly-century old law completely.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Testifying before a federal grand jury, former top Trump administration officials \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli said they repeatedly informed the then-president that he could not seize voting machines as part of his efforts to cling to power in the wake of his defeat in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/05/politics/election-voting-machines-trump-national-security/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to new reporting by CNN. }}}\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli said they repeatedly informed the then-president that he could not seize voting machines as part of his efforts to cling to power in the wake of his defeat in 2020,\par \par \uc2 Citing three people familiar with the proceedings, CNN reported that Wolf and Cuccinelli were to describe discussions within the administration related to seizing voting machines when they appeared before the grand jury earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 One of the sources told CNN that Cuccinelli testified to the grand jury that he \u8220\'20\'1Cmade clear at all times\u8221\'20\'1D that the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  did not have the authority to seize voting machines.\par \par \uc2 That line of questioning goes to the heart of [special counsel Jack] Smith\u8217\'20\'19s challenge in any criminal case he might bring \u8212\'20\'14 to prove that Trump and his allies pursued their efforts despite knowing their fraud claims were false or their gambits weren\u8217\'20\'19t lawful. To bring any potential criminal charges, prosecutors would have to overcome Trump\u8217\'20\'19s public claim that he believed then and now that fraud really did cost him the election, per CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker meets president of Taiwan in historic US visit\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Kevin McCarthy met Taiwanese president \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2  -wen in California today, becoming the most senior US figure to meet a Taiwanese leader on US soil since 1979, despite threats of retaliation from China, which claims self-ruled Taiwan as its own, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe friendship between America and the people of Taiwan has never been stronger. It is my honor to welcome President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iingwen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @iingwen }}}\uc2  to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Reagan_Library?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Reagan_Library }}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2XSIJRv7Vp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2XSIJRv7Vp }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1643661729912725507?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 McCarthy, a Republican who through his House position is number three in the US leadership hierarchy, welcomed Tsai on Wednesday morning at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library in Simi Valley, California, near Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 China staged war games around Taiwan last August following the visit to Taipei of then-House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and \uc2 Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s defense ministry\uc2  said a Chinese aircraft carrier group was in the waters off the island\u8217\'20\'19s southeast coast ahead of the meeting between Tsai and McCarthy in California.\par \par \uc2 US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said there was nothing new about a Taiwanese president transiting through the United States and Beijing should not use it as an excuse to take any action or ratchet up tensions.\par \par \uc2 Supporters waving Taiwan flags and pro-Taiwan and Hong Kong banners chanted \u8220\'20\'1CJiayou Taiwan\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the equivalent of \u8220\'20\'1CGo Taiwan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Washington switched diplomatic recognition from Taipei to Beijing in 1979.\par \par \uc2 A meeting in California is seen as a potentially less provocative alternative to McCarthy visiting Taiwan, something he has said he hopes to do.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Kevin McCarthy, R-Calif., second from right, welcomes Taiwanese President \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2  -wen as she arrives at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library in Simi Valley, California today. Photograph: Ringo HW Chiu/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even the Mexican president, \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  , has now weighed in to say he does not agree with the criminal charges brought against former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the US, calling the case political, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Supposedly legal issues should not be used for electoral, political purposes. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with what they are doing to ex-president Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/andres-manuel-lopez-obrador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lopez Obrador }}}\uc2  said at a news conference this morning.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a heck of a lot more than current US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said on the matter, as he and White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  continue to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/white-house-press-secretary-and-new-york-times-reporter-get-in-shouting-match-over-trump-case-karine-i-dont-need-a-lecture/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuff requests }}}\uc2  for comment by political journalists on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal crisis.\par \par \uc2 Trump is the first sitting or former US president to face criminal charges, as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-charges-34-felony-counts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty }}}\uc2  to 34 felony counts related to business fraud, allegedly to cover up election finance fraud, in New York on Tuesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Leftist populist \u8220\'20\'1C Amlo \u8221\'20\'1D compared Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case to the December {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/07/peru-president-detained-pedro-castillo-coup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ousting }}}\uc2  of former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/peru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peruvian }}}\uc2  president Pedro Castillo, who was removed from office and arrested after trying to dissolve congress.\par \par \uc2 It should be the people who decide,\u8221\'20\'1D said L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador , who added that he could not say whether Trump was guilty or not.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Midday summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand today\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues to lash out at his opponents \u8211\'20\'13 real and perceived \u8211\'20\'13 the morning after his historic arraignment. In a pair of social media posts, he attacked the investigations against him, accused Democrats of \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponizing\u8221\'20\'1D federal law enforcement agencies and called on Congressional Republicans to \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund\u8221\'20\'1D the DOJ and \uc2 FBI\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Janet Protasiewicz won her race for the Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court, beating out a conservative candidate who had advised Republicans on legal efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the state through the use of \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D. Her win will flip the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, in an election which democracy observers have called the most consequential one of the year, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, redistricting and election rules at stake.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Progressive Cook county board commissioner Brandon Johnson won the election for Chicago mayor on Tuesday evening after pulling ahead of his opponent \uc2 Paul Vallas\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department on Wednesday announced that it had reached a tentative $144.5m settlement with victims and relatives of those killed in the 2017 mass shooting at a church in Sutherland Springs, Texas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Still to come: House speaker Kevin McCarthy and a bipartisan contingent of lawmakers will sit down with Taiwanese President \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2  -wen today in California, a carefully choreographed encounter that comes amid rising tensions between the US and China.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 DoJ reaches tentative settlement over Sutherland Springs shooting\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department on Wednesday announced that it had reached a tentative $144.5m settlement with victims and relatives of those killed in the 2017 mass shooting at a church in Sutherland Springs, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of worshipers were killed or injured when gunman Devin Kelley opened fire during a Sunday service at First Baptist church of Sutherland Springs. The gunman, who died of an apparent self-inflicted gunshot wound, had served in the Air Force. Twenty-six people, including a pregnant woman, were killed and 22 others were injured.\par \par \uc2 After the shooting, dozens of victims and their relatives sued the \uc2 US air force\uc2  , alleging that it failed to report the gunman\u8217\'20\'19s history of violence, including an assault conviction, to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s national background check system. That conviction, they argued, should have prevented the former airman from being able to purchase the guns he used in the assault.\par \par \uc2 A judge had previously ruled that the air force was \u8220\'20\'1C60% liable\u8221\'20\'1D for the attack as a result of its failure to report the conviction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo words or amount of money can diminish the immense tragedy of the mass shooting in Sutherland Springs,\u8221\'20\'1D said associate attorney general Vanita Gupta in the press release. \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement brings the litigation to a close, ending a painful chapter for the victims of this unthinkable crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The DoJ said the settlement was still subject to court approvals.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whitehouse.us19.list-manage.com/track/click?u=c97630621baff8c44fe607661&id=41cba03a2a&e=bc3ff43753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed published by CNN }}}\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked the start of Passover by imploring Americans and democratic citizens around the world to speak out against rising antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 He said the White House would soon release the \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst-ever national strategy to counter antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D, which he said would outline actions the federal government will take based on outreach to more than a thousand \u8220\'20\'1CJewish community stakeholders, faith and civil rights leaders, state and local officials and more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his time in office, the president noted, the White House hosted the first High Holiday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whitehouse.us19.list-manage.com/track/click?u=c97630621baff8c44fe607661&id=a5e2685819&e=bc3ff43753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reception }}}\uc2  and lit the first permanent White House Hanukah {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whitehouse.us19.list-manage.com/track/click?u=c97630621baff8c44fe607661&id=b7a2437901&e=bc3ff43753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 menorah  }}}\uc2  in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit more of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s passover message:\par \par \uc2 To the Jewish community, I want you to know that I see your fear, your hurt and your concern that this venom is being normalized. I decided to run for President after I saw it in Charlottesville, when neo-Nazis marched from the shadows spewing the same antisemitic bile that was heard in Germany in the 1930s,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRest assured that I am committed to the safety of the Jewish people. I stand with you. America stands with you. Under my presidency, we continue to condemn antisemitism at every turn. Failure to call out hate is complicity. Silence is complicity. And we will not be silent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats had plenty to smile about by the end of the day on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After years of demanding accountability for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , they were treated to a series of somber-looking images of the former president sitting in a prosaic Manhattan courtroom, reduced, in their eyes, to a common criminal defendant.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, their preferred candidate prevailed in a consequential Supreme Court race in Wisconsin and in the Chicago mayoral race, voters chose the liberal candidate over his opponent, who once described himself as a Republican.\par \par \uc2 But in North Carolina, their fortunes were reversed.\par \par \uc2 There a Democratic state lawmaker formally switched her political affiliation to the Republican Party on Wednesday, giving the GOP veto-proof control in both chambers of the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 It is a devastating development for Democrats in the state, and especially the Democratic governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  , who had vowed to use his veto power to block hardline conservatives from advancing their policies during the final two years of his administration.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the switch means, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-party-switch-republican-01af019aa58fd44f0e2110c32a48c4c0?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the AP: }}}\par \par \uc2 The party switch announced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-legislature-vetoes-roy-cooper-republicans-0857f32f3fc714fdb3b9e4af0958c492"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state Representative Tricia Cotham, of Mecklenburg County, }}}\uc2  means Republicans now hold the 72 seats required in the 120-seat House to hold a veto-proof majority. Republicans had already held 30 of the 50 seats in the Senate needed to override vetoes if party members are present and voting, but until Wednesday, they were one seat shy of a similar advantage in the House following the November elections.\par \par \uc2 Recently improving margins for Republicans in the General Assembly, capped off by Cotham\u8217\'20\'19s switch, have emboldened the North Carolina party to try again on topics such as gun rights, immigration and voting. Republicans also are interested in further restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following last year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-supreme-court-decision-854f60302f21c2c35129e58cf8d8a7b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade. }}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not be controlled by anyone,\u8221\'20\'1D Cotham said as she announced she would switch her party registration to the GOP. She said the Democratic Party is no longer a big tent party and tries to bully its members. She said that she was considered a \u8220\'20\'1Cspy\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitor\u8221\'20\'1D and that the turning point was when she was criticized for using the American flag and praying-hands emoji on social media and on her vehicles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Adam Gabbatt spent the day covering the frenzy outside the Manhattan courthouse where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was booked and arraigned on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In this video, he speaks to Maga-wearing Trump supporters and sign-wielding Trump antagonists about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s day in court and what it means for the country.\par \par \uc2 Give it a watch here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rosa Parks. Jane Fonda. David Bowie. In the end, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , the first president \u8211\'20\'13current or former \u8211\'20\'13 to ever face criminal charges, will not join ranks of famous people with iconic mug shots. No police snap was taken of the former president during his booking on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 None was needed, it was reported, as mug shots are intended to help authorities quickly identify defendants should they attempt to flee. Trump was not deemed a flight risk and, more to the point, is unlikely to escape notice as one of the most recognizable people on planet Earth.\par \par \uc2 But that didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop the Trump campaign from trying to cash in on the moment.\par \par \uc2 An email sent to Trump supporters showed merchandise in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s official store: a plain white T-shirt featuring a clearly doctored photo of the former president getting booked. A fake chart behind him gave his height as 6ft 5in. Underneath his photo were the words \u8220\'20\'1CNOT GUILTY\u8221\'20\'1D, printed in big block letters, Alaina Demopoulos writes.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s official store \u8211\'20\'13 which also sells hoodies emblazoned with photographs of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  falling down the stairs and \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was right about everything\u8221\'20\'1D bumper stickers \u8211\'20\'13 will send fans the mugshot T-shirt \u8220\'20\'1Cfor free\u8221\'20\'1D, if they donate $47 to his re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 It was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first attempt at monetizing his historic arrest, after \uc2 Rolling Stone{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/trump-mugshot-campaign-1234708971/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  that his campaign planned to use the mugshot \u8220\'20\'1Cin a large marketing blitz\u8221\'20\'1D. In the end, the campaign was denied the opportunity: the Manhattan criminal court didn\u8217\'20\'19t photograph Trump at his arraignment, so organizers went with a mock photo.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-merchandise-mugshot-arrest-stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump campaign tries to cash in on arrest with fake mugshot T-shirt }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 This morning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  issued an all-caps missive, imploring Republicans in Congress to \u8220\'20\'1CDEFUND THE DOJ AND FBI UNTIL THEY COME TO THEIR SENSES.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time Trump and his loyalists have backed such calls, but they make Republican leaders nervous in a year when public safety and crime are front of mind for voters. Republicans worry that these calls will undermine their attempts to cast Democrats who favor policing and criminal justice reform as supportive of the \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund the police\u8221\'20\'1D movement, even though most in the party \u8211\'20\'13 from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on down \u8211\'20\'13 do not.\par \par \uc2 But Trump, facing an array of legal threats, has ramped up his attacks against the \uc2 FBI\uc2  after agents recovered classified documents that Trump hoarded at his Mar-a-Lago property. The DOJ is investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents, as well as his efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election, which culminated in January 6 assault on the US capitol.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s social media posts are a sign, perhaps, that even as the former president faces prosecutors in New York for his alleged role in a hush-money scheme to cover up damaging claims of extramarital affairs at the height of the 2016 presidential election, he is also worried about his legal exposure on other fronts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chicago voters elect progressive as next mayor\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, voters in Chicago elected Brandon Johnson, the progressive Cook county board commissioner, as the city\u8217\'20\'19s next mayor. He beat \uc2 Paul Vallas\uc2  , a more conservative Democrat who made crime a central issue of his campaign. Here\u8217\'20\'19s how our reporter, Leigh Giangreco, characterized the race to succeed mayor \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  , after voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/01/lori-lightfoot-chicago-mayor-election-runoff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  denied her a second term }}}\uc2  in a stunning upset last month.\par \par \uc2 The election had pit two Democrats from the furthest ends of their party\u8217\'20\'19s spectrum against each other. Public safety has been the number one issue and Democrats across the country were watching to see if Johnson, a progressive who has previously supported the defund the police movement, could defeat Vallas, who nabbed the endorsement of Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s police union and once described himself as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nprillinois.org/statehouse/2013-11-08/paul-vallas-a-democrat-who-was-a-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican }}}\uc2 . \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Johnson and Vallas had gone head-to-head after a crowded mayoral primary in February. In that race, incumbent mayor \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  won voters in Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s majority Black wards on the south and west side communities while Congressman Jes\u250\'00\'FAs \u8220\'20\'1CChuy\u8221\'20\'1D Garc\u237\'00\'EDa won Latino voters on the west side. Those votes were up for grabs on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/chicago-mayoral-election-polls-brandon-johnson-paul-vallas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Progressive candidate Brandon Johnson elected Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s new mayor }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liberal judge prevails in Wisconsin Supreme Court race\par \par \uc2 In an analysis of the Wisconsin senate, Sam Levine likens Protasiewicz\u8217\'20\'19s victory to a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical earthquake\u8221\'20\'1D in the state, \u8220\'20\'1Cone of America\u8217\'20\'19s most volatile political battlegrounds\u8221\'20\'1D that has played a central role in recent elections. Though the race was ostensibly nonpartisan, Protasiewicz was forthcoming about her liberal views and especially her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which proved decisive in the race. Her election will tilt the ideological balance of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s seven-member supreme court from conservative to liberal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Sam:\par \par \uc2 Her election to the court means that the Wisconsin 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will be struck down (a case is already coming through the courts). Just as they did across the country in 2022, Democrats made it a central issue in the supreme court campaign and voters turned out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWisconsin voters have made their voices heard. They\u8217\'20\'19ve chosen to reject partisan extremism,\u8221\'20\'1D Protasiewicz said during remarks at her election night party in Milwaukee. \u8220\'20\'1CIt means our democracy will always prevail.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 A challenge is expected shortly thereafter to Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s electoral maps, which are so heavily distorted in favor of Republicans that it is virtually impossible for Democrats to ever win a majority. Protasiewicz has said the maps are \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D and the court is likely to strike them down, making elections much more competitive in the state.\par \par \uc2 These two significant consequences show how Democrats may have finally been able to catch up to Republicans when it comes to focusing on so-called down-ballot races \u8211\'20\'13 little-known contests for offices like state legislatures and state supreme courts that can have huge policy consequences.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning. I\u8217\'20\'19m Lauren Gambino in Washington, taking over for Martin.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to break briefly from the fallout surrounding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s historic arraignment on Tuesday to discuss a few other developments that will have significant consequences for American politics.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin voters elected liberal judge Janet Protasiewicz to the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court in what had been described as the most important election of 2023.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a dispatch from our reporters on the ground in the Midwestern swing state: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman }}}\uc2  in Madison and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine }}}\uc2  in Milwaukee\par \par \uc2 In a historic election, the liberal judge Janet Protasiewicz is projected to win her race for a seat on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court. Her win will flip the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, which has been controlled by a conservative majority for 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Elections and democracy observers have called this election the most consequential one of the year, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, redistricting and election rules at stake. The race pitted Protasiewicz, a Milwaukee circuit court judge and former prosecutor, against Dan Kelly, a former Wisconsin supreme court justice with ties to election deniers and the far right.\par \par \uc2 Protasiewicz will replace the conservative justice Patience Roggensack on 1 August; the court will be controlled by a narrow liberal majority.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liberal judge wins Wisconsin supreme court election, flipping ideological balance }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 While some former allies of Trump, like \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , and some of those in the race for the 2024 Republican nomination against Trump, like \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , have been put in the position of defending the former president in recent days since his indictment, Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has kept his counsel. This morning Alexander Bolton writes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/3934484-mcconnell-lets-an-indicted-trump-twist-in-the-wind/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for The Hill }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 McConnell and his top deputies stayed silent Tuesday, signaling how far they have diverged from their former ally.\par \par \uc2 Many Republican senators blame Trump for the loss of the Senate majority and the disappointing performance of Senate Republican last year. His arraignment Tuesday only adds to the political baggage of the Republican presidential frontrunner.\par \par \uc2 McConnell, who hasn\u8217\'20\'19t spoken to Trump since December of 2020, didn\u8217\'20\'19t make any statement in response to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s arrest Tuesday. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t say anything when news of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s indictment broke Thursday, either.\par \par \uc2 Al Cross, a professor of journalism at the \uc2 University of Kentucky\uc2  and a longtime commentator on McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s career, said McConnell doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel the same pressure as other Republicans to rally around Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  does not feel pressure in the same way that other human beings do. He has steeled himself to resist the typical politician\u8217\'20\'19s urge to talk and it\u8217\'20\'19s paid off for him, you don\u8217\'20\'19t get in trouble for something you didn\u8217\'20\'19t say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cross speculated that McConnell doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to put himself out on a limb by defending Trump when the former president is facing additional possible indictments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be other shoes to drop and I expect \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  knows more about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s situation than we do,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our video team have summarised yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s historic day of media frenzy as news crews followed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s every step \u8211\'20\'13 from Trump Tower back to his Mar-a-Lago residence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 By the way, if you\u8217\'20\'19ve got the time and inclination for it, ABC have published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/read-full-transcript-trumps-arraignment/story?id=98360311"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a full transcript }}}\uc2  of what happened in the courthouse Tuesday in the Trump arraignment hearing, which lasted 57 minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan writes for the Guardian today that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/05/trump-isnt-the-ringmaster-he-once-was-but-were-still-watching-his-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t the ringmaster he once was, but we\u8217\'20\'19re still watching his show }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Will the criminal charges be good for Trump? Trump seems to think so, or at least that\u8217\'20\'19s what he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to project to the public. He raised a lot of money for his third presidential bid over the five days between his indictment and his arraignment: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/04/03/trump-campaign-raised-7-million-since-indictment.html#:~:text=Former%20President%20Donald%20Trump's%202024,his%20expected%20arrest%20and%20arraignment."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $7m }}}\uc2 , according to campaign officials. And as he was inside the courthouse being charged, his campaign sent out a fundraising email, asking supporters to purchase tee shirts featuring a fake mug shot of the former president, along with the words \u8220\'20\'1CNOT GUILTY.\u8221\'20\'1D They cost $47 a piece.\par \par \uc2 And the indictment has placed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s would-be rivals for the Republican nomination in an awkward position: they want to distance themselves from Trump, but they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to alienate his supporters, those die-hards who still make up a ruling majority of the Republican base. If anything, the indictment has made it seem more likely that Trump will secure the Republican nomination, for the same reasons it seemed likely back in 2016: while Republican elites and donors scramble to stop him, and rival candidates define themselves against his example, he\u8217\'20\'19s still the sun around which the Republican party orbits, a force exponentially more powerful than the party itself.\par \par \uc2 Should we even be paying attention to this? Have we learned nothing? But with Trump, even studied indifference to him still makes him the center of political attention, like when you tell someone not to think of a white elephant.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/05/trump-isnt-the-ringmaster-he-once-was-but-were-still-watching-his-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moira Donegan \u8211\'20\'13 Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t the ringmaster he once was, but we\u8217\'20\'19re still watching his show }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/05/trump-isnt-the-ringmaster-he-once-was-but-were-still-watching-his-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t the ringmaster he once was. But we\u8217\'20\'19re still watching his show | Moira Donegan }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 It would be fair to say that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have got plenty of potential court dates ahead of them in the coming months and years. Here is a list from CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dan Berman of all the investigations and court activity that the former president is facing:\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago documents \u8211\'20\'13 Special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  is overseeing the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s criminal investigations into the retention of national defence information at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s resort.\par \par \uc2 2020 election and January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s purview also includes the period after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election loss to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and leading up to the insurrection at the US Capitol. Aspects of the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s probe include the use of so-called fake electors from states that Trump falsely claimed he had won, such as Georgia and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 2020 election: Efforts to overturn Georgia results \u8211\'20\'13 Fulton County, Georgia, district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  oversaw a special grand jury investigating what Trump or his allies may have done in their efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 2020 election and January 6: House select committee \u8211\'20\'13 before concluding at the end of 2022, the House select committee referred Trump to the Justice Department on at least four criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 E. Jean Carroll : Defamation suit over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s denial of rape claims \u8211\'20\'13 Carroll alleged Trump raped her in a New York department store dressing room in the mid-1990s and defamed her when he denied the rape\par \par \uc2 January 6: lawsuits by police officers \u8211\'20\'13 several members of the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  are suing Trump saying his words and actions incited the 2021 riot.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Bob Woodward \u8211\'20\'13 Trump is suing journalist Woodward for alleged copyright violations, claiming Woodward had released audio from interviews without consent.\par \par \uc2 Trump and the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  , Mary Trump and CNN \u8211\'20\'13 Trump is suing his niece and \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  in New York state court over the disclosure of his tax information.\par \par \uc2 Trump and CNN \u8211\'20\'13 Trump has sued CNN in a southern Florida federal court, accusing the network of a \u8220\'20\'1Ccampaign of dissuasion in the form of libel and slander\u8221\'20\'1D. CNN has asked the judge for the case to be \u8220\'20\'1Cdismissed with prejudice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Associated Press is carrying some quotes on the legal basis of the case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  is trying to make, and both of them think Bragg may face an uphill struggle.\par \par \uc2 The indictment raises many thorny issues about state and federal law that could provide openings for the defense to attack the charges to try to get them tossed before the case even gets to trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is that it\u8217\'20\'19s murky,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Hasen, an expert in election law and professor at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  law school. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the district attorney did not offer a detailed legal analysis as to how they can do this, how they can get around these potential hurdles. And it could potentially tie up the case for a long time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 34 counts of falsifying business records would normally be misdemeanors, lower-level charges that would not normally result in prison time. But they were bumped up to felonies \u8211\'20\'13 which carry up to four years behind bars \u8211\'20\'13 because, Bragg says, they were done in an effort to commit or conceal other crimes.\par \par \uc2 The $130,000 payment to Daniels exceeded the federal cap on campaign contributions, Bragg said. He also cited a New York state election law that makes it a crime to promote a candidate by unlawful means.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors filed a \u8220\'20\'1Cstatement of facts\u8221\'20\'1D that told their story of a scheme to protect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential prospects by buying and suppressing unflattering information about him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are an awful lot of dots here which it takes a bit of imagination to connect,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Klein, a Touro Law Center criminal law professor. Bragg said the indictment doesn\u8217\'20\'19t specify the potential underlying crimes because the law doesn\u8217\'20\'19t require it. But given the likelihood of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers challenging it, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19d think they\u8217\'20\'19d want to be on much firmer ground than some of this stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D said Klein, a former New York City public defender.\par \par \uc2 Hasen said it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether candidates for federal office can be prosecuted in cases involving state election laws. The defense may also argue the case can\u8217\'20\'19t be brought in state court if it involves a federal election law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Our columnist Osita Nwanevu writes today that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution is a triumph:\par \par \uc2 One of the major questions in American political and legal thought has been whether presidents may be allowed to commit crimes. As it stands, the position of the Justice Department is that they may ?\u8212\'20\'14 for half a century, it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mailtrack.io/trace/link/19e19b15eaa7b98943bb1c4a7428c0f782a8b11c?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.law.virginia.edu%2Fnews%2F202301%2Fcan-presidents-be-prosecuted-or-sued-professor-explains-differing-visions-immunity%23%3A~%3Atext%3DIt%2520remains%2520official%2520Justice%2520Department%2Cor%2520prosecute%2520a%2520sitting%2520president.&userId=7149563&signature=8295fcc609b9ec91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held }}}\uc2  that a president cannot face criminal prosecution while in office. And while there\u8217\'20\'19s not even a theoretical bar to prosecuting a president once they leave office, no one had ever tried it, leaving the question of whether criminal laws functionally apply to presidents at all, as a practical matter, a matter of speculation.\par \par \uc2 Here \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  has bravely taken a stand: a person may, in fact, be indicted for a crime even if they were once president\u8212\'20\'14 just as though they were an ordinary person to whom laws applied. This is tremendous news. No rifts have opened in the time-space continuum. Frogs, locusts, and lice have yet to descend upon Manhattan. For the time being, it appears that a prosecutor really may attempt to hold a president ?\u8212\'20\'14 or at least a former president ?\u8212\'20\'14 accountable for a suspected crime without reality collapsing in on itself. What\u8217\'20\'19s more, Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s indictment amounts to an insistence that a former president may be indicted even for a relatively low-level crime like falsifying documents ?\u8212\'20\'14 just like any other white collar criminal.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/05/trump-indictment-law-crime-former-presidents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Osita Nwanevu \u8211\'20\'13 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution is a triumph }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/05/trump-indictment-law-crime-former-presidents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution is a triumph | Osita Nwanevu }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 The justice system in New York could not be described as the most fast-paced in the world. Lauren del Valle at CNN has set out the timeline of what we can expect:\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors said they expect to produce the bulk of the discovery in the next 65 days. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team has until 8 August to file any motions and the prosecution will respond by 19 September. Judge Juan Merchan said he will rule on the motions at the next in-person hearing, scheduled for 4 December.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Karen McDougal: who is second woman in Trump case?\par \par \uc2 In advance of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s court hearing we knew that payments made to adult actor Stormy Daniels were at the heart of the case. But it emerged that the prosecution is also citing payments made to Karen McDougal. Joan E Greve writes:\par \par \uc2 According to the Wall Street Journal, the office of the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  , has presented the grand jury with evidence involving the former Playboy model Karen McDougal, who claims to have had an extramarital affair with Trump beginning in 2006.\par \par \uc2 As the Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/national-enquirer-shielded-donald-trump-from-playboy-models-affair-allegation-1478309380?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported in 2016 }}}\uc2 , the parent company of the National Enquirer, which endorsed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidential bid, agreed to pay McDougal $150,000 for her story about the alleged affair. But the tabloid ultimately did not publish McDougal\u8217\'20\'19s account, effectively quashing the story in an industry tactic known as \u8220\'20\'1Ccatch and kill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Karen McDougal pictured in 2010. Photograph: Bennett Raglin/Getty Images for Bacardi\par \par \uc2 In her first televised appearance in 2018 McDougal detailed her relationship with Trump, saying that he would take her to his Manhattan home in Trump Tower through the back entrance and point out Melania\u8217\'20\'19s room. She also said the affair took place in several locations, including Lake Tahoe, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s private golf club in New Jersey, and the Beverly Hills Hotel.\par \par \uc2 The incident bears key similarities to the handling of Daniels\u8217\'20\'19 story about her alleged sexual encounters with Trump beginning in 2006. \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former lawyer, gave Daniels $130,000 for her story in 2016, and that transaction was not publicly reported until 2018. Cohen has said that Trump reimbursed him for the payment, but the former president denies wrongdoing in the hush money scheme, and he has dismissed the allegations of affairs with Daniels or McDougal.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury hearing evidence about the McDougal payment raises the possibility of Trump facing additional charges over the incident, or prosecutors may cite the transaction to establish a pattern of hush money schemes on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s part.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 There has been a fair amount of commentary that the high profile indictment of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would boost his campaign for the Republican nomination for the 2024 election, and help Republicans at the polls. That didn\u8217\'20\'19t bear any fruit immediately, most notably in Wisconsin, where liberal judge Janet Protasiewicz is projected to win her race for a seat on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Her win will flip the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, in an election which democracy observers have called the most consequential one of the year, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, redistricting and election rules at stake.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liberal judge wins Wisconsin supreme court election, flipping ideological balance }}}\par \par \uc2 In yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s other vote, progressive candidate and Cook county board commissioner Brandon Johnson won the election for Chicago mayor on Tuesday evening after pulling ahead of his opponent \uc2 Paul Vallas\uc2  in the evening.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/chicago-mayoral-election-polls-brandon-johnson-paul-vallas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Progressive candidate Brandon Johnson elected Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s new mayor }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is how my colleague David Smith in Washington assessed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech at Mar-a-Largo last night:\par \par \uc2 The former president ignored a plea from the judge in the case to refrain from inflammatory rhetoric, even launching a broadside at the judge\u8217\'20\'19s daughter over her political connections.\par \par \uc2 Supporters wore \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CTrump 2024\u8221\'20\'1D caps and snapped pictures of the president turned defendant. The audience included Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son Eric and his wife, Lara, Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and pillow maker and conspiracy theorist Mike Lindell.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI never thought anything like this could happen in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI never thought it could happen. The only crime that I have committed is to fearlessly defend our nation from those who seek to destroy it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  , alleges that Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the first former president to face criminal charges \u8211\'20\'13 falsified business records to conceal a violation of election laws.\par \par \uc2 He described Bragg, an elected Democrat, as \u8220\'20\'1Ca local failed district attorney charging a former president of the United States for the first time in history on a basis that every single pundit and legal analyst said there is no case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no case. They kept saying there\u8217\'20\'19s no case. Virtually everyone. But it\u8217\'20\'19s far worse than that because he knew there was no case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe criminal is the district attorney because he illegally leaked massive amounts of grand jury information for which he should be prosecuted or, at a minimum, he should resign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/trump-vents-grievances-against-criminal-charges-from-the-safety-of-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18US going to hell\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Donald Trump attacks hush money case in grievance-filled Mar-a-Lago speech }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/trump-vents-grievances-against-criminal-charges-from-the-safety-of-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18US going to hell\u8217\'20\'19: Donald Trump attacks hush money case in grievance-filled Mar-a-Lago speech }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24am BST\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gave a 25-minute speech after his New York arrest, where he listed long-held grievances and complaints about the several investigations he is facing before briefly addressing the indictment. As well as the hush money indictment, Trump is being investigated over his handling of classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago, and pressure he put on state officials over the 2020 election result in Georgia. Trump repeated falsehoods about the nature of the accusations he is facing, and personally attacked the prosecutors and investigators leading the cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20am BST\par \par \uc2 What we know so far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live US politics coverage the day after former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared in a New York courthouse, and then after pleading not guilty to 34 felony counts, returned to his base in Mar-a-Lago to give a speech condemning the prosecution. Here is what we know so far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was charged on Tuesday with 34 felony counts of falsifying business records in a historic case over allegations he orchestrated hush-money payments to two women before the 2016 US election to suppress publication of their alleged sexual encounters with him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump pleaded not guilty to the charges. The frontrunner in the race for the Republican nomination in 2024, Trump was subdued, responding briefly when the judge asked him if he understood his rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump flew home to Florida where he addressed family, friends and supporters at his Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, delivering a litany of grievances against investigators, prosecutors and rival politicians. He falsely described the New York prosecution as election interference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former US president attacked the judge, Justice Juan Merchan, and his family in the speech at the Mar-a-Lago ballroom, in which he also claimed the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to hell\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Merchan, the judge assigned to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case, did not impose a gag order but warned Trump to avoid making comments that were inflammatory or could cause civil unrest. Prosecutors said Trump made a series of social media posts, including one threatening \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he was charged. If convicted of any one of the 34 felony charges, Trump could face a maximum of four years in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge set the next hearing for 4 December. Legal experts said a trial may not even get under way for a year. An indictment or conviction will not legally prevent Trump from running for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mugshot was not taken, according to two law enforcement officials, though the Trump camp did create their own one to put on a T-shirt as part of a fundraising effort.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230405ej45001eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
