\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Wisconsin voters cast ballots in crucial state supreme court election\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levine in Milwaukee and Alice Herman in Madison \par \uc2 1,218 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2023\par 15:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , election rules, legislative maps at stake in most expensive judicial race in US history\par \par \uc2 Voters in Wisconsin are casting ballots on Tuesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/13/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-gerrymandered-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the most important elections}}}\uc2  of 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a contest that will determine the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The court will probably determine the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wisconsin, as a lawsuit challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 ban is already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/legal-challenge-wisconsins-1849-abortion-ban-awaiting-its-day-court-where-does-case-stand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 winding its way}}}\uc2  through the courts. It is also poised to play a hugely consequential role in setting election rules for the 2024 presidential election in Wisconsin, a key battleground state. It could also get rid of the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislative maps, which are so distorted in favor of Republicans that it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pbswisconsin.org/news-item/wisconsins-assembly-maps-are-more-skewed-than-ever-what-happens-in-2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly impossible}}}\uc2  for Democrats to ever win a majority.\par \par \uc2 Janet Protasiewicz, a liberal Milwaukee judge, is facing off against Dan Kelly, a conservative who lost his seat on the supreme court in 2020. Conservatives currently have a 4-3 majority on the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, but one of its conservative justices is retiring, meaning that the outcome of the election will determine the ideological balance of the court.\par \par \uc2 The race is the most expensive judicial race in American history. More than $45m has been spent, shattering the $10m record that was spent in Wisconsin in 2020 as well as the national record of $15m spent on an Illinois race in 2004. Protasiewicz\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has received significant financial backing from the Wisconsin Democratic party, while Kelly has has been bolstered by spending from outside groups, most notably a Super Pac backed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/02/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP mega-donors}}}\uc2  Richard and \uc2 Elizabeth Uihlein\uc2 . Kelly has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-funding-donors-election-deniers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received donations}}}\uc2  from individuals who tried to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dominated the race, as have concerns about voting rights and crime.\par \par \uc2 In Menomonee Falls, a Milwaukee suburb in conservative Waukesha county, a steady stream of voters poured into cast votes at the Good Shepherd church, a local polling station. Several voters pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their top issue in the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is top on my list. I\u8217\'20\'19m definitely pro-choice, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anybody else should be telling me or any other woman what to do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Karen Bitzan, a 64-year-old self-described homemaker, outside the polling place, where it was cold and drizzling on Tuesday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand the Republicans who say you can\u8217\'20\'19t have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but then they have no plan of how to protect those children who are forced to be born to parents who don\u8217\'20\'19t want them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lisa Ruiz, a 67-year-old retiree supporting Kelly, also pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the issue that drove her to the polls. \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is my number one. I stand against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s bringing more Christians to come and vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Menomonee Falls is part of a state senate district where there is a closely watched election on Tuesday that could give Republicans a supermajority in the state legislature. Republicans could use that advantage to override vetoes from \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, as well as to potentially impeach state officials. Dan Knodl, the Republican state senate candidate, has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2023/03/27/knodl-says-he-would-consider-impeaching-protasiewicz-if-hes-in-senate/70052973007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would consider}}}\uc2  impeaching Protasiewicz if he wins.\par \par \uc2 But several voters said on Tuesday they were hoping that a reconstituted supreme court would reconsider the state legislative districts, upending the Republican advantage in the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Kelly wins, it means they basically still have a stranglehold on the state, except when they have a statewide election. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not good news,\u8221\'20\'1D Terese Dineen, 70, said after she voted in Brookfield, another Milwaukee suburb.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just think it\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous that a state that\u8217\'20\'19s so evenly divided is just not represented,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bill Anderson, 57, a project manager in Brookfield.\par \par \uc2 Also on the ballot on Tuesday were two GOP-backed referendum questions dealing with cash bail and welfare benefits. Democrats say those questions are a blatant effort to juice Republican turnout and some voters expressed frustration at how hard they were to understand. \u8220\'20\'1CI would like a referendum question to make referendum questions more understandable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Debra Tomkins, a voter in Madison, the state capital.\par \par \uc2 In Milwaukee, as a heavy rain began falling around noon, canvassers dressed in neon vests gathered at the office of Black Leaders Organizing Communities (Bloc), a civic engagement group focused on Black communities. An organizer reminded canvassers to tell voters that they could still return their mail-in ballots in person and that those who voted a provisional ballot without identification would need to return with an accepted form of ID to have their vote counted.\par \par \uc2 The majority of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Black population is in Milwaukee. Earlier this year, Robert Spindell, a Republican on the six-member body that oversees voting in the state, celebrated low turnout in the city in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really angering all of us. It makes us work harder. We know we have to knock 10 extra doors to make up for however many people are trying to misinform, spread misinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kyle Johnson, 27, Bloc\u8217\'20\'19s political director.\par \par \uc2 New maps in Wisconsin could also make a huge difference in Milwaukee, where Black voters have been packed into as few districts as possible to dilute their overall influence. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so many other issues that we\u8217\'20\'19re not able to move forward on unfortunately because of redistricting and specifically because of gerrymandering,\u8221\'20\'1D said Angela Lang, the group\u8217\'20\'19s executive director.\par \par \uc2 Voters and election officials reported high turnout at polling places on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung voters normally don\u8217\'20\'19t vote in judicial elections, but this year is different,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ben Wikler, chair of the Democratic party of Wisconsin, during a get-out-the-vote event on the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2  campus in Madison. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s this real sense that with reproductive freedom on the line and democracy on the line, this is a can\u8217\'20\'19t-miss election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/umichvoter/status/1643334209895907328"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A video on Twitter}}}\uc2  showed long lines of students waiting to vote at the University of Wisconsin Eau Claire. The wait was around 45 minutes to an hour, said Matthew Lehner, the president of the school\u8217\'20\'19s college Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CThe clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office simply wasn\u8217\'20\'19t prepared for the numbers and new registrations, which were off the charts,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Lehner said he and other students had contacted local officials, who had provided more resources and the wait has since gone down.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits were driving students to vote, Lehner said. \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people are just more interested in electoral politics and politics in the state. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a massive increase in students all across the state of Wisconsin voting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin was expecting severe weather on Tuesday afternoon, including high winds, hail and a potential tornado. The Dane county clerk, Scott McDonell, told the Guardian he was concerned about how the weather might affect turnout and was telling people to vote early.\par \par \uc2 Meagan Wolfe\uc2 , Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s chief election official, told reporters in a call that she was working with Wisconsin emergency management to monitor the weather.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSevere weather is a very common contingency that Wisconsin election officials are prepared for,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Polls close at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230404ej440018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
