\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Liberal judge wins Wisconsin supreme court election, flipping ideological balance\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Herman in Madison and Sam Levine in Milwaukee \par \uc2 841 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2023\par 14:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, redistricting and election rules were at stake in decision affecting key swing state\par \par \uc2 In a historic election, the liberal judge Janet Protasiewicz won her race for a seat on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court on Tuesday. Her win will flip the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, which has been controlled by a conservative majority for 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Elections and democracy observers have called this election the most consequential one of the year, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, redistricting and election rules at stake. The race pitted Protasiewicz, a Milwaukee circuit court judge and former prosecutor, against Dan Kelly, a former Wisconsin supreme court justice with ties to election deniers and the far right.\par \par \uc2 Protasiewicz will replace the conservative justice Patience Roggensack on 1 August; the court will be controlled by a narrow liberal majority.\par \par \uc2 The race smashed campaign finance records for state judicial elections, drawing more than $45m, according to a WisPolitics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wispolitics.com/2023/wispolitics-review-spending-in-supreme-court-race-nears-45-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2 . By comparison, in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s last supreme court race in 2020, donors brought in about $10m. Political groups and wealthy individuals across the country have opened their coffers on both sides of the race, with Protasiewicz raising nearly $9m from the Democratic party and outside groups pledging more than $6m on pro-Kelly advertisements.\par \par \uc2 The massive contributions underscore the stakes of the race \u8211\'20\'13 from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral maps, which experts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/expert-republicans-virtually-100-percent-certain-retain-majorities-under-gop-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 identified}}}\uc2  as one of the most gerrymandered in the country.\par \par \uc2 In 2020 the Wisconsin supreme court narrowly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisonsin-supreme-court-trump-lawsuit-e6b3aa222b4141c0844d541c4b041964"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  an attempt by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to overturn the results of the presidential election; the court could see a similar challenge in 2024. Following the 2020 elections, Kelly was hired by the Wisconsin GOP to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/daniel-kelly-wisconsin-supreme-court-trump-fake-electors-rcna71276"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advise}}}\uc2  on a plan to have a group of Republicans falsely claim to be electors. The plan failed and Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 10 Democratic electors voted for Joe Biden, reflecting the popular vote in the state.\par \par \uc2 In a March interview with the Guardian, Protasiewicz said the future of democracy in Wisconsin and at the national level motivated her to run. \u8220\'20\'1CI thought about our democracy, and our democracy being at stake. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why I decided to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the issues that we care about are going to come in front of this court. But primarily, primarily, our democracy is on the line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in June, an 1849 law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  went back into effect in Wisconsin. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly emerged as a top issue in this race, with voters across the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/03/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mobilizing}}}\uc2  around the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/wisconsin-abortion-ban-lawsuit-josh-kaul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge}}}\uc2  to the ban is currently making its way through state courts and will probably end up in front of the state supreme court this year.\par \par \uc2 During the race, Protasiewicz was open about her personal support for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, and although Kelly refrained from sharing his views on the campaign trail, his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/02/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 benefited}}}\uc2  from more than $1m from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Women Speak Out Pac and earned endorsements from three anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups in the state.\par \par \uc2 With a liberal majority on the court, the 1849 ban could be overruled.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the announcement of Protasiewicz\u8217\'20\'19s win Tuesday night, \uc2 Mandela Barnes\uc2 , Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s former lieutenant governor who ran unsuccessfully for a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat in 2022, told the Guardian that her victory would be incredibly significant for the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf she pulls this off we can restore balance, we can restore fairness, we can restore actual justice,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s exciting about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At Protasiewicz\u8217\'20\'19s election night watch party in Milwaukee, supporters followed the election on their phones and broke out in excitement as favorable results were reported. The room erupted once the race was called for Protasiewicz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s one of those people who\u8217\'20\'19s Wisconsin to the bone,\u8221\'20\'1D Sonya Bice, 57, a lawyer in Madison, said about Protasiewicz. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s one of those people who\u8217\'20\'19s willing to get out there and run in what everyone knew was going to be a very ugly race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Progressive groups in the state are preparing to take advantage of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s new liberal majority. Nicole Safar, the executive director of Law Forward, a progressive non-profit legal group, said organizers were considering how best to challenge the state\u8217\'20\'19s rigged legislative maps.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLaw Forward and our allies and our co-counsel are seriously looking at what a partisan gerrymander claim under the Wisconsin constitution looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In a special election that is still too close to call, voters will decide between Republican Dan Knodl and Democrat Jodi Habush Sinykin to represent Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s northern suburbs. If Knodl wins, the Republican party will have a supermajority in the state senate, paving the way for the party to impeach state officials \u8211\'20\'13 a process that Knodl says he would consider launching to pull Protasiewicz from the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230405ej450008g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
