\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump addresses indictment in brief \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now) and Maanvi Singh (earlier) \par \uc2 5,740 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2023\par 03:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full story on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full story on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment \u8211\'20\'13 and the aftermath \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-charges-34-felony-counts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be closing this blog shortly. Here is a summary of today\u8217\'20\'19s events so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was charged on Tuesday with 34 felony counts of falsifying business records in a historic case over allegations he orchestrated hush-money payments to two women before the 2016 US election to suppress publication of their alleged sexual encounters with him. Prosecutors in Manhattan accused Trump, the first sitting or former US president to face criminal charges, of trying to conceal a violation of election laws during his successful 2016 campaign. The two women in the case are adult film actor Stormy Daniels and former Playboy model Karen McDougal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump pleaded not guilty to the charges. The frontrunner in the race for the Republican nomination in 2024, Trump was subdued, responding briefly when the judge asked him if he understood his rights. At one point, the judge put his hand to his ear as if to prompt an answer. Trump made no comment when he left court just under an hour later.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump flew home to Florida where he addressed family, friends and supporters at his Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, delivering a litany of grievances against investigators, prosecutors and rival politicians. He falsely described the New York prosecution as election interference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor Chris Conroy said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  falsified New York business records in order to conceal an illegal conspiracy to undermine the integrity of the 2016 presidential election and other violations of election laws.\u8221\'20\'1D While falsifying business records in New York on its own is a misdemeanour punishable by no more than one year in prison, it is elevated to a felony punishable by up to four years when done to advance or conceal another crime, such as election law violations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  defended the charges in a press conference after the arraignment. \u8220\'20\'1CWe today uphold our solemn responsibility to ensure that everyone stands equal before the law. No amount of money and no amount of power changes that enduring American principle,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight it hard,\u8221\'20\'1D Todd Blanche, a lawyer for Trump, told reporters after the arraignment. He said that while Trump was frustrated, upset and angry about the charges, \u8220\'20\'1C \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s motivated. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to stop him. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to slow him down. And it\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what he expected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Justice Juan Merchan, the judge assigned to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case, did not impose a gag order but warned Trump to avoid making comments that were inflammatory or could cause civil unrest. Prosecutors said Trump made a series of social media posts, including one threatening \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he was charged. If convicted of any one of the 34 felony charges, Trump could face a maximum of four years in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge set the next hearing for 4 December. Legal experts said a trial may not even get under way for a year. An indictment or conviction will not legally prevent Trump from running for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mugshot was not taken, according to two law enforcement officials, though the Trump camp did create their own one to put on a T-shirt as part of a fundraising effort.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 In an opinion piece for the Guardian, Sidney Blumenthal, former senior adviser to President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , argues that every indictment will make Trump stronger:\par \par \uc2 The indictment of \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  has not driven a wooden stake through his heart. He has risen, omnipresent and ominous again, overwhelming his rivals, their voices joined into his choir, like the singing January 6 prisoners, proclaiming the wickedness of his prosecution. As he enters the criminal courthouse to pose for his mugshot and to give his fingerprints, evangelicals venerate him as the adulterous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forward.com/culture/542018/trump-indictment-king-david-comparison-evangelical/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 King David}}}\uc2  or the martyred {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.christianheadlines.com/contributors/michael-foust/billboard-comparing-trump-to-jesus-christ-is-removed-after-backlash.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christ}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump does not have to raise his hand to signal to the House Republicans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/03/31/house-gop-debates-public-urination/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echo}}}\uc2  his cry of \u8220\'20\'1CWITCH-HUNT\u8221\'20\'1D. He owns the House like he owns a hotel.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 From the report of every new indictment to its reality, Republican radicalization will accelerate. Every concrete count will confirm every conspiracy theory. Every prosecution and trial, staggered over months and into the election year, from New York to Georgia to Washington, will be a shock driving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  further to Trump. Every Republican candidate running for every office will be compelled to declare as a matter of faith that Trump is being unjustly persecuted or be themselves branded traitors.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-republicans-murdoch-koch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Every indictment will make Trump stronger \u8211\'20\'13 and Republicans wilder | Sidney Blumenthal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Politico has painted a picture of the atmosphere at Mar-a-Lago, with a telling comment from former House Speaker Newt Gingrich.\par \par \uc2 Allies, aides, club members and the press were packed into the gilded ballroom of Mar-a-Lago, waiting for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to arrive\u8230\'20\'26 In the ballroom at the Florida estate, there was no sense of sobriety in the air. It felt, instead, like a Maga movie set.\par \par \uc2 The room was lit up with bright spotlights for the cameras. And as the assembled guests waited for the man of the hour to arrive, the setting took on the feel of a catwalk for Trump world\u8217\'20\'19s upper crust. Family, staff and top surrogates walked in smiling and waving.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Tuesday, in a way, was like a campaign relaunch, still grievance-filled but with Trump world feeling that they are in a better position. The polling that just months ago was used as evidence of his failure to rally the base has dramatically shifted, now showing the former president with leads upward of 20 percentage points over DeSantis. It underscored the central paradox of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political career: His standing benefits from the crises he endures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re back to all Trump all the time,\u8221\'20\'1D said former House Speaker and past presidential candidate Newt Gingrich. \u8220\'20\'1CNothing makes him happier.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video report on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Florida earlier, during which he delivered a litany of grievances against investigators, prosecutors and rival politicians. He falsely described the New York prosecution as election interference:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m just cutting away from the indictment for a moment to the results in Wisconsin, where a Democratic-backed Milwaukee judge has won the high stakes supreme court Race, ensuring liberals will take over majority control of the court for the first time in 15 years with the fate of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban pending.\par \par \uc2 Milwaukee County Circuit Judge Janet Protasiewicz defeated former Justice Dan Kelly, who previously worked for Republicans and had support from the state\u8217\'20\'19s leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 Janet Protasiewicz arrives 10 minutes after the polls closed, for her election night watch party Tuesday 4 April 2023 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Photograph: Mark Hertzberg/ZUMA Press Wire/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The new court controlled 4-3 by liberals is expected to decide a pending lawsuit challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Protasiewicz made the issue a focus of her campaign and won the support of Planned Parenthood and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups.\par \par \uc2 Four of the past six presidential elections in Wisconsin have been decided by less than a percentage point. Trump turned to the courts in 2020 in his unsuccessful push to overturn his roughly 21,000-vote loss in the state.\par \par \uc2 Protasiewicz, a Milwaukee County judge, largely focused her campaign around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying she supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights but stopping short of saying how she would rule on a pending lawsuit challenging Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 174-year-old ban that was enacted a year after statehood.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44am BST\par \par \uc2 With that, let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at the day\u8217\'20\'19s newspaper front pages with my colleague Jonathan Yerushalmy.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  says, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-charges-34-felony-counts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump pleads not guilty to 34 charges in hush-money case}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, with the paper highlighting the judge\u8217\'20\'19s order that the former president refrain from rhetoric that could cause civil unrest.\par \par \uc2 enltrGuardian front page, Wednesday 5 April 2023: Trump pleads not guilty to 34 charges in hush-money case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FB8GRnC5Fn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FB8GRnC5Fn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Guardian (@guardian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian/status/1643359878516289536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Time magazine gained a reputation for producing iconic covers throughout the Trump presidency, and they hit the mark again on Wednesday, with the simple headline: \u8220\'20\'1CUnprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrTIME's new cover: Unprecedented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s4uRgTntCp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/s4uRgTntCp}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x5wybdYFjH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/x5wybdYFjH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TIME (@TIME) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TIME/status/1643373512592089089?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Times splashes with, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump in the dock\u8221\'20\'1D. The paper\u8217\'20\'19s US correspondents describe how a \u8220\'20\'1Cstony-faced Trump was released from custody after an hour-long arraignment hearing ahead of a trial likely to take place next year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWednesday's Times: Trump in the dock {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TheTimes?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TheTimes}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Times?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Times}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LQhwo2SLEP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LQhwo2SLEP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tomorrows Papers Today (@TmorrowsPapers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TmorrowsPapers/status/1643368728241815552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump in the eye of the Stormy\u8221\'20\'1D, is the Mirror\u8217\'20\'19s headline. The paper goes on to say that, \u8220\'20\'1CFinally\u8230\'20\'26 ex-President charged over \u8216\'20\'18hush-money\u8217\'20\'19 payments to porn star\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWednesday's Mirror: Trump In The Eye Of The Stormy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DailyMirror?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DailyMirror}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Mirror?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Mirror}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uieMhukdA6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uieMhukdA6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tomorrows Papers Today (@TmorrowsPapers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TmorrowsPapers/status/1643371476362338304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 You can read the full roundup here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/05/in-the-eye-of-the-stormy-how-papers-across-the-world-reacted-to-trumps-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In the eye of the Stormy\u8217\'20\'19: how papers across the world reacted to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s charges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am BST\par \par \uc2 So, how was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment covered in the US media \u8211\'20\'13 and have any lessons been learned since 2016? The AP\u8217\'20\'19s David Bauder has taken a look:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to over-dramatize what this means for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Chris Jansing said today.\par \par \uc2 Oh, but many tried.\par \par \uc2 Hour after hour today, the story occupied the full attention of broadcast and cable news networks. They waited for glimpses of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s face to interpret his expression, followed his motorcade\u8217\'20\'19s movements from the air, speculated on how it must feel to be arrested.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s travels from Florida to New York led cable news networks to revisit the worst of earlier excesses. Throughout the day, aerial camera shots followed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plane as it took off from Florida and landed in New York, and as his motorcade traveled to Trump Tower in Manhattan \u8211\'20\'13 the backdrop to hours of speculation about the case.\par \par \uc2 At one point, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son Eric posted on social media a picture of a television set inside the plane showing a Fox News Channel picture of the plane waiting on a Florida tarmac. \u8220\'20\'1CWatching the plane \u8230\'20\'26 from the plane,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 New York state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-indictment-new-york-judge-merchan-arraignment-032a097661c259709a948ce0e70a872a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court Judge Juan Merchan}}}\uc2  declined media requests for video coverage of the hearing where Trump heard the charges against him and pleaded not guilty. That led to constant, mostly empty talk about what might happen.\par \par \uc2 Will Trump\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade to the court take Fifth Avenue or the FDR Drive? (The latter.) Will a mug shot of Trump be taken and released? (No.) Would the former president speak to the media before he goes into the court? (No.) After the hearing is done? (Also no.)\par \par \uc2 His walk out the door was judged \u8220\'20\'1Cfive seconds of history\u8221\'20\'1D by ABC\u8217\'20\'19s David Muir. Those views of Trump, along with still pictures of him during the arraignment, turned political and legal commentators into facial-expression and body-language experts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Romney: 'prosecutor has stretched...to fit a political agenda'\par \par \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , the former presidential nominee, who as a Utah senator was the only Republican to vote to convict Trump in both his impeachment trials, has criticised the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office for its handling of the hush money case in which the former president pleaded not guilty on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s character and conduct make him unfit for office,\u8221\'20\'1D Romney said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.romney.senate.gov/romney-statement-on-indictment-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 , as Trump was arraigned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven so, I believe the New York prosecutor has stretched to reach felony criminal charges in order to fit a political agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is above the law, not even former presidents, but everyone is entitled to equal treatment under the law. The prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s overreach sets a dangerous precedent for criminalizing political opponents and damages the public\u8217\'20\'19s faith in our justice system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/mitt-romney-trump-unfit-office-new-york-charges-political"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitt Romney: Trump is unfit for office but New York charges are political}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 There are thorny legal issues raised by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s indictment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is that it\u8217\'20\'19s murky,\u8221\'20\'1D Richard Hasen, an expert in election law and professor at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  law school told the Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the district attorney did not offer a detailed legal analysis as to how they can do this, how they can get around these potential hurdles. And it could potentially tie up the case for a long time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are an awful lot of dots here which it takes a bit of imagination to connect,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Klein, a Touro Law Center criminal law professor. Bragg said the indictment doesn\u8217\'20\'19t specify the potential underlying crimes because the law doesn\u8217\'20\'19t require it. But given the likelihood of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers challenging it, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19d think they\u8217\'20\'19d want to be on much firmer ground than some of this stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D said Klein, a former New York City public defender.\par \par \uc2 Manhattan District Attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  speaks during a press conference after the arraignment of former US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  4 April 2023 in New York City. Photograph: Kena Betancur/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Hasen said it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether candidates for federal office can be prosecuted in cases involving state election laws. The defense may also argue the case can\u8217\'20\'19t be brought in state court if it involves a federal election law.\par \par \uc2 While the prosecution\u8217\'20\'19s theory is certainly unusual, it\u8217\'20\'19s not unwinnable, some experts said.\par \par \uc2 Bragg is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to bring in witnesses, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to show a lot of documentary evidence to attempt to demonstrate that all these payments were in furtherance of the presidential campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jerry H.? Goldfeder, a veteran election lawyer in New York and the director of Fordham Law School\u8217\'20\'19s Voting \uc2 Rights and Democracy\uc2  Project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt remains to be seen if he can prove it beyond a reasonable doubt,\u8221\'20\'1D Goldfeder said. But, he added, \u8220\'20\'1CDo not underestimate District Attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  and do not overestimate Mr. Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 On Fox, Laura Ingraham is running a segment on the decision by MSNBC to not broadcast Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks in Florida.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re embarrassed by the \u8220\'20\'1Cflimsy\u8221\'20\'1D indictment and knew Trump would \u8220\'20\'1Cuse his comments to tell the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Hi, my name is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helen Sullivan}}}\uc2  and I\u8217\'20\'19m taking over our live coverage of this historic day from my formidable colleague Maanvi Singh.\par \par \uc2 If you have questions, comments, or would like to get in touch you can find me on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  surrendered to authorities and New York and pleaded not guilty to 34 charges of falsifying business records, he delivered a brief, grievance-laden speech from his his Florida residence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump became the first American president to face criminal charges. Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  said the ex-president faces 34 felony counts of falsifying documents \u8220\'20\'1Cwith intent to defraud and intent to conceal another crime\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthese are felony crimes in New York state, no matter who you are\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s court appearance, during which he was finger-printed, but not cuffed, came five days after a New York grand jury voted to indict him, based on a years-long investigation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The charges are focused on payments Trump made to hide an affair with adult film star Stormy Daniels, as well as hush money deals with Playboy model Karen McDougal and a former Trump Tower doorman. The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has accused Trump of having \u8220\'20\'1Corchestrated a scheme\u8221\'20\'1D with the intent \u8220\'20\'1Cto influence the 2016 presidential election by identifying and purchasing negative information about him to suppress its publication and benefit the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s electoral prospects\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Separately, Trump faces a criminal investigation into his role during the January 6 insurrection and his retention of classified documents at Mar-a-Lago after leaving office. He is also facing an investigation into efforts to overturn the elections in Georgia. The New York state attorney general has sued Trump, his family, and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  over financial wrong doing. He is also facing a defamation suit arising from allegations of rape.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a rambling speech, Trump collapsed long-held grievances with complaints about the several investigations he is facing, focused especially on the classified documents case. He repeated falsehoods about the nature of the accusations he is facing, and personally attacked the prosecutors and investigators leading the cases.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president only spoke for about 25 minutes \u8211\'20\'13 which was much shorter than his standard. But otherwise, the remarks had many elements of his standard rally stump speech.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m signing off, but my colleagues in Australia will continue to bring you updates and analysis.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Judge in hush money case\par \par \uc2 Trump called justice Juan Merchan a \u8220\'20\'1CTrump-hating judge with a Trump-hating wife whose daughter worked for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s daughter is president of Authentic, an agency that has worked with the campaigns of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  , \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  and other Democrats. But that is not a conflict of interest for the justice, or grounds for a recusal by judicial ethics standards.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Classified documents\par \par \uc2 During the speech, Trump also claimed that the Presidential Records Act involves a negotiation with the \uc2 National Archives and Records Administration\uc2  over documents, which is false. In fact, Nara gets custody of presidential documents the moment he leaves office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump was joined tonight by his children Don Jr, Eric and Tiffany, as well as supporters including \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2 , Mike Lindell, far-right representatives \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , and former Arizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake.\par \par \uc2 Missing tonight were Trump\u8217\'20\'19s eldest daughter \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , who has distanced herself from her father after working for his administration, and Melania Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Media outlets cut away from Trump's speech or avoid altogether\par \par \uc2 CNN cut away from its live coverage of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech as the former president continued to rail against the charges against him.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, MSNBC opted not to broadcast Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks at all. Instead, host Rachel Maddow said the outlet would monitor his remarks for any news rather than cover them in full.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is basically a campaign speech in which he is repeating his same lies and allegations against his perceived enemies,\u8221\'20\'1D Maddow said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s just giving his normal list of grievances. We don\u8217\'20\'19t consider that necessarily newsworthy and there is a cost to us as a news organization of knowingly broadcasting untrue things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"We're not takin' it." Here's Rachel Maddow explaining how MSNBC is not broadcasting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  live but monitoring his speech for newsworthiness, should there be any. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tFrtHhXdbD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tFrtHhXdbD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maddow Blog (@MaddowBlog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MaddowBlog/status/1643412712674787330?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 NPR also did not air Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech live.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn a day of wall-to-wall Trump coverage, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NPR?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NPR}}}\uc2  is taking a different approach. Yes, we'll cover the news. Yes, we have reporters at the courthouse & Trump Tower. But we're covering lots of other news too, and we will not air Trump's speech live. Here's why: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HengUR6kCg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HengUR6kCg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WgPLcupxVA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WgPLcupxVA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mary Louise Kelly (@NPRKelly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NPRKelly/status/1643228785762770944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact-check: classified documents\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has repeatedly misconstrued the investigation into his possession of classified documents, comparing what he did to what his predecessors did.\par \par \uc2 Trump took classified documents to Mar-a-Lago, whereas former president Barack Obama turned over documents, according to the \uc2 National Archives and Records Administration\uc2  itself. In the cases of other former presidents, the Nara moved documents out of DC to other facilities.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 The ex-president finished up abruptly, after speaking for about 25 minutes\par \par \uc2 After listing off a number of grievances, attacking those involved in the multiple investigations and criminal cases against him, and rambling a number of of-repeated falsehoods about the 2020 elections, he walked off stage.\par \par \uc2 The speech was in many ways a standard performance, but shorter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact-check: \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18laptop from hell\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  began his remarks at Mar-a-Lago by quickly bringing up \u8220\'20\'1C Hunter Biden \u8217\'20\'19s laptop from hell, which the former president falsely claimed exposes the Biden family as \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives have latched on to the story about the laptop since it was reportedly left by Hunter in a computer repair shop in 2020, and argue it contains data somehow proving corruption on the part of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his relatives. Data on the laptop, which analysts and news media examined extensively, showed that Hunter tried to use his family name to his advantage, but did not show corruption on the part of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump finally addressed the indictment \u8230\'20\'26 briefly\par \par \uc2 He attacked Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , and his family, bringing up Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s wife\u8217\'20\'19s tweets. He also attacked the judge assigned to the case, calling him a \u8220\'20\'1CTrump-hating judge with a Trump-hating wife and family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump did not, however, deny paying Stormy Daniels and Karen McDougal hush money to cover up an extramarital affair.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 So far, this has been a version of the classic Trump stump speech \u8211\'20\'13 rambling, repetitive, and bereft of fact.\par \par \uc2 The ex-president has started off by listing a number of unrelated political grievances, referring back to his first impeachment and issues with social media companies, and lobbed accusations against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He reiterated antisemitic rhetoric to discredit the Manhattan district attorney, denied the charges, then launched into a rambling, heavily embellished rant on the unrelated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/trump-lawyer-evan-corcoran-mar-a-lago-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  into the top-secret documents found at Mar-a-Lago, then started on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/trump-new-york-investigation-ivanka-donald-eric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the civil fraud suit}}}\uc2  brought by the New York state attorney general.\par \par \uc2 The speech blurs distinctions between the investigations and court battles he is facing ahead, lumping them all into a singular enemy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes stage\par \par \uc2 Trump walked on as Proud to be an American played. The former president will be making his first public remarks since getting charged with crimes.\par \par \uc2 The atmosphere in the room is that of a classic Trump political rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 New role for Trump as TV host turned president reboots as The Defendant\par \par \uc2 He hosted The Apprentice. He played The President. Now, at the age of 76, came the role that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  had spent his life avoiding: The Defendant.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a single photograph showed Trump sitting in a prosaic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  courtroom with two lawyers to his left and two more to his right. Behind him were two uniformed police officers wearing handcuffs on their belts. One had a police radio on his shoulder, the other a Covid-protective mask over her face.\par \par \uc2 Two grey, ordinary notice boards adorned the plain wood wall. A small Stars and Stripes was pinned to one at an oblique angle. But perhaps most striking about the image was that, while everyone else was engaged in the moment, Trump stared back at the camera with an ambiguous expression.\par \par \uc2 For his millions of critics in blue America, this was the face of a criminal defendant at his moment of reckoning. It was the final fall for a man who used to walk with kings, command the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful military and casually threaten political opponents such as \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  with jail.\par \par \uc2 But his millions of fans in red America will have seen something else. America\u8217\'20\'19s faith in law enforcement is matched only by its romance with glamorous criminals such as Bonnie and Clyde or Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid. This was the day of The Outlaw \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Its neat symbol came in the form of a characteristically fake image. About half an hour before Trump pleaded not guilty to 34 felony counts of falsifying business records over a hush money payments to two women, his campaign sent out a fundraising email selling T-shirts with a mocked-up mugshot of Trump and the legend: \u8220\'20\'1CNot guilty.\u8221\'20\'1D (In reality, no mugshot was taken.)\par \par \uc2 It was a typically audacious move that said everything about how, while this was a hideous day for Trump legally, it was seen by many as a victorious day for him politically and financially.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/trump-courtroom-photo-defendant-arraignment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New role for Trump as TV host turned president reboots as The Defendant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has landed in Florida.\par \par \uc2 He was greeted by supporters including Mike Lindell, the MyPillow owner and prominent disseminator of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/03/mike-lindell-shasta-county-california-dominion-voting-systems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election misinformation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many of the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s greeters were dressed in American flag colors and some were holding Trump 2024 signs.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  chant and wave flags during a rally to welcome him home. Photograph: Wilfredo Lee/AP\par \par \uc2 At Mar-A-Lago, where Trump is expected to speak soon, Arizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake was among the well-known followers awaiting him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 The charges, explained\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  in New York and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  in Washington report:\par \par \uc2 In a 13-page statement of facts, the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office accused Trump of having \u8220\'20\'1Corchestrated a scheme\u8221\'20\'1D with the intent \u8220\'20\'1Cto influence the 2016 presidential election by identifying and purchasing negative information about him to suppress its publication and benefit the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s electoral prospects\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The charges, according to the felony indictment unsealed on Tuesday, stem from payments made to adult film star Stormy Daniels, who said she had a sexual encounter with Trump in 2006, as well as hush money deals made with Playboy model Karen McDougal, who wanted to sell her story of an affair with Trump ahead of the 2016 election, and a former Trump Tower doorman, who claimed Trump had fathered a child out of wedlock.\par \par \uc2 Trump has denied the sexual encounters and any wrongdoing, casting himself as the victim of a political \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his arraignment. Photograph: EyePress News/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe today uphold our solemn responsibility to ensure that everyone stands equal before the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  said at his press conference after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment. \u8220\'20\'1CNo amount of money, no amount of power changes that enduring American principle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Facing scrutiny over his decision to pursue the case, Bragg forcefully defended the case. He argued that falsifying business records was the \u8220\'20\'1Cbread and butter\u8221\'20\'1D of his office\u8217\'20\'19s white-collar investigations and that \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue and accurate business records\u8221\'20\'1D were all the more important in Manhattan, which he called the \u8220\'20\'1C??financial capital of the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to prosecutors, Daniels was paid $130,000 by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s then lawyer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  to buy her silence in the final days of the presidential campaign. Cohen said the payments were made at the direction of Trump, who reimbursed him while serving as president. Those payments, distributed to Cohen through Trump\u8217\'20\'19s company, were falsely classified as legal expenses, prosecutors say.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Cohen pleaded guilty to federal crimes involving the hush money payment and was sentenced to three years in prison, which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has used to undermine his credibility.\par \par \uc2 Separately, prosecutors say, the parent company of the National Enquirer, \uc2 American Media Inc\uc2 , arranged two \u8220\'20\'1Ccatch and kill\u8221\'20\'1D deals to squash stories that could potentially damage Trump\u8217\'20\'19s electoral prospects. One involved a $30,000 payoff to the former Trump Tower doorman. The tabloid reached a $150,000 agreement with McDougal, purchasing the rights to her story in an effort to keep it from going public.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors doubled down on the timing of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions, which they said could have undermined his campaign during the 2016 election. And they asked for protective orders for discovery materials, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s escalatory posts on his platform Truth Social, such as when he vowed \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D in the event he was indicted.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-charges-34-felony-counts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump pleads not guilty to 34 felony charges in hush money case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 In New York, Trump got an underwhelming show of support.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of pro- and anti-Trump protesters had gathered outside the Manhattan criminal court, and the crowds were expected to go wild as the former president arrived and was taken into the custody.\par \par \uc2 But in the event, few knew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-court-arraignment-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump had arrived}}}\uc2  until he was already in the building and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-pdf-full-text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under arrest}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It made for a slightly underwhelming scene as the two opposing crowds \u8211\'20\'13 separated by metal barriers \u8211\'20\'13 were filled with whispers, rather than chants.\par \par \uc2 Snippets of information were passed from person to person at about 1.30pm. A Trump-supporting woman reported that her boss\u8217\'20\'19s friend, who manages a restaurant in New Jersey, believed the ex-president had arrived and was in court.\par \par \uc2 But another woman had a CNN live stream on her phone which showed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s car was still en route to the court. It turned out the screen had frozen, however, and eventually a general consensus emerged: Trump was in court, and had been arraigned on more than 30 charges relating to hush money payments to an adult film star.\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters near the New York criminal court awaiting the arrival of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on 4 April 2023. Photograph: Ken Cedeno/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The anti-Trump protesters, many of whom had had been dancing, singing and chanting since about 9.30am that morning, let out a loud cheer. Someone had been giving out whistles, and they were blown in jubilation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a play on the chant that Trump supporters aimed at Hillary Clinton through the 2016 election and beyond \u8211\'20\'13 could be heard around Collect Pond Park, a former open sewer where the public had been contained by police.\par \par \uc2 On the Trump side of the barricade, the mood was quiet. No one wailed, no one fell to their knees, there was just a low murmur as mumbles and expletives were uttered from underneath a sea of red Maga hats.\par \par \uc2 They had been more animated in the morning, although the centerpiece of the protest \u8211\'20\'13 an appearance by \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the QAnon-dabbling, hard-right Republican conspiracy theorist \u8211\'20\'13 had descended into farce almost immediately.\par \par \uc2 Some anti-Trumpers had infiltrated the Trump side, and launched a highly successful attempt to silence the Georgia congresswoman. Greene, escorted by security, was armed with a megaphone, but she could be barely be heard above the sound of whistling and shouting. From about 10 yards away it was possible to make out the words \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, the name of the Manhattan district attorney who has brought the case against Trump, but the rest was just noise.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/trump-protests-reaction-new-york-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump gets underwhelming show of support on surreal day in New York}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to make first public comments after arraignment\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to make his first public remarks after his arraignment earlier today in New York this evening from his home in Florida.\par \par \uc2 This is the first time in US history that a former president has been charged with a crime. Trump pleaded not guilty to 34 felony charges of falsifying business records and conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 After entering his plea, Trump posted on his Truth Social account that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno case\u8221\'20\'1D against him, and \u8220\'20\'1Cthere was nothing done illegally\u8221\'20\'1D. He is expected to reiterate that message in his speech tonight.\par \par \uc2 Already, Trump has used his arraignment as an opportunity to rile up supporters and raise funds, calling on followers to \u8220\'20\'1CPROTEST\u8221\'20\'1D his arrest and launching threatening, racist attacks against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/who-is-alvin-bragg-donald-trump-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Bragg}}}\uc2 , the Manhattan district attorney who is overseeing the case.\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  speaks at a press conference outside the Manhattan federal court on 4 April 2023. Photograph: Angela Weiss/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Bragg has charged Trump with crimes primarily connected to a hush money payment to Stormy Daniels, who said she had a sexual encounter with Trump in 2006. But Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors have also accused Trump of undermining the integrity of the 2016 elections by orchestrating a scheme to purchase and suppress negative stories.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s journey to and from New York to face the charges and enter his plea has been closely tracked by a media circus, which the president has played into.\par \par \uc2 Although Trump was fingerprinted while in custody, like any other defendant, he was not handcuffed, nor did he have his mugshot taken. Still, his campaign team is selling $36 T-shirts with a fake booking photo (one that embellishes his height by two inches and his face with a soft-focus halo).\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will be monitoring and fact-checking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech here on the liveblog.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230404ej44002uy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
