\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pleads not guilty to 34 charges in New York hush money case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Joanna Walters in New York (now), Joan E Greve and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 10,610 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2023\par 23:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former president charged with falsifying business recordsThe charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 full text of indictmentTrump arraigned: what that means and what happens next\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 After a huge day in Manhattan, it\u8217\'20\'19s now time to turn attention to Florida, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just landed after his appearance in court in New York. The former US president is giving a speech there, due at 8.15pm ET and we are launching an entirely new live blog now, in the run-up and to cover the event.\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, here\u8217\'20\'19s how the day went:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plane just landed in Florida and he is making his way back to his Mar-a-Lago home in Palm Beach.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1643344479733317632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left New York}}}\uc2  shortly before 5pm local time after surrendering to authorities and pleading not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records in the first degree.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  held a press conference confirming that Trump faces 34 felony counts of falsifying business records \u8220\'20\'1Cwith intent to defraud and intent to conceal another crime\u8221\'20\'1D and adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthese are felony crimes in New York state, no matter who you are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bragg proposed a trial start date of January 2024, weeks before voting begins in the Republican presidential primary. The judge presiding over the case, Juan Merchan, will likely provide some clarity on the schedule at the next in-person hearing in December.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump did not speak to reporters upon leaving court, having pleaded not guilty to the charges against him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just landed back in Florida. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the afternoon from Reuters:\par \par \uc2 The former US president pleaded not guilty in a history-making moment on Tuesday to 34 felony counts of falsifying business records, as prosecutors accused him of orchestrating payments to two women before the 2016 US election to suppress publication of their sexual encounters with him.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors in Manhattan allege that Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the first sitting or former US president to face criminal charges \u8211\'20\'13 falsified business records to conceal a violation of election laws during his successful 2016 campaign.\par \par \uc2 The two women were adult film actress Stormy Daniels and former Playboy model Karen McDougal.\par \par \uc2 Wearing a dark blue suit and red tie, Trump sat, subdued, with his hands folded at the defense table as he entered his plea flanked by his lawyers. \u8220\'20\'1CNot guilty,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump, 76, said when asked how he pleaded.\par \par \uc2 The front-runner in the race for the Republican nomination in 2024, Trump responded with answers like \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D when the judge asked him if he understood a right. At one point, the judge put his hand to his ear as if to prompt an answer.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor Chris Conroy said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  falsified New York business records in order to conceal an illegal conspiracy to undermine the integrity of the 2016 presidential election and other violations of election laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although falsifying business records in New York on its own is a misdemeanor punishable by no more than one year in prison, it is elevated to a felony punishable by up to four years when done to advance or conceal another crime, such as election law violations.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors during the arraignment said Trump made a series of threatening social media posts, including one threatening \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he was charged. The judge asked the parties to \u8220\'20\'1Cplease refrain from making statements that are likely to incite violence or civil unrest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump said nothing as he entered the courtroom or when he left roughly an hour later.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrives in New York criminal court for his arraignment on 4 April. Photograph: John Lamparski/NurPhoto/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 George Conway, the prominent anti-Trump Republican lawyer who is in the process of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/04/kellyanne-conway-george-conway-divorce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 untangling himself}}}\uc2  from the Washington power couple that was the Conways \u8211\'20\'13 George and senior aide to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Kellyanne Conway \u8211\'20\'13 has been cheekily tweeting.\par \par \uc2 His choice of clips speak for themselves.\par \par \uc2 enltrHow it started \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/r6Tmko4Qke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/r6Tmko4Qke}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Conway?? (@gtconway3d) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gtconway3d/status/1643377045618008070?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHow it\u8217\'20\'19s going \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sXrmkMEPQO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sXrmkMEPQO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Conway?? (@gtconway3d) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gtconway3d/status/1643377051821326342?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told Britain\u8217\'20\'19s King Charles in a phone call a little earlier today that first lady Jill Biden will attend the king\u8217\'20\'19s 6 May coronation, the White House said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The US president is not attending the coronation in London.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s absence was rumored last month after an anonymous White House official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6260313/biden-king-charles-coronation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Time}}}\uc2  that the coronation did \u8220\'20\'1Cnot feel like an event \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will attend\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/prince-charles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charles}}}\uc2  became king following the death of his mother, Queen Elizabeth II, in September.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth ruled for more than 70 years, becoming the longest-serving monarch in British history.\par \par \uc2 A little more from my colleague Gloria Oladipo this morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/03/joe-biden-king-charles-coronation-may"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told King Charles that first lady Jill Biden will attend the king\u8217\'20\'19s 6 May coronation. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 This historic day in US politics is not over \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is landing back in Florida soon and is going to make a speech at his Mar-a-Lago home in Palm Beach later this evening, where invitees are beginning to gather in the twinkly ballroom.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s fresh from pleading not guilty to 34 felony counts in criminal court in New York City, his birthplace and the metropolis where he made his name and fortune, before embarking on one of the wildest political ascendancies America has ever seen.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to launch a dedicated live blog when this one closes, at the top of the hour and will then be ready to cover the evening event as it happens.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be reporting points from the speech, with some checks and context, but we have decided not to live stream the speech, so as to avoid pumping any lies and incendiary, threatening language that might be included directly out to the public in this forum.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to return to his Mar-a-Lago estate in Palm Beach, Florida, after being arraigned in New York City. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 A clip of the highlights of Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s press conference earlier, held at the courthouse where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had just pleaded not guilty to 34 charges of falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 As Bragg alleges, the fiddling of the business records was \u8220\'20\'1Cmade to cover up other crimes. These are felony crimes in New York state, no matter who you are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prosecutor alleges that, among other things, the fiddled records were meant to conceal state election financing crimes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House slams Tennessee Republicans over gun safety politics\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Tennessee who are taking action to kick out Democratic rivals because they joined a protest against gun violence after another horrific school shooting are \u8220\'20\'1Cshrugging in the face\u8221\'20\'1D of the tragedy, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said earlier today at the daily media briefing, in Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans introduced three resolutions to expel Democratic state representatives Gloria Johnson, Justin Jones and Justin Pearson four days after the protest. The chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leadership also compared the gun control protest to an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Expelling a house member is an extremely rare occurrence, with only two of the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s members removed since the civil war.\par \par \uc2 The three have already been stripped of their committee assignments as more sanctions are expected, according to the Tennessee house speaker, Cameron Sexton.\par \par \uc2 At the press briefing in the west wing moments ago, Jean-Pierre slammed the actions by the Republicans.\par \par \uc2 enltrMore from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  on Tennessee Republican lawmakers seeking to expel three Democrats: "By doing what they're doing with these three Democratic legislators, they're shrugging in the face of yet another tragic school shooting while our kids continue to pay the price."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joey Garrison (@joeygarrison) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joeygarrison/status/1643307519954001944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 A shooter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gunned down}}}\uc2  three nine-year-olds and three adult staff at a private elementary school in Nashville, Tennessee, late last month.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Jean-Pierre found several different ways to rebuff requests for comment from the White House on the criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in New York, just moments after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s predecessor arrived at the criminal court in lower Manhattan and in a few moments will appear in court to hear charges unsealed after last week\u8217\'20\'19s indictment.\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  speaks during a press briefing at the White House in Washington, DC, USA, 04 April 2023. Photograph: Yuri Gripas/ABACA/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , one of seven Republican senators who voted to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for inciting the deadly January 6 insurrection in 2021, criticized the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office over its handling of the hush-money case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s character and conduct make him unfit for office. Even so, I believe the New York prosecutor has stretched to reach felony criminal charges in order to fit a political agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Romney said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.romney.senate.gov/romney-statement-on-indictment-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is above the law, not even former presidents, but everyone is entitled to equal treatment under the law. The prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s overreach sets a dangerous precedent for criminalizing political opponents and damages the public\u8217\'20\'19s faith in our justice system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At his press conference this afternoon, the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , argued his office was obligated to pursue the case because investigators collected evidence indicating illegal activity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe today uphold our solemn responsibility to ensure that everyone stands equal before the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo amount of money, no amount of power changes that enduring American principle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump begins trip back to Florida\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1643344479733317632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left New York}}}\uc2  after surrendering to authorities and pleading not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records in the first degree.\par \par \uc2 Trump will soon return to Florida, where he will deliver remarks on the charges he faces at his Mar-a-Lago resort at 8.15pm ET.\par \par \uc2 In a fundraising email to supporters sent moments ago, Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we are living through the darkest hours of American history, I can say that at least for this moment right now, I am in great spirits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then asked his supporters to consider contributing to his 2024 presidential campaign, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI have never been more certain that we will win back the White House and save our Great Nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle leaves court in Manhattan. Photograph: Xinhua/Rex/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 At his press conference, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  asserted that the scheme to pay hush money to adult film star Stormy Daniels to suppress the story of her alleged affair with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ran afoul of multiple laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe scheme violated New York election law, which makes it a crime to conspire to promote a candidacy by unlawful means,\u8221\'20\'1D the Manhattan district attorney said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 130,000 dollar wire payment exceeded the federal campaign contribution cap, and the false statements in [\uc2 American Media Inc\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s] books violated New York law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , took several questions from reporters after delivering his prepared remarks on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s indictment over hush-money payments.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the timing of the indictment, Bragg said, \u8220\'20\'1CI bring cases when they\u8217\'20\'19re ready. Having now conducted a rigorous, thorough investigation, the case was ready to be brought, and it was brought.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another reporter noted that Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor declined to pursue charges against Trump in this case and asked why the district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office decided to do so now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have had available to the office additional evidence that was not in the office\u8217\'20\'19s possession prior to my time here,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , argued his office was obligated to pursue the case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  regardless of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s reputation and resources.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe today uphold our solemn responsibility to ensure that everyone stands equal before the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg said at his press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CNo amount of money, no amount of power changes that enduring American principle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his lawyers have accused the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , of overstating the significance of the allegations against the former president.\par \par \uc2 At his press conference, Bragg emphasized that the charges filed against Trump reflect the serious importance of ensuring business is conducted in a lawful manner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrue and accurate business records are important everywhere to be sure,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are all the more important in Manhattan, the financial center of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 'We cannot and will not normalize serious criminal conduct,' Bragg says\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , is now holding a press conference to discuss the 34 charges filed against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bragg confirmed that Trump faces 34 felony counts of falsifying business records \u8220\'20\'1Cwith intent to defraud and intent to conceal another crime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot and will not normalize serious criminal conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D Bragg said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , will soon hold a press conference to discuss the 34 charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the hush money case.\par \par \uc2 As reporters prepared for Bragg to arrive, photographers took photos of two posters set up next to the podium, which outlined the charges that Trump has pleaded not guilty to.\par \par \uc2 One poster was labeled, \u8220\'20\'1CCatch and kill scheme to influence the 2016 election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the arraignment, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal team suggested that it may be more realistic to begin the trial in spring 2024, according to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell, who is in New York:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Trump lawyers said in court that they thought Spring 2024 trial date is more realistic than Manhattan prosecutors suggested trial start in Jan. 2024 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump due back in court Dec. 4 when Merchan likely to rule on expected motion to dismiss and others.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1643343487608209414?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , has proposed a trial start date of January 2024, weeks before voting begins in the Republican presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 The judge presiding over the case, Juan Merchan, will likely provide some clarity on the schedule at the next in-person hearing in December. At that point, Merchan will also likely rule on the expected motion to dismiss from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to multiple reports, the next in-person hearing in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case will be held in December, and a trial would not start until January 2024 at the earliest.\par \par \uc2 That schedule means Trump may be asked to appear in court just as voting begins in the 2024 Republican presidential primary, as the 2024 Iowa caucuses are scheduled to take place on 5 February.\par \par \uc2 As of now, Trump remains the frontrunner to win the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney office\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manhattanda.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Donald-J.-Trump-SOF.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement of facts}}}\uc2  regarding the indictment alleges that the parent company of the National Enquirer, \uc2 American Media Inc\uc2 , paid off a woman who claimed to have had a sexual relationship with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAMI ultimately paid $150,000 to Woman 1 in exchange for her agreement not to speak out about the alleged sexual relationship, as well as for two magazine cover features of Woman 1 and a series of articles that would be published under her byline,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement of facts says. \u8220\'20\'1CAMI falsely characterized this payment in AMI\u8217\'20\'19s books and records, including in its general ledger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That woman is believed to be Karen McDougal, a former Playboy model who says she had an extramarital affair with Trump. The Wall Street Journal reported last week that the grand jury was hearing evidence about the financial transaction with McDougal, as well as the hush-money payments to Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to the statement of facts from the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, the parent company of the National Enquirer, \uc2 American Media, Inc\uc2 , at one point bought a story about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fathering a child out of wedlock.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[I]n or about October or November 2015, the AMI CEO learned that a former Trump Tower doorman (the \u8216\'20\'18Doorman\u8217\'20\'19) was trying to sell information regarding a child that the Defendant had allegedly fathered out of wedlock,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement of facts reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the AMI CEO\u8217\'20\'19s 4 direction, AMI negotiated and signed an agreement to pay the Doorman $30,000 to acquire exclusive rights to the story. AMI falsely characterized this payment in AMI\u8217\'20\'19s books and records, including in its general ledger. AMI purchased the information from the Doorman without fully investigating his claims, but the AMI CEO directed that the deal take place because of his agreement with the Defendant and Lawyer A.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manhattanda.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Donald-J.-Trump-SOF.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its statement of facts}}}\uc2  regarding the indictment, the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office accuses Trump of having \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly and fraudulently falsified New York business records to conceal criminal conduct that hid damaging information from the voting public during the 2016 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom August 2015 to December 2017, the Defendant orchestrated a scheme with others to influence the 2016 presidential election by identifying and purchasing negative information about him to suppress its publication and benefit the Defendant\u8217\'20\'19s electoral prospects,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement of facts reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to execute the unlawful scheme, the participants violated election laws and made and caused false entries in the business records of various entities in New York.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump indictment released as Bragg holds press conference\par \par \uc2 The full indictment outlining the charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been unsealed, and it can be read {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manhattanda.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Donald-J.-Trump-Indictment.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The indictment shows that the former president is facing 34 counts of falsifying business records in the first degree, which is a class E felony in the state of New York.\par \par \uc2 Trump has pleaded not guilty to the charges, and the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , is just about to kick off his press conference to discuss today\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump leaves courthouse without speaking to reporters\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just left the Manhattan criminal court, about two hours after arriving there to be arrested and arraigned over charges linked to a 2016 hush-money scheme.\par \par \uc2 The former president once again declined to speak to reporters as he left the courthouse, ignoring shouted questions about how he pleaded in the case. Multiple outlets have reported that Trump pleaded not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records in the first degree.\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , will soon hold a press conference to discuss the arraignment. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York law classifies falsifying business records in the first degree as a class E felony, which is the lowest level of felony charges in the state.\par \par \uc2 Now that Trump has been arraigned, the indictment approved by a New York grand jury last week can be publicly unsealed, offering more details on the exact charges the former president is facing. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await more details on the 34 counts that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is reportedly facing, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with his Council of Advisors on Science and Technology.\par \par \uc2 Reporters tried to ask Biden for his thoughts on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment, but the president once again declined to comment on his predecessor\u8217\'20\'19s legal challenges, per CBS News.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen asked by reporters if he thinks AI is dangerous, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1CIt remains to be seen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When I asked if the Trump indictment is politically divisive, Biden smiled and laughed.\par \par \uc2 He did not answer questions about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WSJ}}}\uc2  reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/EvanGershkovich?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #EvanGershkovich}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1643329006341615619?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump pleads not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has officially entered a plea of not guilty to 34 counts of falsifying business records in the first degree in connection a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president may speak to reporters after leaving the courtroom, and the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , plans to soon hold a press conference. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some of the first photographs of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sitting in the Manhattan courtroom are now being released. The former president is seen sitting at the defense table with his legal team.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sits at the defense table with his defense team in a Manhattan court. Photograph: Seth Wenig/AP\par \par \uc2 The judge presiding over the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  supreme court Justice Juan Merchan, issued a ruling late last night that only a handful of still photographers would be allowed to take pictures inside the room. No electronic devices are allowed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump in courtroom to be arraigned\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was seen entering the courtroom where he will now be arraigned for charges linked to a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 The former president offered no comment to reporters as he entered the courtroom. He is expected to plead not guilty to all charges.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  makes his way into the courtroom. Photograph: Ed Jones/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 '\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will have a fair trial,' Schumer says\par \par \uc2 Moments before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s arraignment is expected to begin, the Democratic Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , expressed confidence that the former president will receive a fair trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will have a fair trial that follows the facts and the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 enltrI believe that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will have a fair trial that follows the facts and the law. There\u8217\'20\'19s no place in our justice system for any outside influence or intimidation in the legal process. As the trial proceeds, protest is an American right, but all protests must be peaceful.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1643316384246407169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no place in our justice system for any outside influence or intimidation in the legal process. As the trial proceeds, protest is an American right, but all protests must be peaceful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is currently under arrest at the Manhattan criminal court, where he is expected to soon plead not guilty to all the charges he faces. Schumer is one of two Democratic senators who represent the state of New York.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House aides also described the experience of watching him surrender to New York authorities as \u8220\'20\'1Csurreal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alyssa Farah Griffin, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House director of strategic communications who has severely criticized the former president over his role in the deadly January 6 insurrection, said Trump is now \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most alone [he] has been in a long time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not flanked by aides, lawyers, body men & so on,\u8221\'20\'1D Griffin said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s face to face with the American legal system that has caught up with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSurreal to watch. This is the most alone Trump has been in a long time. He\u8217\'20\'19s not flanked by aides, lawyers, body men & so on. He\u8217\'20\'19s face to face with the American legal system that has caught up with him.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alyssa Farah Griffin (@Alyssafarah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Alyssafarah/status/1643308607474114565?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Moments before starting his trip to the Manhattan criminal court, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shared a rather obvious message with his followers on the social media platform Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHeading to Lower Manhattan, the Courthouse. Seems so SURREAL \u8211\'20\'13 WOW, they are going to ARREST ME,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CCan\u8217\'20\'19t believe this is happening in America. MAGA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has already used his Truth Social account to repeatedly attack Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , whose office oversaw the hush-money investigation.\par \par \uc2 The former president will likely double down on those attacks tonight, when he delivers remarks at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida at 8.15pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  waved to the assembled crowd as he arrived at the Manhattan courthouse where he has been arrested and will soon be arraigned.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of journalists, security personnel and protesters have gathered outside the Manhattan criminal court to witness the unprecedented spectacle of a former US president surrendering himself to authorities.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  waves to the crowd as he arrives at the Manhattan Criminal Courthouse for his arraignment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4pEJuMWIoU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4pEJuMWIoU}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pgyyatQXXy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pgyyatQXXy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1643304676559839275?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump under arrest in New York \u8211\'20\'13 what we know so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now under arrest at the Manhattan courthouse where he will soon be arraigned for charges linked to a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment is scheduled for 2.15pm ET at the Manhattan criminal court. At the arraignment, Trump is expected to plead not guilty to all charges linked to hush-money payments to adult film star Stormy Daniels, who claims to have had an affair with the former president. After the arraignment, Trump will likely be allowed to return home to Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York authorities will process Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrest, and they are expected to fingerprint the former president. But it remains unclear whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mug shot will be taken, and it appears he will not be put in handcuffs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to deliver remarks at his Mar-a-Lago resort at 8.15pm ET. The former president has already aggressively dismissed any suggestion of wrongdoing on his part, and he will likely only intensify his attacks on prosecutors after being arraigned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No electronic devices will be allowed in the courtroom. The judge overseeing the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  supreme court Justice Juan Merchan, issued a ruling late last night that only a handful of still photographers would be allowed to take pictures inside the room.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Reporters lined up outside the courthouse overnight in the hopes of getting a seat in the arraignment room. Several dozen reporters are expected to be allowed inside the room to witness the unprecedented event of a former US president formally responding to criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A trial may still be months away. Once Trump enters his initial plea, Merchan will likely set a schedule for pre-trial hearings, but it may take several months for the actual trial to begin.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at Manhattan courthouse for arraignment\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived at the Manhattan courthouse where he will soon be arraigned on charges linked to a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Before the arraignment begins at 2.15pm ET, Trump will be formally arrested and processed by New York authorities. He is expected to be fingerprinted, but it is unclear whether he will have his mug shot taken.\par \par \uc2 At the arraignment, Trump is expected to plead not guilty to all charges, and the judge presiding over the case, New York supreme court Justice Juan Merchan, will then likely allow the former president to return home to Florida.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more details coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he left Trump Tower to make his way to the Manhattan courthouse where he will be arraigned, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  raised a fist to supporters waiting outside.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leaves Trump Tower in New York. Photograph: Bryan Woolston/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump leaves Trump Tower for arraignment\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has left Trump Tower to make the short trip to the Manhattan courthouse where he will be arraigned at 2.15pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Cameras captured the former president\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade traveling the four miles between Trump Tower and 100 Centre St, where an entrance has already been cleared for his arrival.\par \par \uc2 When he arrives, Trump will be formally arrested, fingerprinted and processed before appearing at his arraignment, where he is expected to plead not guilty to all charges. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 We expect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to depart his New York home on Fifth Avenue very soon and start to make his way to the criminal courthouse in lower Manhattan. He\u8217\'20\'19s due to appear in court a little later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court has rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request to block senior aides of his, while he was president, from testifying to special counsel Jack Smith in the federal criminal inquiries into the now candidate for the Republican nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters in Wisconsin are casting ballots today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/13/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-gerrymandered-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the most important elections}}}\uc2  of 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a contest that will determine the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyerJoe Tacopina has been on television and said the former president wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t plead guilty to lesser charges, even if it could resolve the case.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will be arraigned at 2.15pm ET at a courthouse in lower Manhattan. At the arraignment, Trump is expected to plead not guilty to all charges linked to his involvement in a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election. After the arraignment, Trump will likely be allowed to return home to Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to be arrested and processed shortly before his arraignment. As part of his arrest, Trump will be fingerprinted and likely photographed, but his lawyer has said he does not expect Trump to be handcuffed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to deliver remarks at his Mar-a-Lago resort at 8.15pm ET. The former president has already aggressively dismissed any suggestion of wrongdoing on his part, and he will likely only intensify his attacks on prosecutors after being arraigned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Court rejects Trump bid to stop top aides testifying to special counsel - reports\par \par \uc2 Media reports coming in that a federal appeals court has rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request to block senior aides of his while he was president from testifying to special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 Smith is the special counsel appointed by the Department of Justice last year who is helming investigations into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged hiding of classified documents at Mar-a-Lago and role in fomenting the attack on the US Capitol on January 6, 2021, when extremist supporters tried to stop Congress certifying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory over Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: A federal appeals court panel has rejected Trump's bid to block top aides from testifying to special counsel Jack Smith's Jan. 6 investigation.\par \par \uc2 Several close Trump advisers are the subject of this order, which was part of a rushed series of overnight filings. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bFiNsXLNpy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bFiNsXLNpy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1643286993869189123?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And this:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: A federal appeals court panel just rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to prevent top aides & advisors from testifying to Special Counsel Jack Smith. More bad news for Trump & more evidence that if you mess with Jack Smith, you will lose.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victor Shi (@Victorshi2020) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Victorshi2020/status/1643288236318687233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s one opinion:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump's federal trial could not come soon enough. It should have started two years ago. GOP would not have won the House if Trump & GOP co-conspirators like Greene, Gosar, Gaetz & Boebert were held criminally accountable for Jan 6 failed coup attempt.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Greenberg (@JournalistJG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JournalistJG/status/1643295354618793984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrived in New York yesterday he entered his Trump Tower skyscraper alone, with his wife, Melania, noticeably absent.\par \par \uc2 Now there are some reports that she just turned up, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you any other news on that as it emerges.\par \par \uc2 enltrMelania Trump seen arriving at Trump Towers in New York City ???\par \par \uc2 ?? Insiders recently claim that the Trumps could be heading for divorce. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MelaniaTrump?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MelaniaTrump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TrumpArraignment?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TrumpArraignment}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TrumpIndictment?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TrumpIndictment}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7ubSsiGGYa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7ubSsiGGYa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MirrorUSNews (@MirrorUSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MirrorUSNews/status/1643291476929961997?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outside the criminal court building in lower Manhattan, handfuls of protesters and a scrum of media are in a brief news vacuum as they await the arrival of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president has not left Trump Tower uptown on Fifth Avenue yet, despite some reports that he would surrender to the authorities downtown at 11am. So we wait.\par \par \uc2 In true New York City style, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of scaffolding around, a mix of poles and roughly painted wooden panels that ends up casting shade, trapping garbage, hindering navigation on the sidewalk and giving the location an even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidmackau/status/1643230745807265792"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less salubrious}}}\uc2  environment than usual.\par \par \uc2 The interior of the building is not exactly cathedral-like splendor, either. For defendants it\u8217\'20\'19s generally a sobering and dispiriting experience to be arraigned here \u8211\'20\'13 an arraignment being the first appearance in front of a judge after being arrested or surrendering to authorities, to hear the criminal charges against you.\par \par \uc2 The scene is colorful and a little chaotic.\par \par \uc2 enltrA \u8220\'20\'1CTrump or Death\u8221\'20\'1D flag. Who says it\u8217\'20\'19s not a cult? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Trump?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Trump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TrumpArraignment?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TrumpArraignment}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lvzX2LcwQl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lvzX2LcwQl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Corn (@DavidCornDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidCornDC/status/1643259589129916416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CHillary\u8221\'20\'1D and a fan.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CAll this is just a big show,\u8221\'20\'1D Gregory Williams, a 57-year-old Bronx resident, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nateschweber?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nateschweber}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI got the popcorn. This is American theater at its best.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sxYMW978uT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sxYMW978uT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j4Knz3XJ0B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/j4Knz3XJ0B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nick Confessore (@nickconfessore) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nickconfessore/status/1643260808758013952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Protesters:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnti-Trump protesters being kept separate from Trumpers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TrumpArraignment?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TrumpArraignment}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bVhi1tX5UW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bVhi1tX5UW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Corn (@DavidCornDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidCornDC/status/1643260523985747970?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Protesters:\par \par \uc2 enltrPolice seem to have separated pro and anti-Trump protesters here in front of the court house. Both sides yelling at each other, chanting etc {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9yANVxsObn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9yANVxsObn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shelby Talcott (@ShelbyTalcott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShelbyTalcott/status/1643274895919284228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine is on the ground in Wisconsin, where voters are heading to the polls to choose the newest member of the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The court is expected to soon weigh in on whether an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban dating back to 1849 should be enforced after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled to overturn Roe v Wade last summer.\par \par \uc2 And \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access appears to be weighing heavily on the minds of Wisconsin voters as they cast their ballots today:\par \par \uc2 enltrVoters are pouring in at a steady clip at a polling place in Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin this morning. Every voter I spoke with pointed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their number 1 issue in today\u8217\'20\'19s state Supreme Court race\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1643278437631635457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters have gathered outside the Manhattan courthouse where he will be arraigned this afternoon, but a handful of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s critics are also on the scene.\par \par \uc2 One anti-Trump protester was photographed holding a sign that read: \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D During the 2016 presidential campaign, Trump rally attendees frequently chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CLock her up!\u8221\'20\'1D in reference to Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  over her mishandling of sensitive government emails.\par \par \uc2 Anti-Trump protesters demonstrate outside Manhattan Criminal Courthouse. Photograph: Amanda Perobelli/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Another anti-Trump protester held a sign reading, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump 4 Prison\u8221\'20\'1D. As of now, Trump is still the frontrunner in the 2024 Republican presidential primary, and the indictment does not prevent him from seeking office.\par \par \uc2 An anti-Trump protester holds a sign outside Manhattan Criminal Courthouse. Photograph: Amanda Perobelli/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will get his mug shot taken when he is processed by New York authorities today, but one new report suggests he will not.\par \par \uc2 Yahoo News\u8217\'20\'19 Michael Isikoff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/exclusive-trump-to-be-charged-tuesday-with-34-felony-counts-but-spared-handcuffs-and-mug-shot-001241750.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported yesterday}}}\uc2  that Trump has been charged with 34 felony counts for falsification of business records, and noted that the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office had decided against getting a mug shot of the former president:\par \par \uc2 [One] source said, Trump will not be put in handcuffs, placed in a jail cell or subjected to a mug shot \u8211\'20\'13 typical procedures even for white-collar defendants until a judge has weighed in on pretrial conditions. Manhattan District Attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office, which has been consulting with the Secret Service and New York City court officials, concluded there was no reason to subject the former president to handcuffs or a mug shot.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/trump-wants-to-be-handcuffed-for-court-appearance-in-stormy-daniels-case-sources-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2  that Trump hoped to be handcuffed because he wanted to turn the arrest and arraignment into a \u8220\'20\'1Cspectacle\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  of New York was spotted outside the courthouse where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be arraigned this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Bowman told Semafor that he felt compelled to make an appearance because he wanted to push back against the rhetoric he\u8217\'20\'19s heard from one of his House colleagues, far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe should not be here,\u8221\'20\'1D Bowman told Semafor\u8217\'20\'19s Kadia Goba. \u8220\'20\'1CShe should not be pushing rhetoric that is harmful and dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSpoke to Rep. \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  earlier who said he came out to push back in against Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe should not be here and she should not be pushing rhetoric that is harmful and dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K3r4GDx7MM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/K3r4GDx7MM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kadia Goba (@kadiagoba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kadiagoba/status/1643269129137258496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin voters cast ballots in one of the year's most important elections\par \par \uc2 Voters in Wisconsin are casting ballots today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/13/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-gerrymandered-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the most important elections}}}\uc2  of 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a contest that will determine the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The court will probably determine the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wisconsin and it is also poised to play a hugely consequential role in setting election rules for the 2024 presidential election in the critical battleground state.\par \par \uc2 The race is the most expensive judicial race in American history. More than $45m has been spent, shattering the $10m record that was spent in Wisconsin in 2020 as well as the national record $15m spent on an Illinois race in 2004.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine and Alice Herman are on the ground in Wisconsin talking to voters throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 enltrPolls are open in Wisconsin! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E8vb8x32Dk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/E8vb8x32Dk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alice Herman (@aliceraeherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aliceraeherman/status/1643262827946287108?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has arrived at a pro-Trump rally near the Manhattan courthouse where he will be arraigned this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of reporters swarmed around Greene as she arrived, and journalists appeared to far outnumber attendees at the rally.\par \par \uc2 Jess Bidgood, a reporter for the \uc2 Boston Globe\uc2 , joked, \u8220\'20\'1CI would estimate a 1,000: 1 reporter to protester ratio here at the \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  rally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI would estimate a 1,000: 1 reporter to protester ratio here at the \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WlcPzQvo1S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WlcPzQvo1S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jess Bidgood (@jessbidgood) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jessbidgood/status/1643262522433196033?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Although much of today\u8217\'20\'19s news cycle is focused on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s arraignment, there are other major developments happening today in both domestic and international news.\par \par \uc2 On the domestic front, Wisconsin and Chicago will hold crucial elections today. Wisconsin voters will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 head to the polls}}}\uc2  to choose a new member of the state supreme court, after a conservative judge stepped down. If liberal judge Janet Protasiewicz wins the race, she could flip majority control of the court.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Chicago voters will choose their next mayor, after incumbent Democrat \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  failed to qualify for today\u8217\'20\'19s runoff race.\par \par \uc2 In major international news, Finland has formally joined \uc2 Nato\uc2 , becoming the 31st member of the alliance. The Finnish flag was raised outside the Nato headquarters in Brussels, Belgium, earlier today:\par \par \uc2 enltrFinland's flag is raised at \uc2 NATO\uc2  headquarters in Brussels as it officially becomes a member of \uc2 NATO\uc2 . Finland is now the 31st member of \uc2 NATO\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fE9D6LvFFQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fE9D6LvFFQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1643256997578514433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arraignment will get under way soon\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s arraignment is scheduled to take place in a few hours. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will be arraigned at 2.15pm ET at a courthouse in lower Manhattan. At the arraignment, Trump is expected to plead not guilty to all charges linked to his involvement in a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election. After the arraignment, Trump will likely be allowed to return home to Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to be arrested and processed shortly before his arraignment. As part of his arrest, Trump will be fingerprinted and likely photographed, but his lawyer has said he does not expect Trump to be handcuffed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to deliver remarks at his Mar-a-Lago resort at 8.15pm ET. The former president has already aggressively dismissed any suggestion of wrongdoing on his part, and he will likely only intensify his attacks on prosecutors after being arraigned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No electronic devices will be allowed in the courtroom. The judge overseeing the case, New York supreme court Justice Juan Merchan, issued a ruling late last night that only a handful of still photographers would be allowed to take pictures inside the room.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Reporters lined up outside the courthouse overnight in the hopes of getting a seat in the arraignment room. Several dozen reporters are expected to be allowed inside the room to witness the unprecedented event of a former US president formally responding to criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A trial may still be months away. Once Trump enters his initial plea, Merchan will likely set a schedule for pre-trial hearings, but it may take several months for the actual trial to begin.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressman George Santos, the Republican who has faced widespread criticism for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/02/house-ethics-committee-george-santos-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misrepresenting}}}\uc2  seemingly every aspect of his resume and biography, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GrahamKates/status/1643247275785822211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been spotted}}}\uc2  outside the courthouse in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 Reports indicate that \uc2 Santos\uc2  plans to attend the nearby pro-Trump rally being held by the New York Young Republican Club, where far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is expected to speak.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reporters have waited for hours outside the courthouse in lower Manhattan, hoping to get a seat in the room where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be arraigned this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 But not everyone near the courthouse is particularly interested in the unprecedented event of a former US president facing criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 Reporter Soo Youn, a Guardian contributor, shared this photo of a couple getting married next door to the courthouse this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning from downtown Manhattan where this lovely couple is getting married right next door to the media scrum waiting for the Trump indictment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vJxcxZDgKX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vJxcxZDgKX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Soo Youn (@lalasoo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lalasoo/status/1643235754389168130?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 This is Joan E Greve in Washington, taking over for Martin Belam. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will soon appear at an arraignment in Manhattan, where he will formally respond to charges over his involvement in a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Joe Tacopina, has indicated the former president will plead not guilty to all charges, and he will then likely be allowed to return to his home in Florida. Trump plans to deliver a speech defending himself at his Mar-a-Lago resort this evening.\par \par \uc2 The live blog will have updates and analysis as the arraignment gets underway, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyer says former president won't consider plea deal\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Joe Tacopina has been on television and said the former president wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t plead guilty to lesser charges, even if it could resolve the case.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press report he said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe the case would ever make it to a jury, but he conceded: \u8220\'20\'1CReally, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of mystery here because we\u8217\'20\'19re doing something that\u8217\'20\'19s never been done before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there will be a typical processing, which does not take long, 20-30 minutes. There won\u8217\'20\'19t be handcuffs,\u8221\'20\'1D Tacopina told ABC\u8217\'20\'19s Good Morning America. \u8220\'20\'1CBut, yeah, he\u8217\'20\'19ll be processed the way anyone else would be \u8211\'20\'13 to a degree.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 From hush money news to criminal court: brief timeline\par \par \uc2 Here is a reminder, courtesy of Reuters, of the timeline of how we got to today:\par \par \uc2 January 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 The Wall Street Journal reports that Trump arranged a $130,000 payment to porn star Stormy Daniels in October 2016 to prevent her from discussing a sexual encounter she said she had with Trump in 2006. Trump has consistently denied having an affair with Daniels, whose real name is Stephanie Clifford.\par \par \uc2 February 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , a former private lawyer and fixer for Trump, says he paid Daniels using his own money and was not directed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s company or campaign to make the payment. He said Trump never reimbursed him for the payment. Cohen would later contradict both statements under oath, stating Trump did in fact direct him to make the payment and reimbursed him.\par \par \uc2 April 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 Trump, when asked by reporters if he knew about the payment to Daniels, responded, \u8220\'20\'1CNo.\u8221\'20\'1D Asked why Cohen made the payment, Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 May 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 In an ethics disclosure, Trump acknowledges reimbursing Cohen for the $130,000 paid for Daniels.\par \par \uc2 August 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 Cohen pleads guilty to criminal charges in Manhattan federal court, including campaign finance violations over the hush money payments. He testified that Trump directed him to make the payments \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the principal purpose of influencing the election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 August 2019 \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 , the Manhattan district attorney at the time, issues a subpoena to the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  for records of hush money payments.\par \par \uc2 July 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s office indicts the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and its top financial executive on tax fraud charges. Trump himself is not charged with a crime, and the indictment contains no references to hush money payments.\par \par \uc2 December 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 The Trump Organization\uc2  is found guilty of tax fraud after a trial in New York state court in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 January 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Having replaced Vance as district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office begins presenting evidence about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged role in the 2016 hush money payments to a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 March 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Manhattan prosecutors invite Trump to testify before the grand jury, which legal experts say is a sign an indictment could come soon. Cohen testifies before the grand jury.\par \par \uc2 18 March 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Trump says on his social media platform Truth Social that he expects to be arrested on 21 March and calls on his supporters to protest. A spokesperson for Trump said the former president had not been notified of any arrest.\par \par \uc2 23 March 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s office says Trump created a false expectation that he would be arrested, and tells Republican congressmen seeking communications, documents and testimony about the probe that they were interfering with an ongoing investigation.\par \par \uc2 24 March 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Trump warns of potential \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he is charged with a crime.\par \par \uc2 30 March 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 Media reports say Trump is indicted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Kaitlan Collins and Kristen Holmes report that sources close to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have said that the former president is keen to speak while in New York today, ahead of his already planned speech this evening. They write:\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is eager to speak publicly about his indictment, according to multiple people familiar with his thinking.\par \par \uc2 Though he is not scheduled to speak until he arrives at Mar-a-Lago tonight, Trump has weighed saying something while still in Manhattan. He had initially considered doing so outside the courthouse but decided against that because of security considerations.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear if he will talk while in New York, and advisers have urged him to hold off until he has the command of his own ballroom tonight, where hundreds of his supporters, surrogates and friends are expected to gather.\par \par \uc2 Advisers have warned Trump that any unplanned remarks put him at high risk of hurting his case. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago speech is expected to have legal eyes on it before he delivers it tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Hill this morning is carrying some quotes from Vin Weber, a Republican strategist and former member of the House Republican leadership. Weber is warning that the indictment of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sets a dangerous precedent.\par \par \uc2 He argues that the impeachment of \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  lowered the bar for what might be considered an impeachable offence, and that the Stormy Daniels hush money case is doing the same, and risks people attempting political prosecutions of their opponents in the future. He said:\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s bad for America, bad for the Republican Party and it\u8217\'20\'19s bad for the political system in our country. Once you start down this path, there\u8217\'20\'19s no way you\u8217\'20\'19re going to reverse it. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we saw with impeachment.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to see political prosecutions brought, some of them for meritorious reasons, some of them to advance the careers of the prosecutors. But all of this is harmful to America and our political process.\par \par \uc2 There are people in this vast country of ours who have less than sterling motivations and you want them to be inhibited by rules that we\u8217\'20\'19ve established, informal rules, that are designed to protect the whole system.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will not be making a hugely long journey from Trump Tower to court today. He is expected to appear at about 14.15 ET (18.15 GMT / 19.15 BST).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2023/04/trump_manhattan-zip/giv-134255a2CvV5Mypgb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 There are already some people on the streets waiting for the day to unfold.\par \par \uc2 Lucas Camp, of Astoria, holds a sign near Trump Tower. Photograph: Bryan Woolston/AP People, including members of the media, who had to wait in line overnight in an attempt to get a seat in the courtroom, queue outside of Manhattan Criminal Court in New York City on 4 April 2023. Photograph: Stefani Reynolds/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump arraignment is not the only big political story today. Chicago, the third largest city in the US, goes to the polls today for a mayoral run-off.\par \par \uc2 Leigh Giangreco reports from Chicago for the Guardian that the election pits two Democrats from the furthest ends of their party\u8217\'20\'19s spectrum against each other. Democrats across the country are watching to see if Brandon Johnson, a progressive who has previously supported the defund the police movement, will defeat Paul Vallas, who nabbed the endorsement of Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s police union and once described himself as a Republican.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/chicago-mayoral-election-polls-brandon-johnson-paul-vallas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago heads to polls in heated mayoral election}}}\par \par \uc2 Voters in Wisconsin are also casting ballots today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/13/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-gerrymandered-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  one of the most important elections}}}\uc2  of 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a contest that will determine the ideological balance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine writes that the court will likely determine the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wisconsin, as a lawsuit challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 ban is already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/legal-challenge-wisconsins-1849-abortion-ban-awaiting-its-day-court-where-does-case-stand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 winding its way}}}\uc2  through the courts. It is also poised to play a hugely consequential role in setting election rules for the 2024 presidential election in Wisconsin, a key battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Janet Protasiewicz, a liberal Milwaukee judge, is facing off against Dan Kelly, a conservative who lost his seat on the supreme court in 2020. Conservatives currently have a 4-3 majority on the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, but one of its conservative justices is retiring, meaning that the outcome of the election will determine the ideological balance of the court.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin voters to cast ballots in crucial state supreme court election}}}\par \par \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2 , a former US secretary of labor, writes about Wisconsin for the Guardian today, saying:\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s criminal court is obviously important. Holding a former president accountable to the rule of law is essential.\par \par \uc2 But what\u8217\'20\'19s happening today in Wisconsin may prove as, if not more, important to the future of American democracy. It will either strengthen or weaken the levers of self-government in a state where those levers could make all the difference.\par \par \uc2 You can read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/robert-reich-opinion-wisconsin-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Reich \u8211\'20\'13 The most consequential politics story in the US isn\u8217\'20\'19t the Trump arraignment}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/robert-reich-opinion-wisconsin-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The most consequential politics story in the US isn\u8217\'20\'19t the Trump arraignment | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stephen Collinson at CNN offered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/04/04/politics/trump-legal-threats-analysis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this analysis}}}\uc2  earlier this morning, writing that today\u8217\'20\'19s courthouse appearance is not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s only woe:\par \par \uc2 The ex-president \u8211\'20\'13 the first to face criminal charges \u8211\'20\'13 also appears to face serious problems in a potentially more perilous case involving his alleged mishandling of secret documents being investigated by special counsel Jack Smith. Charges look like an increasing possibility as the Justice Department secures evidence about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents after leaving the White House.\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors have secured daily notes, texts, emails and photographs and are focused on cataloguing how Trump handled classified records around Mar-a-Lago and those who may have witnessed the former president with them. The new details coincide with signs the Justice Department is taking steps consistent with the end of an investigation.\par \par \uc2 Monday was a dark day for Trump. He was returning to his old stomping ground in Manhattan under duress, to turn himself in on Tuesday over the first-ever criminal charges ever laid against an ex-president. Trump has long been a force of nature who rebels against constraints and has always been impossible for his staff to control. But now he will be subject to the dictates of a judge and the rules and conventions of the legal system, which will be far harder for him to disrupt and divert than the institutions of political accountability he has subverted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Sidney Blumenthal, former senior adviser to President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , writes for the Guardian today, arguing that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-republicans-murdoch-koch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 every indictment will make Trump stronger \u8211\'20\'13 and Republicans wilder}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Between the motion of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first indictment and the act of the last Republican primary, more than a year from now, on 4 June 2024, the shadow will fall on the only party with an actual nomination contest. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pandemonium will only have an electoral valence for the foreseeable future in its precincts. His damage to the constitution, the national security of the United States and the rule of law will be extensive, but his most intense and focused political destruction will be circumscribed within the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 From the report of every new indictment to its reality, Republican radicalization will accelerate. Every concrete count will confirm every conspiracy theory. Every prosecution and trial, staggered over months and into the election year, from New York to Georgia to Washington, will be a shock driving Republicans further to Trump. Every Republican candidate running for every office will be compelled to declare as a matter of faith that Trump is being unjustly persecuted or be themselves branded traitors.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-republicans-murdoch-koch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sidney Blumenthal \u8211\'20\'13 Every indictment will make Trump stronger, and Republicans wilder}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-republicans-murdoch-koch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Every indictment will make Trump stronger \u8211\'20\'13 and Republicans wilder | Sidney Blumenthal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am BST\par \par \uc2 If you are still slightly confused as to what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has actually been charged with, you can be forgiven, since the precise details are yet to emerge. My colleague Joan E Greve has what we do know:\par \par \uc2 Why is Trump appearing in court?\par \par \uc2 A grand jury voted to indict Trump last Thursday over allegations that he illegally reimbursed his former attorney, \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , for a $130,000 payment to Stormy Daniels, an adult film star who claims to have had an extramarital affair with the former president beginning in 2006. Cohen paid Daniels in the final days before the 2016 presidential election, as she was preparing to go public with her story about the alleged affair. (Trump has said the affair never took place.)\par \par \uc2 Trump has acknowledged reimbursing Cohen, but he denies any illegal wrongdoing. The office of the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , has been investigating the matter for months, and Bragg confirmed on Thursday that he was working with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team to coordinate his surrender.\par \par \uc2 What charges is Trump facing?\par \par \uc2 That remains unclear. As of Tuesday morning, the indictment remains under seal, but the document will probably be released to the public after Trump is formally arrested and appears at his arraignment.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-arrested-news-updates-indictment-counts-new-york-rcna77595"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 , Trump is facing about 30 charges related to document fraud in the hush-money scheme. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Joe Tacopina, has already started challenging the charges, accusing Bragg of having \u8220\'20\'1Ctaken a misdemeanor and tried, cobbled together, to make it a felony by alleging a violation of federal campaign violations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Joan E Greve\u8217\'20\'19s explainer here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-arraignment-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump is being arraigned \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what that means and what happens next}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-arraignment-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump is being arraigned \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what that means and what happens next}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will make history this week as the first US president to be charged with a criminal offence. Ahead of this landmark moment, Hugo Lowell spoke to Michael Safi for our Today in Focus podcast and told him that once again, with Trump we are in uncharted territory. You can listen to the podcast here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2023/apr/04/the-indictment-of-donald-trump-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The indictment of Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am BST\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting that today\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings in Manhattan are expected to be relatively brief, and that being charged will not prevent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  running for the Republican nomination, or indeed the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Even a conviction would not prevent that, although the projected timeframe for the case is such that it may not even get back to court before the election in November 2024.\par \par \uc2 After today\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment, Trump is expected to be released by authorities because the charges against him don\u8217\'20\'19t require that bail be set.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press report that a demonstration of support is expected, and that New York\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Eric Adams, had a message for Trump fans heading to the city, saying on Monday \u8220\'20\'1CWhile there may be some rabble rousers thinking of coming to our city tomorrow, our message is clear and simple: Control yourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump pollster John McLaughlin said the former president would approach the day with \u8220\'20\'1Cdignity\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHe will be a gentleman,\u8221\'20\'1D McLaughlin said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19ll show strength and he\u8217\'20\'19ll show dignity and \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19ll get through this and win the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07am BST\par \par \uc2 If you missed it, here is what the former president\u8217\'20\'19s arrival at Trump Tower in New York yesterday ahead of today\u8217\'20\'19s courthouse appearance looked like:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 What we know so far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of what is set to be an historic day in US politics, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  due to appear in a New York courthouse as the first American president to be indicted on a criminal charge. Here is what we know so far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At about 14.15 ET (18.15 GMT / 19.15 BST) on Tuesday, he will appear at the courthouse where a grand jury convened by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  handed down its indictment last week, to learn the exact details of which laws he is alleged to have broken.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At his arraignment, he is expected to be photographed and fingerprinted, but will not be handcuffed per an agreement his legal team reached with Bragg, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Joe Tacopina said last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers opposed videography, photography and radio coverage of the arraignment, saying it would \u8220\'20\'1Cexacerbate an already almost circus-like atmosphere around this case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Late on Monday, Judge Juan Merchan ruled that five photographers would be admitted for several minutes before the arraignment, with TV cameras allowed only in the hallways of the building.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Important details of the case could be revealed before Trump sets foot in the courtroom. Media organizations have petitioned Merchan to make public Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s indictment, which reportedly contains upwards of 30 charges and at least one felony related to the hush money payment he facilitated to adult film star Stormy Daniels ahead of the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A protest by Trump supporters is expected to be held a few streets away from the Manhattan criminal court at noon ET (16.00 GMT / 17.00 BST).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to leave New York as soon as the hearing has finished, and has will deliver remarks at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Palm Beach, Florida, at 8.15pm ET (12.15am GMT / 1.15am BST). He may be limited in what he can say if the judge decides to issue a gag order on those involved in the case.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m Martin Belam in London, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest reaction as the day builds to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s court appearance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230404ej440015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
