\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida closes in on six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban while also allowing no-permit gun carry\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2023\par 12:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation needs to move through house before gaining DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s likely signature while gun-carry law enacted today\par \par \uc2 Florida took another step to the right on Monday when the state senate approved a bill to ban abortions after six weeks, a measure supported by Republican governor and expected presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who on the same day signed into law a bill allowing the public to carry concealed guns without a permit.\par \par \uc2 The latest proposal to restrict reproductive rights must still be approved by the house in the state legislature before it reaches the governor\u8217\'20\'19s desk. Florida currently prohibits abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 A six-week ban would more closely align Florida with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions of other Republican-controlled states and give DeSantis a political win on an issue important with GOP primary voters ahead of his potential White House run.\par \par \uc2 The bill would have larger implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access throughout the south, as the nearby states of Alabama, Louisiana and Mississippi prohibit the procedure at all stages of pregnancy and Georgia bans it after fetal cardiac activity can be detected, which is around six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the new weapons law will allow anyone who can legally own a gun in Florida to carry one without a permit. It means training and a background check will not be needed for people to carry concealed guns in public. The state now has nearly 3 million permit holders.\par \par \uc2 The bill signing came five years after then governor \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , also a Republican, signed a bill creating gun restrictions after 17 students and faculty {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were killed}}}\uc2  at Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school in Parkland in 2018.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction, Erin Grall, a Republican state senator who sponsored the bill, said: \u8220\'20\'1CBodily autonomy should not give a person the permission to kill an innocent human being. We live in a time where the consequences of our actions are an afterthought and convenience has been substitution for responsibility, and this is unacceptable when it comes to the protection of the most vulnerable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The proposal allows exceptions to save the life of the woman and exceptions in the case of pregnancy caused by rape or incest until 15 weeks of pregnancy. In those cases, a woman would have to provide documentation such as a medical record, restraining order or police report. DeSantis has called the rape and incest provisions sensible.\par \par \uc2 It would require that the drugs used in medication-induced abortions \u8211\'20\'13 which make up the majority of those provided nationally \u8211\'20\'13 could be dispensed only in person by a physician.\par \par \uc2 The new bill would only take effect if the state\u8217\'20\'19s current 15-week ban is upheld in an ongoing legal challenge that is before the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Democratic state senator Lauren Book urged women to contact her office directly, saying on the senate floor: \u8220\'20\'1CPlease don\u8217\'20\'19t take matters into your own hands. Do not put your safety at risk. No back-alley abortions. There are people and funds that will help you. No matter where you live, no matter how desperate of a situation you are in, no matter how helpless it may seem. I promise, you are not alone. Call my office,\u8221\'20\'1D Book said.\par \par \uc2 Protesters opposing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban made their voices heard during the legislative debate and some were kicked out of the state capitol.\par \par \uc2 Kat Duesterhaus, leader of the activist group Bans Off Miami and a communications director for the \uc2 National Organization for Women\uc2 , shouted her opposition in the chamber and referred to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shredding of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights last June, when it decided the Dobbs case which included overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaternal mortality rates are three times higher in states that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  post-Dobbs,\u8221\'20\'1D Duesterhouse shouted before being escorted out.\par \par \uc2 The bill has every chance of reaching DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 And as he signed the gun rights bill, later on Monday, Democrats and gun safety advocates, pointing to mass shootings in Florida like the massacre at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/11/pulse-shooting-orlando-2016-anniversary-gun-control-reform-uvalde-buffalo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2016 Pulse nightclub in Orlando}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Parkland shooting}}}\uc2 , said the new law will only make the state more dangerous. It came just days after three children and three adult staff were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gunned down}}}\uc2  at an elementary school in Nashville, Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , issued a statement on the new gun law, saying, in part: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is shameful that so soon after another tragic school shooting, Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed into law a permitless concealed carry bill \u8230\'20\'26 This is the opposite of commonsense gun safety \u8230\'20\'26 President Biden has been clear: too many lives are being ripped apart by gun violence. The president continues to call on Congress to ban assault weapons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230403ej43002mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
