\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If we can do it, you can do it\u8217\'20\'19: US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups ramp up activities in UK\b0\par\par\uc2 Katherine Stewart \par \uc2 1,811 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2023\par 07:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Emboldened by victories at home, some of the most prominent American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are exporting their tactics overseas\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are stepping up efforts to spread US-style \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics to the UK, ramping up spending with the ambition of shaking up political life beyond American borders.\par \par \uc2 Fresh off their historic victory in bringing about the end of the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, these groups are importing familiar tactics, including public protests and demonstrations, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling centers or so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis pregnancy centers\u8221\'20\'1D, and the cultivation of ties with clerical leaders.\par \par \uc2 These efforts are meeting significant opposition in Britain, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is widely supported and generally available up to 24 weeks and parliament recently passed legislation targeting harassment outside clinics. But reproductive rights advocacy groups are warily observing the US movement\u8217\'20\'19s expansion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat US Christian right and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are establishing bases in the UK means that the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and related sexual and reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 will become increasingly contested in public debate and at a political level, even when there is broad social acceptance for the UK \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  model,\u8221\'20\'1D says Neil Datta, executive director of the European Parliamentary Forum for Sexual and Reproductive Health.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can expect that the successes they have had in the US in these areas to be adapted to a UK context in the coming years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If we can do it \u8211\'20\'13 you can do it\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRethink \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Day,\u8221\'20\'1D a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://m.facebook.com/events/1252875085259607/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seminar}}}\uc2  that took place in February at St Mary\u8217\'20\'19s College Oscott in Birmingham, England, illustrated the cross-border reach of some of the most prominent US-based activist groups.\par \par \uc2 The event was aimed at motivating dozens of attendees to engage in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism. Fast-paced and interactive presentations urged them to participate in clinic demonstrations. Activists distributed pamphlets with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  talking points and rebuttals to pro-choice positions and during breakout sessions audience members rehearsed these arguments. Apart from the Catholic entities co-hosting the event \u8211\'20\'13 St Mary\u8217\'20\'19s College Oscott is a Catholic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://oscott.net/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  seminary}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the four groups principally involved in presentations were all UK affiliates of US-based organizations, and some presenters had deep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adf.uk/support-isabel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ties}}}\uc2  to other major groups in America\u8217\'20\'19s Christian nationalist movement.\par \par \uc2 Long a feature of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics in the US, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests at UK clinics and hospitals have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/11/britain-protest-buffer-zone-abortion-clinics-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged}}}\uc2  in recent years, and the presenters at the Birmingham event can claim much of the credit. They included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marchforlife.co.uk/aiovg_videos/ben-thatcher-march-for-life-uk-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ben Thatcher}}}\uc2 , director of March for Life UK, a spinoff of the US-based March for Life, which draws tens of thousands of participants to Washington DC annually. Another speaker, Dave Brennan, is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrephosUK?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 director }}}\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brephos.org/about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brephos}}}\uc2 , a project of the US-based Center for Bio Ethical Reform (CBR) that aims to help \u8220\'20\'1Cchurches respond to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must acknowledge that we are in spiritual warfare for our souls \u8230\'20\'26 and HE [Satan] is determined,\u8221\'20\'1D Brennan, who devotes much of his effort to clerical outreach, advised conference-goers.\par \par \uc2 Isabel Vaughan-Spruce, the first presenter of the day, helps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.40daysforlife.com/en/birmingham-uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lead}}}\uc2  the UK division of the US-based 40 Days for Life, a Texas-based group that specializes in training protesters and organizing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic demonstrations. The group also runs a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.40daysforlife.com/en/university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 university}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, an online program where, for $497, users can access training videos on recruiting fellow protesters and performing sidewalk \u8220\'20\'1Ccounseling\u8221\'20\'1D, obtain anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  signs and materials, and receive coaching from the 40 Days for Life staff. The group now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.40daysforlife.com/en/university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  to operate more than 1,000 branches in 65 countries.\par \par \uc2 40 Days for Life started its UK activities with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oan1T0rDCG0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigns}}}\uc2  in Northern Ireland in 2009, and now boasts at least 15 chapters in the UK. Its leader, Robert Colquhoun, received support for his work when he enrolled in The Leadership Institute\u8217\'20\'19s International School of Fundraising. The Leadership Institute, a Virginia-based organization, offers various forms of training and networking opportunities to rightwing politicians and activists in the US and around the world. In the fiscal year 2019, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/510235174"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly available}}}\uc2  tax forms, the organization spent $92,494 on \u8220\'20\'1Ceducational seminars\u8221\'20\'1D and $25,871 on grantmaking in Europe, along with substantial sums in the Middle East, east Asia, sub-Saharan Africa, Central America and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a real uptick in protest activity over this year,\u8221\'20\'1D Katherine O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, a spokesperson for the non-profit British Pregnancy Advisory Services, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1COur fear with Roe v Wade being overturned is not only has it inspired anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists globally, but also that American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations may have a pool of money they won\u8217\'20\'19t need to spend in the US and it will divert it here and around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Our fear with Roe v.Wade being overturned is \u8230\'20\'26 that American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations may have a pool of money \u8230\'20\'26 it will divert it here and around the world\par \par \uc2 Katherine O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\par \par \uc2 The motivations of these groups are clear. At the UK March for Life in September 2022, Sean Carney, the US CEO of 40 Days for Life, stood in front of a banner with the slogan, \u8220\'20\'1CLife from Conception, No Exception\u8221\'20\'1D, and referenced the overturning of Roe v Wade. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we can do it,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the crowd assembled in London, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Playing a long game\par \par \uc2 In the US, the extended culture war has given rise to a massive political and legal advocacy infrastructure to prosecute the case against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. At the center of that infrastructure is the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a rightwing legal advocacy group. Greg Scott, vice-president of communications for the \uc2 ADF\uc2 , told the Guardian that the organization\u8217\'20\'19s budget exceeded $102m in the fiscal year 2021-2022; in 2018, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/541660459/202011319349300606/full"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 figure}}}\uc2  was approximately $60m. According to the \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/541660459/202230489349301023/full"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly available tax data}}}\uc2  for 2020, the most recent year on file, the organization claimed close to $10m on overseas expenditures; in the fiscal year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/541660459/201701009349301040/full"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2015-2016}}}\uc2 , the figure was just over $3m. \uc2 ADF\uc2  declined to answer questions from the Guardian about its more recent overseas expenditures.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF\uc2  is a key player behind a series of supreme court cases that have eroded the separation of church and state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/case/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization decision, which led to the overturning of Roe v Wade. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uk.news.yahoo.com/texas-abortion-pill-case-lawyers-224910276.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also }}}\uc2  brought the current case seeking to revoke \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval for mifepristone, one of the drugs used for medication abortions, and is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/us-supreme-court-makes-jokes-ignores-facts-lgbtq-rights-hang-balance-2022-12-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing}}}\uc2  a supreme court case that seeks to give business owners the right to refuse service to LGBTQ+ couples in the name of religious liberty.\par \par \uc2 Consistent with messaging from other rightwing religious organizations, the \uc2 ADF\uc2  presents itself as a champion of freedom of religion and speech. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are dedicated to the promotion of fundamental freedoms for all, and ADF International\u8217\'20\'19s efforts are focused on areas where human rights are under threat,\u8221\'20\'1D ADF International\u8217\'20\'19s legal communications director, Elyssa Koren, told the Guardian. Its critics, however, see it as an organization whose main focus is to impose conservative Christian ideas on the population through the legal system. The \uc2 ADF\uc2  has played a role, for example, in the promotion of anti-sodomy laws around the world, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/this-right-wing-legal-pow_b_6185878"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2  in Belize that, before it was overturned, made gay sex punishable by 10 years\u8217\'20\'19 imprisonment.\par \par \uc2 Already a key player in the US, the \uc2 ADF\uc2  long had its eye on the rest of the world. With offices in cities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  Vienna, Brussels, Strasbourg, London and Geneva, the goals of ADF International rely on some of the same novel legal arguments and concepts of \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech\u8221\'20\'1D and religious liberty. According to the EU {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/mar/28/us-fundamentalists-spent-38m-on-european-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Transparency Register, the ADF spent \u8364\'20\'AC585,000}}}\uc2  ($636,000) on lobbying in the fiscal year 2021-2022. Vaughan-Spruce is one of the public faces of this effort to expand the visibility of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right wing, under the guise of free speech. Last fall, police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/news/midlands-news/isabel-vaughan-spruce-45-charged-25794626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged }}}\uc2  her with four counts of breaching a buffer zone. The ADF UK, which provided her legal counsel, cast the charges as persecution for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe crime of silent prayer\u8221\'20\'1D. Those charges were eventually dropped, but she was rearrested last week for violating the same buffer zone.\par \par \uc2 Father Paul Gough, a Roman Catholic priest who also spoke at the Birmingham event, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/uk-news/priest-woman-arrested-silently-prayed-26255478"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ealingtimes.co.uk/news/national/23326365.priest-accuses-government-censoring-silent-prayers-near-abortion-clinic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cprotesting and engaging in an act that is intimidating to service users\u8221\'20\'1D of a Birmingham clinic. His charges were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://localtoday.news/mn/uk-court-acquits-woman-priestess-of-thought-crime-for-silent-prayer-near-abortion-clinic-152033.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecatholicnetwork.co.uk/fr-sean-gough-isabel-vaughan-spruce-receive-not-guilty-verdict-for-silent-prayer-thoughtcrime/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2 , with the help of \uc2 ADF\uc2 . He subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/video/6320516153112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  on the Tucker Carlson show on Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, I was praying for free speech, which I believe is threatened in the United Kingdom,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seeing a steady increase with anti-choice harassment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Louise McCudden, a UK-based adviser with MSI Reproductive Choices. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that anti-choice groups across the UK have been emboldened by the repeal of Roe v Wade, and that they like to copy US-style tactics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We are seeing a steady increase with anti-choice harassment\par \par \uc2 Louise McCudden\par \par \uc2 In the UK, where the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoys wide support, the growing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity around reproductive health facilities has sparked a backlash that appears to be limiting the movement\u8217\'20\'19s policy gains. The UK supreme court recently recognized that harassment around healthcare facilities violates the rights of those seeking reproductive and sexual health services and information, and the UK parliament {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/13/snp-leadership-candidates-urged-to-commit-to-abortion-clinic-buffer-zones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently moved}}}\uc2  toward legislating the establishment of buffer zones around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 In addition to protest tactics and messaging, US organizations are contributing to the influx of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling centers or so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis pregnancy centers\u8221\'20\'1D. There are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/uploads/filer_public/81/a3/81a30c3d-c40f-4bd9-aa28-be52e2180b1b/ppnc-cpc-fact-sheet.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about}}}\uc2  4,000 such operations in the US, the majority affiliated with large networks like Heartbeat International, which has four affiliates in the UK. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bbc.com/news/uk-64751800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an investigation}}}\uc2  by the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s Panorama, at least 57 such centers operate in the UK, more than one-third of which provide misleading or unethical advice. One US-based organization, Stanton Healthcare, which operates a clinic in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stantonbelfast.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Belfast}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inews.co.uk/news/anti-abortion-group-misleading-women-scotland-1710460"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stantonscotland.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanded}}}\uc2  into Scotland. In 2018, a Times of London reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/belfast-anti-abortion-centre-stanton-healthcare-peddling-false-cancer-claims-to-women-669bnk725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visited }}}\uc2  the Belfast clinic and recorded a conversation in which she was told \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make her breasts \u8220\'20\'1Cfill with cancer\u8221\'20\'1D and was warned, \u8220\'20\'1CYou could get your womb perforated, you might be left sterile.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bpas.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from}}}\uc2  the British Pregnancy Advisory Services, cautions it would be dangerous to underestimate the potential impact of these groups. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are well funded, well organised and well connected with influential parliamentarians,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are going into schools, into universities, and have a real drive to recruit the \u8216\'20\'18next generation\u8217\'20\'19 of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. They know they are playing the long game, and they believe that they will win, even if it takes decades.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230402ej42000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
