\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump grand jury reportedly examining second hush-money payment \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2023\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Prosecutors looking into payment to Karen McDougal \u8211\'20\'13 reportSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 House Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425be6a8f082ce94b435f1b#block-6425be6a8f082ce94b435f1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled legislation}}}\uc2  to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide, but the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s control of the chamber and hostility to the procedure means the bill will remain a symbolic effort, at least for now. Meanwhile, it turns out that the grand jury empaneled by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  is hearing about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425da608f08800f71af6c0d#block-6425da608f08800f71af6c0d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not one, but two}}}\uc2  alleged hush money payments that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may have facilitated ahead of the 2016 election. There\u8217\'20\'19s still no telling if and when an indictment will happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else went on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425acdb8f082ce94b435e06#block-6425acdb8f082ce94b435e06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a proclamation}}}\uc2  in recognition of today\u8217\'20\'19s Transgender Day of Visibility that decried an \u8220\'20\'1Cepidemic of violence\u8221\'20\'1D against the group.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The squabbling in a Republican-convened House committee investigating \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Weaponization of the Federal Government\u8221\'20\'1D grew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425cac18f082ce94b435fc4#block-6425cac18f082ce94b435fc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly intense}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin, the centrist Democratic senator who stymied progressive demands over the past two years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64258e918f08800f71af681a#block-64258e918f08800f71af681a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on the White House}}}\uc2  to negotiate with Republicans over the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prayer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425a14e8f0865ff78f53874#block-6425a14e8f0865ff78f53874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is all}}}\uc2  one Republican lawmaker has to offer when it comes to solving America\u8217\'20\'19s epidemic of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite it all, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425e5648f08800f71af6c64#block-6425e5648f08800f71af6c64"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to gain support}}}\uc2  among Republicans, a new Fox News poll shows.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite all the investigations surrounding him, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appears to be consolidating his standing among Republicans as he embarks on a second campaign for the White House.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/official-polls/fox-news-poll-trumps-lead-grows-in-gop-primary-race-now-over-50-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News poll released yesterday}}}\uc2  shows the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lead over other Republicans growing, with Trump polling at 54% support against the 24% backing Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 his most strongest presumed challenger. That\u8217\'20\'19s a gap of 30 percentage points, up from the 15 percentage point gap he had last month.\par \par \uc2 None of the other Republicans in the survey, including former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley and ex-congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , crack double digits, according to the poll.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to the Wall Street Journal, a key indicator of which direction Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation is going is the presence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2018/aug/06/david-pecker-donald-trump-national-enquirer-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Pecker}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pecker is the former CEO of \uc2 American Media\uc2 , which owns tabloid the National Enquirer. According to the Journal, Pecker bought exclusive rights to Karen McDougal \u8217\'20\'19s story in order to keep it out of the public eye in the weeks before the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Now it seems that Pecker is cooperating with Bragg. Citing people familiar with the matter, the Journal reports that Pecker spoke to the grand jury investigating Trump in January, and again earlier this week, with his testimony focused on a broader scheme by Trump to suppress negative stories from coming out as he ran for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manhattan grand jury examining second Trump hush money payment: report\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan grand jury that is considering whether to bring charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a hush money payment he allegedly facilitated just before the 2016 election is also examining a second payment made to a woman who claimed she had an affair with the real estate mogul, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-grand-jury-digs-into-hush-money-paid-to-second-woman-c1818ffb?mod=hp_lead_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The $150,000 payment being examined by the grand jury was allegedly made to Karen McDougal, a former Playboy model who said she had a relationship with Trump in 2006 that lasted 10 months. The panel is also looking into a $130,000 payment Trump allegedly arranged to be made to adult film actor Stormy Daniels just before the 2016 presidential election, in exchange for her keeping quiet about an affair with him.\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  was expected to last week indict Trump for the payment to Daniels, but the decision has been pushed back repeatedly. The revelation that the grand jury was hearing evidence of a second alleged hush money payment may explain the delay.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of angry scenes in Congress, there have been some chaotic goings-on today over at the \u8220\'20\'1CSelect Subcommittee on the Weaponization of the Federal Government\u8221\'20\'1D, chaired by Jim Jordan, the hardline Republican from Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Stacey Plaskett\uc2 . Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 It all hinges on how two Republican witnesses, the Missouri senator \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  and the attorney general of Louisiana, \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , appeared to give statements about supposed censorship involving the Biden administration and big tech platforms, but departed without being cross-examined.\par \par \uc2 Amid Democratic protests and Republican counters, \uc2 Linda Sanchez\uc2  of California, a Democrat, told Jordan: \u8220\'20\'1CIf allowing them to leave is not weaponisation, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In another confrontation, Mike Johnson of Louisiana, a Republican, sought to introduce into the congressional record a letter from Landry in which, he said, the state AG \u8220\'20\'1Cdecries all political violence and calls for an end to that and asks for respect for all political viewpoints\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The ranking Democrat on the panel, \uc2 Stacey Plaskett\uc2 , the delegate from the US Virgin Islands, sighed and said: \u8220\'20\'1CAnother thing we can\u8217\'20\'19t examine because he\u8217\'20\'19s not here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jordan said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can examine it, it\u8217\'20\'19s a document.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Plaskett said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, examine him for what he wrote and the intent behind what he said.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Johnson walked over and plonked the document on Plaskett\u8217\'20\'19s desk, Jordan said: \u8220\'20\'1CI would just point out that \u8230\'20\'26 we got the document right here, I can hand it to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Plaskett picked up the document, walked over the dais to Johnson, and threw it back on his desk.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the video:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMikeJohnson}}}\uc2  submits a letter written by an excused witness.\par \par \uc2 Del. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StaceyPlaskett?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @StaceyPlaskett}}}\uc2  gets up, walks over the throws it back at Rep. Johnson. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wkdTFIxsoo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wkdTFIxsoo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1641452563773161482?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Footage of an extraordinary confrontation between two members of Congress, the far-right Republican \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , from Georgia, and the Florida Democrat \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2 , continues to spread widely online.\par \par \uc2 Jared Moskowitz\uc2 . Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The exchange happened yesterday, during a House oversight committee hearing about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/12/a-bill-was-supposed-to-fix-washington-dcs-problems-instead-it-polarized-a-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 governance of Washington DC}}}\uc2  which grew contentious amid Republican attacks and questions about crime and, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/republican-lauren-boebert-house-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in particular}}}\uc2 , public urination.\par \par \uc2 Moskowitz said: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think parents in this country, as they\u8217\'20\'19re putting their young kids into pajamas at night and are tucking them into bed, you think they\u8217\'20\'19re worried about public urination in Washington DC? Or do you think they\u8217\'20\'19re worried about sending their kid to school and their kid not coming home?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referring to the school shooting in Nashville, Tennessee on Monday in which three children and three adults were killed, Moskowitz said: \u8220\'20\'1CMass murder in schools is crime. That\u8217\'20\'19s crime. You want to talk about 1,300 cars being stolen? 550 people have been murdered in school. Who cares about the cars? What about the kids? No hearing for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene said children could be made safer by arming more people in schools.\par \par \uc2 Growing angry, Moskowitz said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, there are six people that are dead in that school [in Nashville] including three children because you guys got rid of the assault weapons ban. Because you guys made it easy for people who don\u8217\'20\'19t deserve to have weapons, who are mentally incapable of having weapons of war, [to be] able to buy those weapons and go into schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid the good guys with the gun stop six people from getting murdered? No, but you know what? AR-15s, you ever seen what those bullets do to children? You know why you don\u8217\'20\'19t hunt with an AR-15, with a deer? Because there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing left. And there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing left of these kids when people go into school and murder them while they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to read.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moskowitz then referred to widespread Republican moves to ban books about race, sexuality, gender and other culture war issues from public schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are worried about banning books,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CDead kids can\u8217\'20\'19t read.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can watch part of the exchange {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1641200399729270784"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 After the White House remarks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425b60c8f0865ff78f539eb#block-6425b60c8f0865ff78f539eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier}}}\uc2 , we also have brief comments from the secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , about the reported arrest in Russia on espionage charges of Evan Gershkovich, an American citizen and reporter for the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Evan Gershkovich. Photograph: The Wall Street Journal/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Blinken says: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply concerned over Russia\u8217\'20\'19s widely-reported detention of a US citizen journalist. We are in contact with the Wall Street Journal on this situation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhenever a US citizen is detained abroad, we immediately seek consular access, and seek to provide all appropriate support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the strongest possible terms, we condemn the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s continued attempts to intimidate, repress, and punish journalists and civil society voices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department of State\u8217\'20\'19s highest priority is the safety and security of US citizens abroad. We reiterate our strong warnings about the danger posed to US citizens inside the Russian Federation. US citizens residing or traveling in Russia should depart immediately, as stated in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mcas-proxyweb.mcas.ms/certificate-checker?login=false&originalUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fgcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com.mcas.ms%2F%3Furl%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Flnks.gd%252Fl%252FeyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJidWxsZXRpbl9saW5rX2lkIjoxMDAsInVyaSI6ImJwMjpjbGljayIsInVybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vdHJhdmVsLnN0YXRlLmdvdi9jb250ZW50L3RyYXZlbC9lbi90cmF2ZWxhZHZpc29yaWVzL3RyYXZlbGFkdmlzb3JpZXMvcnVzc2lhLXRyYXZlbC1hZHZpc29yeS5odG1sIiwiYnVsbGV0aW5faWQiOiIyMDIzMDMzMC43NDI5MzI1MSJ9.qwIFo5srg9wGnrk4fz0lXcdsGmWclS6N7K6NFc_qzAg%252Fs%252F1436012980%252Fbr%252F157128839874-l%26data%3D05%257C01%257CSimmonsJX%2540state.gov%257Ccbe3baa07a33402770b208db3139248c%257C66cf50745afe48d1a691a12b2121f44b%257C0%257C0%257C638157893720630675%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C3000%257C%257C%257C%26sdata%3DpPbMN0wfZBv0Ol7CLzh7gEMIMtn1%252F3lQzT4thykI2s4%253D%26reserved%3D0%26McasTsid%3D20893&McasCSRF=4a83441ab940ec7f010b3d11e83a5053e67dbf18ecd4684bc6578b409a593bbf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Travel Advisory for Russia}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The charges against Gershkovich carry a maximum prison sentence of 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest Guardian report, from Shaun Walker, our central and eastern Europe correspondent:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/30/us-condemns-arrest-of-wsj-journalist-as-russia-accused-of-hostage-taking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US condemns arrest of WSJ journalist as Russia accused of \u8216\'20\'18hostage taking\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Democratic press conference concluded, a reporter asked Judy Chu about the chances of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act passing, given the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s control of the House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel very confident that in two years we will be in a position to put it on the floor once again. And we are determined, also, of course, to keep our majority in the Senate. So, I think that the future is bright, and in two years, we can get this passed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chu, who is introducing the bill that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrat \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  chimed in, saying that despite the bill\u8217\'20\'19s dim chances, supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to keep fighting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re coming at us \u8230\'20\'26 using every tool available to them, to put their hands on bodies to deny access to this critical life saving healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Pressley said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so we\u8217\'20\'19re doing the same, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s litigation, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s legislation or mobilization, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t stop organizing because we don\u8217\'20\'19t have the gavel and we\u8217\'20\'19re not in cycle. And we don\u8217\'20\'19t stop legislating because we don\u8217\'20\'19t have the gavel and we\u8217\'20\'19re not in cycle. The other side isn\u8217\'20\'19t stopping and neither are we.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 California Democrat Judy Chu is the sponsor of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, and is introducing it for the second time in the House.\par \par \uc2 She cast it as a necessary response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade, and the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to cracking down on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans had their way, this would be forever a nation of forced birth. They\u8217\'20\'19ve already proposed a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, so no matter where you live, politicians would have more say about what happens to your body than you do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said during an event with House Democratic leaders outside the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are all standing here today because every person, no matter their circumstances, no matter how they became pregnant, deserves dignity, safety and care in seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because you should not have more rights if you\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant in California than if you get pregnant in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Chu said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd most of all, because no one, not the president not a supreme court justice, not your partner, should be able to force you to remain pregnant if you do not wish to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jeffries to the GOP: 'Back up off the women of America'\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  kicked off the press conference introducing the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act by taking aim at \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme Maga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D he said want to control women\u8217\'20\'19s health care choices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act is so critical because extreme Maga Republicans want to impose a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna stop them,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeffries said. \u8220\'20\'1CExtreme Republicans want to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care across the nation. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna stop them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExtreme Republicans think that they should be the ones who make a decision about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and we\u8217\'20\'19re here to say, back up off the women of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 House Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6425a6df8f082ce94b435da1#block-6425a6df8f082ce94b435da1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are about to reintroduce}}}\uc2  legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, a symbolic effort that has no chance of passing the chamber as long as Republicans remain in control. We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you posted on the press conference set to begin shortly, at 12:45 pm eastern time. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6425b60c8f0865ff78f539eb#block-6425b60c8f0865ff78f539eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington is reacting}}}\uc2  to news that Russia has detained an American reporter working for the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425acdb8f082ce94b435e06#block-6425acdb8f082ce94b435e06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a proclamation}}}\uc2  in recognition of today\u8217\'20\'19s Transgender Day of Visibility that decried an \u8220\'20\'1Cepidemic of violence\u8221\'20\'1D against the group.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin, the centrist Democratic senator who stymied progressive demands over the past two years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64258e918f08800f71af681a#block-64258e918f08800f71af681a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on the White House}}}\uc2  to negotiate with Republicans over the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prayer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/30/biden-debt-ceiling-manchin-energy-bill-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6425a14e8f0865ff78f53874#block-6425a14e8f0865ff78f53874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is all}}}\uc2  one Republican lawmaker has to offer when it comes to solving America\u8217\'20\'19s epidemic of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House 'deeply concerned' by detention of American journalist in Russia\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s reported detention of Evan Gershkovich, an American citizen and reporter for the Wall Street Journal, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Russian authorities arrested Gershkovich on Wednesday in the Urals city of Ekaterinburg and accused him of espionage, a charge that carries a prison sentence of up to 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Jean-Pierre\u8217\'20\'19s full statement:\par \par \uc2 We are deeply concerned by the troubling reports that Evan Gershkovich, an American citizen, has been detained in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Last night, White House and State Department Officials spoke with Mr. Gershkovich\u8217\'20\'19s employer, the Wall Street Journal. The Administration has also been in contact with his family. Furthermore, the State Department has been in direct touch with the Russian government on this matter, including actively working to secure consular access to Mr. Gershkovich. The targeting of American citizens by the Russian government is unacceptable. We condemn the detention of Mr. Gershkovich in the strongest terms. We also condemn the Russian government\u8217\'20\'19s continued targeting and repression of journalists and freedom of the press. I want to strongly reiterate that Americans should heed the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s warning to not travel to Russia. U.S. citizens residing or traveling in Russia should depart immediately, as the State Department continues to advise.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 For more on how rightwing figures have used the Nashville school shooting to attack transgender people and other LGBTQ+ groups, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 An already vigorous assault by Republicans on LGBTQ+ rights around the US is certain to gather pace in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville school shooting}}}\uc2 , advocacy groups are warning.\par \par \uc2 Hard-right figures wasted little time in seizing on the reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/28/nashville-school-shooter-identity-transgender"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transgender identity of the Covenant school killer}}}\uc2  to advance tenets of a \u8220\'20\'1Chateful\u8221\'20\'1D agenda that has become an obsession of Republican-controlled statehouses from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandoweekly.com/news/all-the-anti-lgbtq-laws-being-proposed-in-florida-and-how-you-can-fight-back-33857786"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/press-releases/human-rights-campaign-tennessee-continues-obsession-with-anti-lgbtq-legislation-with-house-passage-of-religious-refusal-bill-and-second-anti-drag-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In contrast to a muted response to numerous mass shootings in which the majority of the killers were white, male and cisgender, these extremists appear to be manipulating the Nashville shooter\u8217\'20\'19s self-identification to make their case for even more anti-trans legislation, even as they eschew gun control.\par \par \uc2 They include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DonaldJTrumpJr/status/1640520340630585345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump Jr}}}\uc2  seeking an end to what he calls \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D gender-affirming care; \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  having her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/marjorie-taylor-greene-twitter-account-nashville-school-shooting-vengeance-post/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter account temporarily suspended}}}\uc2  for misrepresenting a planned protest against anti-trans laws; and homophobic and transphobic rants from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/laura-ingraham-killers-identity-medias-preferred-criteria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News hosts Laura Ingraham}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the latter blasting the trans movement as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/tucker-carlson-says-trans-movement-natural-enemy-christianity-1791016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natural enemy of Christianity}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/far-right-demonize-lgbtq-nashville-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Desperate and bigoted\u8217\'20\'19: US right uses latest shooting to malign trans people}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden decries 'epidemic of violence' against transgender Americans\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  warned of \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscriminatory state laws\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Cepidemic of violence\u8221\'20\'1D targeting transgender Americans in a proclamation recognizing this year\u8217\'20\'19s Transgender Day of Visibility.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s statement came as GOP-led states nationwide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/arkansas-bans-trans-students-from-using-bathroom-that-matches-gender"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass laws}}}\uc2  that ban gender-affirming care for minors or restrict transgender people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to use their preferred pronouns on official documents or the bathrooms of their choice. It also came days after the mass shooting at a Nashville elementary school by a gunman who identified as transgender \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/far-right-demonize-lgbtq-nashville-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some rightwing figures seized on}}}\uc2  to further demonize the group.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2023/03/30/a-proclamation-on-transgender-day-of-visibility/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House proclamation}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Transgender Day of Visibility celebrates the joy, strength, and absolute courage of some of the bravest people I know \u8212\'20\'14 people who have too often had to put their jobs, relationships, and lives on the line just to be their true selves. Today, we show millions of transgender and nonbinary Americans that we see them, they belong, and they should be treated with dignity and respect. Their courage has given countless others strength, but no one should have to be brave just to be themselves. Every American deserves that freedom.\par \par \uc2 Transgender Americans shape our Nation\u8217\'20\'19s soul \u8212\'20\'14 proudly serving in the military, curing deadly diseases, holding elected office, running thriving businesses, fighting for justice, raising families, and much more. As kids, they deserve what every child deserves: the chance to learn in safe and supportive schools, to develop meaningful friendships, and to live openly and honestly. As adults, they deserve the same rights enjoyed by every American, including equal access to health care, housing, and jobs and the chance to age with grace as senior citizens. But today, too many transgender Americans are still denied those rights and freedoms. A wave of discriminatory State laws is targeting transgender youth, terrifying families and hurting kids who are not hurting anyone. An epidemic of violence against transgender women and girls, in particular women and girls of color, has taken lives far too soon. Last year\u8217\'20\'19s Club Q shooting in Colorado was another painful example of this kind of violence \u8212\'20\'14 a stain on the conscience of our Nation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats to make quixotic push for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 House Democrats will today introduce legislation to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, but the measure has no chance of passing the chamber as long as Republicans maintain their majority.\par \par \uc2 House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , whip Katherine Clark and other members of Democratic leadership will introduce the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act of 2023 in a press conference at 12.45pm ET. The legislation would create a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect against restrictions on the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 such as those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/13/abortion-restrictions-us-state-legislatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many GOP-led states have enacted}}}\uc2  since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 A version of the bill was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.markey.senate.gov/news/press-releases/senator-markey-joins-senators-baldwin-blumenthal-in-introducing-legislation-to-restore-and-protect-americans-right-to-an-abortion-nationwide#:~:text=The%20Women's%20Health%20Protection%20Act%20creates%20federal%20rights%20for%20patients,intrude%20upon%20personal%20decision%2Dmaking."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this month proposed in the Senate}}}\uc2 , but the push is largely symbolic. Republicans remain broadly against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, dooming the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s chances both in the House and the Senate, where they can use the filibuster to stop its passage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the shooting at a Nashville elementary school earlier this week that killed six people, three of them children, Republicans in Congress have made clear that they plan to do nothing in response to gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Well, perhaps not nothing. Tim Burchett, a House GOP lawmaker from Tennessee, told Fox News today that he\u8217\'20\'19d keep praying for America\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/23/us-gun-violence-mass-shootings-2022-walmart-virginia-colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rampant gun violence}}}\uc2  to stop:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Tim Burchett (R-TN), when asked why his response to the Nashville school mass shooting made people mad:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey come back to me and say, \u8216\'20\'18Burchett, look what your prayers have done for us.\u8217\'20\'19 The people doing the praying aren\u8217\'20\'19t the ones doing the shooting.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4bgzj9Tnhq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4bgzj9Tnhq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1641436062907088897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Congress, emotions are running high after the shooting at a Nashville elementary school, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Amid continuing national grief and anger over the Nashville elementary school shooting, in which three children and three adults were killed, two members of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  got into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/03/30/jamaal-bowman-thomas-massie-shouting-gun-control/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shouting match}}}\uc2  outside the chamber on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 While speaking to reporters, \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 , a Democrat from New York and a former school principal, called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cgutless\u8221\'20\'1D for refusing to support meaningful gun control reforms.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , a far-right Republican from Kentucky, overheard Bowman\u8217\'20\'19s comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are you talking about?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s never been a school shooting in a school that allows teachers to carry guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/nashville-school-shooting-congress-jamaal-bowman-thomas-massie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville school shooting prompts shouting match between congressmen}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  may be taking flak from the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 right flank, the president appears to be in the midst of a pivot to the center that\u8217\'20\'19s frustrated progressives, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 When he was running for president in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  promised \u8220\'20\'1Cno more drilling on federal lands, period\u8221\'20\'1D. This month, he approved an $8bn oil project in Alaska, violating that campaign pledge.\par \par \uc2 Biden had said he wholeheartedly supports granting statehood to the District of Columbia. Last week, he signed a Republican bill overturning changes to the DC criminal code, which critics attacked as a violation of home rule.\par \par \uc2 Biden previously accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of waging \u8220\'20\'1Can unrelenting assault on our values and our history as a nation of immigrants\u8221\'20\'1D because of his handling of the US-Mexican border. This month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/06/us/politics/biden-immigration-family-detention.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  emerged that the Biden administration has considered reinstating the practice of detaining migrant families who cross the border illegally. Immigrant rights advocates have denounced the idea, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/immigration-senate-democrats-denounce-biden-border-restriction-illegal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another proposal}}}\uc2  to further restrict who can seek asylum in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/biden-2024-policies-climate-oil-campaign-pledges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Progressives decry Biden\u8217\'20\'19s pivot to center in run-up to 2024: \u8216\'20\'18Feet to the fire\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 One thing to keep in mind about Joe Manchin: his days in the Senate may be numbered.\par \par \uc2 He represents West Virginia, which years ago was a Democratic bastion, but is now considered one of the most Republican states in the country. Manchin is among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a group of Democratic senators representing red states}}}\uc2  that are up for re-election next year, giving Republicans a great opportunity to seize control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Thus, breaking with the Biden administration may be in Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s interest \u8211\'20\'13 though he still hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said whether he\u8217\'20\'19ll stand for re-election to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin calls for 'meaningful, serious reforms' to government spending\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin acted as something of a congressional kingmaker for the first two years of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency. With Democrats needing unanimity among the party\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers to get anything through the Senate without Republican support, Manchin flexed his muscles to, among other things, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/31/joe-manchin-hails-deal-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 water down provisions}}}\uc2  addressing climate change from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s signature legislation, the Inflation Reduction Act (IRA).\par \par \uc2 Manchin saw his power diluted in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, when the Democrats increased their margin in the Senate and lost the House, ending the chances for Biden to get any big legislation through Congress for the next two years. But Manchin is still an influential voices and perhaps the most conservative Democrat in the Senate, and thus his criticism of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s strategy on the debt ceiling, and implementation of the IRA, is worth listening to.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some of what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-inflation-reduction-act-betrayal-joe-manchin-debt-ceiling-budget-fossil-fuels-green-energy-dc37738e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wrote in the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Instead of implementing the law as intended, unelected ideologues, bureaucrats and appointees seem determined to violate and subvert the law to advance a partisan agenda that ignores both energy and fiscal security. Specifically, they are ignoring the law\u8217\'20\'19s intent to support and expand fossil energy and are redefining \u8220\'20\'1Cdomestic energy\u8221\'20\'1D to increase clean-energy spending to potentially deficit-breaking levels. The administration is attempting at every turn to implement the bill it wanted, not the bill Congress actually passed. Ignoring the debt and deficit implications of these actions as the time nears to raise the debt ceiling isn\u8217\'20\'19t only wrong, it\u8217\'20\'19s policy and political malpractice.\par \par \uc2 I believe the only person who can rein in this extremism is Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 The first step is for the president to sit down with fiscally minded Republicans and Democrats to negotiate common-sense reforms to out-of-control fiscal policy. While we can all acknowledge that raising the debt limit is an absolute necessity and Republicans shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t threaten otherwise, are we seriously to believe there is no room to negotiate? Does the federal government operate so efficiently and effectively that there truly isn\u8217\'20\'19t a dollar of waste, fraud or abuse? Let\u8217\'20\'19s get serious.\par \par \uc2 In short, Manchin has two demands: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has the power, today, to direct his administration to follow the law, as well as to sit down with congressional leaders and negotiate meaningful, serious reforms to the federal budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Manchin breaks with Biden on debt ceiling strategy\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s right-leaning editorial pages are rarely comforting reading for Democrats, and on Wednesday, they played host to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-inflation-reduction-act-betrayal-joe-manchin-debt-ceiling-budget-fossil-fuels-green-energy-dc37738e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a column criticizing the Biden administration}}}\uc2  from perhaps its top frenemy: Joe Manchin. West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator has acted as the gatekeeper for much legislation over the past two years of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration, and in the column, he took issue with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s refusal to negotiate with Republicans over America\u8217\'20\'19s debt limit. Manchin called for the White House to instead sit down with the opposition to find ways to reduce spending, which he argued was on an unsustainable path.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated House of Representatives is expected to finish up consideration of a bill meant to lower energy costs via increased oil and gas drilling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters at 2pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will not stop a Republican-backed measure to end the national emergency over the Covid pandemic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/covid-biden-senate-national-emergency-bill-f0e08810c28cc648a9b778a86d2dc7e1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230330ej3u001bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
