\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Florida,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  refuge in US south, poised to pass six-week ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Salom\u233\'00\'E9 G\u243\'00\'F3mez-Upegui \par \uc2 963 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 March 2023\par 20:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor signals he will sign the proposed bill, which would slam door shut for many patients traveling to Florida for care\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposed by Florida Republicans earlier this month threatens to reverberate across the American south.\par \par \uc2 Following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization to overturn the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Florida became a strategic refuge for women seeking to access reproductive healthcare from states that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 places as varied as Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Alabama and Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last six months since Dobbs, the number of out-of-state patients coming to [us] for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care has quadrupled,\u8221\'20\'1D Damien Filer, a representative of Planned Parenthood of South, East, and North Florida (PPSEN), told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIn Jacksonville and Tallahassee, our health centers on the state\u8217\'20\'19s northern border, our general patient load has more than doubled, with the majority being from out of state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/content/download/7208/file/TrimesterByReason_2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from}}}\uc2  Florida\u8217\'20\'19s agency for health care administration, 82,192 abortions were performed in the state in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 7,324 more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/content/download/7203/file/TotalsByCounty_2020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the number performed in 2020}}}\uc2  when Roe v Wade was still standing. The number of out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients in Florida grew from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/content/download/7203/file/TotalsByCounty_2020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,988}}}\uc2  in 2020 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ahca.myflorida.com/content/download/7205/file/TotalsByCounty_2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6,708}}}\uc2  in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 a 68% increase that probably obscures the full year-on-year impact, since Roe only fell toward the second half of 2022.\par \par \uc2 Dr Robyn Schickler, the chief medical officer of Planned Parenthood of south-west and central Florida, says she often sees out-of-state patients forced to go to great lengths to get the reproductive healthcare they need. She recalled a patient in her early 20s who came in from Texas to Orlando last year around 13 weeks pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHurricane Ian came through, we had to close the center, cancel and reschedule a bunch of patients, and she ended up having to stay and ride out the hurricane,\u8221\'20\'1D Schickler said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got her in as soon as we reopened so that she could go back home, but instead of just coming in and getting the healthcare she needed, she had to ride out a hurricane away from her home \u8211\'20\'13 that was really wild.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schickler says the sheer volume of out-of-state patients has also created wait times that, in turn, have pushed Floridians from the northern part of the state further south for care.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/7/BillText/Filed/PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed bill}}}\uc2  introduced earlier this month is expected to pass the Republican-controlled legislature and be signed by the governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . It would go into effect only if the Florida supreme court upholds the current 15-week ban in a case it will decide at some point this year.\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban would include exceptions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life, and the limit would remain at 15 weeks in the case of rape or incest. However, women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the rape and incest exception would be forced to prove their victim status with documents such as restraining orders, police reports or hospital records \u8211\'20\'13often rendering these exceptions meaningless, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/politics/os-ne-florida-abortion-bill-rape-exception-20230309-xwyvkk5tm5aa3gdslvqrvkdtou-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocates say}}}\uc2 , given the barriers to reporting assault.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis \u8211\'20\'13 who is widely expected to run for president in 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 publicly stated he plans to sign the bill into law. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re for pro-life \u8230\'20\'26 I urged the legislature to work, produce good stuff, and we will sign,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/#americans-views-of-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report published by Pew Research Center in 2022}}}\uc2  revealed 62% of American adults believe abortions should be legal in \u8220\'20\'1Call or most cases\u8221\'20\'1D, while a mere 37% believe it should be illegal. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/sites/default/files/ct/news/documents/2020-11/topline_reuters_florida_state_poll_w6_11_02_2020_.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 Ipsos/Reuters poll}}}\uc2  found that 56% of likely voters in Florida believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most cases, and a similar number disagreed with the supreme court decision overturning Roe, according to a 2022 \uc2 University of South Florida\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 Dr Shelly Tien, a board-certified obstetrician-gynecologist and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in north-east Florida, believes the proposed bill is bound to have a profound effect on already marginalized patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of the patients I see that are coming from out-of-state are driving because it\u8217\'20\'19s cheaper, and many patients are driving through the night,\u8221\'20\'1D Tien said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had patients show up that are very hungry. I\u8217\'20\'19ve cared for patients that have to miss and reschedule appointments because their childcare falls through or they\u8217\'20\'19ve been unable to find someone to care for their children. I\u8217\'20\'19ve had patients in relationships with active intimate partner violence trying to find a time when their partner, who is also the perpetrator, is out of town so they can sneak away and have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks is only two weeks after a missed period, and by that point, many women haven\u8217\'20\'19t realized they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. Women have irregular periods all the time for many reasons, so to prevent them from seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after six weeks is, for all intents and purposes, a total ban. Essentially, a ban like this completely robs women, girls and their families of having any say in their own health,\u8221\'20\'1D Tien said.\par \par \uc2 Providers are bracing for the need to send a growing number of Floridians elsewhere for care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlready with a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, there are many patients we have to refer out of state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amber Gavin, vice-president of Advocacy and Operations at A Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA six-week ban is unbelievably cruel. It narrows the window of when folks can access care and makes it so much harder,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, we will continue referring patients out-of-state to get their care elsewhere, whether that\u8217\'20\'19s North Carolina, Virginia or other places.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230328ej3s002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
