\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says gun violence is \u8216\'20\'18ripping our communities apart\u8217\'20\'19 after Nashville school shooting \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 6,023 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2023\par 20:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President repeats call for Congress to pass assault weapons ban after three children and three adults killed at elementary schoolSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the politics blog now, but you can follow developments in the Nashville school shooting through our ongoing news coverage.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we were following today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  condemned the \u8220\'20\'1Csick and heartbreaking\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elementary school shooting in Nashville, Tennessee}}}\uc2 , that claimed the lives of three children and three adults. The president repeated his call for lawmakers to pass an assault weapons ban, saying gun violence was \u8220\'20\'1Cripping our communities apart\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The New York grand jury mulling a felony charge for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over a hush money payment to adult film star Stormy Daniels convened for the first time in a week. But it\u8217\'20\'19s still unclear when the panel might be asked to vote on a possible criminal indictment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge in Georgia ordered Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to respond by 1 May to a motion by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team to throw out a report by a grand jury investigating his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/17/trump-report-georgia-crimes-charges-grand-jury-investigation-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interference in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Only one in four Democrats want Biden to run for a second term in 2024, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_032723/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll by }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_032723/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monmouth University}}}\uc2  found. More than four in 10 would prefer to see the president step aside for another candidate, according to the poll of self-identified Democrats and Democratic-leaning voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, Democratic senator for Massachusetts, said she\u8217\'20\'19s running for a third term in the chamber, and has plans to \u8220\'20\'1Cend corruption in Washington, make the economy work for the middle class, and protect democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Africa, meeting the leaders of Ghana, Tanzania and Zambia, and seeking to rebuild bridges with nations previously neglected by the US. The vice-president arrived in Africa with a $139m package of bilateral security, economic and development assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke of his heart going out to parents of the children killed in Monday\u8217\'20\'19s school shooting in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 Parents of students murdered in previous school shootings, and other activists have taken to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to vent their frustrations, demand action, and send condolences to today\u8217\'20\'19s bereaved families.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Manuel Oliver, a gun reform activist whose 17-year-old son Joaquin Oliver was among the 17 victims of the 2018 Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school massacre in Parkland, Florida:\par \par \uc2 enltrI suggest a NATIONAL STRIKE from all levels of education until federal laws occur. Not fighting back for the next victim of gun violence makes us part of the problem. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/enoughisnow?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #enoughisnow}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AMarch4OurLives?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AMarch4OurLives}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Team_Enough?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Team_Enough}}}\uc2  Please SHARE!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manuel Oliver (@manueloliver00) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/manueloliver00/status/1640424185036980228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Kimberly Garcia lost her 10-year-old daughter Amerie Jo Garza in last year\u8217\'20\'19s shooting at Robb elementary school, Uvalde, Texas:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur kids aren\u8217\'20\'19t safe. Schools aren\u8217\'20\'19t safe. My daughter wasn\u8217\'20\'19t safe, her life was taken from her. My son isn\u8217\'20\'19t safe and it keeps me up all night. How am I supposed to be okay with leaving him at school ? There\u8217\'20\'19s no way.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kimberly Garcia (@kim_amerie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kim_amerie/status/1640412850463072256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 From the March for Our Lives student group founded after the Parkland shooting:\par \par \uc2 enltrThree children shot and killed.\par \par \uc2 As we wait for more details, our hearts are with the families and the community in Nashville. No child should go to school in fear of being shot.\par \par \uc2 Adults are failing kids.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SXaUJnvd9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SXaUJnvd9a}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 March For Our Lives ?? (@AMarch4OurLives) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AMarch4OurLives/status/1640396971906338816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Shannon Watts, a gun reform activist who founded the Moms Demand Action group after the 2012 Sandy Hook elementary school killings of 20 children and six adults:\par \par \uc2 enltrTHIS is last year's Christmas card from Tennessee Rep. Andy Ogles, a Republican who represents the district that Covenant School is in in Nashville. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/tnleg?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #tnleg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IpkLzZs5m5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IpkLzZs5m5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shannon Watts (@shannonrwatts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shannonrwatts/status/1640410270014263299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And one from the White House :\par \par \uc2 enltrAnother school shooting. I am truly without words \u8212\'20\'14 our children deserve better.\par \par \uc2 We stand \u8212\'20\'14 all of us \u8212\'20\'14 with Nashville.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill Biden (@FLOTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS/status/1640432440542896133?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Fox News producer who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/21/fox-news-producer-dominion-case-misleading-testimony-abby-grossberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed she was \u8220\'20\'1Cintimidated\u8221\'20\'1D into giving misleading testimony}}}\uc2  in the $1.6bn \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  defamation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/23/dominion-fox-news-defamation-lawsuit-winner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  has made an updated court filing after she was fired, Reuters is reporting.\par \par \uc2 Abby Grossberg said Fox\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers left her feeling she \u8220\'20\'1Chad to do everything possible to avoid becoming the \u8216\'20\'18star witness\u8217\'20\'19 for Dominion or else I would be seriously jeopardizing my career at Fox News\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2 . Photograph: Mike Blake/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Grossberg is a former producer for \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Sunday morning show and later \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prime-time show.\par \par \uc2 Both presenters relentlessly pushed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s big lie that the 2020 presidential election was stolen from him, and frequently entertained Trump\u8217\'20\'19s acolytes and supporters who falsely claimed Dominion machines switched his votes to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Grossberg said Fox fired her on Friday, four days after she originally sued and was put on administrative leave. Her amended lawsuits filed Monday in Manhattan federal court and Delaware superior court accuse Fox of discrimination, retaliation, sexism and misogyny.\par \par \uc2 She also filed complaints against Fox on Monday with the US equal employment opportunity commission and New York city commission on human rights, Reuters said.\par \par \uc2 Fox, part of \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Fox Corp\uc2 , said Grossberg \u8220\'20\'1Cignored\u8221\'20\'1D its warning that she might lose her job if she revealed privileged communications with lawyers. It also said it would defend against Grossberg\u8217\'20\'19s legal claims, which were \u8220\'20\'1Criddled with false allegations against Fox and our employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More on this story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/21/fox-news-producer-dominion-case-misleading-testimony-abby-grossberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News producer accuses network lawyers of \u8216\'20\'18coercive\u8217\'20\'19 coaching in Dominion case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'We have to do more to protect our schools'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just spoken at the White House about the Nashville school shooting, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Csick\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Ca family\u8217\'20\'19s worst nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president was addressing a summit of women business leaders in the East Wing, but veered from scripted remarks to address Monday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elementary school shooting}}}\uc2  that claimed the lives of three children and three adults:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s heartbreaking, a family\u8217\'20\'19s worst nightmare, and I want to commend the police who responded incredibly swiftly, within minutes.\par \par \uc2 We have to do more to stop gun violence. It\u8217\'20\'19s ripping our communities apart, ripping at the very soul of the nation. And we have to do more to protect our schools so they are not turned into prisons.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks about the Nashville school shooting on Monday from the White House. Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 Biden repeated his call, made at his state of the union address in February, for lawmakers to act on gun reform:\par \par \uc2 So I call on Congress again to pass my assault weapons ban. It\u8217\'20\'19s about time that we begin to make some more progress, but there\u8217\'20\'19s more to learn.\par \par \uc2 He also addressed mental health, and referred to military personnel who returned home after experiencing trauma:\par \par \uc2 My son [Beau] was in Iraq for a year, [in] other places. So many members of the military are coming back with post traumatic stress after witnessing the violence and participate.\par \par \uc2 Well, these children, these teachers should be should be focusing on their mental health as well.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll: Only one in four Democrats want Biden to run\par \par \uc2 Only one in four Democrats want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to run for a second term, a just released poll by \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  has revealed.\par \par \uc2 More than four in 10 would prefer to see the president step aside for another candidate, according to the poll of self-identified Democrats and Democratic-leaning voters.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 These voters, however, do not have a clear idea of who they would like to see as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 Three in four Democrats (74%) have a favorable opinion of Biden, and just 14% hold an unfavorable view. Yet 44% would like Biden to make way for someone else to run for the White House as a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Only 25% say their preference is for Biden to pursue a second term, while 30% say they have no preference either way.\par \par \uc2 You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_us_032723/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 read the Monmouth poll here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre: Israel reform delay a 'space for compromise'\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has welcomed Monday afternoon\u8217\'20\'19s announcement by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  that he was delaying a judicial overhaul until the next parliament session in a few weeks\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 There has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/26/benjamin-netanyahu-fires-defence-minister-yoav-gallant-judicial-overhaul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widespread unrest}}}\uc2  in the country in protest at the unpopular reform bill.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at her afternoon press briefing, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, praised the Netanyahu move:\par \par \uc2 We welcome this announcement as an opportunity to create additional time and space for compromise. A compromise is precisely what we have been calling for.\par \par \uc2 And we continue to strongly urge Israeli leaders to find a compromise as soon as possible. We believe that it is the best path forward for Israel and all of its citizens.\par \par \uc2 Democratic societies are strengthened by checks and balances, and fundamental changes to a democratic system should be pursued with the broadest possible base of popular support.\par \par \uc2 You can follow the latest on the protests in Israel on our live blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/mar/27/netanyahu-israel-judicial-changes-protests-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli PM Netanyahu says he is \u8216\'20\'18not ready to divide the nation in pieces\u8217\'20\'19 after mass protests over judicial overhaul \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House on Tennessee school shooting: 'Enough is enough'\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had been briefed on the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heartbreaking news of another shooting of innocent schoolchildren}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at her afternoon briefing, Jean-Pierre said \u8220\'20\'1Cenough was enough\u8221\'20\'1D, and reminded reporters that the president called in his state of the union address in February for lawmakers to act:\par \par \uc2 How many more children have to be murdered before Republicans in Congress will step up and act to pass the assault weapons ban, to close loopholes in our background check system, or to require the safe storage of guns?\par \par \uc2 Once again the president calls on Congress to do something before another child is senselessly killed in a preventable act of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said Biden had taken more action than any president before him on gun safety, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/joe-biden-signs-gun-control-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping bipartisan package of reforms last year}}}\uc2 . But, she said, that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough:\par \par \uc2 While we don\u8217\'20\'19t know yet all the details in this latest tragic shooting, we know that too often our schools and communities are being devastated by gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Schools should be safe spaces for our kids to grow and learn and for our educators to teach.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden has reacted to the elementary school shooting in Tennessee that claimed the lives of three children and three adults.\par \par \uc2 The first lady was speaking at an event in Washington DC:\par \par \uc2 We just learned about another shooting in Tennessee, a school shooting. I am truly without words. Our children deserve better and we stand, all of us, we stand with Nashville in prayer.\par \par \uc2 More on this story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least three children and three adults killed in shooting at Nashville elementary school}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 An airport executive who was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to head the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FAA\uc2 ) blasted \u8220\'20\'1Ccheap, unfounded partisan attacks\u8221\'20\'1D for his decision to withdraw, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Phil Washington\uc2 , chief executive of Denver international airport, said Monday he wrote to the president over the weekend to say he was stepping down:\par \par \uc2 I no longer saw a respectful, civil, and viable path forward to senate confirmation.\par \par \uc2 I faced cheap and unfounded partisan attacks and procedural obstruction with regard to my military career that would have further lengthened the already delayed confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans said Washington was unqualified to serve, citing his limited aviation experience and failure to answer some key questions.\par \par \uc2 Democrats were forced to cancel a planned committee vote last week on his confirmation after some senators remained undecided.\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , an independent who caucuses with Democrats, was one of those unconvinced by Washington, even after a one-on-one phone call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration should quickly nominate a permanent \uc2 FAA\uc2  administrator with the necessary, substantial aviation safety experience and expertise,\u8221\'20\'1D she said Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia prosecutors ordered to respond to Trump filing\par \par \uc2 There are developments in another of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal battles, this time in Georgia where a judge has ordered the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office to respond to a motion by the former president to throw out a report by a grand jury investigating his interference in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team also wants all testimony from the inquiry rejected, and district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to be barred from continuing to investigate or prosecute Trump.\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . Photograph: John Bazemore/AP\par \par \uc2 Fulton county superior court judge Robert McBurney ordered Willis to respond by 1 May and state if an in-person hearing is needed to resolve any issues.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Willis said her office would reply through its court filings, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 The filing is a longshot effort by Trump to escape one of many legal challenges he faces, including the state inquiry in New York into a hush money payment to adult film star Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury in that case reconvened this morning as it mulls a felony charge for Trump for hiding a $130,000 payment to cover up an affair.\par \par \uc2 He also faces a twin justice department investigation into his efforts to overturn his 2020 defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and his hoarding of classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida after he left office in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia investigation began shortly after the release of a recording of a January 2021 phone call between Trump and Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  in which suggested his fellow Republican should \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D the exact number of votes needed to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s narrow loss in the state to Biden.\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury heard from about 75 witnesses and considered other evidence before issuing a report that includes recommendations for Willis on criminal charges, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has increased his national lead in the Republican presidential primary but could face a closer tussle with his chief rival, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , in the first two states to vote, new polls show.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has not declared his run but is expected to do so later this spring. Trump has hit the campaign trail, staging his first 2024 rally in Waco, Texas on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has struggled to reconcile support for Trump over the former president\u8217\'20\'19s reportedly imminent indictment in New York with political attacks as he looks to differentiate himself in the primary. Correspondingly, Trump has begun to attack DeSantis in familiar slashing fashion.\par \par \uc2 This morning, a new survey from the Center for American Political Studies at Harvard and the \uc2 Harris Poll\uc2  gives Trump a 26-point national lead over DeSantis, by 50% to 24%, a four-point gain since February.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  was third with 7%. Nikki Haley, the former South Carolina governor, was fourth with 5% support.\par \par \uc2 The website Axios, meanwhile, published the results of two polls from a Republican firm.\par \par \uc2 In head-to-head matches, Public Opinion Strategies put DeSantis eight points up on Trump in Iowa, which will kick off the primary in February 2024, and level in New Hampshire, the second state to vote.\par \par \uc2 But there was better news for Trump when Public Opinion Strategies asked respondents to choose from the whole field of declared and potential contenders.\par \par \uc2 Then, Trump and DeSantis were tied in Iowa while Trump led by 12 points in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 Other surveys have shown such potential for anti-Trump candidates to split the vote and give the former president the nomination without a majority.\par \par \uc2 That happened in 2016, when Trump first won the Republican nomination. That year, the Texas senator Ted Cruz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/2016-election-results/primary/iowa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won Iowa}}}\uc2  before Trump swept to victory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/09/donald-trump-wins-new-hampshire-republican-primary-us-election-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in New Hampshire}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump was not seriously challenged thereafter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Salom\u233\'00\'E9 G\u243\'00\'F3mez-Upegui reports on troubling developments in Florida, a relative refuge in the US south for women seeking full access to reproductive healthcare\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  Republicans earlier this month threatens to reverberate across the American south.\par \par \uc2 Following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization to overturn the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Florida became a strategic refuge for women seeking to access reproductive healthcare from states that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 places as varied as Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Alabama and Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last six months since Dobbs, the number of out-of-state patients coming to [us] for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care has quadrupled,\u8221\'20\'1D Damien Filer, a representative of Planned Parenthood of South, East, and North Florida (PPSEN), told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Jacksonville and Tallahassee, our health centers on the state\u8217\'20\'19s northern border, our general patient load has more than doubled, with the majority being from out of state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/7/BillText/Filed/PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed six-week ban}}}\uc2  introduced earlier this month is expected to pass the Republican-controlled Florida legislature and be signed by the governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . It would go into effect only if the Florida supreme court upholds the current 15-week ban in a case it will decide at some point this year.\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban would include exceptions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life, and the limit would remain at 15 weeks in the case of rape or incest. However, women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the rape and incest exception would be forced to prove their victim status with documents such as restraining orders, police reports or hospital records \u8211\'20\'13 often rendering these exceptions meaningless, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/politics/os-ne-florida-abortion-bill-rape-exception-20230309-xwyvkk5tm5aa3gdslvqrvkdtou-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocates say}}}\uc2 , given the barriers to reporting assault.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/27/florida-abortion-refuge-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  refuge in US south, poised to pass six-week ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steven van Zandt, the musician and actor who starred as Silvio Dante in The Sopranos and plays guitar as Little Steven in Bruce Springsteen\u8217\'20\'19s E Street Band, called \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  his \u8220\'20\'1Cbrother from another mother\u8221\'20\'1D today, in a message of support for the Maryland Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s fight against cancer.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy brother from another mother! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jC6uVIzq7L"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jC6uVIzq7L}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??????Stevie Van Zandt???? (@StevieVanZandt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StevieVanZandt/status/1640209679690153990?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Raskin, 60, is undergoing chemotherapy for large B-cell lymphoma, a process which causes hair loss, and has taken to wearing bandannas. Van Zandt is known for wearing such headgear on stage.\par \par \uc2 In February, Raskin shared a picture of a bandanna given to him by Van Zandt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jamie_raskin/status/1624476400420810752?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1624488293038542852%7Ctwgr%5E2220875057c5df0e94feaa90a96e99ea9bc8f39a%7Ctwcon%5Es3_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2023%2F02%2F11%2F1156350137%2Fstevie-van-zandt-jamie-raskin-bandana-chemo-cancer-springsteen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CLook what I received from one of the greatest musicians on earth, a gift I will treasure almost as much as his song \u8216\'20\'18I Am a Patriot\u8217\'20\'19. You are about to see a step up in my chemo head-cover fashions for the next few months. Rock on Stevie, keep spreading the light.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raskin also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/02/11/1156350137/stevie-van-zandt-jamie-raskin-bandana-chemo-cancer-springsteen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told HuffPost}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI give all honor to Little Steven for creating this look for American men going through something.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Van Zandt, 72, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat gift is from all of us who want to thank you every day for giving us hope that there is a politician that cares about justice!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raskin rose to national prominence during the presidency of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . A professor of constitutional law, he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://raskin.house.gov/2021/1/speaker-pelosi-names-raskin-lead-impeachment-manager"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lead House manager}}}\uc2  in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second impeachment, for inciting the Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 Early on Monday, Van Zandt tweeted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StevieVanZandt/status/1640210540726239233"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 picture}}}\uc2  with Raskin, both with bandannas in place, and his message of support. The actor and musician also posted a picture with Raskin and the \uc2 CBS\uc2  reporter Robert Costa, who he called his \u8220\'20\'1CDC bodyguards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about Raskin, from our book critic, Charles Kaiser :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/jan/09/unthinkable-review-jamie-raskin-son-tommy-capitol-attack-trump-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unthinkable review: Jamie Raskin, his lost son and defending democracy from Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 The headline news so far is the grand jury looking into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hush money payment to an adult film star has reconvened in New York city, and is listening to evidence.\par \par \uc2 But we don\u8217\'20\'19t know yet if the panel, which is meeting for the first time in almost a week at Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s behest, is hearing from new witnesses. Or when it might be asked to vote on a criminal indictment for the former president.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s good health news for Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/pennsylvania-senator-john-fetterman-to-leave-hospital-soon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expecting to leave hospital soon}}}\uc2  after five weeks\u8217\'20\'19 treatment for depression.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, Democratic senator for Massachusetts, says she\u8217\'20\'19s running for a third term in the chamber, and has plans to \u8220\'20\'1Cend corruption in Washington, make the economy work for the middle class, and protect democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Africa, meeting with the leaders of Ghana, Tanzania and Zambia, and seeking to rebuild bridges with nations previously neglected by the US. The vice-president arrived in Africa with a $139m package of bilateral security, economic and development assistance, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Coming up this afternoon: White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is scheduled to brief reporters at 1pm. And \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak later after meeting women business leaders at a summit in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s good news over the health of Pennsylvania senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  has the details:\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  is expected to return to office soon after spending the last five-plus weeks in a hospital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/16/senator-john-fetterman-hospital-clinical-depression"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 receiving treatment for mental depression}}}\uc2 , a spokesperson has said, though the staffer stopped short of offering an exact timeline.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn will be out soon. Over a week but soon,\u8221\'20\'1D Joe Calvello, a spokesperson for the Pennsylvania senator, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/pennsylvania/john-fetterman-depression-hospital-return-soon-senate-pennsylvania-20230324.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Philadelphia Inquirer}}}\uc2  in an article published on Friday. Saying that the team caring for Fetterman at Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s Walter Reed hospital was \u8220\'20\'1Camazing\u8221\'20\'1D, Calvello added: \u8220\'20\'1CRecovery is going really well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Inquirer\u8217\'20\'19s report noted that a hospital stay of more than five weeks is a relatively long time to be receiving inpatient care for depression. But, the report added, a Fetterman aide said the lengthy stay was \u8220\'20\'1Cabout John getting the care he needs and not rushing this\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks is a grain of sand in [the] six-year term\u8221\'20\'1D to which Fetterman was elected, the aide said, according to the Inquirer. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s doing what he needs to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1635721122606874631"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A CNN journalist }}}\uc2  had reported being told earlier in March by a source close to Fetterman that the longer hospital stay resulted from doctors taking extra care to get the senator\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmedication balance exactly right\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A rising star among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , Fetterman checked into Reed to be treated for clinical depression on 15 February. That stay started a week after he was hospitalized for feeling light-headed. He had also suffered a stroke while campaigning last year.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/pennsylvania-senator-john-fetterman-to-leave-hospital-soon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania senator John Fetterman to leave hospital \u8216\'20\'18soon\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump New York grand jury back in session\par \par \uc2 The New York grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over hush money payments to adult film star Stormy Daniels is back at work, and is hearing more evidence Monday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still unclear, however, when the panel, which is meeting in a state office building in Lower Manhattan, might be asked to vote on a possible criminal indictment for the former president.\par \par \uc2 A canine unit provides security at the state office building where a grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reconvened Monday. Photograph: Seth Wenig/AP\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s reconvening was the first time the panel heard testimony since last Monday, the day before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-arrest-remarks-based-on-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump, falsely, insisted he was to be arrested}}}\uc2 . The AP said it confirmed the developments with \u8220\'20\'1Ca person familiar with the matter who spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss secretive proceedings\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Uncertain is whether any additional witnesses might be called to testify.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, spent the weekend furiously denouncing the inquiry on social media, and at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-possible-indictment-stormy-daniels-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally in Texas}}}\uc2 , having previously told supporters of his upcoming arrest.\par \par \uc2 That didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen, and one of his attorneys admitted on Sunday that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unfounded remarks about his imminent detention were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-arrest-remarks-based-on-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mere speculation prompted by \u8220\'20\'1Crumors\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has also drawn ire from opponents and some fellow Republicans for his \u8220\'20\'1Creckless\u8221\'20\'1D rhetoric warning of \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he is indicted. \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/24/trump-rhetoric-hakeem-jeffries-democrats-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s going to get someone killed}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The jury is mulling a felony charge of falsifying business records against Trump after he allegedly tried to hide a $130,000 payment to Daniels, with whom he has denied an affair.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of four current investigations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/20/trump-legal-issues-criminal-investigations-new-york-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dragging down Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for the Republican 2024 presidential nomination}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been movement in recent weeks in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s inquiries into his efforts to overturn his 2020 defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and mishandling of classified documents he hid at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida after leaving office.\par \par \uc2 And in Georgia, Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is looking into his call to the secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , in January 2021 asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D to reverse Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Florence has invited students and their parents from a Florida Christian charter school to come and see Michelangelo\u8217\'20\'19s statue of David to show them the 16th century masterpiece is not pornographic.\par \par \uc2 Hope Carrasquilla, principal of the Tallahassee Classical School, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/25/florida-principal-resigns-michelangelo-david"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was ousted}}}\uc2  after a parent complained children were \u8220\'20\'1Cexposed to pornography\u8221\'20\'1D when they were shown pictures of David in class.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Phil Sears, Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 The school\u8217\'20\'19s governing board told her to stand down or be fired, reflecting the push by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s hard right Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  to impose conservative values in schools and hand parents unprecedented powers.\par \par \uc2 Dario Nardella, the mayor of Florence, the Italian city where the Renaissance masterpiece is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.florence-museum.com/michelangelo-david.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on display at the Accademia Gallery}}}\uc2 , has extended the invitation to Carrasquilla.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, Nardella said confusing art with pornography was \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cecilie Hollberg, the gallery\u8217\'20\'19s director, told the AP: \u8220\'20\'1CTo think that David could be pornographic means truly not understanding the contents of the Bible, not understanding western culture and not understanding Renaissance art.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The agency reported that several parents and teachers plan to protest Carrasquilla\u8217\'20\'19s exit at a school board meeting tonight.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/mar/25/florida-school-principal-fired-michelangelo-porn-desantis-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Florida, parents are always right \u8211\'20\'13 even when they think a Michelangelo is porn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and other Republican House extremists have been gladhanding January 6 defendants at a Washington DC jail. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  has the details:\par \par \uc2 A jail in Washington has become the latest focal point of the US culture wars after a congressional delegation led by the Republican extremist \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  visited defendants charged in 2021\u8217\'20\'19s deadly January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol and championed them as \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical prisoners\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Greene high-fived the detainees and shook their hands, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/wireStory/greenes-dc-jail-visit-pulls-gop-closer-jan-98117113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2 . As the tour group was leaving, the defendants chanted \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go Brandon!\u8221\'20\'1D, an offensive phrase denigrating Democratic president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 . Photograph: Stefani Reynolds/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Greene was joined by fellow far-right Republican members of the House oversight committee during a two-hour tour of the DC jail on Friday. The group included extremist Colorado congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , who embraced Micki Witthoeft, the mother of Ashli Babbitt, the woman shot dead by police as she participated in the Capitol riot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/house-lawmakers-tour-dc-jail-holding-jan-6-defendants-rcna76628"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is at least the second visit that Greene has made in a campaign to reframe the incarcerated January 6 rioters from alleged violent insurrectionists into martyrs of the far-right cause. This time, however, her stunt was joined by Democratic members of the oversight committee who attended the tour so that they could hold their Republican peers to account, they said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t let \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and these \u8230\'20\'26 extremists tell lies about the insurrectionists and their attack on our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the Democratic visitors, Robert Garcia of California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertGarcia/status/1639313975602020352"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said before the tour began}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/marjorie-taylor-greene-led-delegation-to-visit-capitol-attack-defendants-in-jail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene led delegation to visit Capitol attack defendants in jail}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris rebuilding bridges on African tour\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Africa, rebuilding bridges with nations neglected by the US while aiming to blunt China\u8217\'20\'19s growing influence in the region.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president met Ghana\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Nana Akufo-Addo\uc2  on Monday in Accra, and will hold summits with the leaders of Tanzania and Zambia as she promotes US business interests.\par \par \uc2 Harris is the fifth senior Biden administration official to visit Africa this year in what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/03/26/kamala-harris-us-africa-relations-tour-00088889?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico says}}}\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing less than the resetting of relations between the US and the countries she\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled to visit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe energy and creativity of Ghana\u8217\'20\'19s young leaders will shape the future of Africa \u8211\'20\'13 and the world. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5vjmRhZw92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5vjmRhZw92}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1640134640877936642?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2 , the \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador; \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , the treasury secretary; \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , secretary of state; and first lady Jill Biden have all visited in recent months. The president plans to make the trip later this year.\par \par \uc2 Observers say the mending of fences is necessary, and overdue, following the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s attitude towards the continent. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  drew global derision for his 2018 comment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jan/12/unkind-divisive-elitist-international-outcry-over-trumps-shithole-countries-remark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referring to some African nations as \u8220\'20\'1Cshitholes\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris arrived in Africa with a $139m package of bilateral security, economic and development assistance, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Her week-long trip follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/13/african-leaders-gather-in-us-as-joe-biden-aims-to-reboot-rocky-relations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December summit}}}\uc2  hosted by Biden in Washington with African leaders, in which the president announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/dec/14/house-hearing-lgbtq-violence-sandy-hook-biden-african-leaders-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-639a1bbb8f0834f3c0579528#block-639a1bbb8f0834f3c0579528"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was \u8220\'20\'1Call in\u8221\'20\'1D on Africa\u8217\'20\'19s future}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren announced Monday that she\u8217\'20\'19s running for a third term in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts Democrat, a progressive who ran for the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential nomination, says she\u8217\'20\'19s seeking reelection to \u8220\'20\'1Cend corruption in Washington, make the economy work for the middle class and protect democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe\u8217\'20\'19ve won some big victories for working families in Massachusetts and across the country, but there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more to do. So today I\u8217\'20\'19m making it official: I\u8217\'20\'19m running for re-election to keep up the fight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ebG3vJCot3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ebG3vJCot3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@ewarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1640307743352397825?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI first ran for Senate because I saw how the system is rigged for the rich and powerful and against everyone else. I won because Massachusetts voters know it, too. And now I\u8217\'20\'19m running for Senate again because there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren, 73, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1640307743352397825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign video}}}\uc2  released Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 A criminal indictment for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for paying off adult film star Stormy Daniels could come as early as today, as the former president continues to rail against the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake\u8221\'20\'1D investigation by New York prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for confirmation that a grand jury convened by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  has reconvened on Monday, as expected, to hear final testimony in the case sparked by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to silence Daniels about their affair before the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Security has been stepped up around the Lower Manhattan courthouse where the jury has been meeting in secret, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7chicago.com/donald-trump-rally-alvin-bragg-arrest-protest/13025782/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to ABC News}}}\uc2  and other media outlets. Bragg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/da-bragg-investigating-trump-received-threatening-letter-white-powder-rcna76591"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received death threats}}}\uc2  last week, and a suspicious white powder was sent to his office.\par \par \uc2 The sun rises on Monday over the state office building in Lower Manhattan where a grand jury is investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Seth Wenig/AP\par \par \uc2 The former president, meanwhile, spent the weekend furiously denouncing the inquiry on social media, and at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-possible-indictment-stormy-daniels-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally in Texas}}}\uc2 , having previously told supporters falsely that he would be arrested last week.\par \par \uc2 He wasn\u8217\'20\'19t, and one of his attorneys admitted on Sunday that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unfounded remarks about his imminent detention were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-arrest-remarks-based-on-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mere speculation prompted by \u8220\'20\'1Crumors\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has also drawn ire from opponents and some fellow Republicans for his \u8220\'20\'1Creckless\u8221\'20\'1D rhetoric warning of \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath and destruction\u8221\'20\'1D if he is indicted. \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/24/trump-rhetoric-hakeem-jeffries-democrats-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s going to get someone killed}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The jury is mulling a felony charge of falsifying business records against Trump after he allegedly tried to hide a $130,000 payment to Daniels, with whom he has denied an affair.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of four current investigations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/20/trump-legal-issues-criminal-investigations-new-york-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dragging down Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for the Republican 2024 presidential nomination}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been movement in recent weeks in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s inquiries into his efforts to overturn his 2020 defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and mishandling of classified documents he hid at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida after leaving office.\par \par \uc2 And in Georgia, Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is looking into his call to the secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , in January 2021 asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D to reverse Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 While we await developments, have a read of my colleague Ed Pilkington\u8217\'20\'19 s report on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Joseph Tacopina conceding on Sunday that Trump effectively made up his insistence he was to be placed under arrest last week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-arrest-remarks-based-on-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lawyer says ex-president based remarks about arrest last week on \u8216\'20\'18rumors\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics blog readers. We begin the new week where we left the last, watching for a grand jury in New York City to reconvene and possibly hand down a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/trump-wants-to-be-handcuffed-for-court-appearance-in-stormy-daniels-case-sources-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal indictment of }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/22/trump-wants-to-be-handcuffed-for-court-appearance-in-stormy-daniels-case-sources-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for paying off adult film star Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 The episode has turned into something of a three-ring circus, with the former president railing against Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-possible-indictment-stormy-daniels-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weekend rally in Texas}}}\uc2 , having previously told supporters, falsely, that he would be arrested last week.\par \par \uc2 He wasn\u8217\'20\'19t, and one of his attorneys admitted on Sunday that the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s unfounded remarks about his imminent detention were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/26/trump-arrest-remarks-based-on-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mere speculation prompted by \u8220\'20\'1Crumors\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The grand jury, meanwhile, did not sit on Thursday or Friday, and we\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to see if it gets back to business today. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you any developments as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hosts the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Business Summit in Washington DC, and is scheduled to deliver remarks at 2.30pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on a goodwill trip to Africa, meeting leaders of Ghana, Tanzania and Zambia, and a host of business and community leaders. The vice-president is attempting to rebuild relations after then-president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 denouncement of some African nations as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jan/12/unkind-divisive-elitist-international-outcry-over-trumps-shithole-countries-remark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shithole countries}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate convenes this afternoon to take up measures that would formally end the Gulf and Iraq wars of 1991 and 2002. Biden says he supports the repeal of authorizations for military interventions, which advanced to a final vote with bipartisan support last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The first briefing of the week from the White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , is scheduled for 1pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230327ej3r001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
