\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Idaho hospital to stop delivering babies as doctors flee over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 557 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par 19:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Near-total ban on abortions is driving doctors away, hospital says, leading to lack of nearby labor and delivery care for thousands\par \par \uc2 An Idaho hospital has planned to stop delivering babies, with the medical center\u8217\'20\'19s managers citing increasing criminalization of physicians and the inability to retain pediatricians as major reasons.\par \par \uc2 Bonner General Health, the only hospital in Sandpoint, in the north-west of the state, announced on Friday it would no longer provide labor, delivery and a host of other obstetrical services.\par \par \uc2 The more than 9,000 residents of Sandpoint will now forced to drive 46 miles for the nearest labor and delivery care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idahostatesman.com/living/health-fitness/article273303190.html#storylink=topdigest_latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Idaho Capital Sun }}}\uc2  reported.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bonnergeneral.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Bonner-General-Health-Press-Release-Closure-of-LD-3.17.2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2 , the hospital said the decision to eliminate the obstetrics unit stemmed from the \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical climate\u8221\'20\'1D in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHighly respected, talented physicians are leaving. Recruiting replacements will be extraordinarily difficult,\u8221\'20\'1D officials said in a press release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made every effort to avoid eliminating these services,\u8221\'20\'1D the hospital\u8217\'20\'19s board president, Ford Elsaesser, added in the statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hoped to be the exception, but our challenges are impossible to overcome now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The hospital\u8217\'20\'19s statement also said that the closure comes as the number of deliveries at Bonner continues to decline, with only 265 babies delivered last year and fewer than 10 pediatric patients admitted.\par \par \uc2 The hospital also lacks enough pediatricians to manage its neonatal resuscitations and perinatal care, finding no permanent solution after contacting to active and retired physicians to fill vacancies.\par \par \uc2 Hospital officials are hoping to keep obstetrics services available until 19 May, but said it largely depends on staffing.\par \par \uc2 New patients are no longer being seen at the hospital, effective immediately, while current patients are being offered alternative referrals.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=2ahUKEwjp55vK5er9AhXPj4kEHc-rAw8QFnoECA0QAQ&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Froe-v-wade&usg=AOvVaw1GKDPBUZayOuQB5p8RpTlY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in June}}}\uc2  eliminated the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that Roe v Wade established, states with total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have passed laws with the threat of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2022/11/23/1137756183/doctors-who-want-to-defy-abortion-laws-say-its-too-risky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prison time}}}\uc2  for doctors who perform abortions in violation of state law.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court decision legalized an Idaho state ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. The state is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/15/idaho-abortion-ban-texas-law-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first}}}\uc2  to pass a copy of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s controversial bill. Idaho is also one of six that prosecutes doctors for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/idaho-hospital-bonner-general-stops-labor-delivery-services-citing-political-climate-doctor-shortages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 In August, the justice department filed a lawsuit against Idaho for its near-total ban on abortions, with doctors in the state writing in a court brief that physicians were often forced to choose between violating the state ban or federal healthcare law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-lawsuits-washington-f77c346a77bd09b0c1e05f7bcecc9762"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 The implications of the ban is driving doctors out of the state, the Bonner hospital\u8217\'20\'19s press release said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Idaho legislature continues to introduce and pass bills that criminalize physicians for medical care nationally recognized as the standard of care,\u8221\'20\'1D the hospital\u8217\'20\'19s statement said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CConsequences for Idaho physicians providing the standard of care may include civil litigation and criminal prosecution, leading to jail time or fines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Amelia Huntsberger, a Bonner General Health obstetrician-gynecologist, wrote in an email to the Capital Sun that she would be leaving the hospital and the state because of its restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, and because the Idaho legislature was terminating its maternal mortality review committee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a sad, sad state of affairs for our community,\u8221\'20\'1D Huntsberger wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230320ej3k002jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
