\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s make these folks famous\u8217\'20\'19: the leftwing push to raise 18 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 profiles\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,519 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2023\par 10:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Indivisible is targeting little-known GOP House members in swing districts for the 2024 election. Co-founder Ezra Levin says: \u8216\'20\'18They are basically Marjorie Taylor Greenes in how they vote\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Juan Ciscomani. Tom Kean Jr. Brian Fitzpatrick. Marc Molinaro. \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2 . Brandon Williams \u8230\'20\'26 Many Americans would struggle to identify who these people are or what they do.\par \par \uc2 They are all, in fact, Republican members of Congress. And progressive activists argue that their fate is more crucial to the future of American democracy than more high-profile rightwing political figures such as \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indivisible, a leftwing political umbrella movement founded in response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election as president in 2016, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unrepresentative18.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a campaign}}}\uc2  to unseat 18 Republican members of the House of Representatives from districts that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won in the election of 2020.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CUnrepresentatives\u8221\'20\'1D initiative is based on the premise that these 18 districts \u8211\'20\'13 not the safe, deep red ones of Gaetz and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/08/campaign-millions-maga-extremist-marjorie-taylor-greene-marcus-flowers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greene}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 will determine if Republicans maintain control of the US lower chamber next year. They are the \u8220\'20\'1CAchilles heel\u8221\'20\'1D of the Maga (Make America great again) House.\par \par \uc2 The way you accomplish that is by keeping your head down, by not making a lot of headlines\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are folks who are not in the headlines,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ezralevin?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ezra Levin}}}\uc2 , co-founder and co-executive director of Indivisible, acknowledging that the sole exception is Congressman George Santos because of his outlandish lies. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the other 17, I would guess practically no Americans have ever heard of and are not hearing of right now because they have a different pathway to re-election. They understand this. They\u8217\'20\'19re not dummies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although the 18 are in swing districts, they are not really moderates. They are under pressure to raise money for their next election campaign. That means they have to make commitments to donors about how they will vote in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 which is in line with Greene and the Maga wing of the party about 95% of the time.\par \par \uc2 Speaking from Austin, Texas, Levin explained: \u8220\'20\'1CThey are basically Marjorie Taylor Greenes in how they vote. But then that gets to the third step: they\u8217\'20\'19ve got to convince the constituents in their own districts that, while Congress is messed up and there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of dysfunction there, they\u8217\'20\'19re normal, everyday folks who just want the best for their constituents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s tricky to do that when you have a voting record that looks like \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . But that is the strategy. The way you accomplish that is by keeping your head down, by not making a lot of headlines, by not advertising every vote you take that looks like \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These Republicans work hard to cultivate a low profile away from the bright lights of Fox News or other rightwing media, steering clear of hot button topics such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Maga circuses such as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/05/cpac-trump-maga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative Political Action Conference}}}\uc2  (CPAC).\par \par \uc2 But now Levin, a former congressional staffer, intends to shine a light on them and ensure they have no hiding place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a clear goal and that is: let\u8217\'20\'19s make these folks famous \u8211\'20\'13 famous locally, specifically. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make it as clear as possible to their constituents that they are in fact backing up the Maga majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indivisible is coordinating groups in the battleground districts across eight states and supporting them with training, media training and public relations help, and funding for billboards and ads, props and costumes.\par \par \uc2 The effort includes rapid response-style protests calling attention to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 votes and pressuring them to publicly condemn their fellow Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 worst positions, highlighting such instances in local media.\par \par \uc2 Levin hopes that this might sometimes persuade the 18 Republicans to flip their votes, for example on lifting the debt ceiling: six would be enough to stave off a default.\par \par \uc2 In New York we fought on the field that the Republicans chose and I do think that was a mistake\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe second possible outcome is that you don\u8217\'20\'19t flip their vote but everybody knows then in the district that they voted with the Magas. If you accomplish that, then they\u8217\'20\'19re more easy to defeat next year because they\u8217\'20\'19ll have a harder time accomplishing that last step in their re-election strategy, which is trying to convince their constituents that they are not indeed part of the Maga problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats fared much better than widely expected in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, maintaining control of the Senate and only narrowly losing the House \u8211\'20\'13 even that outcome might have been avoided if only the party had not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/23451416/democrats-win-midterms-blue-red-new-york-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 underperformed badly in New York}}}\uc2 . A third of Indivisible\u8217\'20\'19s targets are in the Empire state, traditionally a Democratic stronghold.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn New York many folks on the Democratic side played up an artificial rise in crime,\u8221\'20\'1D Levin recalled. \u8220\'20\'1CThe dominant story was not how extreme these Republicans are and how they\u8217\'20\'19re coming after your freedoms, your \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, your schools, your community, your democracy. It was fought on an entirely different field. We fought on the field that the Republicans chose and I do think that was a mistake. That is a shame because had we taken all those Biden-won seats, there would be a Democratic trifecta right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even so, Levin found plenty of grounds for optimism in the midterms as Republicans fell short of expectations and Trump-endorsed extremists were wiped out in Arizona, Pennsylvania and elsewhere. He did not approve of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/07/democrats-boosted-extremists-republican-primaries-was-that-wise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to boost election deniers}}}\uc2  in Republican primaries \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying with fire, a dangerous strategy\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but believes the 2024 landscape is propitious.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see these 18 Democratic districts currently represented by Republicans, eminently winnable. I see a presidential contest in which the Republican party is tearing itself apart with [Florida Governor Ron] DeSantis or Trump or folks who are trying to take both of them on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I see a Senate map that is indisputably tougher than the presidential and the House map but one that is quite winnable. You look at the polling that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing now in Montana, in Ohio, in West Virginia, in Arizona, some of these tough seats that we\u8217\'20\'19d better hold, and they look pretty darn good for us, which is why for Indivisible\u8217\'20\'19s political work, our north star is retake the House, hold the Senate, hold the presidency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Levin argues that, should Democrats replace the Arizona senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , now an independent who has defended a Senate procedural rule known as the filibuster, with challenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/23/ruben-gallego-arizona-senate-kyrsten-sinema-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruben Gallego}}}\uc2 , they have a shot at reforming the filibuster and working towards the codification of Roe v Wade, the recently overturned supreme court ruling that enshrined a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As long as the Marjorie Taylor Greenes are wielding the gavel, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to have at best a tenuous grip on power\par \par \uc2 Biden is an important part of that equation. Levin notes that the president was widely criticised for focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/joe-biden-speech-political-violence-preserve-democracy-midterm-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 democracy}}}\uc2  in his last two speeches of the midterms campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CHe got a ton of flak for that. There were folks even on our side calling it a strategic blunder. And yet he did indeed double down on that strategy and the proof is in the pudding. It was the best midterm margins arguably in modern American history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is no sign of the Republican fever breaking for now. Greene has risen to prominence in the House and appears to wield influence over the speaker, Kevin McCarthy. Trump and DeSantis are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/donald-trump-ron-desantis-republicans-maga-presidential-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racing to the right}}}\uc2  ahead of the Republican presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 But Levin keeps faith in the survival of US democracy. \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe that the Republican party can be saved. It\u8217\'20\'19s got to be drilled into their heads that as long as the Marjorie Taylor Greenes are wielding the gavel, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to have at best a tenuous grip on power. That is doable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of Republicans were privately and publicly predicting a massive red wave in 2022. They are not dummies. The folks who look at the same numbers I look at know the reason why they lost is because, when the folks got into the voting booth, they looked at the names on the list and they thought, well, the Republicans are being driven by folks who are coming after my schools, my communities, my freedoms, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, my family, I can\u8217\'20\'19t empower them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Levin added: \u8220\'20\'1CTheir brand is in the gutter because they\u8217\'20\'19re empowering the Marjorie Taylor Greenes. They don\u8217\'20\'19t currently have the latitude to kick folks like them out of the party. There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason why George Santos is still a member of the House of Representatives. But if they suffer enough electoral defeats they will be forced into moderation and the dream: to have two pro-democracy parties in the Congress. We\u8217\'20\'19re not there right now but I do think it\u8217\'20\'19s an achievable outcome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230320ej3k001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
