\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Are Texas\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws being used for state-sponsored spousal harassment?\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,250 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2023\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Texas man is suing his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends for helping her get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 whether he wins or not, the lawsuit is sending a terrifying message to women\par \par \uc2 Are Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws being used for state-sponsored spouse harassment?\par \par \uc2 Meet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/10/texas-abortion-law-jonathan-f-mitchell-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jonathan Mitchell}}}\uc2 . The former solicitor general of Texas is not a household name but you\u8217\'20\'19ll be familiar with his work. He\u8217\'20\'19s the architect of the dystopian Texas law that lets private citizens act as vigilantes and sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D the procedure. As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/12/us/politics/texas-abortion-lawyer-jonathan-mitchell.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  noted in a 2021 profile of Mitchell, he\u8217\'20\'19s devoted much of the past decade to \u8220\'20\'1Choning a largely below-the-radar strategy of writing laws deliberately devised to make it much more difficult for the judicial system \u8211\'20\'13 particularly the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 to thwart them.\u8221\'20\'1D In other words: he\u8217\'20\'19s brilliant at finding sneaky ways to inflict his beliefs on everyone else. And he appears to have made it his life\u8217\'20\'19s work to weaponize the law to terrorize and control women.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s latest project is representing a Texas man called Marcus Silva who is currently suing his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends for helping her get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Silva is demanding more than $1m in damages from each of the two friends his ex-wife talked and texted with when she planned her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the woman who provided \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. He\u8217\'20\'19s also planning to sue the manufacturer of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 What gives Silva the right to do this? Good question. Mitchell and Silva have been very creative and are testing the bounds of current \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and homicide laws. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawandcrime.com/abortion/texas-man-files-wrongful-death-lawsuit-against-ex-wifes-friends-who-helped-her-get-abortion-pill-accuses-them-of-murder/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit begins}}}\uc2  by stating: \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the law of Texas, a person who assists a pregnant woman in obtaining a self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has committed the crime of murder and can be sued for wrongful death\u8221\'20\'1D; it then goes on to cite sections of the Texas penal code that talk about homicide but don\u8217\'20\'19t mention \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While procuring and supplying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills is prohibited in Texas, the law is clear that self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t a criminal act. Silva is basically cobbling together interpretations of various different laws to argue that his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends are \u8220\'20\'1Cmurderers\u8221\'20\'1D who are liable for the wrongful death of the terminated fetus.\par \par \uc2 Silva\u8217\'20\'19s case largely rests on private text messages between his ex-wife and her friends. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how he got hold of these messages but his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends were obviously worried he might snoop though her phone. \u8220\'20\'1CDelete all conversations from today,\u8221\'20\'1D one of his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t want him looking through it.\u8221\'20\'1D It\u8217\'20\'19s also clear that Silva\u8217\'20\'19s ex-wife didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to share news of her pregnancy with him because she was afraid of how he\u8217\'20\'19d act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know either way he will use it against me,\u8221\'20\'1D she allegedly wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I told him before, which I\u8217\'20\'19m not, he would use it as [sic] try to stay with me. And after the fact, I know he will try to act like he has some right to the decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to screenshots of private text messages, Silva\u8217\'20\'19s case also includes a photo of what he says is a picture of his ex and her friends from Halloween last year, dressed as characters from The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s tale. \u8220\'20\'1COn Halloween of 2022, [two defendants and Silva\u8217\'20\'19s ex-wife] celebrated the murder by dressing up in Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale costumes for Halloween,\u8221\'20\'1D the complaint says. It seems like he got that photo from the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page of ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s employer, which has now set its page to private.\par \par \uc2 So is Silva going to win? It seems unlikely; many legal experts believe there is no legal basis for the suit. The terrifying thing, of course, is that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really matter whether he wins or not: this lawsuit is more about sending a message to women. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to cause such fear and chilling that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter whether [Mitchell] is right,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joanna Grossman, a law professor at SMU Dedman School of Law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/03/10/texas-abortion-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWho is going to want to help a friend find an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is some chance that their text messages are going to end up in the news? And maybe they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get sued, and maybe they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get arrested, and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to get dropped eventually, but in the meantime, they will have been terrified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I know that we\u8217\'20\'19re only supposed to use the word \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorism\u8221\'20\'1D when talking about brown people but I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how else to describe this lawsuit other than domestic terrorism or state-sponsored spousal abuse. A number of rightwing outlets have published the names of Silva\u8217\'20\'19s ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends and their photos and I imagine they are being harassed by forced-birth activists. Further, Silva isn\u8217\'20\'19t just some random guy with a vendetta. He\u8217\'20\'19s being supported by the former solicitor general of Texas; he has a powerful reactionary machine behind him. And, already, the rightwing media is urging others to see Silva as a blueprint. \u8220\'20\'1CSilva is a model of how men must be proactive in standing up for their rights as fathers,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/restoring-america/faith-freedom-self-reliance/texas-man-rightly-sues-women-who-facilitated-abortion-of-his-pre-born-child"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an op-ed}}}\uc2  in the rightwing Washington Examiner proclaimed. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t some one-off lawsuit. This is part of a playbook.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Republicans want the death penalty for women who have abortions\par \par \uc2 Again, what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Texas is just one part of an exhausting array of increasingly dsytopian assaults on reproductive rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/sc-republicans-propose-bill-subject-women-abortions-death-penalty-rcna75060"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A shocking new bill in South Carolina would make anyone}}}\uc2  who gets an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  subject to the state\u8217\'20\'19s homicide laws, including the death penalty. There are no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Guess who Pornhub\u8217\'20\'19s parent company has been acquired by?\par \par \uc2 A private equity firm called (drum roll please) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2023/03/pornhub-parent-mindgeek-acquired-canadian-private-equity-firm-netflix-documentary-1235302442/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethical Capital Partners.}}}\uc2  As I\u8217\'20\'19m sure I don\u8217\'20\'19t need to tell you, Pornhub isn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly known for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2020/dec/16/pornhub-untold-damage-pain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ethical standards}}}\uc2 . But nor are private equity firms.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I kept begging for pain relief\u8217\'20\'19: the women forced to give birth without gas and air\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGas and air\u8221\'20\'1D, a mix of oxygen and nitrous oxide, is the commonest form of pain relief if you\u8217\'20\'19re giving birth in a British hospital. A number of hospitals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/mar/16/i-kept-begging-for-pain-relief-the-women-forced-to-give-birth-without-gas-and-air"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have recently suspended its use}}}\uc2 , however, after discovering exposure may pose health risks to midwives. Some women are being forced to give birth with nothing but paracetamol for pain relief.\par \par \uc2 Gwyneth Paltrow loves vitamin IVs\par \par \uc2 Some people (me) occasionally eat a gummy vitamin for wellness. Other people (Gwyneth Paltrow) routinely hook themselves up to IVs and drip a cocktail of phosphatidylcholines into their body. It turns out there is such a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/gwyneth-paltrow-iv-drip-1850227472"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thing as too much money}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 French bulldogs are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/mar/15/most-popular-dog-breed-french-bulldog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially the US\u8217\'20\'19s favourite dog breed}}}\uc2 , according to the American Kennel Club. They\u8217\'20\'19ve ousted Labrador retrievers from the top spot after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/877fb7e674fb4df1a0cb0b9aa06c002b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a record 31 years}}}\uc2 . While cute, Frenchies are controversial as their in-breeding means they tend to have a lot of health problems. My advice, as the proud owner of a weird little mongrel, is to go to the shelter and get a mutt. They are paw-fect.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230318ej3i001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
