\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous for Black women to give birth in Texas, and it could be about to get worse\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,945 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2023\par 15:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and a looming Medicaid deadline could make a bad maternal health crisis worse. Will lawmakers act in time?\par \par \uc2 When Nakeenya Wilson learned she was pregnant with her third child, she felt fear, not joy.\par \par \uc2 The Texas mother had nearly lost her life while giving birth to her son in 2016, leaving her with deep anxiety over her pregnancy the following year. Her unborn child became stuck in her pelvis, a complication known as shoulder dystocia. Medical staff straddled Wilson and manually pushed on her stomach, a painful procedure. He emerged blue, limp and not breathing, recalls an emotional Wilson.\par \par \uc2 The situation grew increasingly dire as she began to hemorrhage, almost bleeding to death. From the outset of her hospital visit she says she received poor care from nursing staff, who were uncommunicative, delayed a scheduled induction and kept forgetting her name. Without first informing her, a nurse gave Wilson a drug to halt the excessive bleeding, leading to a spike in blood pressure that had already been elevated during her pregnancy due to pre-eclampsia, placing her at risk for seizure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was scared I was going to die,\u8221\'20\'1D says Wilson. \u8220\'20\'1CI felt ignored and like my pain and my requests for treatment weren\u8217\'20\'19t being taken seriously. It was an incredibly traumatic experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eventually, the bleeding ceased and Wilson\u8217\'20\'19s son recovered. She went home emotionally scarred and reconsidering plans to further expand her family.\par \par \uc2 Wilson\u8217\'20\'19s story is emblematic of the risk pregnant patients, particularly Black women, face in the US. The country holds the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/publications/issue-briefs/2020/nov/maternal-mortality-maternity-care-us-compared-10-countries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest}}}\uc2  maternal death rate among similarly industrialized countries and is the only developed nation where these deaths are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/blog/2022/us-maternal-mortality-crisis-continues-worsen-international-comparison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing}}}\uc2 . In 2021, those deaths surged to their highest levels in nearly 60 years, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/hestat/maternal-mortality/2021/maternal-mortality-rates-2021.htm#anchor_1559670130302"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new data}}}\uc2  from the the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC).\par \par \uc2 In Texas, where Wilson is from, the maternal mortality rate has historically hovered above or close to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/hestat/maternal-mortality/2020/maternal-mortality-rates-2020.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US average}}}\uc2  over the years, about 20.2 deaths per 100,000 live births before the pandemic. Black women are disproportionately affected both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/maternal-mortality/disparities-pregnancy-related-deaths/infographic.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationally}}}\uc2  and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/sites/default/files/legislative/2022-Reports/Joint-Biennial-MMMRC-Report-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , according to the latest data, from 2019. And these disparities persist even when accounting for class: the effects of structural racism on Black mothers overpower socioeconomic factors like household income, so the wealthiest Black women and their newborns will still experience worse outcomes than those from the lowest-income white families, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w30693/w30693.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent California-based study}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Maternal health experts argue that expanding Medicaid coverage for mothers to a full year postpartum would significantly alleviate the glaring crisis in Texas, but state lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/30/texas-maternal-mortality-crisis-black-women-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2  of doing so during their last legislative session in 2021. While no one is currently being moved off Medicaid due to the pandemic public health emergency, that could change {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.medicaid.gov/federal-policy-guidance/downloads/cib010523.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by 1 April}}}\uc2 , when states will be re-evaluating eligibility, adding renewed urgency for lawmakers to act before nearly 3 million Texans \u8211\'20\'13 mostly young adults, children and new moms \u8211\'20\'13 lose coverage.\par \par \uc2 Wilson, a maternal health community advocate, now sits on the state\u8217\'20\'19s Maternal Mortality and Morbidity Review Committee, which studies pregnancy-related deaths and offers recommendations to the state.\par \par \uc2 In December, after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/09/14/maternal-mortality-data-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial delay}}}\uc2 , the state finally released the latest data, from 2019, on maternal mortality in the state. The findings revealed Black communities continue to face the worst pregnancy outcomes in the state: Black women are twice as likely as white women and four times as likely as Hispanic women to die from pregnancy and childbirth \u8211\'20\'13 inequalities that have persisted for a decade. Obstetric hemorrhage \u8211\'20\'13 the leading cause of maternal death in Texas and the complication that nearly killed Wilson \u8211\'20\'13 declined overall in recent years, but Black women experienced an increase of nearly 10%, comprising a quarter of overall cases.\par \par \uc2 When rates are improving for all other populations but getting even worse for Black women, we need to really acknowledge there is a major disconnect in care\par \par \uc2 Nakeenya Wilson\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen rates are improving for all other populations but getting even worse for Black women, we need to really acknowledge there is a major disconnect in care,\u8221\'20\'1D says Wilson.\par \par \uc2 Maternal health advocates hope that state lawmakers seize on attention to the report to help alleviate the problem during the current legislative session, which ends in May. The need to take action has never been greater, they say, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/us-abortion-trigger-bans-laws-tennessee-texas-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complete \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , in effect following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade, places the lives of those who experience complicated pregnancies at high levels of risk.\par \par \uc2 Preventative deaths\par \par \uc2 For years, Texas has only offered Medicaid coverage for 60 days postpartum, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/medicaid/issue-brief/medicaid-postpartum-coverage-extension-tracker/#note-0-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 while nearly 30 states}}}\uc2  have sought to expand their coverage to one year, an option {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/policy-watch/postpartum-coverage-extension-in-the-american-rescue-plan-act-of-2021/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made easier}}}\uc2  by a provision in the American Rescue Plan Act of 2021.\par \par \uc2 Texas is home to the highest number of uninsured residents in the US as well as the highest percentage of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ccf.georgetown.edu/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/Maternal-Health-3a.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uninsured women of childbearing age}}}\uc2 . It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/medicaid/issue-brief/status-of-state-medicaid-expansion-decisions-interactive-map/#:~:text=To%20date%2C%2040%20states%20(including,analysis%20of%20state%20expansion%20activity."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of only 11 states}}}\uc2  that have declined federal incentives to expand Medicaid across the board under the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 Expanding coverage would have a larger impact on women of color: nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marchofdimes.org/peristats/data?reg=99&top=11&stop=653&lev=1&slev=4&obj=1&sreg=48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds of Black women}}}\uc2  are on Medicaid when they give birth, compared with less than a third of white women.\par \par \uc2 In perhaps one of the most striking findings, and in line with previous years\u8217\'20\'19 data, the latest Texas report showed 90% of maternal deaths in the state in 2019 were probably preventable.\par \par \uc2 For years, the review committee\u8217\'20\'19s top recommendation has been to extend Medicaid coverage to new mothers from two months to 12 months, as about one-third of deaths in the state occurred between 43 days to a year postpartum. Continuous healthcare coverage is essential to reducing morbidity and mortality risks, the recent report found.\par \par \uc2 Yet after the Texas house passed a measure in 2021 to expand Medicaid to one year postpartum, the more conservative Texas Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/30/texas-maternal-mortality-crisis-black-women-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sliced that proposal to just six months}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest Texas report showed 90% of maternal deaths in the state in 2019 were probably preventable\par \par \uc2 The six-month extension has yet to go into effect as the federal government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/politics/texas/article/Biden-administration-rejects-Texas-postpartum-17352885.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to approve}}}\uc2  the piecemeal effort, reportedly because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/08/04/texas-medicaid-postpartum-application/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of language}}}\uc2  in the bill that could be interpreted to exclude women who have had abortions. It is still under review by the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Service.\par \par \uc2 As she has in the past four legislative sessions, the Democratic house representative Shawn Thierry is working to mitigate the crisis by filing a package of maternal health bills, among them a fresh {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/Search/DocViewer.aspx?ID=88RHB018241B&QueryText=%22thierry%22&DocType=B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal to extend}}}\uc2  Medicaid to 12 months postpartum that addresses the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s reported concerns. While the leadership of the Texas house {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DadePhelan/status/1601227979421790209?s=20&t=HyfdpyGqZFi-Ir2tIz0QMQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed support}}}\uc2  for an extension, it remains to be seen how the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2023/02/13/lt-gov-dan-patrick-focuses-on-tax-property-tax-relief-and-power-grid-in-top-bills/?sailthru_id=626811f44f757f64bae0fc28&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=politics_02142023&utm_term=Politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultra-conservative senate}}}\uc2  will act.\par \par \uc2 For the first time, the committee that released the recent Texas data factored discrimination into maternal mortality rates, finding it contributed to 12% of deaths.\par \par \uc2 Wilson \u8211\'20\'13 who considers the figure probably the \u8220\'20\'1Ctip of the iceberg\u8221\'20\'1D in the overall picture \u8211\'20\'13 says that the state should make efforts to combat systemic racism in hospital settings, which can often lead to undertreating pain management for people of color.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI had a terrible experience with this nurse, but she is indicative of a wider, institutional problem,\u8221\'20\'1D says Wilson. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to start looking at the healthcare system\u8217\'20\'19s biases \u8211\'20\'13 either implicit or explicit \u8230\'20\'26 or we are never going to see improvement for Black women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a Black mother, Thierry is driven by her own near-death experience giving birth in 2012. During an emergency C-section she was administered an epidural too high in her spine, nearly paralyzing her. Thierry wailed in pain but medical staff dismissed her calls until she begged for anesthesia. The lawmaker, a successful attorney with private health insurance, says she almost died at the hands of medical staff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wasn\u8217\'20\'19t heard, I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t respected and I could have died,\u8221\'20\'1D says Thierry. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my duty now to help make sure other women don\u8217\'20\'19t experience what I went through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thierry has also proposed measures to require healthcare providers and medical students to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/Search/DocViewer.aspx?ID=88RHB011651B&QueryText=%22thierry%22&DocType=B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 be trained in cultural competency}}}\uc2  and implicit biases; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/Search/DocViewer.aspx?ID=88RHB016641B&QueryText=%22thierry%22&DocType=B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  why major disparities exist specifically for pregnant Black women; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/Search/DocViewer.aspx?ID=88RHB006631B&QueryText=%22thierry%22&DocType=B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speed up access}}}\uc2  to state data on maternal death, which faces a significant backlog \u8211\'20\'13 as evidenced by the fact that the report recently released by the state analyzes information from four years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The situation is dire\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Months before Roe fell, ushering in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , Texans were living under a six-week ban considered at the time to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most restrictive \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law in the US}}}\uc2 . Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws now carry no exception for rape, incest or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonpublicmedia.org/articles/news/2022/11/02/436587/to-protect-her-twin-baby-texas-woman-was-forced-to-seek-abortion-care-out-of-state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lethal fetal abnormality}}}\uc2 . Today, performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas is a felony punishable by up to life in prison. The laws, say health experts, have added major barriers to not only elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but life-saving medical intervention during planned pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Despite the law\u8217\'20\'19s narrow exception for the life of the patient, doctors and hospitals \u8211\'20\'13 facing steep criminal and civil penalties \u8211\'20\'13 are often erring on the side of caution. Doctors are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turning away patients}}}\uc2  or delaying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care until life-threatening conditions arise, including infection, sepsis, excessive bleeding and even death, found a study in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMp2207423?query=featured_home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New England Journal of Medicine}}}\uc2 . A handful of other nightmarish stories out of Texas \u8211\'20\'13 including that of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/story/news/2023/02/07/amanda-zurawski-state-of-the-union-biden-speech-texas-abortion-law/69881615007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an Austin woman}}}\uc2  who came close to death in an ICU after contracting a bacterial infection \u8211\'20\'13 highlight the harsh reality denying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for medically complicated pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Texas officials have yet to clarify when the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans allow for emergency intervention, perpetuating confusion and fear among the medical community. In fact, the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/executive-management/20220714_1-0_Original%20Complaint%20Biden%20Admin.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the Biden administration}}}\uc2  to block national guidance that ensures doctors who provide emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care are protected by federal law. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently filed Texas lawsuit}}}\uc2  seeks to clarify those medical exceptions.\par \par \uc2 There is palpable anxiety among advocates and the medical community that this picture will cause maternal mortality rates to rise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe situation here is very dire and extreme. We are already hearing a lot of haunting and traumatic stories,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dr Bhavik Kumar, a member of Physicians for Reproductive Health. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that when places have restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, they also have extremely high maternal mortality rates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the maternal death rate was 62% higher in states that had \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or serious restrictions on access compared to states with stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, according to a 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/publications/issue-briefs/2022/dec/us-maternal-health-divide-limited-services-worse-outcomes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study from the Commonwealth Fund}}}\uc2 . And a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thegepi.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/GEPI-State-of-Repro-Health-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  released in January from the Gender Equity Policy Institute found that women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are nearly three times as likely to die during pregnancy, childbirth or soon after giving birth.\par \par \uc2 Researchers stress that state lawmakers who impose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans also often fail to comparatively invest in maternal and reproductive healthcare access, with one report noting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/publications/issue-briefs/2022/dec/us-maternal-health-divide-limited-services-worse-outcomes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than a third}}}\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -restrictive states have opted to extend postpartum Medicaid coverage for up to one year.\par \par \uc2 Momentum is growing \u8211\'20\'13 even in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://khn.org/news/article/states-consider-postpartum-medicaid-extension-months/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative-led states}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to extend postpartum Medicaid coverage. Thierry hopes this legislative session her Republican colleagues prove they vote consistent with their ostensible pro-life values.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are pro-life then you have to be pro-maternal care,\u8221\'20\'1D says Thierry. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to care as much about \u8216\'20\'18unborn children\u8217\'20\'19 as we do born children and their mothers. There is no in between, otherwise it\u8217\'20\'19s just hypocrisy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230317ej3h001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
