\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The right is stealthily working to remove Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  medication\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 913 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 March 2023\par 15:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal judge is poised to restrict mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 even though the drug has been safely and effectively used in the US for more than 20 years\par \par \uc2 This week a Republican-appointed federal judge weighed whether to grant an injunction that could remove mifepristone, the drug used in most American abortions, from the market nationwide. And the hearing almost happened in secret.\par \par \uc2 US district court judge Matthew Kacsmaryk had initially planned to keep Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing in the case \u8211\'20\'13 in which a group of rightwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are suing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to reverse its 20-year-old approval of mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 quiet. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/news/judge-kacsmaryk-mifepristone-abortion-secret"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a conference call}}}\uc2  with lawyers for the anti-choice groups and the Department of Justice, Kacsmaryk asked attorneys not to disclose the existence of the hearing (\u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a gag order,\u8221\'20\'1D he said repeatedly), and said that the event would only be made public late on Tuesday to minimize popular awareness. \u8220\'20\'1CIt may even be after business hours.\u8221\'20\'1D The judge\u8217\'20\'19s courtroom in Amarillo, Texas, is hours away from any major city. It was only because of a press leak that the hearing was known to the public at all.\par \par \uc2 It was just one of many of the alarming irregularities in the lawsuit, in which Kacsmaryk seems poised to grant the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 wish and issue an injunction that will radically reduce access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 For one thing, the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 standing is exceptionally shaky: it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear why the collection of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents \u8211\'20\'13 including one doctor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/publications/files/so-called_medication_abortion_reversal_7-14-2020_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Delgado}}}\uc2 , whose attempt to design an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -reversal clinical trial sent 25% of the test subjects to the hospital \u8211\'20\'13 have standing to sue the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s especially unclear why they have standing to sue in Amarillo; the federal judicial district has become a popular venue for rightwing litigation in part because Kacsmaryk, an exceptionally conservative jurist willing to publish poorly reasoned, policy-driven opinions, is the only federal judge there.\par \par \uc2 For another thing, the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 requests are exceptionally far-reaching. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups want Kacsmaryk to declare the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone illegal, even though the drug has been available in the US, and proven to be safe, for more than 20 years, and even though a judicial reversal of \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval for a medication would be highly unusual and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2023/02/texas-judge-abortion-case-actually-limited-mifepristone.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only dubiously legal}}}\uc2 . At the hearing on Wednesday, lawyers for the plaintiffs acknowledged that there was no precedent for the court to order the suspension of a long-approved medication. If Kacsmaryk approves the injunction \u8211\'20\'13 and all indications are that he will \u8211\'20\'13 the drug could become inaccessible nationwide, even in Democratic-controlled states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 For another thing, the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 claims are so profoundly divorced from fact that it is difficult to believe that they are being made in good faith. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups \u8211\'20\'13 including the doctor whose study sent women to the hospital \u8211\'20\'13 say that they are challenging the drug because they believe, falsely, that mifepristone is unsafe. Lawyers from the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , the rightwing legal outfit that is representing the plaintiffs and which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/news/2020/04/10/why-alliance-defending-freedom-hate-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 designated as a hate group}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2 , pursued this idea on Wednesday in court. \u8220\'20\'1CHow many more women have to die?\u8221\'20\'1D attorney Erik Baptist asked.\par \par \uc2 In fact, no one dies from mifepristone. One of the most aggressively studied and tested drugs in the world since its creation in France in 1987, mifepristone, which blocks the pregnancy hormone progesterone and stops a pregnancy from progressing, has been found effective and overwhelmingly safe; it has a lower rate of serious complications than Tylenol. One study found that \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant adverse outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D occurred {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3711556/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in less than 1%}}}\uc2  (0.65%) of mifepristone patients; the most common of these was continued pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 What women do die from \u8211\'20\'13 died from in massive numbers before Roe, and will die from again, if medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes unavailable - is illegal surgical abortions.\par \par \uc2 Since Dobbs, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement has correctly been aiming to de-stigmatize illegal, self-managed abortions, encouraging women to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stock up}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plancpills.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the pills}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://laslibres.org.mx/2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in advance}}}\uc2  so that they have them if they need them. The idea was that women shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be scared to use the pills: mifepristone, taken together with the contraction-inducing drug misoprostol, is so overwhelmingly safe and effective that women who could access the pills could confidently and secretly manage their own abortions, even in ban states. But if medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes inaccessible, women may attempt more dangerous methods to self-induce. This is the real reason anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are targeting mifepristone: not because it endangers women, but because it keeps them safe.\par \par \uc2 The injunction doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily have to end medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America as we know it. For one thing, there are already groups, both foreign and domestic, that are mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, including mifepristone, to all 50 states, regardless of local law. Women\u8217\'20\'19s solidarity, inventiveness and determination will always outmatch punitive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes. For another, an established misoprostol-only protocol for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already been proven effective.\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers have already signaled their intention to switch to misoprostol-only; the drug is available over the counter in Mexico. But though they are effective, misoprostol-only abortions are also significantly more painful than those conducted with mifepristone. For the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups in court, that\u8217\'20\'19s likely part of the point.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230316ej3g0018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
