\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Access to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill in the balance as Texas judge hears mifepristone case\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell in Amarillo, Texas \par \uc2 1,266 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 March 2023\par 13:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump-appointed judge says he will rule \u8216\'20\'18as soon as possible\u8217\'20\'19 on case brought by far-right anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups\par \par \uc2 A Texas court heard a closely watched case on Wednesday on the future of a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication amid protests against the presiding judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to publicize the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Justice department officials, drug company attorneys and lawyers from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  gathered in the remote city of Amarillo, Texas, for a hearing before Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk with the district court for the northern district of Texas. Kacsmaryk was asked by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups to grant a preliminary injunction revoking the Food and Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, one of two medications used in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/data_stats/abortion.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50%}}}\uc2  of all abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 A decision overturning approval of the drug would apply nationwide, not only in the states that have banned or restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a hearing that lasted more than four hours, the judge asked both sides questions about the administrative law governing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and whether the plaintiffs had standing to bring the case. Appearing to take pains to seem neutral, he gave little inclination of how he would rule, but promised a decision would come \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible\u8221\'20\'1D. He offered nothing beyond that in terms of a timeline.\par \par \uc2 Attorney Erik Baptist, arguing for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , said \u8220\'20\'1Cany relief must be complete, universal and nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe harms of chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs know no bounds\u8221\'20\'1D. Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been repeatedly found to be extremely safe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny injunction would cause significant harm by depriving patients of a drug that has been on the market for two decades,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Straus Harris, arguing for the Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 One of the alliance\u8217\'20\'19s chief arguments against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  is that it misused its authorities when it originally approved the pill.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  reviewed the drug under its so-called accelerated approval program, which was created in the early 1990s to speed access to the first HIV drugs. Since then, it has been used to expedite drugs for cancer and other \u8220\'20\'1Cserious or life-threatening diseases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The alliance, which was also involved in the lawsuit that led the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade, argues that pregnancy is not a disease and therefore mifepristone should not have been considered for accelerated approval.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe contrast between these illnesses and the \uc2 FDA\uc2  jamming pregnancy into \u8230\'20\'26 the \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations could not be more stark,\u8221\'20\'1D Baptist told Kacsmaryk.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 FDA\uc2  says the group\u8217\'20\'19s argument is flawed on multiple counts. First, \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations make clear that pregnancy is considered a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical condition\u8221\'20\'1D that can be serious and life-threatening in some cases.\par \par \uc2 Second, while the \uc2 FDA\uc2  reviewed the drug under its accelerated approval regime, it did not expedite the drug\u8217\'20\'19s review. In fact, approval only came after four years of deliberation. Instead, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  used regulatory powers under the accelerated program to add extra safety restrictions to mifepristone, including requiring physicians to be certified before prescribing it.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the plaintiffs argued that they have standing to sue because the physicians they represent had to treat women dying or very ill from \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed chemical abortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unlawful actions have harmed women and girls for far too long,\u8221\'20\'1D the alliance concluded.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for the government said that adverse effects requiring medical intervention are exceedingly rare, and that the statute of limitations for challenging the approval of the drug had long run out.\par \par \uc2 Outside, Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers held a \u8220\'20\'1Ckangaroo court\u8221\'20\'1D protest, with demonstrators dressed as judges and kangaroos in reference to Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to keep the hearing secret by not publicizing it in advance on the court\u8217\'20\'19s docket. Anonymous sources leaked the news to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/03/11/texas-abortion-pill-hearing-kacsmaryk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  and it was eventually formally announced on Monday evening. A decision could come as soon as Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of people were in line by 6am CT in order to enter the northern Texas court for the hearing, which was scheduled to begin at 9am.\par \par \uc2 That delay in public notice \u8220\'20\'1Creally has had a chilling effect on our ability to exercise our right to peaceful protest\u8221\'20\'1D, said Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March.\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers planned to hold a mock trial outside the courthouse, reading aloud statements that the Trump-appointed judge has previously made about women, immigration and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to make sure that folks understand exactly what kind of person is running this kangaroo court inside and the ways in which he has actually made very clear that he is not an impartial jurist, but in fact, a politician who is trying to legislate from the bench,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 This was the first hearing in the case, Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine v \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2 . Any decision would probably be appealed to the conservative US court of appeals for the fifth circuit, and possibly to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 If Kacsmaryk overturns the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone, it is unclear how access to the drug would be affected in the short term, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2023/02/texas-judge-abortion-case-actually-limited-mifepristone.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some legal experts argue}}}\uc2  that the agency would not be required to enforce the decision. Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers have said they would continue to prescribe misoprostol, the other drug used in the two-step protocol, which has been found to be effective on its own in ending pregnancies, although at a slightly lower rate than when used in conjunction with mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone has been available in the US since 2000 and internationally since 1988. While it has been found to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2022-02-17/abortion-pill-mifepristone-is-safer-than-tylenol-and-almost-impossible-to-get"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safer than Tylenol}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/2020/07/10/abortion-pill-restricted-fda-record-safer-than-penicillin-viagra/5412810002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viagra}}}\uc2 , it is regulated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wDwQIW56uwo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more strictly than fentanyl}}}\uc2 . The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups hope that Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s conservative history is an indication he will rule in their favor.\par \par \uc2 Although the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine has a Tennessee mailing address, it incorporated in Amarillo in August 2022 before filing suit against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in November \u8211\'20\'13 thereby ensuring the case would be heard by Kacsmaryk, who has called gay people \u8220\'20\'1Cdisordered\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed that being transgender is a \u8220\'20\'1Cmental disorder\u8221\'20\'1D. He has ruled against Biden administration guidelines banning discrimination against transgender people. Another one of his decisions requires minors to obtain parental consent before acquiring birth control.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/news/judge-kacsmaryk-mifepristone-abortion-secret"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Friday call}}}\uc2  with attorneys representing the Alliance, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and the drug company Danco, which manufactures mifepristone, Kacsmaryk asked \u8220\'20\'1Cthe parties avoid further publicizing the date of the hearing\u8221\'20\'1D, citing death threats to court staff. The scheduling of that call was not published on the court\u8217\'20\'19s official docket until after the fact, and Kacsmaryk advised the attorneys that he would not publish notice of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing until \u8220\'20\'1Cafter business hours\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After anonymous sources leaked news of the hearing to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , five media companies and three press freedom groups sent a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://default.salsalabs.org/Tf2737eb3-2da8-44a4-9423-ccfb159de034/f26a2f6e-b588-43c9-8743-98de2e2b1028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to Kacsmaryk, urging him to \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately docket notice of the hearing\u8221\'20\'1D to allow press adequate time to travel to the remote courthouse, and calling his attempt to limit attendance at the hearing \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D. The court\u8217\'20\'19s website was updated with notice of the 9am hearing on Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers planned a second protest for Wednesday evening, with demonstrators encouraged to come dressed as clowns \u8211\'20\'13 in reference to a comment by Kacsmaryk on the Friday call, when he asked attorneys them not to share details of the hearing so \u8220\'20\'1Cwe don\u8217\'20\'19t have any unnecessary circus-like atmosphere\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230315ej3f001e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
