\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Protesters denounce \u8216\'20\'18kangaroo court\u8217\'20\'19 after high-stakes Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill hearing\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell \par \uc2 911 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 March 2023\par 13:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters gathered in a remote Texas city despite efforts by Judge Kacsmaryk to keep the hearing secret\par \par \uc2 Dozens of protesters were gathered outside the JM Jones federal building in downtown Amarillo, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Holding aloft signs that read \u8220\'20\'1CDefend Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CNot Your Uterus, Not Your Opinion\u8221\'20\'1D, they chanted \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D as passing cars honked in support and court security guards looked on.\par \par \uc2 As they stood on the busy street corner, a truck sponsored by the women\u8217\'20\'19s advocacy group UltraViolet circled the block, displaying a large banner reading: \u8220\'20\'1CA majority of Americans support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Judge Kacsmaryk, you can\u8217\'20\'19t hide from us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk, we've got our eyes on you ??\par \par \uc2 Our billboard truck is circling Amarillo, TX today during the hearing that Judge Kacsmaryk tried to keep secret. Our message is clear, you can\u8217\'20\'19t hide from us, the majority of Americans in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/liberateabortion?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #liberateabortion}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jbKnsOO4ut"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jbKnsOO4ut}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 UltraViolet has the #ReproReceipts (@UltraViolet) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UltraViolet/status/1636076446165905408?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The occasion for the protest was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/15/texas-abortion-pill-ban-judge-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four-hour hearing held}}}\uc2  earlier in the day by Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, in a lawsuit challenging the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone. The Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers who planned the protest lamented the fact that the hearing had not been publicized until Monday evening, preventing more protesters from traveling to the remote Texas city, which is roughly an eight-hour drive from Austin and a five-and-a-half-hour drive from Dallas.\par \par \uc2 Citing threats to the court, Kacsmaryk had sought to keep the hearing secret to minimize public attention, a delay that prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067.127.0.pdf?eType=EmailBlastContent&eId=73a02723-c49f-4729-9293-853a0713e8be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outrage}}}\uc2  from media groups who said his efforts were unconstitutional and contravened the public\u8217\'20\'19s right to access highly consequential court proceedings. The controversial case could severely curtail medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide and throw the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority to regulate drugs into disarray. Kacsmaryk said during Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing that he would rule \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Despite the late notice, about 30 demonstrators from the Texas Panhandle and neighboring eastern New Mexico turned out.\par \par \uc2 They were eager to show that Texans support medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a number noted that doing so comes with social and physical risks in a deeply conservative area with lax gun laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou really do have to think your job and your family,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harper Metcalf, a 34-year-old Amarillo resident and member of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March Amarillo, who wore sunglasses and a face mask to prevent anyone she knew who might be driving by from recognizing her.\par \par \uc2 Mario Mireles, a professor of microbiology at nearby Amarillo College, also donned a face mask and sunglasses. It felt \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot riskier here\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, than when he had attended protests at the supreme court in Washington DC last year.\par \par \uc2 Lindsay London, a registered nurse and mother of two, had an explanation for the caution: \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone and everyone can have a firearm here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amarillo residents were joined by demonstrators from Eastern New Mexico Rising, a progressive movement based in the nearby New Mexican towns of Clovis and Portales, who turned out to show their support and in recognition of the fact that Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling could affect the entire nation, including residents of states like New Mexico where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is protected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI served this country to protect our rights, not to have them abolished,\u8221\'20\'1D said Derek White, a 29-year-old member of Eastern New Mexico Rising, who served in the air force for six years, including on deployments to Afghanistan and Iraq.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor every one of us who\u8217\'20\'19s here, there\u8217\'20\'19s three or four people who are scared to be here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Victoria Robledo, a member of Eastern New Mexico Rising. She had called out of work to make it to the demonstration, bringing her four-year-old son and three-month-old baby \u8211\'20\'13 who, she says, has attended many other protests.\par \par \uc2 If Robledo\u8217\'20\'19s baby was the youngest participant, 80-year-old Janda Raker may have been the oldest. A longtime reproductive rights organizer, Raker collaborated with the Dallas-based TEA Fund for six years, to help anyone who called the organization\u8217\'20\'19s helpline \u8211\'20\'13 whether by funding their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care or driving them the four hours to Albuquerque in neighboring New Mexico for their procedure. She says she vividly remembers a time before Roe when unmarried women couldn\u8217\'20\'19t access contraception.\par \par \uc2 Since Texas banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, Raker says she can no longer do that work, but is eager to show her support by demonstrating.\par \par \uc2 Organizers encouraged protesters to don kangaroo costumes in a denunciation of what they view as bogus legal claims before a highly ideological judge known for his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views. Jaime Cruz, 23, heeded the call, arriving in costume and with a gavel in hand. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s going on in there is unconstitutional, so we\u8217\'20\'19re showing the circus that\u8217\'20\'19s going on inside, outside,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lasting legacies is all of his court appointees and that\u8217\'20\'19s made crystal clear with Kacsmaryk cherry-picked to make this decision,\u8221\'20\'1D said London, the registered nurse, in reference to allegations that the plaintiffs effectively chose to file in Amarillo to ensure their lawsuit would appear before Kacsmaryk. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to believe he\u8217\'20\'19s giving justice a fair chance, but I have a feeling he\u8217\'20\'19s made up his mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230316ej3g001hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
