\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump-appointed judge to rule \u8216\'20\'18as soon as possible\u8217\'20\'19 after hearing in  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,396 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 March 2023\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal judge in Texas holds hearing on status of mifepristone, which a far-right group claims is unsafe despite \uc2 FDA\uc2  approvalSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In a hearing today, Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Texas federal judge appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-641213478f08cc8edb7d6cc0#block-641213478f08cc8edb7d6cc0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared open}}}\uc2  to a far-right group\u8217\'20\'19s arguments that could lead to the nationwide banning of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Kacsmaryk said he\u8217\'20\'19d rule on the case \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D Meanwhile, the feud between Trump and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  continues. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411c27e8f089dc4386c2b3d#block-6411c27e8f089dc4386c2b3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to attack}}}\uc2  the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s record, and a group linked to the ex-president has filed a formal complaint over DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411dd6e8f08384b8c708453#block-6411dd6e8f08384b8c708453"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Chinese tycoon linked to \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  and other Trump allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411e7e58f08384b8c7084e4#block-6411e7e58f08384b8c7084e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was indicted}}}\uc2  by the federal government.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411e37c8f08384b8c7084ac#block-6411e37c8f08384b8c7084ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  DeSantis for his opposition to military aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411d6508f08384b8c7083da#block-6411d6508f08384b8c7083da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed exceptions}}}\uc2  to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban for rape and incest, and to protect the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-641219fa8f08384b8c7087df#block-641219fa8f08384b8c7087df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stumped for}}}\uc2  his trademark legislation in a visit to swing-state Nevada, arguing it lowered prescription drug costs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary Lloyd Austin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64120f608f089dc4386c2ffd#block-64120f608f089dc4386c2ffd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to his counterpart in Moscow}}}\uc2  a day after an American drone was downed following a collision with a Russian plane over the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  was once so powerful in the Republican party that he was their nominee for the presidency in 2012, a contest he ended up losing to Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 Today, the GOP has changed so dramatically \u8211\'20\'13 thanks in large part to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 that Semafor reports the Utah senator declined to share his views on whether Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  should run for president:\par \par \uc2 enltrRomney says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to weigh in on whether DeSantis should jump into the GOP presidential primary with striking candor:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrankly, the McCain-Romney-Reagan wing of the party is like three feathers now. So I don't expect having much influence there\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joseph Zeballos-Roig (@josephzeballos) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/josephzeballos/status/1636091337635160068?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden argues trademark legislation lowered prescription drug costs\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is delivering a speech in Las Vegas, Nevada, where he is cheering lower prescription drug prices he credits to last year\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the Inflation Reduction Act.\par \par \uc2 The legislation passed by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic allies in Congress is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/16/biden-climate-healthcare-bill-inflation-reduction-act-democrats-us-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the biggest piece of legislation Washington has enacted to fight climate change}}}\uc2 , and also contained provisions to lower the cost of medications. The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/03/15/fact-sheet-seniors-across-the-country-are-saving-millions-of-dollars-in-health-care-costs-because-of-president-bidens-prescription-drug-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today released data}}}\uc2  on the progress made by the legislation since its passage, while Biden has traveled to the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city to stump for its reforms.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the speech live below:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/cecilia-nowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cecilia Nowell}}}\uc2  was in the room where a Texas judge was considering a case brought by far-right groups seeking to ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she had to say:\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  court heard a closely watched case on Wednesday on the future of a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication amid protests against the presiding judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to publicize the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Justice department officials, drug company attorneys and lawyers from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  gathered in the remote city of Amarillo, Texas, for a hearing before Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, who has been asked by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups to grant a preliminary injunction revoking the Food and Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, one of two medications used in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/data_stats/abortion.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50%}}}\uc2  of all abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 In a hearing that lasted more than four hours, the judge asked both sides questions about the administrative law governing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and whether the plaintiffs had standing to bring the case. Appearing neutral, he gave little inclination of how he would rule, but promised a decision would come \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible\u8221\'20\'1D. He offered nothing beyond that in terms of a timeline.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/15/texas-abortion-pill-ban-judge-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas judge hears case brought by far-right groups seeking to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump-appointed judge seems open to arguments against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\par \par \uc2 A Texas federal judge appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared sympathetic today to arguments from a far-right group trying to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills banned in the United States, according to reporters who attended the hearing in Amarillo, Texas:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust got out of the Amarillo courthouse: Kacsmaryk appeared to seriously entertain claims that mifepristone is unsafe \u8212\'20\'14 and asked plaintiffs for guidance on whether his court could order the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to withdraw approval. Wow.\par \par \uc2 Story with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PerryStein?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PerryStein}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amarimow?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @amarimow}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OrUn3Ya4TL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OrUn3Ya4TL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Kitchener (@CAKitchener) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAKitchener/status/1636076762533617667?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more on this story as it develops.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At his press conference, defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  said he had spoken to his Russian counterpart and insisted Moscow operate military flights in a \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and professional\u8221\'20\'1D manner, while underscoring that the United State will continue flying where international law allows.\par \par \uc2 For the latest on the downing of the US drone and the war in Ukraine in general, follow the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/mar/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-moscow-should-respect-international-airspace-says-uk-defence-minister-after-drone-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: US says drone incident with Russia \u8216\'20\'18is being investigated\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Pentagon officials are due to hold a press briefing shortly, a day after a Russian aircraft hit a US drone flying over the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 US defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  vowed a little earlier today that America will continue to \u8220\'20\'1Cfly and to operate wherever international law allows\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Austin said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis hazardous episode is part of a pattern of aggressive, and risky, and unsafe actions in international airspace. So make no mistake, the United States will continue to fly and to operate wherever international law allows. And it is incumbent upon Russia to operate as military aircraft in a safe and professional manner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can follow all the details of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of the diplomatic fallout from this incident, and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion itself in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/mar/15/russia-ukraine-war-live-moscow-should-respect-international-airspace-says-uk-defence-minister-after-drone-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine war live blog}}}\uc2  and our other stories.\par \par \uc2 The defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , speaks during a virtual meeting of the Ukraine Defense Contact Group at the Pentagon today. Photograph: Andrew Caballero-Reynold/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Senate\uc2  has cleared a crucial hurdle in the nomination process for former Los Angeles mayor Eric Garcetti to become US ambassador to India, after being nominated by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There was bipartisan support in the upper chamber earlier today to advance Garcetti\u8217\'20\'19s nomination and he is now set for a confirmation vote this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Senate advances Eric Garcetti\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for U.S. ambassador to India, 52-42, with the help of seven Republicans. He will be confirmed later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 GOP yes: Young, Hagerty, Collins, Daines, Graham, Marshall, Cassidy\par \par \uc2 Dem no: Kelly, Brown, Hirono\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1636054843197382656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Garcetti\u8217\'20\'19s process from nomination to confirmation has been unusually long and rocky, following allegations that he had not acted on sexual assault and harassment accusations against a top aide, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/03/15/garcettis-ambassadorial-bid-clouded-by-scandal-faces-final-confirmation-test-00087162"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 . Garcetti denied he knew of the accusations before they became public.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is greeted by Los Angeles Mayor Eric Garcetti upon his arrival in Los Angeles last October. In the foreground is congresswoman and now the new mayor of Los Angeles, \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2 . Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmaker \uc2 Greg Steube{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://steube.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-steube-introduces-the-safe-storage-lockers-for-house-office-buildings-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has introduced legislation}}}\uc2  to install weapons lockers in the buildings used by the House of Representatives, so that employees can carry weapons on their commute and store them at work.\par \par \uc2 Here he is on Fox News explaining his proposal:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2  (R-FL) explains his legislation to install weapons lockers in the Capitol:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve gotta have some avenue for law-abiding citizens to be able to protect themselves when they\u8217\'20\'19re walking to and from work that work in our federal office buildings.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/egTk31FTGS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/egTk31FTGS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1636000622641045507?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A Trump-appointed federal judge in Amarillo, Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6411cf1b8f08384b8c708352#block-6411cf1b8f08384b8c708352"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has convened a hearing}}}\uc2  that could result in a nationwide ban on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the request of far-right groups opposed to the procedure. There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling when a decision in the case could come, but it may be as soon as today. Meanwhile, the feud between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  continues, with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411c27e8f089dc4386c2b3d#block-6411c27e8f089dc4386c2b3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning to attack}}}\uc2  the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s record and a group linked to the ex-president filing a formal complaint over DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411dd6e8f08384b8c708453#block-6411dd6e8f08384b8c708453"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Chinese tycoon linked to \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  and other Trump allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411e7e58f08384b8c7084e4#block-6411e7e58f08384b8c7084e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was indicted}}}\uc2  by the federal government.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411e37c8f08384b8c7084ac#block-6411e37c8f08384b8c7084ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  DeSantis for his opposition to military aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/mar/15/trump-desantis-2024-texas-abortion-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6411d6508f08384b8c7083da#block-6411d6508f08384b8c7083da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed exceptions}}}\uc2  to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban for rape and incest and to protect the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill hearing in Texas isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only major court case going on this week. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court may soon decide to overrule itself. Why? So it can get rid of state legislative districts that aren\u8217\'20\'19t as advantageous for Republicans as they would like:\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina supreme court heard oral arguments on Tuesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/north-carolina-voting-rights-cases-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major gerrymandering case}}}\uc2  that could have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/06/supreme-court-voting-rights-moore-v-harper-gerrymander-voter-id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant implications}}}\uc2  for US voting rights.\par \par \uc2 In a highly unusual move, the North Carolina court appears poised to overrule itself and get rid of congressional and state legislative districts it approved last year. The GOP-drawn map that was struck down could have produced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/02/04/north-carolina-congressional-map-struck-down-00005974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11-3 advantage}}}\uc2  for Republicans in the congressional delegation. The one that replaced it was far less advantageous to the GOP and wound up producing a 7-7 split in the 2022 midterm elections. The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision would probably allow Republicans to get a more advantageous map back in place.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/north-carolina-court-gerrymandering-case-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina court appears poised to overrule itself in gerrymandering case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Protesters have gathered outside the federal courthouse in Amarillo, Texas where a judge could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/15/texas-abortion-pill-ban-judge-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as soon as today}}}\uc2  issue a ruling that would stop sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The group includes Jaime Cruz, who dressed up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kangaroo_court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a kangaroo}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Jaime Cruz bangs a gavel in a kangaroo costume during the Women's March protest in Amarillo, Texas. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 As well as others who chose more traditional tactics:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates outside the J. Marvin Jones Federal Building and Courthouse in Amarillo, Texas. Photograph: Moises Avila/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Besides protesters, there was also a lengthy line just to get into the building, where seats for the public are limited:\par \par \uc2 People wait in line to enter the J. Marvin Jones Federal Building and Courthouse. Photograph: Moises Avila/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US prosecutor indicts Trump-linked Chinese tycoon\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that a federal prosecutor has unveiled an indictment against a Chinese tycoon tied to \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  and other top allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know so far about the charges:\par \par \uc2 Ho Wan Kwok, a Chinese tycoon with close links to prominent Trumpist Republicans including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2 , has been indicted on 12 counts relating to an alleged $1bn fraud.\par \par \uc2 The charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/ho-wan-kwok-aka-miles-guo-arrested-orchestrating-over-1-billion-dollar-fraud-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced by the US attorney for the southern district of New York}}}\uc2  on Wednesday include wire fraud, securities fraud, bank fraud and money laundering.\par \par \uc2 Kin Ming Je, a Hong Kong and UK dual citizen also known as William Je and described as Kwok\u8217\'20\'19s financier, was also named in the charges and faced a further count of obstruction of justice.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney for the SDNY, \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/ho-wan-kwok-aka-miles-guo-arrested-orchestrating-over-1-billion-dollar-fraud-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAs alleged, Ho Wan Kwok, known to many as Miles Guo, led a complex conspiracy to defraud thousands of his online followers out of over $1bn.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/15/ho-wan-kwok-arrest-fraud-conspiracy-steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese business tycoon and Bannon ally Ho Wan Kwok arrested in $1bn fraud conspiracy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  apparently moves closer to announcing a presidential run, he earlier this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/desantis-trump-republican-support-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came out in opposition}}}\uc2  to further American aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Though the stance puts him in line with his chief rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , other Republicans were quick to signal their displeasure with DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s comments, including Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and Roger Wicker, the top Republican on the Senate foreign relations committee.\par \par \uc2 Needless to say, Democrats were also not pleased with the governor\u8217\'20\'19s comments, which came in response to a questionnaire from Fox News commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . CBS News reports that on the Senate floor today, the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  hit back at DeSantis:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn his floor remarks, Schumer criticized DeSantis on his Ukraine stance.\par \par \uc2 "I have to wonder what he would have thought if he was around in the 1930's. We know what happened then when many refused to stand up to aggression,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jack Turman III (@jackturmanIII) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jackturmanIII/status/1636022486071386115?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump allies accuse DeSantis of 'shadow presidential campaign'\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-hit-ethics-complaint-trump-super-pac-rcna74977"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2  that allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have filed a formal complaint against \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , accusing the Florida governor of running a \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D that violates the state\u8217\'20\'19s election law.\par \par \uc2 The petition was brought before the \uc2 Florida Commission on Ethics\uc2  by Make America Great Again Inc, a Super Pac aligned with the former president, which asks the government body to investigate \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether pro-DeSantis Super Pacs, his \u8216\'20\'18personally lucrative book tour\u8217\'20\'19 and a continued wave of state-level campaign contributions, among other things, \u8216\'20\'18are unlawful because they serve his personal political objectives, are in furtherance of his personal financial gain at the expense of Florida taxpayers, and are intended to influence his official decision to resign from office,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D NBC News reports.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their report:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies face a tall order in getting the commission to investigate DeSantis, considering he appointed five of the nine members.\par \par \uc2 The draft complaint details steps DeSantis has taken in recent months that appear to orchestrate a coming presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is widely expected to run for president but has not yet formally announced. The complaint alleges, however, that he has already checked all the boxes for someone considering a run for the White House, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-faces-first-major-iowa-test-trump-rcna73632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making stops in early primary states}}}\uc2  ; writing a book (his is titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Courage to Be Free\u8221\'20\'1D); raising tens of millions of dollars to go into a state-level committee that could be transferred to a federal super PAC; and watching a constellation of supporter-led super PACs and an outside nonprofit group pop up, some with the stated intention of getting DeSantis to run for president.\par \par \uc2 The pro-Trump super PAC says those steps, when taken together, violate a handful of Florida laws about officeholders\u8217\'20\'19 accepting illegal gifts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis letter provides ample evidence to support a finding of probable cause by the \uc2 Florida Commission on Ethics\uc2  that Governor DeSantis, in concert with certain associated political committees, political consultants and a 501(c)(4) organization, has solicited and received millions of dollars\u8217\'20\'19 worth of illegal gifts in violation of Florida State ethics laws and the Florida Constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D the draft complaint reads.\par \par \uc2 It is addressed to chairman of the Ethics Commission, Glenton Gilzean, whom DeSantis appointed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 For today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill lawsuit in Amarillo, Texas, reporters on the scene say they lined up at the federal courthouse in the wee hours of the morning for a chance to get inside:\par \par \uc2 enltrBright and early at the Amarillo courthouse. They\u8217\'20\'19re only allowing 19 press and 19 members of the public. No overflow room here. 6am and all the public spots are already taken. The hearing doesn\u8217\'20\'19t start for three hours. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UpJh9iESeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UpJh9iESeb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Kitchener (@CAKitchener) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAKitchener/status/1635961238977904640?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom one big issue to another.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Amarillo?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Amarillo}}}\uc2  covering the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/abortion?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  news. Federal hearing set for this morning could decide the fate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 Dozens showed up before 5am to wait in line for a select number of spots. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/mifepristone?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #mifepristone}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gSdnfMYRjT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gSdnfMYRjT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mireya Villarreal (@ABCMireya) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCMireya/status/1635992690398560257?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Wisconsin, Republican lawmakers who control {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/13/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-gerrymandered-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the badly gerrymandered states\u8217\'20\'19s }}}\uc2  legislature are proposing exceptions to its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-ban-wisconsin-republicans-exceptions-36e41d37ce8ba416ee2f4ad1730aa511"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t restore rights lost when Roe v Wade was overturned last year, Republicans have offered to create exceptions for rape and incest, and to protect the life of the mother. The Democratic governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , meanwhile, has filed a lawsuit attempting to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban, which was passed in 1849.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 Republican Assembly Speaker \uc2 Robin Vos\uc2  told \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2  in an interview Tuesday that he hoped Democrats and Evers would be open to clarifying the health of the mother exception and creating rape and incest exceptions for up to 12 weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Evers said during his successful reelection campaign last year that he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abortion-legislature-government-and-politics-fb862a019c9b7a6f22bc850ec842ca41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 veto any bill}}}\uc2  that does not do away with the ban entirely and return the law as it was before Roe v. Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 A paragraph was deleted from this post to remove incorrect Associated Press copy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump-appointed judge to weigh fate of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\par \par \uc2 This morning, a Trump-appointed federal judge will hear a case brought by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group attempting to stop the nationwide distribution of a drug used in the procedure. A ruling in the group\u8217\'20\'19s favor could upend one of the avenues remaining for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states that banned the procedure following the overturning of Roe v Wade last year. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/cecilia-nowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cecilia Nowell}}}\uc2  is in Amarillo, Texas, for the hearing, and has this report:\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  court is hearing a closely watched case on Wednesday morning on the future of a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication amid protests against the presiding judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to publicize the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Justice department officials, drug company attorneys and lawyers from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  gathered in the remote city of Amarillo, Texas, for a hearing before Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, who has been asked by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups to revoke the Food and Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, one of two medications used in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/data_stats/abortion.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50%}}}\uc2  of all abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 Outside, Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers invited demonstrators to dress as judges and kangaroos for a \u8220\'20\'1CKangaroo Court\u8221\'20\'1D protest, in reference to Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to keep the hearing secret by not publicizing it in advance on the court\u8217\'20\'19s docket. Anonymous sources leaked the news to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/03/11/texas-abortion-pill-hearing-kacsmaryk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  and it was eventually formally announced on Monday evening. A decision could come as soon as Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/15/texas-abortion-pill-ban-judge-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas judge hears case brought by far-right groups seeking to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s judiciary committee will today hold a hearing on gun safety, after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last year to expand the right to carry a concealed weapon nationwide. Democratic senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  is not on the committee, but if he was, one wonders what he would have to say, considering his comments about Republicans in an interview yesterday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A Democratic US senator at the forefront of a push to enact new gun control measures has said Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t give a crap\u8221\'20\'1D about children or gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Connecticut\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who has been a leading force for Democrat gun control efforts since the 2012 Sandy Hook elementary school shooting killed 26 people in his state, 20 of them children \u8211\'20\'13 made the comment in a wide-ranging interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.salon.com/2023/03/14/senator-chris-murphy-salon-talks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Salon}}}\uc2  that was published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In the interview, Murphy said that it was inexplicable for Republicans to claim they care about the wellbeing of children while thwarting efforts to shield them from gun violence, including by blocking legislation that would restrict sales of assault-style weapons.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/chris-murphy-republicans-children-gun-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Murphy: Republicans \u8216\'20\'18don\u8217\'20\'19t give a crap\u8217\'20\'19 about children or gun violence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors in New York involved in the criminal investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s social media company last year started examining whether it violated money laundering statutes in connection with the acceptance of $8m with suspected Russian ties, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The company \u8211\'20\'13 Trump Media, which owns Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Truth Social platform \u8211\'20\'13 initially came under criminal investigation over its preparations for a potential merger with a blank check company called Digital World (DWAC) that was also the subject of an earlier probe by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Towards the end of last year, federal prosecutors started examining two loans totaling $8m wired to Trump Media, through the Caribbean, from two obscure entities that both appear to be controlled in part by the relation of an ally of Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The expanded nature of the criminal investigation, which has not been previously reported, threatens to delay the completion of the merger between Trump Media and DWAC, which would provide the company and Truth Social with up to $1.3bn in capital, in addition to a stock market listing.\par \par \uc2 Even if Trump Media and its officers face no criminal exposure for the transactions, the optics of borrowing money from potentially unsavory sources through opaque conduits could cloud Trump\u8217\'20\'19s image as he seeks to recapture the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The extent of the exposure for Trump Media and its officers for money laundering remains unclear. The statutes broadly require prosecutors to show that defendants knew the money was the proceeds of some form of unlawful activity and the transaction was designed to conceal its source.\par \par \uc2 But money laundering prosecutions are typically based on circumstantial evidence and can be based on materials that show that the money in question was unlikely to have legitimate origins, legal experts said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/15/trump-media-investigated-possible-money-laundering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal investigators examined Trump Media for possible money laundering, sources say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump plans to end DeSantis's 'free ride' with attack campaign\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was once an ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and while he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t broken publicly with him, the former president certainly has. The reason is DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s clear presidential ambitions and the fact that he seems to have a receptive audience in the GOP. Polls routinely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  him as number-two behind Trump among GOP voters\u8217\'20\'19 choice for the presidential nomination next year, with gaps of varying width between the two men. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/03/15/trump-opposition-file-desantis-00087081?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign plans to make sure his lead is as wide as possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe team itself has felt like he has had a free ride without scrutiny for a number of years,\u8221\'20\'1D Bryan Lanza, a Trump associate who worked on his 2016 presidential campaign, told Politico about DeSantis. \u8220\'20\'1CJust because he\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive and willing to fight doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make him Maga. Maga is the policies and there is a tremendous amount of sunlight between Trump policies and DeSantis policies. The more and more that gets highlighted the more DeSantis is going to get exposed as just another member of the establishment and compared to Jeb Bush.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But as the piece makes clear, Trump has lost some support he once had in his first campaign more than six years ago.\par \par \uc2 Tom Marino\uc2  was the co-chair of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pennsylvania campaign in 2015, but has switched his support to DeSantis. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he has to say about the former president now: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was a good policy guy and I\u8217\'20\'19d put him up there with \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  on policy, but presidentially he was a disaster the way he acted, the calling people names.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican civil war brews as Trump prepares to neutralize DeSantis\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. He did it in 2016, and now he\u8217\'20\'19s preparing to do it again next year, if not sooner. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has plans to crush the campaigns of every other Republican that runs for president in 2024, particularly \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor viewed as the second-most popular man in the GOP after the former president. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/03/15/trump-opposition-file-desantis-00087081?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , Trump has a big pile of opposition research to deploy against him, and among its most potent allegations will be accusations that during his time as a federal prosecutor, DeSantis went easy in child pornography cases. Considering he\u8217\'20\'19s already come up with one of his trademark nicknames for the governor \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CRon DeSanctimonious\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 this turns of events seemed inevitable.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  wants the \uc2 National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  to investigate all the largest American railroads, not just \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 , operator of the train that derailed and spilled toxic chemicals in East Palestine, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Texas federal judge is today considering a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups that, if successful, could cut off access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate judiciary committee will hold a hearing on gun safety after the supreme court last year expanded the right to carry a concealed weapon nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230315ej3f001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
