\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump-appointed judge limits information on medication  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  lawsuit\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 815 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 March 2023\par 05:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The suit could determine whether US women can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs, but judge is trying to limit disruptions and protests\par \par \uc2 A judge in Texas overseeing a lawsuit in which a conservative group is challenging the legality of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone scheduled the first hearing in the case for Wednesday, but directed that court officials not make the timing public until the evening before.\par \par \uc2 According to sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/03/11/texas-abortion-pill-hearing-kacsmaryk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , Matthew Kacsmaryk, a US district court judge in Amarillo appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2019, ordered the hearing kept out of the court docket as a way to try to limit disruptions and protests, and also asked that lawyers arguing the case not to disclose information.\par \par \uc2 The hearing will present an opportunity for lawyers at the US justice department, which represents the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ), and the drug\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturer, Danco Laboratories, to present arguments for continued federal approval.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was brought by the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , which seeks to limit rights for LGBTQ+ people, expand Christian practices in public schools and outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Observers said Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision to delay placing the hearing in the public schedule was highly problematic, given the case could affect 40 million US women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith an issue as controversial as this, you want to have as much access as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D Carl Tobias, professor of law at the \uc2 University of Richmond\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s some tension if there are very real security concerns, but justice should tolerate that, too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not surprising people want to have as much access as they possibly can without being a danger to anyone who may also want to observe the proceedings, but it\u8217\'20\'19s certainly troubling if the judge wants the lawyers to be quiet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want people to hear what his criticisms are, what questions he\u8217\'20\'19s asking, how persuasive the arguments are, and to have maximum transparency and openness in federal court proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The case is regarded as the most consequential since a conservative-dominated supreme court containing three Trump picks last year ended the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Dobbs ruling, throwing the question back to the states.\par \par \uc2 The Post said Kacsmaryk told attorneys he wanted to delay publicising the hearing because court staff, and himself and his family, had faced threats.\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk has presided over cases challenging Biden administration policies on immigration, LGBTQ+ rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, but none have been so contentious as the case over mifepristone, which the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved in 2000.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit argues the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was wrong to do so, that the government ignored what it claims to be harmful side effects and that the court should order the regulator to reverse its decision.\par \par \uc2 Julie Marie Blake, an attorney for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , recently told \uc2 CBS\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely failed its responsibility to protect women and girls\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But regulators have repeatedly deemed two-step medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a combination of mifepristone and misoprostol, to be safe.\par \par \uc2 Physicians and health officials have argued in court briefs both that reversing \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone would cause \u8220\'20\'1Cprofound and irreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D to women and that the drug has \u8220\'20\'1Can exceptionally low rate of complications\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates say withdrawal of the drug would have substantial implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The debate has become heated. This month, the national pharmacy chain \uc2 Walgreens{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/03/walgreens-abortion-pills-pressure-conservative-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it would not dispense the drug in 21 states where Republican attorneys general have threatened legal action against its distribution.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said it planned to dispense mifepristone in any jurisdiction where it is legally permissible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce we are certified by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , we will dispense this medication consistent with federal and state laws,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said.\par \par \uc2 California said its public healthcare system would cut ties with the chain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia won\u8217\'20\'19t be doing business with \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 or any company that cowers to the extremists and puts women\u8217\'20\'19s lives at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1632811406344192000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1632811406344192000%7Ctwgr%5Ed12e903f4eaf689f991d01b8179a3157e1649120%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2023%2F03%2F07%2F1161590750%2Fcalifornia-walgreens-mifepristone-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Illinois governor, Jay Pritzker, also condemned the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen across the nation will be denied their right to access healthcare they are legally entitled to because of this awful corporate decision,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovPritzker/status/1631492285757108227?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Walgreens\uc2  must rethink this policy. To all the other pharmacy providers, we\u8217\'20\'19ll stand with you so you can provide this lifesaving care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pritzker said he met the \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  chief executive, \uc2 Roz Brewer\uc2 , to express \u8220\'20\'1Chis deep concern about their position and urged them to rethink their stance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  wrote to the 21 Republican attorneys general to repeat assurances it would not distribute the drug in their states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe intend to be a certified pharmacy and will distribute mifepristone only in those jurisdictions where it is legal and operationally feasible,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  senior director of external relations, Fraser Engerman, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230313ej3d000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
