\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans push wave of bills that would bring homicide charges for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 March 2023\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Proliferation of bills in Texas, Kentucky and elsewhere \u8216\'20\'18exposes fundamental lie of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19, experts say\par \par \uc2 For decades, the mainstream anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement promised that it did not believe women who have abortions should be criminally charged. But now, Republican lawmakers in several US states have introduced legislation proposing homicide and other criminal charges for those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 The bills have been introduced in states such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fastdemocracy.com/bill-search/tx/88/bills/TXB00062304/#billtexts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/recorddocuments/bill/23RS/hb300/orig_bill.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess125_2023-2024/prever/3549_20221215.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://webserver1.lsb.state.ok.us/cf_pdf/2023-24%20INT/SB/SB287%20INT.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arkleg.state.ar.us/Bills/FTPDocument?path=%2FBills%2F2023R%2FPublic%2FHB1174.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas}}}\uc2 . Some explicitly target medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; some look to remove provisions in the law which previously protected pregnant people from criminalization; and others look to establish the fetus as a person from the point of conception.\par \par \uc2 It is highly unlikely that all of these bills will pass. But their proliferation marks a distinct departure from the language of existing bans and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, which typically exempt people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from criminalization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis exposes a fundamental lie of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, that they oppose the criminalization of the pregnant person,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dana Sussman, the acting executive director of Pregnancy Justice. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are no longer hiding behind that rhetoric.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some members of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement have made it clear the bills do not align with their views, continuing to insist that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, rather than pregnant people themselves, should be targeted by criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[We] oppose penalties for mothers, who are a second victim of a predatory \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kristi Hamrick, the chief media and policy strategist for Students for Life of America. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to see a billion-dollar industry set up to profit by preying on women and the preborn held accountable. The pro-life movement as a whole has been very clear on this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America echoed the same sentiment: that the organization unequivocally rejects prosecution of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 The bills are likely to be controversial as they proceed, even within conservative circles: Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2022/dec/13/abortion-restrictions-us-state-legislatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have frequently hit walls}}}\uc2  when trying to pass anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, with lawmakers at odds over exactly how far bans should go.\par \par \uc2 The reproductive justice organization If/When/How points out these bills are an indication of the different wings and splinter groups in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, increasingly evident since the Dobbs decision last year that overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing, post-Dobbs, is a splintering in tactics that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are using, and emboldening on the part of more hardline\u8221\'20\'1D factions within the movement, said Farah Diaz-Tello, senior counsel and legal director at If/When/How.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat has always been an undercurrent\u8221\'20\'1D in the movement, Diaz-Tello added. \u8220\'20\'1CAs we see other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents declaring their opposition to criminalization of people who end their pregnancies, this is the opportunity for them to really step up and put those principles into action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bills being introduced in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arkleg.state.ar.us/Bills/FTPDocument?path=%2FBills%2F2023R%2FPublic%2FHB1174.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas}}}\uc2 ,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fastdemocracy.com/bill-search/tx/88/bills/TXB00062304/#billtexts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/recorddocuments/bill/23RS/hb300/orig_bill.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess125_2023-2024/prever/3549_20221215.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  look to establish that life begins at conception. Each of these bills explicitly references homicide charges for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Homicide is punishable by the death penalty in all of those states.\par \par \uc2 Bills in Oklahoma, South Carolina and Texas also explicitly target medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which so far has fallen into a legal grey zone in much of the country.\par \par \uc2 A bill in Alabama has also been announced, although not yet been introduced, by Republican representative Ernest Yarbrough, that would establish fetal personhood from conception and repeal a section of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that expressly prevents homicide charges for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The state\u8217\'20\'19s current law makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a class A felony, on the same level as homicide, but exempts women seeking abortions from being held criminally or civilly liable.\par \par \uc2 Laws that establish fetal personhood also bring the risk of opening pregnant people up to battery and assault charges for endangering a fetus. Such charges have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/law/2022/may/18/abortion-prosecution-fetal-homicide-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already been documented}}}\uc2  in hundreds of cases, using criminal laws championed in recent decades by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that recognize fetuses as potential victims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt never starts or stops with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sussman of the far-reaching effects of fetal personhood laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat means that not getting prenatal care, not taking pre-natal vitamins, working a job that is physically demanding \u8211\'20\'13 all of those things could impose some risk to the fetus \u8211\'20\'13 and that could be a child neglect or child abuse case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such laws have been used to target pregnant people who have taken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.thinkprogress.org/criminalization-pregnancy-us-43e4741bb514/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prescribed medication, taken illegal drugs or drunk alcohol}}}\uc2  while pregnant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eji.org/news/alabama-mother-prosecuted-for-taking-prescription-during-pregnancy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even when there has been no adverse outcome on the fetus.}}}\par \par \uc2 Some of the bills, such as the one in Arkansas, allow a partner to file an unlawful death lawsuit against a pregnant person who has had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ways in which pregnant people could become a mere vessel for an entity that has separate and unique rights is becoming closer and closer to reality. And there are ways in which this could be used that we haven\u8217\'20\'19t even contemplated yet,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sussman.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230310ej3a001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
