\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 How a pastor is trying to revive a 150-year-old US law to ban  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell \par \uc2 1,403 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 March 2023\par 19:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mark Lee Dickson is trying to get the federal anti-obscenity law at the heart of ordinances enforced across the US\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2  closed her Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic after Roe v Wade fell, the founder and CEO of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health wanted to reopen just across the border in New Mexico, to make care as accessible as possible to Texans who could no longer access it in their state. But anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates had other plans.\par \par \uc2 Hagstrom Miller was considering purchasing a building in the border town of Hobbs when, last November, the city passed an ordinance banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and declaring itself \u8220\'20\'1Ca sanctuary city for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D. Earlier this year, the towns of Clovis and Eunice followed suit, as did the counties of Roosevelt and Lea. Hagstrom Miller and her team decided instead to open their new clinic in Albuquerque, a more progressive city about 200 miles from the Texas border, where they hope providers and patients will feel more welcomed. The clinic is currently awaiting approval of its licensing paperwork before officially opening.\par \par \uc2 There is no ban or gestational limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New Mexico. These cities and counties near the Texas border are writing their own rules, joining a sanctuary movement that began in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 forcing New Mexicans and out-of-state patients visiting the state for care to travel to larger cities like Albuquerque and Las Cruces.\par \par \uc2 The New Mexico state legislature is on the cusp of passing a law that would strike down these ordinances. But pastor Mark Lee Dickson of Right To Life of East Texas says anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates would challenge the law in court, arguing that the federal anti-obscenity law at the heart of the ordinances should be enforced across the US. He hopes that the fight over local ordinances turns into a court battle that culminates in a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Similar fights between cities, states and the federal government could soon spread across the country. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout a national law with the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jurisdictions are going to fight each other,\u8221\'20\'1D said Greer Donley, a law professor at the \uc2 University of Pittsburgh\uc2 . In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4032931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paper}}}\uc2  published last year, Donley and her colleagues predicted a slew of jurisdictional battles over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe were to fall. The ordinance strategy playing out in New Mexico might prove to be among the first.\par \par \uc2 Reviving a 150-year-old law\par \par \uc2 In 2019, Waskom, Texas, became the first \u8220\'20\'1CSanctuary City for the Unborn\u8221\'20\'1D after Dickson convinced the town\u8217\'20\'19s all-male city council to pass legislation declaring it as such. To date, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sanctuarycitiesfortheunborn.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his organization\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1C65 US cities and two counties have passed ordinances outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D Most are in Texas, but others are spread as far as Ohio and Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Before the supreme court overturned Roe last June, these ordinances were unenforceable \u8211\'20\'13 they didn\u8217\'20\'19t actually make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal because Roe superseded them \u8211\'20\'13 and largely irrelevant, as no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics were based in the towns that passed them.\par \par \uc2 But now, with Texans no longer able to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in their home state, New Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s border cities have become appealing alternatives for providers hoping to serve Texans in need \u8211\'20\'13 and targets for the sanctuary city movement.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s unique about the ordinances in New Mexico, unlike those introduced in Texas, is that they do not use language specifically banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Instead, they require locals to abide by a federal law which was passed in 1873, and is still on the books although it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been enforced in more than a century.\par \par \uc2 Nicknamed the Comstock Act after the postal inspector and anti-vice activist Anthony Comstock who advocated for them, the law bans the mailing, importation or transportation of \u8220\'20\'1Cobscene or crime-inciting\u8221\'20\'1D materials including \u8220\'20\'1Cany drug, medicine, article, or thing designed, adapted, or intended for producing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Dickson says this prohibits the transportation of both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and \u8220\'20\'1Cany surgical equipment used for an elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 effectively banning both medication and procedural abortions.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/olc/opinion/file/1560596/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a legal opinion}}}\uc2  issued last December, the justice department wrote that the Comstock Act does not apply to prescribed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications, which are often sent in the mail and can be used for a variety of purposes, including managing miscarriages and stopping a hemorrhage.\par \par \uc2 Dickson disagrees. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone\u8217\'20\'19s ignoring these federal statutes,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn New Mexico, these cities and counties are requiring compliance to federal statutes, and we know that these federal statutes trump state laws and state constitutions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He says that if New Mexico tries to overturn these ordinances, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates will take the fight to the courts. And he hopes that a conservative majority supreme court will see it his way and require the enforcement of the Comstock Act nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Hoping to set up a court battle, Dickson and his fellow anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates are aiming to pass anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordinances across the country where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics are located. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wowt.com/2022/12/09/bellevue-abortion-ban-petition-nearly-halfway-signature-goal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bellevue, Nebraska}}}\uc2 , where CareE Clinics for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Reproductive Excellence operates a location, Dickson says anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have gathered enough signatures to petition the city council to vote on an ordinance. (Care is planning to open another location in Pueblo, Colorado, where the city council narrowly rejected a sanctuary ordinance in December.) Next, they hope to pass ordinances in Bristol, Virginia, where Bristol Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://khn.org/news/article/abortion-clinic-bristol-tennessee-virginia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relocated}}}\uc2  from Tennessee last year, and Danville, Illinois, where a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wcia.com/news/abortion-clinic-coming-to-danville/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clinic}}}\uc2  is trying to open.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Our focus is on buying time\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 State leaders have taken a strong stand against the eastern New Mexican cities and counties that have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , advancing multiple strategies to overturn the bans.\par \par \uc2 On 23 January, New Mexico attorney general Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Torrez filed an extraordinary writ asking the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court to invalidate the bans, saying that they violate the state constitution. A decision has yet to be issued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis, ladies and gentlemen, is not Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D Torrez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nmag.gov/new-mexico-attorney-general-files-extraordinary-writ-to-secure-womens-right-to-reproductive-healthcare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CLocal communities are not empowered to regulate medical services. They are not empowered to regulate access to health care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 25 January, Democratic state representatives introduced HB 7, the Reproductive and Gender-Affirming Health Care Freedom Act, a bill which would prevent public entities, including ??local municipalities, from restricting or discriminating against people seeking reproductive or gender-affirming health care. The bill is likely to pass this session with a Democratic majority in the legislature.\par \par \uc2 But Dickson says that HB 7 won\u8217\'20\'19t stop the local bans. \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever the state passes doesn\u8217\'20\'19t supersede these federal statutes,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. The state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cproblem really isn\u8217\'20\'19t with our ordinances. Their problem is with the laws that Congress passed in 1873.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in eastern New Mexico, a coalition of progressive citizens have come together as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://enmrising.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eastern New Mexico Rising}}}\uc2 , with the aim of collecting enough petition signatures to force Roosevelt county to put its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to a referendum vote. (The coalition attempted a similar petition in Clovis, gathering 447 signatures, but the city clerk ruled that only 238 of the needed 269 signatures could be verified.) Their aim is to repeal the ordinances so that locals can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care if a court battle does end up dragging out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur focus is just on buying our local people more time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laura Wight, cofounder of Eastern New Mexico Rising. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more time that we can buy a safety net for our local citizens so that they can get the medication they need and get the health care access they need legally, that\u8217\'20\'19s what we care about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hagstrom Miller hopes that local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wholewomanshealth.com/abortion-wayfinder/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wayfinder program}}}\uc2 , which helps patients schedule out-of-town appointments and access financial and logistical support, will be able to help patients reach their Albuquerque clinic, but she acknowledges that travel just isn\u8217\'20\'19t an option for many patients \u8211\'20\'13 such as those with children, limited financial resources or facing domestic violence. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://data.census.gov/table?q=S1701:+POVERTY+STATUS+IN+THE+PAST+12+MONTHS&g=0100000US,$0400000&tid=ACSST5Y2020.S1701https://data.census.gov/table?q=S1701:+POVERTY+STATUS+IN+THE+PAST+12+MONTHS&g=0100000US,$0400000&tid=ACSST5Y2020.S1701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US census}}}\uc2 , New Mexico ranked as the third poorest state in the country in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo many people are being forced to carry pregnancies against their will, or navigate doing their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with pills\u8221\'20\'1D because they cannot travel, she said. \u8220\'20\'1COur work still needs to be to restore access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all the communities at the federal level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230309ej39001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
