\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Five women denied  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  care in Texas sue state over bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,690 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2023\par 11:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The women were refused abortions despite their nonviable pregnancies posing a serious risk to their health. Plus, the secrets of lifelong friendshipsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Five women denied abortions in Texas, along with two doctors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have sued the state after they were refused \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care}}}\uc2  despite experiencing severe complications with their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 None of the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 fetuses had a chance of survival. The state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are supposed to allow for the procedure in cases where there is a fatal diagnosis for the fetus, as well as when the pregnancy poses substantial harms to the pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s health.\par \par \uc2 And yet, under the overlapping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in effect in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 which threaten doctors with losing their medical licenses, hundreds of thousands of dollars in fines and up to 99 years in jail for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care \u8211\'20\'13 the plaintiffs claim they were not given the healthcare they needed and were entitled to, writes Poppy Noor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are scared and outraged at the thought of being pregnant in this state,\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda Zurawski, one of the plaintiffs in the case said on Tuesday in a press conference about the lawsuit in front of the Texas capitol in Austin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are the lawyers aiming for? \u8220\'20\'1CWe want the state of Texas to acknowledge the women behind me should have received timely \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Molly Duane, the lead litigator in the case, outside the Texas capitol. She said the lawsuit aimed to establish that what happened to the plaintiffs was a violation of their basic human rights according to the Texas constitution.\par \par \uc2 Biden reportedly considers detaining migrant families in major reversal\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is considering detaining families who cross into the US illegally as it prepares to end Covid-19 restrictions at the US-Mexico border, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/07/biden-migrant-families-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to officials familiar with the plans}}}\uc2 . That would be a significant reversal after officials in late 2021 stopped holding families in detention facilities.\par \par \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  officials are working through how to manage an expected increase of migrants at the border once the pandemic curbs that have been in place since 2020 are lifted in May. Detention was one of several ideas under discussion and nothing had been finalized, the officials said.\par \par \uc2 If families were detained, they would be held for short periods, perhaps a few days, and their cases expedited through immigration court, one official said. The officials were not authorized to speak publicly about internal deliberations and spoke on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , declined to comment on \u8220\'20\'1Crumors\u8221\'20\'1D that the policy was under consideration. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that it is, I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that it\u8217\'20\'19s not,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She refused to say whether President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  believed the detention of families was humane.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do immigration advocates say? \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration is seeking to find a balance that protects the rights of those fleeing persecution and violence and the desire to enhance the orderliness of asylum processing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sergio Gonzales, the executive director of the Immigration Hub. \u8220\'20\'1CDetaining families has no place in this quest. We implore the administration to reject this shameful, retrograde practice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  feared \uc2 Fox\uc2  hosts may have gone \u8216\'20\'18too far\u8217\'20\'19 on 2020 voter fraud claims, court files show\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  said the Fox News hosts \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  and Laura Ingraham maybe \u8220\'20\'1Cwent too far\u8221\'20\'1D in their coverage of voter fraud claims, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/08/rupert-murdoch-fox-news-hosts-2020-voter-fraud-claims-dominion-voting-systems-court-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an email submitted as evidence}}}\uc2  in the defamation lawsuit brought by \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  against \uc2 Fox\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dominion is suing Fox News Networks for $1.6bn, accusing the cable TV network of amplifying debunked claims that their voting machines were used to rig the 2020 US presidential election against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in favor of Biden.\par \par \uc2 The reams of documents that became public on Tuesday offer a window into \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s internal deliberations as it covered the election. They show top executives, producers and hosts discussing concerns about the network\u8217\'20\'19s reputation and casting doubt on the plausibility of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 More than 6,500 pages were released on Tuesday, although the full extent of the evidence is not clear as many filings are heavily redacted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did Murdoch say? In one exhibit, Murdoch, the chair of \uc2 Fox Corporation\uc2 , emails Fox News president Suzanne Scott the day after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration, asking: \u8220\'20\'1CIs it \u8216\'20\'18unarguable that high-profile \uc2 Fox\uc2  voices fed the story that the election was stolen and that January 6th an important chance to have the result overturned\u8217\'20\'19? Maybe Sean and Laura went too far. All very well for Sean to tell you he was in despair about Trump but what did he tell his viewers?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has backpedalled after mocking a disabled \uc2 Twitter\uc2  employee in tweet \u8216\'20\'18storm\u8217\'20\'19. Haraldur Thorleifsson was locked out of his computer, but after nine days of no answer from the company, decided to tweet the chief executive to find out if he still had a job only to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/mar/07/elon-musk-twitter-employee-feud-haraldur-thorleifsson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met with laughter and questions about his disability}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK home secretary, \uc2 Suella Braverman\uc2 , has denied the\par \par \uc2 government is breaking the law with its immigration proposals, despite telling Conservatives there was a more than 50% chance the plans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2023/mar/08/braverman-small-boats-plan-law-mo-farah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be incompatible with the European convention on human rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US is preparing to relax Covid-19 testing restrictions for travellers from China as soon as Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/08/us-expected-to-ease-covid-testing-for-arrivals-from-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to two people familiar with the decision}}}\uc2 . The curbs were put in place on 28 December and took effect on 5 January during a surge in infections in China when Beijing suddenly eased pandemic restrictions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House said it backed legislation introduced on Tuesday by a dozen senators to give the administration new powers to ban the Chinese-owned video app TikTok and other foreign-based technologies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/mar/07/white-house-bipartisan-bill-tiktok-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if they posed national security threats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators announced yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/07/ohio-train-derailment-norfolk-southern-us-safety-board-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a special investigation into the rail operator Norfolk Southern}}}\par \par \uc2 after a\par \par \uc2 derailment on the Ohio-Pennsylvania border in February and several other accidents, including the death of a train conductor just hours earlier on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Laura Bates \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18For teenage girls, escaping harassment, revenge porn and deepfake porn is impossible\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Laura Bates wrote the definitive book on online misogyny, which led to the police installing a panic alarm in her home. Bates explains how the \u8220\'20\'1Cmanosphere\u8221\'20\'1D radicalizes boys, how the media feeds the problem \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/mar/07/laura-bates-for-teenage-girls-escaping-harassment-revenge-porn-and-deepfake-porn-is-impossible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 why she is still hopeful}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Teenagers live in a world dominated by phones, platforms for constant communication, online porn and internet videos. For millions of girls, what that means is terrifyingly clear: \u8220\'20\'1CThe impossibility of escaping from harassment, revenge pornography, deepfake porn \u8211\'20\'13 just a whole bombardment,\u8221\'20\'1D Bates says. \u8220\'20\'1CI was talking to a 14-year-old girl at a book event the other day. She said 10 boys had messaged her, pressuring her to send them nude pictures, in a single night. That landscape of what teenage girls are navigating is completely new.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/mar/08/international-womens-day-2023-events-around-the-world-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Day 2023: events around the world \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: \u8216\'20\'18It feels unconditional\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 the secrets of lifelong friendships\par \par \uc2 , according to lifelong friends\par \par \uc2 Friends are essential to our health and happiness, and even affect how long we live. Research shows overwhelmingly that friendship is good for us. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not their primary purpose but friendships have this massive effect on your mental health and welfare, and on your physical health and welfare \u8211\'20\'13 they even affect how long you\u8217\'20\'19re going to live,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dunbar.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at the data, the effect is far stronger than all the things your family doctor worries about on your behalf. This is my pitch for the \uc2 NHS\uc2 : just find everybody a friend or two.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/mar/08/it-feels-unconditional-the-secrets-of-lifelong-friendships-according-to-lifelong-friends"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emma Beddington spoke to friendship lifers}}}\uc2  who have stayed close over decades of good and bad times and everything in between. Are there any secrets, and do they have advice for the rest of us?\par \par \uc2 Climate check: EU targets 40% of clean tech to be made within the bloc by 2030\par \par \uc2 The EU executive is considering a target that would lead to 40% of the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s clean tech being made in Europe by the end the decade, as part of a response to a wave of subsidies from the US and China. According to a draft of the EU\u8217\'20\'19s Net-Zero Industry Act, which is due to be outlined next week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/eu-sets-target-of-40-of-clean-tech-to-be-made-within-the-bloc-by-2030"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40% of green tech needed to meet the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s climate and energy targets}}}\uc2  should be made in the EU by 2030. The 40% target, which could change before the draft is finalized, is part of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s answer to the US Inflation Reduction Act (IRA), which offers $369bn of subsidies to green-tech manufacturers, as well as China\u8217\'20\'19s long-running policy of lavish state support for the sector. Critics argue the IRA discriminates against European companies selling to the US and provides inducements for them to shut up shop in Europe and move production to America.\par \par \uc2 Last\par \par \uc2 thing: \u8216\'20\'18Alligators don\u8217\'20\'19t make good pets, y\u8217\'20\'19all\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Texas zoo rescues reptile stolen as egg\par \par \uc2 A Texas zoo has retrieved an 8ft alligator that was stolen as an egg more than 20 years ago, then kept as a back-yard pet. In an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post accompanying footage of three agents gingerly lifting the reptile into a truck and releasing it into a zoo enclosure, the state parks and wildlife department said: \u8220\'20\'1CAlligators don\u8217\'20\'19t make good pets, y\u8217\'20\'19all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A Parks and Wildlife Department spokesperson said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/08/texas-zoo-rescues-alligator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a game warden found the animal}}}\uc2 , named Tewa, during an unrelated investigation in Caldwell county last month. A woman confessed to taking an egg from Animal World and Snake farm zoo, near Austin. She did not have a permit to keep the alligator as a pet.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230308ej38001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
