\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  attacks \u8216\'20\'18shameful\u8217\'20\'19 Fox News over use of January 6 footage \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,574 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2023\par 20:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader accuses host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  of \u8216\'20\'18manipulating\u8217\'20\'19 images of Capitol attack provided by House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8226\'20\'22 Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A military veteran accused of telling an undercover \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent about a plan to \u8220\'20\'1Cwipe out\u8221\'20\'1D the nation\u8217\'20\'19s Jewish population was convicted on Tuesday of storming the Capitol during the January 6 riot.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that Virginia resident Hatchet Speed, a former navy reservist assigned to an agency that operates spy satellites, will be sentenced on 8 May. He was convicted by US district court judge \uc2 Trevor McFadden\uc2  in a trial without a jury.\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW: U.S. District Judge \uc2 Trevor McFadden\uc2  has convicted Navy Reservist Hatchet Speed on all counts for joining the mob that stormed and occupied the U.S. Capitol Building on Jan. 6. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mvfXfpl5Tc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mvfXfpl5Tc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jordan Fischer (@JordanOnRecord) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JordanOnRecord/status/1633133081958703105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Speed was found guilty on all five charges, including a felony count of obstructing an official proceeding, namely the 6 January 2021 joint session of Congress to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  recorded Speed\u8217\'20\'19s conversations with an undercover agent more than a year after the riot, the AP reported. Speed told the agent that he marched to the Capitol with members of the far-right Proud Boys extremist group.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now, after a day in which \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ears must have been ringing loudly.\par \par \uc2 The rightwing Fox News host copped a barrage of criticism, from Democrats, the White House, the family of a fallen law enforcement officer, and even Republican senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  for his skewed presentation of footage of the January 6 Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 The videos were controversially gifted to Carlson by a generous congressional benefactor in the form of Republican speaker Kevin McCarthy, and he aired some of them on Monday night, portraying a violent mob of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -incited rioters as \u8220\'20\'1Cpeaceful, orderly and meek\u8221\'20\'1D sightseers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House lambasted Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  over the introduction on Tuesday of a bill that would further restrict the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, from 15 to six weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, denounced as \u8220\'20\'1Ca rumor\u8221\'20\'1D a report that the administration was considering reinstating a Trump-era immigration policy that would detain families at the southern border. But a number of Democrats say they are concerned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the defense secretary, made an unannounced trip to Iraq, promising to keep US military forces in the country, almost exactly two weeks before the 20th anniversary of the 2003 Iraq war that toppled \uc2 Saddam Hussein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A report claimed Democrats are growing fearful that a third-party candidate could take votes away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during the 2024 presidential election and hand Republican favorite and former president Trump a ticket back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden laid out some of his budget plans in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/07/opinion/joe-biden-medicare.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guest opinion piece}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , highlighting the preservation of Medicare as a priority and bashing Republicans over benefits for future generations. The president will unveil his full budget on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Please join us again tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican leader in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , has criticised Fox News for misrepresenting the January 6 riot after his counterpart in the House gave \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  exclusive access to 41,000 hours of security footage.\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Asked by reporters if Kevin McCarthy had made a mistake, McConnell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1633188651805954056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMy concern is how it was depicted, which was a different issue. Clearly the chief of the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 , in my view, correctly describes what most of us witnessed firsthand on January 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson made first use of the footage on Monday night, seeking to portray the Capitol rioters as peaceful protesters.\par \par \uc2 In fact, on 6 January 2021 supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stormed the Capitol after he told them to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D in service of his lie that his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the result of electoral fraud.\par \par \uc2 The riot was an attempt to stop certification of that result. It failed, but nine deaths have been linked to the attack, including suicides among law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s broadcast stoked outrage among Democrats and those who survived the attack or lost family members through it.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, blasted Carlson for creating \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most shameful hours we have ever seen on cable television\u8221\'20\'1D and showing \u8220\'20\'1Ccontempt for the facts, disregard of the risks, and knowing full well he was lying to his audience\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Carlson, Schumer said, \u8220\'20\'1Ctold the bald-faced lie that the Capitol attack, which we all saw with our own eyes, somehow was not an attack at all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In what counted for strong remarks from a very cautious, not to say ruthlessly partisan operator, McConnell added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a mistake, in my view, for Fox News to depict this in a way that is completely at variance with what our chief law enforcement official here at the Capitol thinks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/07/jan-6-footage-tucker-carlson-brian-sicknick-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Sleaze-slinging\u8217\'20\'19 Fox News denounced by family of January 6 officer who died}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more on Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 troubles by my colleague Martin Pengelly, who has news of another complaint affecting \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rightwing empire:\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 US Federal Election Commission\uc2  complaint over the collusion of Fox News with the Trump campaign in 2020 could be the first of many, the complainant said, amid continued fallout from dramatic court filings in Dominion Voter Systems\u8217\'20\'19 $1.6bn defamation suit against the network.\par \par \uc2 Media Matters for America\uc2 , a liberal watchdog, filed its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FEC}}}\uc2  complaint last week, over the revelation that \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  personally gave \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law and adviser, confidential information about a Biden campaign ad.\par \par \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  and \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  at a 2014 movie premiere in New York. Photograph: Patrick McMullan/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 A progressive political action committee, End Citizens United, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/fox-corp-trump-campaign-hit-fec-complaint-rcna73342"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also}}}\uc2  filed a complaint.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://harvardlawreview.org/2016/03/defining-the-press-exemption-from-campaign-finance-restrictions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defined}}}\uc2  by the Harvard Law Review, \uc2 FEC\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccampaign finance restrictions do not apply to costs associated with producing news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Media Matters alleges that \u8220\'20\'1Cpress exemption\u8221\'20\'1D does not apply to Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s decision to give the Biden ad to Kushner.\par \par \uc2 Saying the move was \u8220\'20\'1Cdiametrically opposed to \uc2 Fox Corporation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regular press activity\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/media-matters-filing-complaint-fec-over-rupert-murdoch-sharing-confidential-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2  says: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Fox Corporation\uc2 , through Murdoch, appears to have engaged in the exact type of campaign activity to which the commission has repeatedly affirmed the press exemption does not apply.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTherefore, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox}}}\uc2  Corporation cannot try to exploit the press exemption to avoid the consequences of making an illegal corporate in-kind contribution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The complaint seeks the maximum fine permitted and \u8220\'20\'1Cappropriate remedial action\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/06/fox-news-federal-election-commission-complaint-trump-collusion-rupert-murdoch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News hit with election complaint after Biden ad given to Trump son-in-law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House is adding its voice to a barrage of criticism aimed at Fox News and \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Csanitizing\u8221\'20\'1D the January 6 Capitol riot by airing selected footage on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  branded the rightwing network, and its star host, \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful\u8221\'20\'1D for their skewed presentation of the attack, which attempted to portray the violent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters who overran the Capitol as tourists.\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  addresses reporters at the White House on Tuesday. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, was equally dismissive at her Tuesday briefing to reporters of Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s claims the mob was merely \u8220\'20\'1Csightseeing\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Anybody who watched that video with their own eyes, in a real way, and saw what happened on that day, would disagree. The president has been very clear January 6 was the worst attack on our democracy since the Civil War.\par \par \uc2 We should be focused on making sure that never happens again. We hope that keeping the Capitol and Congress safe and secure remains congressional leaders\u8217\'20\'19 number one goal.\par \par \uc2 All you have to do is watch those videos and see how horrific it was, see how sad it was. It was an attack on our democracy.\par \par \uc2 Her mention of congressional leaders and their priorities was presumably directed at Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy, who caused outrage by handing over about 44,000 hours of footage from the attack exclusively to Carlson.\par \par \uc2 The primetime Fox host is a Trump loyalist who repeatedly pushed the big lie of a stolen 2020 election on air, despite revelations that he and other Fox presenters and executives who also promoted it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/feb/27/rupert-murdoch-deposition-dominion-lawsuit-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 knew it was false}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/07/jan-6-footage-tucker-carlson-brian-sicknick-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Sleaze-slinging\u8217\'20\'19 Fox News denounced by family of January 6 officer who died}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden family immigration move reports infuriate Democrats\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  says the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8217\'20\'19t comment on rumors that are out there\u8221\'20\'1D about the Biden administration potentially reinstating a Trump-era rule of detaining immigrant families at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/06/us/politics/biden-immigration-family-detention.html?referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported that the move was under consideration}}}\uc2  to stem an expected migrant surge once Title 42, a policy stemming from the Covid pandemic that allowed the swift deportation of migrants, is ended.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not saying it is, I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying it isn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre, the White House press secretary, said at her Tuesday afternoon briefing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department of homeland security is working through ways on how to go forward once Title 42 is lifted. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to let them do their work. [The president] is going to use the tools that he has before him to make\u8230\'20\'26 the immigration system safe, orderly and humane.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ben Ray Luj\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 . Photograph: Eddie Moore/Albuquerque Journal/ZUMA/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The report angered congressional Democrats. New Mexico senator \uc2 Ben Ray Luj\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  told Punchbowl he was frustrated it didn\u8217\'20\'19t come up when he and other Hispanic senators met with homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a time to have honest conversations with one another,\u8221\'20\'1D Luj\u225\'00\'E1n said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is another one of those surprises \u8211\'20\'13 if it\u8217\'20\'19s true \u8211\'20\'13 that was covered by the media. Fortunately for the media, we continue to find out decisions that are being made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas will hold a virtual meeting with congressional Hispanic caucus members at 5pm ET to discuss the uproar over the Times report, Punchbowl says.\par \par \uc2 More on this subject:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/08/biden-us-mexico-border-title-42-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18carrot and stick\u8217\'20\'19 approach to deter migrants met with anger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has expressed its \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep condolences\u8221\'20\'1D to the families of US citizens who were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/us-citizens-kidnapped-mexico-matamoros-tummy-tuck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed in Mexico }}}\uc2  by members of a suspected drugs cartel.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at her daily briefing at the White House, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still working with Mexican officials to learn more and to have all Americans returned to the United States.\par \par \uc2 President Biden has been kept updated on this incident. Senior members of the White House has have also been engaged. We extend our deepest condolences to their families and friends.\par \par \uc2 She added that US investigators were working with Mexican authorities to establish details of the incident.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/us-citizens-kidnapped-mexico-matamoros-tummy-tuck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two Americans kidnapped in Mexico found dead, officials say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Talking of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in Republican strongholds, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is backing five Texas women who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/03/07/1161486096/abortion-texas-lawsuit-women-sue-dobbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing the state}}}\uc2 , having been denied the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/03/07/statement-from-vice-president-harris-on-lawsuit-on-behalf-of-texans-harmed-by-the-states-abortion-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement from the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s office}}}\uc2  at the White House on Tuesday blasted Texas legislators for passing near-total block on abortions:\par \par \uc2 When I convened health care providers at the White House in September 2021 in wake of Texas SB 8, we discussed the harm that doctors and nurses feared their patients would experience as a result of Texas\u8217\'20\'19 extreme laws. Now, multiple women impacted by these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans announced a joint lawsuit against the state of Texas, showing those fears have turned into reality.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit includes devastating, first-hand accounts of women\u8217\'20\'19s lives almost lost after they were denied the health care they needed, because of extreme efforts by Republican officials to control women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies.\par \par \uc2 Many extremist \u8216\'20\'18so-called\u8217\'20\'19 leaders espouse \u8216\'20\'18freedom for all,\u8217\'20\'19 while directly attacking the freedom to make one\u8217\'20\'19s own health care decisions. Like the overwhelming majority of Americans, the President and I believe women \u8211\'20\'13 in consultation with their doctors \u8211\'20\'13 should be in charge of their reproductive health care, not politicians.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re about to hear from White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  at the daily White House briefing, but she\u8217\'20\'19s already made clear the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s feelings on Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal, introduced to the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature this morning.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article272845850.html#featured-carousel-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement to the Miami Herald}}}\uc2 , Jean-Pierre says the move would \u8220\'20\'1Cban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before many women know if they are pregnant\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Politicians like Governor DeSantis espouse \u8216\'20\'18freedom for all,\u8217\'20\'19 while directly attacking the freedom to make one\u8217\'20\'19s own healthcare decisions. This proposal is wrong and out of touch with the overwhelming majority of Americans, including Floridians, who support a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 This ban would prevent not just the nearly four million Florida women of reproductive age from accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after six weeks, but would also impact the nearly 15m women of reproductive age who live in states across the South with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and would no longer be able to rely on Florida as an option to access care.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a furiously busy day so far in US politics, and we still have the daily White House press briefing to come.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, blasted Fox News, and its star rightwing host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , for their \u8220\'20\'1Cshameless manipulation\u8221\'20\'1D of footage of the January 6 Capitol riot aired on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Carlson attempted to portray a violent mob \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters who carried out the deadly insurrection as peaceful sightseers enjoying a day out, and the backlash has been swift and strong.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s loyalist Republican legislature handed extremist governor and probable White House hopeful \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  a key policy objective by proposing a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the defense secretary, made an unannounced trip to Iraq, promising to keep US military forces in the country, almost exactly two weeks before the 20th anniversary of the 2003 Iraq war that toppled \uc2 Saddam Hussein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats are growing fearful that a third-party candidate could take votes away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during the 2024 presidential election and hand Republican favorite and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a ticket back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated House and Senate face a bruising legislative session, which began this morning. Outnumbered by a Republican supermajority in both chambers, the best the party\u8217\'20\'19s members will be able to do on many pieces of legislation is to offer dissent.\par \par \uc2 Still, they\u8217\'20\'19re as upbeat as they can be, and some are saying it with flowers. Here\u8217\'20\'19s first-term state representative Christine Hunschofsky \u8217\'20\'19s view as she prepares to do battle: caffeine, a desk fan and a colorful array of petals.\par \par \uc2 enltrView from my desk this first day of the 2023 Florida Legislative Session - coffee, fan, and flowers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FlaPol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FlaPol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/znWE1njkW9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/znWE1njkW9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Representative Christine Hunschofsky (@RepHunschofsky) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepHunschofsky/status/1633141767183777796?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida's lawmakers seek six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 The Florida legislature is back in session, and lawmakers have wasted no time in promoting an agenda favorable to extremist Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , including a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The bill was filed Tuesday morning as DeSantis, seen as a likely candidate for his party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, was preparing to deliver his state of the state address.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Wade Vandervort/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/politics/os-ne-florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks-bill-20230307-62zzgqxbkbcufmhwukfcc5knqy-story.html?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=Breaking%20News&utm_content=3701678208440"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Orlando Sentinel}}}\uc2 , Republican state senators Erin Grall and Jenna Persons-Mulicka introduced the bill, which builds on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/florida-abortion-ban-ron-desantis-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week ban}}}\uc2  that the legislature approved and DeSantis signed into law last year.\par \par \uc2 Unlike the existing law, the bill for the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban does contain exceptions for rape and incest, up to 15 weeks of pregnancy, and allows for exceptions for medical emergencies that threaten the life or serious harm to the mother, the newspaper reports.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has previously said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.clickorlando.com/news/politics/2023/02/01/we-will-sign-florida-gov-desantis-champions-potential-6-week-abortion-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will sign any new, more restrictive \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  legislation}}}\uc2  presented to him, and with a Republican supermajority in both chambers of the Florida legislature, its passage is seen as almost certain.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists have been critical of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s clampdown since the Supreme Court swept away last summer half a century of federal protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Last month, a Florida couple who are unable to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced they would have to bring their fatally ill baby to term and have it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/18/florida-abortion-law-couple-birth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 die after delivery}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last August, a Florida judge ruled a 16-year-old was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/florida-pregnant-teenager-abortion-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not mature enough}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to consent to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , effectively a court-ordered pregnancy for a minor child.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/05/florida-republicans-push-rightwing-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Republicans seek new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions amid broad rightwing push}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats are becoming increasingly fearful that a third-party candidate could take votes away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during the 2024 presidential election and hand Republican favorite \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a ticket straight back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The claim comes in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/03/07/dems-fret-about-a-no-labels-spoiler-ticket-00085809?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 article on }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/03/07/dems-fret-about-a-no-labels-spoiler-ticket-00085809?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico Playbook}}}\uc2  this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA new two-page memo from Third Way, obtained by Playbook, takes aim at the potential \u8216\'20\'18unity ticket\u8217\'20\'19 being promoted by the centrist group No Labels,\u8221\'20\'1D it says.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Dominic Gwinn/ZUMA Press Wire/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith tens of millions of dollars in financial backing, No Labels\u8217\'20\'19 stated intention is to nominate a moderate alternative to potential extreme major-party nominees as an insurance policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut Third Way notes that No Labels has been cagey about what scenario would prompt it to move forward, including whether it would stand down if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  seeks reelection. In any case, the memo argues, a third-party ticket would mainly peel off Democrats, ultimately boosting the former president who tried to steal an election and incited a riot on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conclusion is inescapable. No Labels is committed to fielding a candidate that will, intentionally or not, provide a crucial boost to Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 and a major obstacle to Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D they write.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, they\u8217\'20\'19ll make it far more likely \u8211\'20\'13 if not certain \u8211\'20\'13 that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000186-ba78-db60-a3bf-faf8e9550000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 You can read the memo in full here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Schumer blasts 'shameful' Fox over January 6 footage\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, has delivered a scathing rebuke of Fox News and its rightwing host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulating\u8221\'20\'1D selected footage of the January 6 riot aired on his show last night.\par \par \uc2 On the chamber floor this morning, he accused the network and its star presenter of disdain towards politicians who were at the Capitol when it was overrun by a violent mob of Trump supporters, and the law enforcement officers who tried to defend it:\par \par \uc2 Last night, millions of Americans tuned into one of the most shameful hours we have ever seen on cable television.\par \par \uc2 With contempt for the facts, disregard of the risks, and knowing full well he was lying to his audience, Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  ran a lengthy segment arguing the January 6 Capitol attack was not a violent insurrection.\par \par \uc2 By diving deep into the waters of conspiracy, and cherry picking from thousands of hours of security footage, Mr Carlson told the bald faced lie that the Capitol attack,which we also with their own eyes, somehow, not an attack at all.\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer: Last night, millions of Americans tuned into one of the most shameful hours we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen on cable television. By diving deep into the waters of conspiracy and cherry-picking from thousands of hours of security footage, Mr. Carlson told the bold-faced lie\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dKEw2tJVKw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dKEw2tJVKw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1633127061530492928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He tried to argue it was nothing more than a peaceful sightseeing tour. Can you imagine, a non-violent demonstration,a perfectly fine and appropriate instance of people expressing their opinion? I so many others who were here in the Capitol, and millions and millions of Americans are just furious with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy today.\par \par \uc2 Many of my staff were here at the Capitol on January 6, their lives were put in danger, as were the lives of many of my colleagues, as well as police, maintenance staff, reporters, countless others.\par \par \uc2 To say January 6 was not violent is a lie. A lie pure and simple. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen a primetime cable news anchor manipulate his viewers the way Mr Carlson did last night.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen an anchor treat the American people and American democracy with such disdain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Austin makes surprise trip to Iraq\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the defense secretary, made an unannounced trip to Iraq on Tuesday and promised the US would maintain its military presence in the country, almost 20 years after it led an alliance that toppled \uc2 Saddam Hussein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUS forces are ready to remain in Iraq at the invitation of the government of Iraq,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd these forces are operating in a non combat, advise assist and enable role to support the Iraqi led fight against terrorism. This is a critical mission. And we\u8217\'20\'19re proud to support our Iraqi partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Iraqi Kurdish regional government president Nechirvan Barzani (right) and defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  in Erbil, Iraq, on Tuesday. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 His visit comes just two weeks before the 20th anniversary of the 2003 invasion that cost tens of thousands of Iraqi civilians their lives and created the instability that many believe paved the way for the rise of Islamic State militants after the western alliance withdrew in 2011, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Austin, the agency says, is the most senior Biden administration to visit Iraq, and was the last commanding general of US forces there after the invasion. He spoke with Iraqi prime minister Mohammed al-Sudani.\par \par \uc2 Sudani said in a statement that his government\u8217\'20\'19s approach was to maintain balanced relations with regional and international governments based on shared interests and respect for sovereignty, and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe stability of Iraq is the key to the security and stability of the region.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US has 2,500 troops in Iraq, and 900 more in Syria, to help \u8220\'20\'1Cadvise and assist\u8221\'20\'1D local troops in combating Islamic State, which seized swathes of territory in both countries from 2014.\par \par \uc2 Between 185,000 and 208,000 Iraqi civilians were killed in the preceding war, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://watson.brown.edu/costsofwar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Costs of War Project}}}\uc2  by the Watson Institute for International Studies at \uc2 Brown University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalist and election denier who still refuses to accept the reality of her defeat in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s governor\u8217\'20\'19s race last November, is emerging as a favorite to become the former president\u8217\'20\'19s running mate in 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-37766378-f037-4bb5-944b-e6069915d954.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lake, a former television reporter turned combative rightwing politician, is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmodel\u8221\'20\'1D for whom he might choose, according to Axios sources \u8220\'20\'1Cwho discussed the topic with him\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Chief among her attributes is her unwavering loyalty and willingness to defend him, \u8220\'20\'1Cno matter the issue or controversy\u8221\'20\'1D, the outlet says.\par \par \uc2 But it warns:\par \par \uc2 Trump friends say Lake carries a big downside. He wants no risk that his running mate could outshine him. Lake would be assumed to be angling for president from the day she entered the White House. And of course losing her winnable governor\u8217\'20\'19s race hurts her mojo.\par \par \uc2 There will be inevitable speculation that the story comes from from within the Lake camp itself, especially given this statement from Trump spokesperson Steve Cheung : \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone who thinks they know what President Trump is going to do is seriously misinformed and trying to curry favor with \u8216\'20\'18potential\u8217\'20\'19 VP candidates. President Trump will choose his running mate on his own time, and those who are playing the media game are doing so at their own peril.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  admits she cried \u8220\'20\'1Cuncontrollably\u8221\'20\'1D for more than 30 minutes following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2017 inauguration, and as she and outgoing president Barack Obama were leaving the White House for the final time.\par \par \uc2 The concession comes in the former first lady\u8217\'20\'19s her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.audible.com/pd/Michelle-Obama-The-Light-Podcast-Podcast/B0BTJ8DDXD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Audible podcast}}}\uc2 , which launches Tuesday, a clip of which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/politics/michelle-obama-podcast-clip-trump-inauguration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided to People magazine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen those doors shut, I cried for 30 minutes straight, uncontrollable sobbing, because that\u8217\'20\'19s how much we were holding it together for eight years,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama says of the moment Air Force One was readied to take them from Joint Base Andrews on 20 January, 2017.\par \par \uc2 enltrI had so much fun talking to my good friend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hodakotb?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HodaKotb}}}\uc2  for the first episode of The Light Podcast, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HGMedia?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HGMedia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We talked about parenting, overcoming self-doubt, and the importance of finding your light.\par \par \uc2 Listen now on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/audible_com?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Audible_com}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vl6kht3SU1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vl6kht3SU1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TheLightxAudible?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TheLightxAudible}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wo7x3izUOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wo7x3izUOi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  (@MichelleObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichelleObama/status/1633105311132274689?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou walk through the Capitol, you wave goodbye, you get on Marine One, and you take your last flight flying over the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D where there weren\u8217\'20\'19t that many people,\u8221\'20\'1D she added in a blatant dig at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false boast, articulated by his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jan/22/sean-spicer-trump-press-secretary-loud-brash-pugnacious-period"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pugilistic first press secretary }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jan/22/sean-spicer-trump-press-secretary-loud-brash-pugnacious-period"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean Spicer}}}\uc2  , that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis was the largest audience to ever witness an inauguration \u8211\'20\'13 period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The podcast is hosted by TV presenter Hoda Kotb. In the first episode, entitled \u8220\'20\'1CKids just want our gladness\u8221\'20\'1D, Obama tells her: \u8220\'20\'1CThat day was so emotional for so many different reasons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were leaving the home we had been in for eight years, the only home our kids really knew. They remembered Chicago but they had spent more time in the White House than anywhere, so we were saying goodbye to the staff and all the people who helped to raise them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Carlson condemned for 'sanitizing' Jan 6 riot footage\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first take on the January 6 Capitol riot footage, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/22/tucker-carlson-jan-6-footage-kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversially provided to him}}}\uc2  as an exclusive by Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy, was widely condemned on Tuesday for \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/03/06/media/tucker-carlson-fox-news-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sanitizing}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D the deadly insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The rightwing TV host showed selected clips from Capitol security cameras on his Fox News show on Monday night, including small pockets of supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wandering around, and a particular focus on the so-called Q-Anon shaman Jacob Chansley, sentenced in November 2021 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/17/qanon-shaman-jacob-chansley-sentenced-capitol-attack-role"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than three years in prison}}}\uc2  for his part in the riot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe footage does not show an insurrection or a riot in progress. Instead it shows police escorting people through the building,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson told his viewers, parroting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s narrative that the rioters were simply sightseeing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTaken as a whole, the video does not support the claim that January 6 was an insurrection. In fact, it demolishes that claim.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrQuite the statement here from the family of \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  officer Brian Sicknick tonight:\par \par \uc2 "Every time the pain of that day seems to have ebbed a bit, organizations like Fox rip our wounds wide open again and we are frankly sick of it. Leave us the hell alone..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V8O5jkl9pR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/V8O5jkl9pR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oliver Darcy (@oliverdarcy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverdarcy/status/1632952103764148225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/tucker-carlson-new-video-provided-speaker-mccarthy-falsely-depicts-jan-rcna73673"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC points out}}}\uc2 , footage Carlson didn\u8217\'20\'19t air shows police and rioters engaged in hours of violent combat, or the assaults on about 140 law enforcement officers. Several people, including police officers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/03/kyle-defreytag-us-capitol-attack-police-officer-dies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost their lives during or after the attack}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the family of Brian Sicknick, a \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officer who died a day after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/27/capitol-rioter-assaulted-officer-brian-sicknick-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confrontation with the rioters}}}\uc2 , issued a statement condemning Carlson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time the pain of that day seems to have ebbed a bit, organizations like Fox rip our wounds wide open again and we are frankly sick of it. Leave us the hell alone,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads in part.\par \par \uc2 On CNN, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , a Republican former congressman and member of the House January 6 committee, called Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s presentation \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, condemned McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s decision to hand the footage to Fox, adding it could lead to the same thing happening again:\par \par \uc2 enltrSCHUMER: "I condemn Mr. Carlson for siding with the enemies of democracy. I strongly condemn Speaker McCarthy's actions and fiercely oppose his decision to share this footage with Carlson."\par \par \uc2 "Conduct like theirs is just asking for another January 6 to happen," he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1633126680117280768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Other media outlets are also trying to obtain the 44,000 hours of security camera footage given to Carlson, so far without success. McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Monday it was working to arrange it, but gave no details.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been laying out some of his budget plans today in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/07/opinion/joe-biden-medicare.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guest opinion piece}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , and wastes little time bashing Republicans over benefits for future generations.\par \par \uc2 The president, whose full budget proposal is set to be unveiled on Thursday, says expanding Medicare will be a priority to maintain a \u8220\'20\'1Crock-solid guarantee that Americans have counted on to be there for them when they retire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden writes:\par \par \uc2 For decades, I\u8217\'20\'19ve listened to my Republican friends claim that the only way to be serious about preserving Medicare is to cut benefits, including by making it a voucher program worth less and less every year. Some have threatened our economy unless I agree to benefit cuts.\par \par \uc2 Only in Washington can people claim that they are saving something by destroying it.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s returning to a tactic that served him well during last month\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union speech, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/09/biden-republican-cut-medicare-social-security-florida-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when he goaded Republicans}}}\uc2  over plans by Florida senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , among others, to incorporate the termination or slashing of welfare benefits, including Medicare and social security, into policy.\par \par \uc2 It prompted some hasty backtracking and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/28/rick-scott-republican-senator-tax-rises-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrambling by Scott}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/03/01/politics/mcconnell-nrsc-scott-rescue-america/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a stern rebuke}}}\uc2  from Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plans for preserving Medicare, meanwhile, include what he says will be \u8220\'20\'1Ca modest increase\u8221\'20\'1D in the contributions of wealthiest Americans.\par \par \uc2 Raising the Medicare tax rate from 3.8% to 5% on income exceeding $400,000 per year, including salaries and capital gains, would \u8220\'20\'1Chelp keep the Medicare program strong for decades to come,\u8221\'20\'1D he writes.\par \par \uc2 Biden is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-budget-2024-republicans-debt-limit-46a5cc7b4ef49d6bc4bf3319930e3d48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heading for Pennsylvania on Thursday}}}\uc2  to release his full budget plans, instead of the more traditional setting of the White House, the Associated Press notes.\par \par \uc2 But with Republicans controlling the House, the budget has little chance of passing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning Tuesday blog readers!\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been laying out some of his budget proposals today in a guest essay {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/07/opinion/joe-biden-medicare.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the New York Times}}}\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s jabbing at Republicans again over their perceived agenda to cut benefits for future generations, and providing details of plans to expand Medicare by imposing a \u8220\'20\'1Cmodest increase\u8221\'20\'1D in contributions by wealthier Americans to pay for it.\par \par \uc2 As the Times notes, the president\u8217\'20\'19s budget stands next to no chance of passing the divided Congress. But it\u8217\'20\'19s a topic that helps draw 2024 attention back from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and who the Republicans might nominate to oppose his re-election, assuming Biden runs.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll take a closer look at that coming up. Meanwhile, here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re following on a busy Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rightwing TV host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is receiving pushback for \u8220\'20\'1Csanitizing\u8221\'20\'1D the January 6 Capitol riot in selective footage aired on his Fox News show on Monday night, provided to him exclusively by Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The growing threat of a third party candidate running in 2024 and soaking up votes from Biden is worrying Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is mulling who he might pick as a running mate in 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios says}}}\uc2 , with election denier and failed Arizona governor candidate Kari Lake emerging as a favorite.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccried uncontrollably for 30 minutes\u8221\'20\'1D after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s January 2017 inauguration after she and outgoing president Barack Obama left the White House for the last time, according to the ex-first lady\u8217\'20\'19s new podcast airing today. The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2023/03/07/michelle-obama-podcast-trump-inauguration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has the story}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have all this, and much more coming up in the blog today. Please stick with us.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230307ej37002eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
