\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  limits  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills sales after pressure from conservative states\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano and agencies \par \uc2 547 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2023\par 13:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican attorneys general threatened the company with legal consequences for sending pills by mail\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  will not distribute the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone in nearly two dozen conservative states after Republican attorneys general threatened the largest US pharmacy companies with legal consequences for sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail.\par \par \uc2 The decision, first reported by Politico, came weeks after the attorneys general sent a letter to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and CVS arguing that sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail would violate federal law and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in those states. A spokesperson for \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said the move was in response to that letter.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  had previously announced plans to become a certified pharmacy to dispense the pill in jurisdictions where it was legal to do so after the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  opted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/now-able-sell-abortion-pill-us-pharmacies-weigh-if-they-should-2023-01-06/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allow}}}\uc2  retail pharmacies to dispense mifepristone pills, including by mail.\par \par \uc2 But on Thursday the company confirmed to Politico that it would not dispense \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail or within their stores in 20 states, including some states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is currently complexity around this issue in Kansas and elsewhere,\u8221\'20\'1D Fraser Engerman, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 senior director of external relations, told the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats were critical of the move. Adam Schiff described \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  as caving. \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for putting a priority on the health of their customers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator Amy Klobuchar said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly why we need to codify the protections of Roe v Wade and guarantee the right to access care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are a critical part of reproductive care nationwide. Of all US abortions, more than half are now with pills rather than with a procedure, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn increasing attention since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade last June.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has limited dispensing of mifepristone to a subset of specialty offices and clinics due to safety concerns for more than 20 years. The agency has repeatedly eased restrictions and expanded access, increasing demand even as state laws make the pills harder to get for many women.\par \par \uc2 But the announcement from \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  suggests that mifepristone access may not expand as broadly as federal regulators intended in January. Typically, the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority to regulate prescription drug access has gone unchallenged. But more than a dozen states now have laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly \u8211\'20\'13 and the pills specifically \u8211\'20\'13 following last year\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision overturning the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Attorneys general from conservative states have also argued that shipments of mifepristone violate a 19th century law that prohibited sending items used in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the mail.\par \par \uc2 An anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-business-texas-lawsuits-71b8e54b97b016bf2cc0d9380d478991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal lawsuit}}}\uc2  in Texas in November seeking to revoke mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval, claiming the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the drug 23 years ago without adequate evidence of safety.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge could rule soon. If he sides with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, mifepristone could potentially be removed from the US market. Legal experts foresee years of court battles over access to the pills.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 4 March 2023. Amy Klobuchar is the senator quoted in the story, not Amy Schumer as we originally said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230307ej37003bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
