\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Artwork referring to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  removed from Idaho public college exhibition\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington \par \uc2 993 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2023\par 07:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Six pieces removed from show about health issues after school officials were given legal counsel about state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18gag rule\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A public college in Idaho is coming under pressure to explain why it has removed from an upcoming exhibition in its Center for Arts & History several artworks dealing with reproductive health and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) \uc2 and the National Coalition Against Censorship have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/letter/aclu-national-coalition-against-censorship-letter-lewis-clark-state-college-exclusion-artwork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jointly written}}}\uc2  to Lewis-Clark State College expressing \u8220\'20\'1Calarm\u8221\'20\'1D at the decision to remove several pieces.\par \par \uc2 Their letter says that the college\u8217\'20\'19s response demonstrated the potential abuses of new laws that have come into effect in Idaho banning the use of public funds to \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Ccounsel in favor\u8221\'20\'1D of pregnancy terminations.\par \par \uc2 Titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lcsc.edu/cah/exhibits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unconditional Care}}}\uc2 , the show invites artists to reflect on some of the most pressing health issues today \u8211\'20\'13 from chronic illness to disability and pregnancy. The participants share the stories of people directly affected by the challenges.\par \par \uc2 Items that touch on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been singled out for removal from the exhibition. Artists were told their work violated Idaho state law that kicked in after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  enshrined in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Scarlet Kim, a staff attorney with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech, privacy and technology project, said that the removal of works of art silenced the voices of women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt jeopardizes a bedrock first amendment principle that the state refrain from interfering with expressive activity because it disagrees with a particular point of view,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said.\par \par \uc2 Monitors of free speech have warned that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s eradication of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections would soon make itself felt within the cultural realm through censorship. Thirteen states, including Idaho, have effectively banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jeremy Young, Pen America\u8217\'20\'19s senior manager for free expression and education, said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans were inevitably spawning bans on speech \u8211\'20\'13 especially in educational environments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without banning speech about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as Lewis-Clark students are now discovering,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Six artworks have been removed from the Unconditional Care exhibition at the instruction of senior college administrators, and a seventh has been edited to remove \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  references. Four of the works are videos and audio recordings created by a New York-based artist, Lydia Nobles, as part of a series named As I Sit Waiting.\par \par \uc2 It highlights the stories of women who have had abortions or were forced to carry pregnancies to term.\par \par \uc2 Katrina Majkut, an artist who was commissioned to curate the Lewis-Clark exhibition, also had one of her own artworks removed. Titled Medical \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Pills, it consists of embroidered images of the medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills mifepristone and misoprostol.\par \par \uc2 College officials objected to the descriptive label that went alongside the artwork which gave basic and accurate facts about the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, as well as factual information on Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in a \u8220\'20\'1Cpost-Roe America\u8221\'20\'1D. Majkut said the administrators would not let her use the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Cpost-Roe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It scares me. It\u8217\'20\'19s frightening where we are going in this country\par \par \uc2 Artist Michelle Hartney\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did try to have some alternative stand-in, such as a curtain placed over the work or a sign that said \u8216\'20\'18Artwork has been removed in accordance with law\u8217\'20\'19, but that was all rejected too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The artist added that she has shown the same body of work in more than 25 college galleries across the country, \u8220\'20\'1Cand have never been censored or had an issue of any kind\u8221\'20\'1D. She said that the show she had curated was not protest art, and it was educational rather than inflammatory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCensorship of art is never OK. I see this as censorship of art, as well as suppression of academic learning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michelle Hartney, a Chicago-based artist, also had a piece removed from her series Unplanned Parenthood which focuses on the 250,000 mothers who wrote to the founder of Planned Parenthood, Margaret Sanger, in the 1920s. The censored item incorporated one of those original handwritten letters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was really mild,\u8221\'20\'1D Hartney said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was simply a woman saying she had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked for her response to the decision to remove the work, Hartney said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt scares me. It\u8217\'20\'19s frightening where we are going in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lewis-Clark State College is based in Lewiston, Idaho, and has about 3,600 students. The Guardian invited the institution to explain why it had opted to censor the show, and a spokesperson replied that \u8220\'20\'1Cafter obtaining legal advice, per Idaho Code Section 18-8705, some of the proposed exhibits could not be included in the exhibition\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Section 18-8705 is part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/Title18/T18CH87/SECT18-8705/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No Public Funds for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Act}}}\uc2  that was passed by Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s Republican legislature in 2021, months after the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the right}}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The law forbids public entities from contracting or participating in any commercial transaction involving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider or affiliate, and creates a \u8220\'20\'1Cgag rule\u8221\'20\'1D that bans individual public employees from counselling in favor of a pregnancy termination or referring anyone to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 The prohibition has spread jitters across the state, especially in public colleges and universities. Last September the general counsel of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chronicle.com/article/is-this-how-censorship-happens?emailConfirmed=true&supportSignUp=true&supportForgotPassword=true&email=ed.pilkington%40theguardian.com&success=true&code=success&bc_nonce=kejgwe1t8t0g72qhonfgdo&cid=gen_sign_in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Idaho}}}\uc2  sent all its staff \u8211\'20\'13 including student workers \u8211\'20\'13 a lengthy memo that told them to remain \u8220\'20\'1Cneutral\u8221\'20\'1D over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cproceed cautiously at any time that a discussion moves in the direction of reproductive health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The memo reached the attention of Joe Biden in the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, what century are we in?\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2022/10/04/what-century-are-we-in-biden-asks-of-university-of-idaho-ban-on-abortion-counseling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US president said}}}\uc2  when he learned of the university\u8217\'20\'19s instructions.\par \par \uc2 Last week a billboard truck displaying advice on how to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills that was being driven through the streets of Boise, Idaho, by the nonprofit Mayday Health was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HealthMayday/status/1631495608463769600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered to leave the city}}}\uc2  by police officers. The group said it was a violation of its basic constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230307ej370012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
