\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Worried that women will be prosecuted for using  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills? It\u8217\'20\'19s already happening\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,042 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 March 2023\par 16:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Privileged women will always be able to get safe terminations but for the rest prosecutions will have a chilling effect\par \par \uc2 South Carolina woman arrested for taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills\par \par \uc2 In October 2021 a 33-year-old woman in Greenville, South Carolina, went to the hospital with labor pains. According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thestate.com/news/local/crime/article272639146.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 police incident report}}}\uc2 , the woman told healthcare workers that she\u8217\'20\'19d taken \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to end her pregnancy; her fetus was estimated to be stillborn at 25 weeks. This week she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thestate.com/news/local/crime/article272639146.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested and charged}}}\uc2  with performing or soliciting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently legal in South Carolina until 20 weeks of pregnancy but it is one of just a handful of states with a law explicitly criminalizing self-managed abortions.\par \par \uc2 This story, which was first reported by the State, a South Carolina paper, is still developing and not all the details are clear. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear, for example, when exactly the woman took the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear why authorities waited so long to charge the woman. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear who reported the woman to the police. However, it seems likely that it was the medical workers she trusted with her care. What is clear is that this will not be the last instance of a woman being arrested for a self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. Also depressingly clear? The fact that stories like this will prevent women from seeking medical care for fear that they might be handed in to the police. Which means more women unnecessarily putting their health in danger.\par \par \uc2 While South Carolina may be one of the few states to outright ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists across the US are trying their best to make accessing mifepristone, the first pill used in the two-drug \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill protocol, as difficult as possible or to outlaw it altogether. Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Trump-appointed federal district judge in Texas, for example, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/03/abortion-pill-billboards-us-states-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently considering a petition}}}\uc2  that would nullify the approval given to mifepristone 22 years ago by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ). Meanwhile, Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gizmodo.com/texas-abortion-websites-bill-internet-service-providers-1850178991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently introduced a bill}}}\uc2  that would censor information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills online. The bill, duplicitously called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/pdf/HB02690I.pdf#navpanes=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women and Child Safety Act}}}\uc2 , would make it illegal for an internet service provider to let someone access information on how to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. It would also criminalize hosting a website that would help someone seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the state of reproductive rights in the US grows increasingly dystopian, it\u8217\'20\'19s important to remember that these draconian laws don\u8217\'20\'19t affect women equally. Privileged women will almost always be able to get a safe and effective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/aug/25/a-republican-theme-on-abortions-its-ok-for-me-evil-for-thee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mistresses}}}\uc2  of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican politicians will almost always be able to get a safe and effective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is women from more marginalized backgrounds who will suffer \u8211\'20\'13 indeed these women have seen their pregnancies policed long before Roe was overturned. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/south-carolina-woman-abortion-pills-arrested-charged-1850178775"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jezebel}}}\uc2  notes, \u8220\'20\'1CThe [South Carolina] woman is identified in the police report as being Black. Black, brown, Indigenous and other people of color have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/08/03/1114181472/criminalization-of-pregnancy-has-already-been-happening-to-the-poor-and-women-of"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disproportionately}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/the-policing-of-native-american-pregnancies-has-to-stop-1848113033"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalized}}}\uc2  for their pregnancy outcomes for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pregnancyjusticeus.org/arrests-and-prosecutions-of-pregnant-women-1973-2020/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decades}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernment should be so small you don\u8217\'20\'19t even realize it\u8217\'20\'19s there,\u8221\'20\'1D the official \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account of the \uc2 Republican National Committee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOP/status/1631392182744522781?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted on Thursday}}}\uc2 . Censoring the internet? Banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication that has been proved to be safe and effective for decades? Throwing women in jail for their reproductive choices? That certainly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like small government to me. But there\u8217\'20\'19s not much use pointing out Republican hypocrisy, is there? They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about being called hypocritical, they just care about power and control. And as their sustained assault on reproductive rights demonstrates, they\u8217\'20\'19re very good at finding ways to get both of those things.\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  F1 show criticized for lack of women\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re tuning into Drive to Survive, which goes behind the scenes in Formula 1, don\u8217\'20\'19t expect to hear from many women. Research from Females in Motorsport found women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/newsbeat-64826799"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke for only six minutes and seven seconds}}}\uc2  in season five of the popular show.\par \par \uc2 Are short men really psychopaths?\par \par \uc2 A new study suggests a link between short men (especially those who wish they were taller) and psychopathy. While this makes for great headlines the study, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/mar/02/short-man-psychopath-study-napoleon-complex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Simon Usborne notes in the Guardian}}}\uc2 , has some flaws. More broadly, Usborne argues, it misses the bigger picture: \u8220\'20\'1CIf shorter men do display any particular psychological traits, they\u8217\'20\'19re more likely, in a society that still equates physical and social standing, to involve self-esteem issues than delusions of grandeur.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jordan Peterson mansplains Christianity to the Pope\par \par \uc2 The (tall) author, academic, and prolific {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/health/archive/2018/08/the-peterson-family-meat-cleanse/567613/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beef-eater}}}\uc2  took umbrage with the pope tweeting about social justice. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing Christian about #SocialJustice,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indy100.com/news/jordan-peterson-pope-christianity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peterson replied}}}\uc2  ( to the pope! ). God grant me the confidence of a mediocre white man who thinks he can argue about religion with the pope.\par \par \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister says ban on same-sex marriage not discrimination\par \par \uc2 Perhaps someone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/japan-kishida-lgbtq-samesex-marriage-discrimination-43baf7af74baf0d8b908124b19eabf0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could give him a dictionary}}}\uc2  and he could quickly look up what \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscrimination\u8221\'20\'1D means.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s finance minister called for a Palestinian town of 7,000 civilians \u8216\'20\'18to be erased\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The response from the Biden administration to this despicable incitement to violence was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/03/01/middleeast/west-bank-smotrich-ned-price-intl/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fairly milquetoast}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tinder robberies have men in Brazil on high alert\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/portuguese/brasil-63733202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nine out of 10 kidnappings}}}\uc2  in S\u227\'00\'E3o Paulo in the past year have reportedly occurred after a date was organized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://restofworld.org/2023/tinder-robberies-dating-apps-brazil/?utm_source=feedly&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=feeds&mc_cid=8f86da58af&mc_eid=8ce16ced76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 through a dating app}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Meet \u8220\'20\'1CNarco Cat\u8221\'20\'1D: a hairless and tattooed Sphynx cat that, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2023/03/03/narco-cat-tattoo-mexican-prison/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 until recently}}}\uc2 , lived in a Mexican prison and was reportedly owned by the leader of a violent gang. Narco Cat, who was tattooed with an \u8220\'20\'1CHecho en M\u233\'00\'E9xico\u8221\'20\'1D design favoured by the Mexicles gang, was liberated from prison in February and is now headed to Texas to live with a new, rather less felonious, family. No doubt a \uc2 Netflix\uc2  special will follow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a response of up to 300 words by email to be considered for publication in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tone/letters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  letters}}}\uc2  section, please {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com?body=Please%20include%20your%20name,%20full%20postal%20address%20and%20phone%20number%20with%20your%20letter%20below.%20Letters%20are%20usually%20published%20with%20the%20author%27s%20name%20and%20city/town/village.%20The%20rest%20of%20the%20information%20is%20for%20verification%20only%20and%20to%20contact%20you%20where%20necessary."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230304ej34001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
