\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Billboards advise on how to get  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills in US states where procedure is banned\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 564 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 March 2023\par 18:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mobile billboards on how to get access to pills by mail are being driven through college campuses in 14 states\par \par \uc2 Women living under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the US are being offered advice on how to get access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail, through a system of mobile billboards which are being driven through college campuses in 14 states carrying the prohibition.\par \par \uc2 The billboards are the creation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mayday.health/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mayday.Health}}}\uc2 , a non-profit set up in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  last June that overturned the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The posters carry QR codes that link to online information providing a step-by-step guide on how to obtain the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill even in states which have banned it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe wish that everybody could just get these medications as easily as you can get Tylenol or Viagra in this country. Where there\u8217\'20\'19s a will, there\u8217\'20\'19s a way,\u8221\'20\'1D Jennifer Lincoln, Mayday\u8217\'20\'19s president, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mpbonline.org/blogs/news/these-billboards-want-you-to-know-how-to-get-abortion-pills-even-if-your-state-banned-abortions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi Public Broadcasting}}}\uc2 , referring to common brands of painkiller and erectile dysfunction medication.\par \par \uc2 Mayday\u8217\'20\'19s bid to help women circumvent tight anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that are now in place in 26 states is part of a storm of legal activity around the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. Advocates on both sides of the bitter struggle are anxiously awaiting the decision of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal district judge in Amarillo}}}\uc2 , Texas who could move any day now to impose an injunction on mifepristone, the first pill used in the two-drug \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill protocol.\par \par \uc2 Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, who was appointed by Donald Trump and who espouses right-wing Christian ideology, is considering a petition from an alliance of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups that attempts to nullify the approval given to mifepristone 22 years ago by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ). If he does impose an injunction it could snarl up the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill across the US for months or even years.\par \par \uc2 Pushing in the opposite direction, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/25/health/abortion-pills-ban-genbiopro.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lawsuit}}}\uc2  was filed last month in West Virginia by GenBioPro, a US producer of mifepristone, arguing that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s federal approval of the medication overrides local state bans. The outcome of that case could also have huge ramifications right across the country.\par \par \uc2 In its advice to women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mayday.health/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mayday points out}}}\uc2  that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill is 99% medically safe, functioning on the same lines as a natural miscarriage. Despite local state bans, it remains legal to receive by mail in all 50 states, the Department of Justice has advised.\par \par \uc2 Some states with Republican-controlled legislatures that have imposed tough \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are seeking to challenge the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s claim. This week a 33-year-old woman was arrested by police in Greenville, South Carolina, and charged with performing or soliciting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after she told hospital staff she had taken an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 The woman is currently out of jail on a bond of $2,500, according to the local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thestate.com/news/local/crime/article272639146.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the State}}}\uc2  newspaper.\par \par \uc2 Mayday\u8217\'20\'19s billboard is touring campuses in Jackson, Missippi; Austin and Dallas in Texas; Boise, Idaho and in other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states.\par \par \uc2 Lincoln urged women to obtain the medication irrespective of their personal situation, saying they need not wait for a crisis but should order them now \u8220\'20\'1Cto know you\u8217\'20\'19ve got this in your back pocket\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230303ej33002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
