\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ohio takes crucial step towards public vote that could secure right to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2023\par 21:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Petition for initiative that would secure constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will now go to state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot board for approval\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups in Ohio cleared a significant hurdle on Thursday in their effort to bring a ballot initiative before voters that would secure a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Ohio attorney general, \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/Media/News-Releases/March-2023/Petition-Summary-Certified-for-Proposed-Constituti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved a petition}}}\uc2  brought by campaigners looking to bring the ballot initiative to voters in November 2023. The petition will now go to the Ohio ballot board for approval, which has 10 days to approve or reject it.\par \par \uc2 The two groups submitting the petition \u8211\'20\'13 Ohioans for Reproductive Freedom and Ohio Physicians for Reproductive Rights \u8211\'20\'13 gathered thousands of signatures from voters in the state to get the petition process started. The groups believe voters want the chance to vote directly on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be protected in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 Following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade last summer an Ohio \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after six weeks of pregnancy immediately came into effect. That ban was put on hold by a state judge in October, restoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state up to 22 weeks of pregnancy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acluohio.org/en/press-releases/ohio-lower-court-grant-preliminary-injunction-six-week-abortion-ban-will-remain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 until further notice}}}\uc2 . But the groups wants to put the issue to rest once and for all by asking the people of Ohio to confirm that they believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive health rights are protected by the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 The groups are in a race against the clock to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the November 2023 ballot, because a number of bills are passing through Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican legislature looking to weaken the citizen-led ballot initiative process. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legislature.ohio.gov/legislation/135/hjr1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One such bill}}}\uc2 , which would increase the threshold at which a ballot initiative can be passed \u8211\'20\'13 from a simple majority to 60% of votes \u8211\'20\'13 has already been passed in the House and awaits debate in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 If it passes, that same question will go to voters on the November 2023 ballot. If \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights proponents manage to get their initiative on the ballot for November, their effort will only require clearing the current 50% threshold.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230302ej32003bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
