\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 UN\uc2  urged to intervene over destruction of US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 931 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2023\par 17:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: letter from human rights groups says overturning of the constitutional right violates US\u8217\'20\'19s obligations as a \uc2 UN\uc2  member state\par \par \uc2 Top human rights organizations are calling on the United Nations to intervene over the destruction of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globaljusticecenter.net/files/UNSpecialProceduresLetter_USAbortionRights.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  shared in advance with the Guardian and sent on Thursday by nearly 200 organizations and experts, the authors detail how, since the overturning of the federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June 2022, some 22 million women and girls of reproductive age live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is now either banned or inaccessible.\par \par \uc2 Among the signatories are the Global Justice Center, Pregnancy Justice, \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  and \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2 . They are joined by a broader coalition of groups and individual advocates for human rights and racial and economic justice.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, the signatories write, deny \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s decisional and bodily autonomy in a way that rejects the agency, dignity and equality of people who can become pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The groups in the letter claim that overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  contravenes the US\u8217\'20\'19s international obligations as a \uc2 UN\uc2  member organization. Member states are obliged to protect and uphold the rights to life, health, privacy, liberty and security, along with freedoms from torture and inhumane, cruel or degrading treatment.\par \par \uc2 The US\u8217\'20\'19s role as a leader on the world stage does not exempt the country from these obligations \u8211\'20\'13 in fact, it should require them to do more, said a representative from the Global Justice Center, which is one of the signatories .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US must be castigated on the world stage for its treatment of women, girls and others who can become pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 the scale and intensity of human rights violations that the US is inflicting on its population are near unfathomable at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christine Ryan, legal director of the Global Justice Center, in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has become almost tragically ironic that the \uc2 US government\uc2  uses the language of human rights to condemn state abuses against citizens of other countries, be that in Iran, or Belarus. These norms must be deployed against the state here at home as well. And for too long, the US has been able to avoid that type of international scrutiny,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The authors say the curtailment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US is of a piece with the country\u8217\'20\'19s history of devaluing the lives of Black women, who are hit worst by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The Dobbs ruling pushed the US even further out of line with its human rights obligations, including its obligation to ensure access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to eliminate structural racism and discrimination,\u8221\'20\'1D said Annerieke Smaak Daniel, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights researcher at \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions compound economic, social, and geographic barriers to healthcare, including contraception, disproportionately impacting Black women\u8217\'20\'19s ability to access the care we need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letter sent on Thursday was addressed to a number of \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies and officials, including the Working Group on Discrimination against Women and Girls; the Special Rapporteur on Torture and other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment; and the Special Rapporteur on the Right to Privacy. In the letter, the signatories ask recipients to communicate with the US about these violations, to request an official visit to the US, and to ask the country to comply with its obligations under international law as a \uc2 UN\uc2  member state.\par \par \uc2 Ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had far-reaching, and in some cases life-threatening risks, the authors write \u8211\'20\'13 including for those seeking miscarriage care, those forced to travel across state lines for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and those denied care for potentially fatal complications such as ectopic pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Officials from the US mission to the \uc2 UN\uc2  and the US Gender Policy Council , a White House office established by the Biden administration, did not respond to a request for comment in time for publication.\par \par \uc2 Signatories in the letter list prior actions from the UN Human Rights Committee\u8217\'20\'19s over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in countries such as Ireland and El Salvador, arguing for similar scrutiny of the US.\par \par \uc2 They note that the \uc2 UN\uc2  committee has already established that denial of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can cause \u8220\'20\'1Cphysical and mental suffering so severe in pain and intensity as to amount to torture\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The letter also includes damning examples since Roe was overturned, including the case of one patient in Wisconsin who was left to bleed at home for 10 days following a miscarriage because hospital staff feared violating the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if they intervened to give care. It also details cases of several patients who had to travel out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being refused care for an ectopic pregnancy, and others who were denied chemotherapy care due to pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Any exceptions allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in very narrow circumstances \u8211\'20\'13 for example, where an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary to save the life of the pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s life, or when the pregnancy is the result of rape \u8211\'20\'13 are practically unworkable, the signatories write.\par \par \uc2 These abuses lie firmly at the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s door, added Ryan from the Global Justice Center.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen consistent lip service from the Biden-Harris administration\u8221\'20\'1D, but not enough action, she said. She pointed out, for example, that even with the loss of Roe, the Biden administration could make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs more readily available {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/08/us-government-abortion-big-steps-will-they-matter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by removing unnecessary regulations on certain drugs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C There has been an absolute calamity in terms of public health, human rights, and the response has been middling to poor,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryan said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230302ej32000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
