\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 UN\uc2  urged to intervene after erasure of US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Mattha Busby \par \uc2 1,462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2023\par 12:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rights groups says overturn of constitutional right violates US\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN\uc2  obligations. Plus, surge in pro-bono Ukraine lobbyingDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Top human rights organizations are calling on the United Nations to intervene over the erasure of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 In a letter shared in advance with the Guardian and sent today by nearly 200 organizations and experts, the authors detail how, since the federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overturned in June 2022, about 22 million women and girls of reproductive age live in states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/02/destruction-us-abortion-laws-human-rights-violation-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where terminations are either banned or inaccessible}}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, the signatories write, deny \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s decisional and bodily autonomy in a way that rejects the agency, dignity and equality of people who can become pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D The groups say overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  contravenes the US\u8217\'20\'19s international obligations as a \uc2 UN\uc2  member state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Litany of damning incidents since Roe v Wade was overturned. One patient in Wisconsin was left to bleed at home for 10 days after a miscarriage, several patients had to travel out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being refused care for ectopic pregnancies, and others were denied chemotherapy care due to pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re lobbying for Ukraine pro bono \u8211\'20\'13 and making millions from arms firms\par \par \uc2 Some of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful lobbyists are providing their services to Ukraine for free \u8211\'20\'13 but at the same time, they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/01/ukraine-lobbyists-washington-defense-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking in millions in fees from Pentagon contractors}}}\uc2  that stand to benefit from the country\u8217\'20\'19s war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine led to an outpouring of support for Kyiv from seemingly every industry in the US. But, arguably, one of the most crucial industries coming to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s aid has been Washington\u8217\'20\'19s powerful lobbying industry.\par \par \uc2 The invasion has led some of the lobbying industry\u8217\'20\'19s biggest players to do the unthinkable \u8211\'20\'13 lobby for free. While there may be altruistic reasons for representing Ukraine pro bono, some lobbying firms also have financial incentives for aiding the country: they have made millions lobbying for arms manufacturers that could profit from the war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Surge in pro-bono Ukraine lobbying. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t recall a comparable surge in pro-bono work for any foreign principal,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Laufman, who previously oversaw the Foreign Agents Registration Act (Fara) enforcement at the justice department.\par \par \uc2 US teachers grapple with a growing housing crisis: \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t afford rent\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Teachers are navigating a difficult terrain: making enough money to afford living {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/02/us-teachers-california-salary-disparities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the districts they work}}}\uc2 . Research by Dr \uc2 Sylvia Allegretto\uc2 , a research associate at the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , a thinktank, found public school teachers nationally make nearly 24% less in weekly earnings than similarly credentialed college graduates in other fields.\par \par \uc2 The so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cwage penalty\u8221\'20\'1D makes it increasingly difficult for teachers to live in the same communities as their students, forcing them to commute long distances to and from school, renting rooms from parents, taking on second jobs and living in school district-operated housing.\par \par \uc2 As a national teacher shortage persists, the shortage of Black and Latino teachers, particularly in diverse, impoverished school districts like Los Angeles, creates a gap between who students from marginalized backgrounds can relate to.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Diversity lack blamed on meager wages. In California, teachers on average make nearly 18% less a week than comparable college graduates. Gray says that disparity puts an \u8220\'20\'1Cadditional tax\u8221\'20\'1D on teachers of color who come into the profession saddled with more debt.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Duke and Duchess of Sussex have been asked by the royal family to vacate their UK home, Frogmore\par \par \uc2 cottage. The move, which is likely to be viewed as antagonistic after the release of \uc2 Prince Harry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s autobiography Spare, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/mar/01/duke-and-duchess-of-sussex-are-asked-to-vacate-their-uk-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reportedly sanctioned}}}\uc2  by King Charles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Romania\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister has presented his \u8220\'20\'1Cnew honorary adviser\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/02/romania-ion-ai-government-honorary-adviser-artificial-intelligence-pm-nicolae-ciuca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an artificial intelligence assistant}}}\uc2  named \u8220\'20\'1CIon\u8221\'20\'1D that will scan social networks to inform the government \u8220\'20\'1Cin real time of Romanians\u8217\'20\'19 proposals and wishes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Bolivian man who claimed to have been missing in the Amazon alone for a month has recounted eating insects and worms, collecting water in his boots and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/02/man-lost-in-amazon-jungle-survives-eating-worms-drinking-urine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drinking his own urine to stay alive}}}\uc2 . If confirmed, Jhonatan Acosta, 30, would be one of the longest-ever lone Amazon survivors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s police have arrested five suspects over a Jewish settler rampage in the occupied West Bank earlier this week that an Israeli general described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpogrom\u8221\'20\'1D and which followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/01/israeli-police-arrest-five-over-settler-rampage-in-west-bank"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deadly Palestinian gun attack}}}\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Fossil fuel companies donated $700m to US universities over 10 years\par \par \uc2 Six fossil fuel companies funneled more than $700m in research funding to 27 universities in the US from 2010 to 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/mar/01/fossil-fuel-companies-donate-millions-us-universities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a study}}}\uc2 . Such funding at universities that conduct climate research can shift not just research agendas, but also policy in the direction of climate solutions the industry prefers, the report\u8217\'20\'19s authors argue.\par \par \uc2 Those solutions typically include biofuels, carbon capture and hydrogen, according to the research by the thinktank Data for Progress and the non-profit organization Fossil-Free Research. Oil majors also invest in public policy and economics research that favors deregulation. \u8220\'20\'1C$700m is probably an absolute bare minimum,\u8221\'20\'1D Grace Adcox, a polling analyst for Data for Progress, said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so little transparency around these gifts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Indonesia\u8217\'20\'19s parents seek justice over child cough syrup deaths\par \par \uc2 More than 200 Indonesian children have died after taking cough syrups that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/02/this-is-my-last-responsibility-indonesias-parents-seek-justice-over-child-cough-syrup-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had been contaminated with toxic chemicals}}}\uc2  commonly found in industrial solvents and antifreeze. Children who survived have been left debilitated. At least 116 medicines from six companies have been banned for containing high levels of diethylene glycol and ethylene glycol.\par \par \uc2 About two dozen parents of the children poisoned are now joining a class action to sue \uc2 Indonesia\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry\uc2 , food and drug agency and eight pharmaceutical companies, including some suppliers of the raw materials. Parents want the government and the companies involved to take responsibility and improve manufacturing processes and disease management standards.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: Giant Jurassic-era insect rediscovered outside \uc2 Walmart\uc2  in Arkansas\par \par \uc2 A giant Jurassic-era insect missing from eastern North America for at least half a century has been spotted clinging to the side of a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  big box in Arkansas. The discovery of a species that was thought to have disappeared from large swaths of North America has stoked speculation that there may be entire populations tucked away in remote parts of the Ozark mountains.\par \par \uc2 The giant lacewing was found by Michael Skvarla, the director of \uc2 Penn State\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insect identification lab. In a co-authored paper recently published in the scientific journal the Proceedings of the Entomological Society of Washington, Skvarla said the specimen had long been incorrectly labelled in his personal collection as an \u8220\'20\'1Cantlion\u8221\'20\'1D, an insect with similar features, until the rediscovery and reappraisal.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Tackle overconsumption by the rich, says acting \uc2 UN\uc2  biodiversity chief\par \par \uc2 Governments and businesses must start implementing this decade\u8217\'20\'19s deal to halt the destruction of Earth\u8217\'20\'19s ecosystems as soon as possible, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/mar/02/overconsumption-by-rich-must-be-tackled-says-acting-un-biodiversity-chief-aoe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the acting UN biodiversity chief has said}}}\uc2 , urging wealthy countries to tackle overconsumption of the planet\u8217\'20\'19s resources.\par \par \uc2 Dr David Cooper, the new acting executive secretary of the Secretariat of the \uc2 Convention on Biological Diversity\uc2  (CBD), said countries and corporations must immediately act on December\u8217\'20\'19s historic Montreal agreement, which includes targets to protect 30% of Earth, reform $500bn of environmentally damaging subsidies, and address and disclose the impact businesses have on biodiversity.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Harassment, hierarchies and discreetly rubbed\par \par \uc2 pants: the exhausting politics of orchestras\par \par \uc2 Orchestras have tended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/mar/01/tar-conductor-orchestra-harassment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to have a pyramid power structure}}}\uc2 , with the conductor at the top, and everyone else further down: a principal player above a sub-principal, both ahead of a \u8220\'20\'1Ctutti\u8221\'20\'1D or section player, and all ahead of a \u8220\'20\'1Cdep\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a non-permanent player deputising, writes Hugh Morris. These structures quickly develop their own internal codes \u8211\'20\'13 such as the orchestra finding \u8220\'20\'1Csubtle ways of letting conductors know that they\u8217\'20\'19re not happy,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dr Anna Bull, the author of Class, Control and Classical Music.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very important to differentiate between the artistic hierarchy and the social, personal and political hierarchy, which, for me, shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be the same structure,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dave Rimbault, a tutti violin at the Royal Liverpool Philharmonic Orchestra and a union rep for the Musicians\u8217\'20\'19 Union. \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, across the sector, there was an issue where that was mirrored.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230302ej32001pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
