\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida court denies habeas corpus petition for fetus of jailed woman\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong \par \uc2 980 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2023\par 15:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Although the case was decided on a technicality, a dissenting judge on panel said the court should have rejected the claim on its merits\par \par \uc2 A Florida appeals court denied an attorney\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to have a woman released from jail ahead of trial by arguing that her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/23/florida-lawyer-jailed-pregnant-woman-fetal-personhood-reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fetus was being illegally detained}}}\uc2  without charge \u8211\'20\'13 but the attorney says he plans to continue the legal battle.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s third district court of appeal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://3dca.flcourts.gov/content/download/860872/opinion/230279_DA08_02242023_163256_i.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed without prejudice}}}\uc2  a petition for a writ of habeas corpus filed by attorney William M Norris on behalf of the \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D of Natalia Harrell.\par \par \uc2 The petition argued that the fetus is \u8220\'20\'1Ca person under the Florida constitution and the United States constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and that it therefore should not effectively be detained without charge.\par \par \uc2 The ruling, written by judge Thomas Logue last Friday, contains \u8220\'20\'1Cno opinion on whether such filing is being brought by a party with standing, whether the claims are legally cognizable, whether they have merit, or what remedies, if any, are available\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Instead, it argued on a technicality that the petition failed to include a factual record of the case \u8211\'20\'13 which includes disputed allegations that Harrell has received inadequate prenatal care while in jail \u8211\'20\'13 and should be pursued in a lower court.\par \par \uc2 However , another judge from the panel in the case, Monica Gordo, published a partially dissenting opinion arguing that the court should reject the claim of \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful incarceration by the government and find habeas corpus does not lie under these limited and specific circumstances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While Gordo agreed that factual disputes about Harrell\u8217\'20\'19s prenatal care needed to be hashed out in a lower court, she argued that the appeals court should rule on the habeas corpus claim, habeas corpus being the common law right for a person being detained to appear before a judge.\par \par \uc2 Gordo noted that there was agreement that the fetus had not been charged with a crime, and wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CTo send this part of the petition back for a determination of facts which are undisputed seems odd \u8230\'20\'26 I see a significant difference between exercising judicial restraint and punting a legal issue placed squarely before the Court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The argument is nothing more than an attempt for the mother to leverage her unborn child as a basis to be released from lawful detention\par \par \uc2 Judge Monica Gordo\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CNo more could the government be accused of unlawfully detaining the unborn child in this case than could the mother be guilty of kidnapping over interstate lines if she chose to visit her grandmother in Georgia while eight months pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gordo charged that the case was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbadly-disguised Trojan horse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe argument is nothing more than an attempt for the mother to leverage her unborn child as a basis to be released from lawful detention,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 Harrell, 24, has been held at the Turner Guilford Knight correctional center in Miami since 26 July, when she was about six weeks pregnant.\par \par \uc2 She is charged with second-degree murder in the shooting death of Gladys Yvette Borcela during an argument in an Uber vehicle. Harrell is seeking immunity from prosecution under Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cstand your ground\u8221\'20\'1D law, which allows individuals to use force in self-defense in some cases.\par \par \uc2 The case has drawn national attention because of the potential ramifications of recognizing embryos and fetuses as persons with constitutional rights. \u8220\'20\'1CFetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D has long been a goal of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement in the US, and it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/31/opinion/abortion-fetal-personhood.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gained significant traction}}}\uc2  in the year since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler, a law professor and expert in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/23/florida-lawyer-jailed-pregnant-woman-fetal-personhood-reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  fetal personhood as a \u8220\'20\'1CPandora\u8217\'20\'19s box\u8221\'20\'1D that would probably result in the total banning of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Norris said that it was not his intention to use the case to set such a precedent, though he said he acknowledged the possibility. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that the unborn child is a person entitles them to a seat at the table when decisions are being made, and that\u8217\'20\'19s the true revolutionary aspect of this case,\u8221\'20\'1D he said by phone on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re doing is we\u8217\'20\'19re using the bits and pieces floating around in the law to make an argument to have an outcome that we want for our client. I\u8217\'20\'19m not trying to achieve an outcome that\u8217\'20\'19s universal \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m not trying to eliminate a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her reproductive health. What I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to get to is that when certain decisions that are made about the woman, you can\u8217\'20\'19t make them without considering the impact on the fetus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe literature on the adverse outcomes on fetal development of incarceration is overwhelming,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 A staff attorney for Pregnancy Justice, Emma Roth, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe inadequacy of prenatal care in jail can violate the constitutional rights of pregnant people, so the lawyer could and should have filed the habeas petition on her behalf rather than on behalf of her fetus. That would also avoid the harmful consequences of further enshrining fetal personhood.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in Florida are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://humanlifefl.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gathering signatures}}}\uc2  in an attempt to place a fetal personhood amendment on the ballot in 2024; the measure would enshrine the idea of an unalienable \u8220\'20\'1Cright to life of the pre-born individual\u8221\'20\'1D and thereby outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pro-choice organizations strongly oppose such measures, which they say are incompatible with full civil rights for women and people who can become pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Norris acknowledged the conflict but said granting a fetus due process would not guarantee any particular outcomes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is indeed a Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is whether we as a society are mature enough to deal with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Norris now plans to pursue his argument before the judge in Harrell\u8217\'20\'19s criminal case, he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230228ej2s001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
