\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Lawyer argues fetus of jailed pregnant woman is being illegally detained\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Carrie Wong \par \uc2 721 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2023\par 21:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida attorney uses \u8216\'20\'18fetal personhood\u8217\'20\'19 argument in attempt to free client that could have consequences for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights\par \par \uc2 A lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to have a pregnant woman released from jail ahead of trial by arguing that her fetus has been subject to \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful and illegal detention\u8221\'20\'1D could have profound consequences for the rights of women in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Attorney William M Norris filed a petition for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23686497/natalia-harrell-habeas-corpus-filing.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writ of habeas corpus}}}\uc2  on behalf of the \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D of Natalia Harrell in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s third district court of appeal on 16 February, the Miami Herald {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/crime/article272551249.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The filing argues that the fetus \u8220\'20\'1Cis a person under the Florida constitution and the United States constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and therefore has the right to due process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe unborn child has not been charged with a criminal offense by respondents or the Miami Dade state attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, yet respondents have unborn child in a detention center known as TGK in Miami Dade county, Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D the filing states.\par \par \uc2 It further alleges that the jail has failed to provide Harrell with adequate prenatal nutrition and medical care, saying that she has not been treated by an obstetrician-gynecologist since October, and that on one occasion she was left inside a transport van with inside temperatures exceeding 100F (37C) for an extended period.\par \par \uc2 Harrell, 24, was six weeks pregnant when she was arrested on 26 July 2022 and charged in connection with the death of Gladys Yvette Borcela during an argument in an Uber on 23 July. Harrell has pleaded not guilty and has been held without bail since her arrest.\par \par \uc2 The state of Florida has urged the court to dismiss the petition and disputed the allegation that Harrell has not received adequate medical care, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/community/miami-dade/article272562777.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami Herald reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Norris did not respond to requests for comment from the Guardian, but in interviews with other media outlets, his rhetoric has echoed that of the \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D movement, which seeks to grant constitutional legal protection to fetuses and embryos.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn unborn child is a person,\u8221\'20\'1D Norris told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/petition-seeks-release-pregnant-florida-inmate-saying-fetus-received-i-rcna71649?cid=sm_npd_nn_tw_ma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe person has constitutional rights, and one of them is the right not to be deprived of liberty without due process of law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D laws are a key {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/31/opinion/abortion-fetal-personhood.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aim of the anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  movement}}}\uc2  in the US following the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking down Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last summer. They are strongly opposed by pro-choice and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights organizations. Pregnancy Justice, the civil rights group formerly known as National Advocates for Pregnant Women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pregnancyjusticeus.org/issues/pregnancy-and-personhood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argues}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not possible to add fertilized eggs, embryos and fetuses to the community of constitutional persons without subtracting people with the capacity for pregnancy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you recognize fetal personhood, this is a Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor and expert in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. Ziegler said it was hard to see how the court could grant a writ in Harrell\u8217\'20\'19s case without establishing \u8220\'20\'1Csome kind of generalizable rule\u8221\'20\'1D of fetal personhood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has the potential to establish that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always illegal and potentially to expose women to punishment or make it a violation of the Florida constitution to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would mean that you can\u8217\'20\'19t imprison people who are pregnant, no matter what crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ziegler said that such far-reaching consequences \u8211\'20\'13 some of which could alienate the \u8220\'20\'1Ctough on crime\u8221\'20\'1D politics of many within the rightwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement \u8211\'20\'13 were why the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement has largely steered clear of habeas corpus petitions in its pursuit of fetal personhood.\par \par \uc2 But the case is yet another indication of the changed legal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/22/diary-doctor-navigating-total-abortion-ban-tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landscape post-Roe}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fetal personhood movement has certainly gained traction, moving from a fringe idea to codified laws across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson for Pregnancy Justice said in a statement, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd while their goal is to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and control people\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy, they\u8217\'20\'19ve given little thought to how this impacts all facets of the law beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling where this will end: HOV lanes, taxes, worker\u8217\'20\'19s comp, child custody/kidnapping cases, criminal law, and on and on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 27 February to clarify that Norris represents only the fetus in this case, not Harrell herself.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230223ej2n001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
