\par\par \uc2 Life and style\par \b \uc2 Dining across the divide US special: \u8216\'20\'18She tried to educate me on why AR-15s aren\u8217\'20\'19t really military-style weapons\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 924 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2023\par 03:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 One is anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pro-guns. The other is pro-choice and thinks \u8216\'20\'18war tools\u8217\'20\'19 shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be in the hands of the public. Could they agree to disagree?\par \par \uc2 Heidi\par \par \uc2 , 62,\par \par \uc2 Price, Utah\par \par \uc2 Occupation Retired school teacher\par \par \uc2 Voting record Usually Democrat\par \par \uc2 Amuse bouche Heidi is an enthusiastic archaeologist and anthropologist. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can learn a lot about how to use the land and protect it,\u8221\'20\'1D she says\par \par \uc2 Janalee, 59,\par \par \uc2 South Jordan, Utah\par \par \uc2 Occupation Campaigner for God, guns and urban green space\par \par \uc2 Voting record Has previously voted Democrat or Independent. Now straight-ticket Republican\par \par \uc2 Amuse bouche Janalee\u8217\'20\'19s great-grandfather, Jesse, had five wives and 44 children. She has 80,000 cousins, she says, \u8220\'20\'1Clike a multilevel marketing scheme\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For starters\par \par \uc2 Janalee We shared an appetizer of loaded rock chips, then I had an omelet with vegetables, bacon and sausage. I was worried we were going to fight. I told Heidi I lost my best friend over Donald Trump, but she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t mean to me about supporting him. It never felt confrontational. We weren\u8217\'20\'19t representing corporations; we were there as grandmothers who care.\par \par \uc2 Heidi I had a Reuben sandwich and fries. Janalee told me she\u8217\'20\'19s a Trump person. I said that\u8217\'20\'19s OK. She said something about a stolen election. I thought, \u8220\'20\'1COh good grief.\u8221\'20\'1D I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the election was stolen. A lot of people like Trump because of his personality, but that\u8217\'20\'19s the reason I don\u8217\'20\'19t like him.\par \par \uc2 The big beef\par \par \uc2 Heidi Janalee tried to educate me on why AR-15s aren\u8217\'20\'19t really military-style weapons. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a problem with handguns, shotguns and rifles, but these new fancy guns \u8211\'20\'13 the ARs, the Uzis that became a problem in 90s \u8211\'20\'13 should not be in the hands of the public. It\u8217\'20\'19s a war tool and we just don\u8217\'20\'19t need it. I said no to guns in the classroom, absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 Janalee I prefer to talk about people violence not gun violence. A gun doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything \u8211\'20\'13 it can just sit on a table fully loaded for 1,000 years. An AR-15 isn\u8217\'20\'19t a military weapon. We have a constitutional right to own them. We did agree that schools should have some kind of sign, maybe like: \u8220\'20\'1CWarning to criminals: we protect our children\u8221\'20\'1D. We agreed that the news media is irresponsible in the way they report stories about guns.\par \par \uc2 Heidi I agree that some news channels only focus on the group that watches them. That\u8217\'20\'19s true on the left and right. They fearmonger and rile people up.\par \par \uc2 Sharing plate\par \par \uc2 Janalee \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the subject that scared us both the most. She said women should be able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So I said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s your understanding of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  ?\u8221\'20\'1D She said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo turn it back to the states.\u8221\'20\'1D I said: \u8220\'20\'1CYes, it did.\u8221\'20\'1D Heidi asked if I could bend on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said: \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe we could agree on 10 weeks?\u8221\'20\'1D I said: \u8220\'20\'1COK, maybe we can agree on 10 weeks, but the methods used to kill babies are still barbaric.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Heidi Janalee is totally against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think every women should have the right to make that decision, and there should be a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 10 weeks to ensure the safety of the woman. Most women know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant by eight weeks. If you go beyond that, then you have to decide to keep the baby or give it up for adoption. There needs to be more support for women to make that decision privately.\par \par \uc2 For afters\par \par \uc2 Janalee Heidi is a teacher so I listened and learned a lot from her about how slavery is taught in schools. We learned about it in elementary school. Heidi said high school students probably need a refresher course. I remembered that in school we created a slave cell as a classroom exercise. Someone would be the enslaver and someone the slave. It was really powerful. I said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhy don\u8217\'20\'19t we do role play about the civil war? One side fights to keep slavery, and the other to end it.\u8221\'20\'1D Because America ended slavery. It\u8217\'20\'19s not the evil empire. But I\u8217\'20\'19m sure slavery still exists, like in China.\par \par \uc2 Heidi We have to learn about slavery and other bad things that happened in this country, so we don\u8217\'20\'19t repeat them. Janalee said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, what about other countries?\u8221\'20\'1D I said that can be done in a world history class. I just stressed: teach the facts. I want students to think on their own. But we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be doing slavery role play.\par \par \uc2 Takeaways\par \par \uc2 Heidi We live in a conservative state, but we\u8217\'20\'19re pretty mellow about it. People have different opinions, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to get in your face about it. We respected each other\u8217\'20\'19s opinions and considered each other\u8217\'20\'19s proposals. Sometimes you have to give a little to get what you want.\par \par \uc2 Janalee Heidi was delightful. We agreed that we need to come together as Americans and stop being divided. We felt like some kind of power is trying to separate us and keep us fighting. We wondered, why is this happening?\par \par \uc2 Additional reporting: Kitty Drake\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Heidi and Janalee ate at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/balancerockeatery/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Balance Rock Eatery & Pub }}}\uc2  in Helper, Utah.\par \par \uc2 Want to meet someone from across the divide? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/oct/11/vaccines-cycling-tax-rises-we-want-your-views-on-divisive-issues?cmp=qrsatmag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Find out how to take part}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230225ej2p000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
