\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Why have young men fallen out of love with romantic relationships?\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,313 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 February 2023\par 18:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Men aren\u8217\'20\'19t naturally stoic: they\u8217\'20\'19re just taught from a young age that emotions are for girls \u8211\'20\'13 and then people wonder why young men are so lonely\par \par \uc2 Why are so many young men single?\par \par \uc2 Sex, numerous studies show, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/people-have-been-having-less-sex-whether-theyre-teenagers-or-40-somethings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 going out of fashion}}}\uc2 . Young people aren\u8217\'20\'19t shagging much any more, a phenomenon that has been widely blamed on technology and online porn. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not just sexual activity that\u8217\'20\'19s declining \u8211\'20\'13 young men in the US appear to have fallen out of love with romantic relationships. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2023/02/08/for-valentines-day-5-facts-about-single-americans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent Pew Research}}}\uc2  study has found that 63% of men under 30 describe themselves as single, compared with 34% of women in the same age bracket. Cue a lot of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/02/23/6-out-of-10-young-men-are-single-disturbing-reasons-why/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatic}}}\uc2  headlines about, as the Hill put it, the \u8220\'20\'1Clarger breakdown in the social, romantic and sexual life of the American male\u8221\'20\'1D. I imagine the Hill is referring to the heterosexual American male here, but Pew also looked at people who identify as LGB and found 62% of LGB men report being single compared to 37% of LGB women.\par \par \uc2 Before we delve deeper into the sexual life of the American male, I\u8217\'20\'19d just like to point out that the \uc2 Pew Research\uc2  study was actually conducted last summer but they republished the findings in a Valentine\u8217\'20\'19s Day listicle. This caught the attention of someone at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/blogs/blog-briefing-room/3868557-most-young-men-are-single-most-young-women-are-not/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill}}}\uc2 , who wrote an article headlined: \u8220\'20\'1CMost young men are single. Most young women are not.\u8221\'20\'1D A screenshot of that article then went viral because, well, those numbers don\u8217\'20\'19t really make much sense, do they? Unlike China and India, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/graphics/2018/world/too-many-men/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 men outnumber women by 70 million}}}\uc2 , there are about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/08/31/global-population-skews-male-but-un-projects-parity-between-sexes-by-2050/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same number}}}\uc2  of young men as women in the US. Who are all the young women dating? Pete Davidson? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/think/opinion/what-tiktok-s-west-elm-caleb-says-about-dating-social-ncna1288021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Elm Caleb}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 Nobody seems entirely sure what the reason for the giant relationship gap is but the most popular theory is that young women are more likely to be dating older men. Another, rather overblown, theory is that the Gay Agenda is working and, considering one-fifth of Gen Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/changing-america/3811406-new-studies-find-millions-of-young-nonbinary-and-transgender-americans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 identifies as queer}}}\uc2 , all the young women are dating each other. Another issue potentially feeding into the data discrepancy is the fact that that there could be gendered differences in how people define a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted relationship\u8221\'20\'1D. (The Pew definition of single is \u8220\'20\'1Cthose who are not married, living with a partner, or in a committed relationship\u8221\'20\'1D.)\par \par \uc2 While we may never solve the mystery behind the relationship gap, there\u8217\'20\'19s been a lot of handwringing about these numbers, mainly from conservative circles who take it as evidence that feminism and the modern world (particularly porn) has emasculated young men. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SethDillon/status/1628615053485154305?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seth Dillon}}}\uc2 , for example, the founder of the conservative satire site the Babylon Bee, tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CYoung women are dating each other or older men in record numbers. As a result, 60% of young men are single and lonely. It\u8217\'20\'19s probably hard to overstate how serious this problem is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Is that really true though? I\u8217\'20\'19m not denying that there\u8217\'20\'19s a serious and worrying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/the-state-our-unions/202208/whats-behind-the-rise-lonely-single-men"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 epidemic of loneliness}}}\uc2  among young American men, but you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to be in a relationship to be happy. I think that rather than focusing on young men being single, the real problem is the fact that men {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harpersbazaar.com/culture/features/a27259689/toxic-masculinity-male-friendships-emotional-labor-men-rely-on-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t have friends}}}\uc2 . Only 21% of men, for example, said they received emotional support from a friend within the past week, compared to 41% of women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/health-wellness/2023/02/03/male-friendship-lonely-close-friends-men/11162423002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a 2021 survey}}}\uc2 . Why is that? Well, the Hill quotes \uc2 Richard Reeves\uc2 , a senior fellow at the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  and the author of the book Of Boys and Men, who explains that \u8220\'20\'1Cmen are less naturally relational than women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That bizarre quote pretty much sums the whole issue up, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t it? Men aren\u8217\'20\'19t naturally stoic: they\u8217\'20\'19re just taught from a young age that feelings and emotions are for girls. They\u8217\'20\'19re taught to lock up their feelings. They\u8217\'20\'19re taught not to put as much value in relationships as women. They\u8217\'20\'19re taught that they\u8217\'20\'19re \u8220\'20\'1Cless naturally relational\u8221\'20\'1D. And then people sit around wondering why young men aren\u8217\'20\'19t in relationships and are so lonely. It\u8217\'20\'19s not porn that\u8217\'20\'19s the problem, it\u8217\'20\'19s patriarchy.\par \par \uc2 Is the word \u8216\'20\'18placenta\u8217\'20\'19 pornographic?\par \par \uc2 The popular AI image generator Midjourney seems to think so. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.technologyreview.com/2023/02/24/1069093/ai-image-generator-midjourney-blocks-porn-by-banning-words-about-the-human-reproductive-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MIT Technology Review}}}\uc2  has discovered that it bans a lot of words relating to the human reproductive system as prompts. Naughty words include: \u8220\'20\'1Curethra\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ccervix\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Chymen\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csperm\u8221\'20\'1D. While some terms relate to the male reproductive system, the bans \u8220\'20\'1Cskew predominantly female \u8230\'20\'26 demonstrat[ing] how the tendency for AI systems to sexualize women extends all the way to their internal organs.\par \par \uc2 A woman died every two minutes because of preventable pregnancy or childbirth-related issues in 2020\par \par \uc2 From 2016 to 2020, maternal mortality rates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/maternal-mortality-rose-europe-north-america-report-rcna71833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stagnated}}}\uc2  in a majority of countries according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240068759"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 World Health Organization report.}}}\uc2  However, they rose in 17 countries including much of Europe and Northern America.\par \par \uc2 Gen Z women expect to make $6,200 less than men after graduating\par \par \uc2 A new survey has found that there isn\u8217\'20\'19t just a gender pay gap, there\u8217\'20\'19s an expectation gap. Women expect to make less after graduating than men do, meaning they\u8217\'20\'19re not as likely to ask {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/02/24/gen-z-women-expect-to-make-6200-less-than-men-after-graduating-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for more money}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Good news for female founders in the UK\par \par \uc2 The number of UK companies started by women has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-22/female-founders-started-record-150-000-new-companies-last-year?tpcc=nlbroadsheet&leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than doubled}}}\uc2  since 2018.\par \par \uc2 Lawyer argues fetus of jailed pregnant woman in Florida is being illegally detained\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fetal personhood movement has certainly gained traction, moving from a fringe idea to codified laws across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/23/florida-lawyer-jailed-pregnant-woman-fetal-personhood-reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a spokesperson for Pregnancy Justice said in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd while their goal is to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and control people\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy, they\u8217\'20\'19ve given little thought to how this impacts all facets of the law beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling where this will end: HOV lanes, taxes, worker\u8217\'20\'19s comp, child custody/kidnapping cases, criminal law and on and on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Only 14% of Republican voters think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be totally illegal\par \par \uc2 A new report from the non-partisan Public Religion Research Institute has found that Americans have become more supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Notably, only 14% of Republicans want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely banned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2023/02/abortion-rights-young-americans-increasing-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared with 22% in 2010}}}\uc2 . That number is largely due to Republican women moderating their views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The study is a reminder that the people driving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the US are an extremist minority and don\u8217\'20\'19t represent popular opinion\par \par \uc2 An Alabama lawmaker wants to make having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a homicide under state law\par \par \uc2 Ernie Yarbrough, a Republican who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/alabama-lawmaker-who-ran-on-medical-freedom-proposes-mu-1850151791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran on a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical freedom\u8221\'20\'1D platform}}}\uc2  has introduced a bill proposing murder charges for having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bills like this have been proposed before and haven\u8217\'20\'19t passed. It\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely this will pass either but it\u8217\'20\'19s a reminder of what the endgame for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists is: punishing and controlling women.\par \par \uc2 The week in potato-archy\par \par \uc2 Dawn Sagar, an Englishwoman, was happily munching crisps (or potato chips, if you\u8217\'20\'19re American) at work when she discovered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-shropshire-64758641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heart-shaped crisp in the packet}}}\uc2 . Ooh, she thought, that\u8217\'20\'19s nice! She sent a photo to her friends and then ate the crisp. As it turns out that was a very expensive (albeit tasty) mistake. Walkers, the crisp company, was running a competition that awarded \u163\'00\'A3100,000 to anyone who finds the best crisp in the shape of a heart. At first I felt sorry for Sagar, whose saga was covered by the likes of the BBC, but having done extensive research into this very important issue I have discovered that heart-shaped crisps are actually pretty common and she may not have won anyway. Hopefully she can take heart from that.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230225ej2p001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
