\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First lady signals \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will seek second presidential term \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,620 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2023\par 21:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jill Biden tells AP: \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s not finished what he\u8217\'20\'19s started\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8fad88f086ef9d795a95a#block-63f8fad88f086ef9d795a95a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made clear}}}\uc2  she thinks her husband, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , will stand for a second term \u8211\'20\'13 though we are still waiting for an announcement from the man himself. Otherwise, top American officials spent most of the day restating their support for Ukraine on the one-year anniversary of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion. Speaking before the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8df708f086ef9d795a736#block-63f8df708f086ef9d795a736"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that anything less than Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full withdrawal from the territory it seized will weaken the global body\u8217\'20\'19s charter, while Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8ed928f08ea98983abcf8#block-63f8ed928f08ea98983abcf8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted the bipartisan nature}}}\uc2  of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support for Kyiv. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8d2bf8f08305414a370c9#block-63f8d2bf8f08305414a370c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many Republicans}}}\uc2  do indeed support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s cause \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8efba8f08ea98983abd0c#block-63f8efba8f08ea98983abd0c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others in the party}}}\uc2  argue it is a distraction from more pressing issues. This divide could prove crucial to the course of the war in the months to come.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Blinken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8e4508f08ea98983abc5c#block-63f8e4508f08ea98983abc5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  China against getting involved in the conflict by providing Russia with weapons.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f90b588f08305414a374bc#block-63f90b588f08305414a374bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  conservative efforts to block access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The American public{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8d8ad8f08ea98983abb6e#block-63f8d8ad8f08ea98983abb6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is divided}}}\uc2  over how long to support Kyiv, with more Republicans preferring limits on US aid, and more Democrats in favor of helping them fight against Russia until the job is done.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Treasury{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8cabc8f08ea98983aba9b#block-63f8cabc8f08ea98983aba9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  new sanctions against Russian individuals and companies involved in the war effort, but such measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8cf278f08ea98983abad3#block-63f8cf278f08ea98983abad3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 haven\u8217\'20\'19t proven}}}\uc2  as successful as Washington has hoped.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It turns out that Democrats in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f914b38f086ef9d795aa5f#block-63f914b38f086ef9d795aa5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have access}}}\uc2  to the 40,000 hours of footage Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy gave \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has released a photo from earlier today, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked the one-year anniversary of the invasion of Ukraine with its president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  and the leaders of the \uc2 G7\uc2 , as America\u8217\'20\'19s top allies are known.\par \par \uc2 The group includes Canada, Germany, the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , Japan, Britain, France and Italy:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, President Biden met with G7 Leaders and President Zelenskyy to continue coordinating our efforts to support Ukraine and hold Russia accountable for its war. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JDs4Z3geY4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JDs4Z3geY4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1629209564309598209?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As Biden inches closer to announcing what is widely expected (most importantly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8fad88f086ef9d795a95a#block-63f8fad88f086ef9d795a95a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by his wife}}}\uc2  ) to be his re-election campaign, a poll released earlier this week brought good news for his standing among Democrats.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/the-2024-presidential-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The NPR/PBS NewsHour/Marist Poll}}}\uc2  shows an even half of Democrats or Democratic-leaning independents believe the party has a better chance with Biden as the nominee, against 45% who think they\u8217\'20\'19d be better off backing someone else. That\u8217\'20\'19s an improvement for the president from November of last year, when it was roughly flipped: then, 54% wanted someone else, while a mere 38% backed Biden.\par \par \uc2 The survey also had bad news for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in his quest to be renominated for the presidency by the GOP. Among Republicans and independents who lean towards the party, 54% believe the GOP is best off with someone other than Trump as the nominee, while 42% thought the ex-president remained the best man for the job.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with congressional Democrats next week, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 His allies hold the majority in the Senate but lost control of the House following last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, though only by a handful of seats. Punchbowl reports he will first meet with House Democrats during their annual retreat in Baltimore:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden will speak to House Dems on Wednesday in Baltimore, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeteAguilar?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PeteAguilar}}}\uc2  announces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qKpRM94FZe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qKpRM94FZe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Bresnahan (@bresreports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bresreports/status/1629211575721549826?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Then with senators:\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer\u8217\'20\'19s office says Biden will speak at a special Senate Dem caucus lunch next Thursday\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1629184586734264323?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/23/kevin-mccarthy-tucker-carlson-jan-6-tapes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 erupted in fury}}}\uc2  when they found out that Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy handed over to \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  40,000 hours of video footage surveillance and other cameras in the Capitol picked up on January 6.\par \par \uc2 The concern was not only that it could reveal details of the building\u8217\'20\'19s security, but also that Carlson, a conservative firebrand who has repeatedly downplayed the severity of the insurrection before his audience of millions, would use the footage to distort what happened that day.\par \par \uc2 As it turns out, Democratic leaders in Congress have access to that footage as well. \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  opinion columnist Greg Sargent confirmed as much from the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/02/23/mccarthy-jan-6-footage-tucker-carlson-propaganda/?utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=wp_opinions&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In his column today}}}\uc2 , he argues that Democrats should fight fire with fire, and release the footage to news organizations in an attempt to counter whatever Carlson has planned for what he\u8217\'20\'19s been given.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a quick dip into Trumpworld, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has an exclusive on the ongoing mess that is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s possession of classified materials:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/12/trump-was-issued-subpoena-for-folder-marked-classified-evening-briefing-discovered-at-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a box of White House schedules, including some that were marked classified}}}\uc2 , at his Mar-a-Lago resort in December because a junior aide to the former president had transported it from another office in Florida after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  completed its search of the property.\par \par \uc2 The former president does not appear to have played a direct role in the mishandling of the box, though he remains under investigation for the possible improper retention of national security documents and obstruction of justice. This previously unreported account of the retrieval was revealed by two sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Known internally as ROTUS, short for Receptionist of the United States, the junior aide initially kept the box at a converted guest bungalow at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  called the \u8220\'20\'1Ctennis cottage\u8221\'20\'1D after Trump left office, and she soon took it with her to a government-leased office in the Palm Beach area.\par \par \uc2 The box remained at the government-leased office from where the junior aide worked through most of 2022, explaining why neither Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer who searched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  in June for any classified-marked papers nor the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents who searched the property in August found the documents.\par \par \uc2 Around the time that Trump returned to Mar-a-Lago from his Bedminster golf club in New Jersey at the end of the summer, the junior aide was told that she was being relocated to a desk in the anteroom of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own office at Mar-a-Lago that was previously assigned to top aide Molly Michael.\par \par \uc2 The junior aide retrieved her work belongings \u8211\'20\'13 including the box \u8211\'20\'13 from the government-leased office and took them to her new Mar-a-Lago workspace around September. At that time, the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s criminal investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retention of national security documents was intensifying.\par \par \uc2 Several weeks after the junior aide moved into her new workspace, federal prosecutors told Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers in October that they suspected the former president was still in possession of additional documents with classified markings despite the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago on 8 August.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  condemned the \u8220\'20\'1Cpartisan and political attacks\u8221\'20\'1D on reproductive rights that have put the fate of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the hands of a single, conservative judge in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Convening a White House meeting with reproductive rights advocates and providers on Friday, Harris addressed the pending lawsuit, brought by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, that threatens the access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not just an attack on women\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental freedoms. It is an attack on the very foundation of our public health system,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now accounts for the majority of abortions in the US. It is also used as a miscarriage treatment. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/09/abortion-pill-trump-judge-possible-ban-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that a decision to reverse a decades-old approval of the drug by the Federal Drug Administration would have \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D consequences for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health.\par \par \uc2 Harris said the legal challenge, as well as legislative efforts in Republican-led states that would restrict access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amounted to an attempt by political activists to undermine the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority, accusing them of trying to \u8220\'20\'1Cquestion the legitimacy of a group of scientists and doctors who have studied the significance of this drug.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice president said supporters of the lawsuit should \u8220\'20\'1Clook in their own medicine cabinets\u8221\'20\'1D and question whether they would be willing to do away with any \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medication that they use to alleviate pain and improve their quality of life. \u8220\'20\'1CMifepristone is no exception to that process,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, in combination with a second drug, in 2000, deeming it a safe and effective way to terminate a pregnancy up to 10-weeks.\par \par \uc2 During the pandemic, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  expanded access to the pills by allowing patients to obtain them by mail through telehealth rather than requiring in-person hospital or clinic visits. The agency further broadened the availability of the medication when it announced in January it would allow certified retail pharmacies to dispense mifepristone, known under the brand name Mifeprex.\par \par \uc2 US District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk has not indicated when he will rule, but advocates are preparing for a possible decision as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court decision to end the Constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Harris has led the administration\u8217\'20\'19s public response.\par \par \uc2 During Friday\u8217\'20\'19s roundtable, she said the participants would discuss ways to ensure Americans are aware of the lawsuit and its possible ramifications as well as what policymakers and providers could to ensure patients \u8220\'20\'1Chave access to the medication that they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Last weekend, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  clandestinely traveled to Ukraine via a mode of travel he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-baltimore-rail-tunnel-project-191caf5db5cbd4facceb4f3369f0c72f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personally prefers}}}\uc2 , but which is unusual for a modern American president: a passenger train. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peterbeaumont"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Beaumont}}}\uc2  spoke to the man who made it happen:\par \par \uc2 Alexander Kamyshin, the head of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s railway company \uc2 Ukrzaliznytsia\uc2 , doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get much sleep at the best of times. On Sunday night, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  was being ferried into Ukraine in a 10-hour night journey from Poland \u8211\'20\'13 in a carriage now known as \u8220\'20\'1CRail Force One\u8221\'20\'1D, he got almost none.\par \par \uc2 Along with others involved in the secret operation to bring the US president to his meeting with \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , Kamyshin watched the progress of the train in a command centre.\par \par \uc2 A handsome bearded man sporting a hipster-ish braid of hair that falls over the shaved sides of his head, Kamyshin is deliberately vague about many of the details.\par \par \uc2 But in the past year, his dedicated team has brought in world leaders, VIPs and diplomatic missions on an almost daily basis as part of a programme called \u8220\'20\'1CIron Diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Security is everything, he told the Guardian in an interview at Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s main railway station. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not had one leak. There have been no photographs from train attendants. We respect the confidence of the delegations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a challenge. It\u8217\'20\'19s our job that we do every day. Imagine,\u8221\'20\'1D he says with smile, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president of the United States coming to a war-torn country by train.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/24/how-ukraine-railways-keeps-people-and-presidents-moving"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Rail Force One\u8217\'20\'19: how Ukraine railways got Joe Biden safely to Kyiv}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video that\u8217\'20\'19s worth watching of Jill Biden describing her husband\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to continue serving as president for a second term:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lcknlSQPOy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lcknlSQPOy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zeke Miller (@ZekeJMiller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZekeJMiller/status/1629186928175198215?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden has long been described as a key figure in US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s orbit as he plans his future \u8211\'20\'13 after today revealing to the Associated Press that he\u8217\'20\'19s close to confirming he\u8217\'20\'19ll seek a second term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Because I\u8217\'20\'19m his wife,\u8221\'20\'1D she laughed, AP writes.\par \par \uc2 But she brushed off the question about whether she has the deciding vote on whether the president runs for reelection.\par \par \uc2 Of course he\u8217\'20\'19ll listen to me, because we\u8217\'20\'19re a married couple,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. But, she added later, \u8220\'20\'1Che makes up his own mind, believe me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden participates in a women's empowerment reception, with Kenyan women leaders in government, business, research, and education, during the second leg of her African visit, at the Chief of Mission\u8217\'20\'19s Residence, in Kenya today. Photograph: Thomas Mukoya/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Biden did the interview in Kenya, during the second leg of her trip to Africa this week. Earlier she was in Namibia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Strongest sign yet that Biden will seek second term\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden has given one of the clearest indications yet that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will run for a second term, telling The Associated Press in an exclusive interview today that there\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty much\u8221\'20\'1D nothing left to do but figure out the time and place for the announcement.\par \par \uc2 Although Biden has long said that it\u8217\'20\'19s his intention to seek reelection, he has yet to make it official, and he\u8217\'20\'19s struggled to dispel questions about whether he\u8217\'20\'19s too old to continue serving as president. Biden would be 86 at the end of a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe says he\u8217\'20\'19s not done,\u8221\'20\'1D the first lady said in Nairobi, the second and final stop of her five-day trip to Africa. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not finished what he\u8217\'20\'19s started. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CHow many times does he have to say it for you to believe it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden aides have said an announcement is likely to come in April, after the first fundraising quarter ends, which is around the time that Barack Obama officially launched his reelection campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Top US officials have restated their support for Ukraine on the one-year anniversary of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion. Speaking before the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8df708f086ef9d795a736#block-63f8df708f086ef9d795a736"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that anything less than Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full withdrawal from territory it seized will weaken the global body\u8217\'20\'19s charter, while \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8ed928f08ea98983abcf8#block-63f8ed928f08ea98983abcf8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted the bipartisan nature}}}\uc2  of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support for Kyiv. And indeed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8d2bf8f08305414a370c9#block-63f8d2bf8f08305414a370c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many Republicans}}}\uc2  support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s cause \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8efba8f08ea98983abd0c#block-63f8efba8f08ea98983abd0c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others in the party}}}\uc2  argue it is a distraction from more pressing issues. This divide could prove crucial to the outcome of the war in the months to come.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Blinken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8e4508f08ea98983abc5c#block-63f8e4508f08ea98983abc5c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  China against getting involved in the conflict by providing Russia with weapons.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The American public{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8d8ad8f08ea98983abb6e#block-63f8d8ad8f08ea98983abb6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is divided}}}\uc2  over how long to support Kyiv, with more Republicans preferring limits on US aid, and more Democrats in favor of helping them fight against Russia until the job is done.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Treasury{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8cabc8f08ea98983aba9b#block-63f8cabc8f08ea98983aba9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  new sanctions against Russian individuals and companies involved in the war effort, but such measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/feb/24/biden-zelenskiy-meeting-g7-ukraine-aid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63f8cf278f08ea98983abad3#block-63f8cf278f08ea98983abad3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 haven\u8217\'20\'19t proven}}}\uc2  as successful as Washington has hoped.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 But the bipartisan comity over Ukraine has its limits.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been a definite increase over the past year in the number of lawmakers who have questioned Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support to Ukraine, particularly among Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Their argument is that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cares more about Ukraine than various issues at home, especially those they\u8217\'20\'19ve turned into cudgels against the administration such as border security, or the recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/15/ohio-train-derailment-palestine-toxic-chemical-leak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derailment of a train carrying toxic chemicals}}}\uc2  in East Palestine, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 This tweet from GOP senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  captures the dynamic well:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Republican Party can be the party of Ukraine and globalists or the party of East Palestine and working Americans. Not both\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  (@HawleyMO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HawleyMO/status/1629139650588573699?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s in the House where some of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/17/how-big-a-threat-does-the-hard-right-pose-to-us-support-for-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s biggest congressional foes can be found}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t care more about Ukraine than we do our own country. President Biden has failed to lead on the train derailment, the border, inflation, crime, and so much more,\u8221\'20\'1D House Republican Jake LaTurner said in a statement released today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe White House continues to prioritize Ukraine while leaving American communities behind. It\u8217\'20\'19s unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And while the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  issued a statement of strong support for Ukraine today, his counterpart in the House, speaker Kevin McCarthy, has made no public statement that this blog is aware of.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back in Washington, \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  was one of several Republican lawmakers who tweeted strong statements of support for Ukraine on the war\u8217\'20\'19s one-year anniversary \u8211\'20\'13 which caught the eye of Democratic president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden has been eager to play up the bipartisan nature of US support for Ukraine. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Romney, who represents Utah in the Senate and was the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president in 2012, had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is in America\u8217\'20\'19s interest to support Ukraine. If Russia can invade, subjugate, and pillage Ukraine with impunity, it will do the same again to others, and a world at war diminishes the security of Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  (@MittRomney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MittRomney/status/1628817687098060800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And here is Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response:\par \par \uc2 enltrI think Senator Romney would be the first to tell you that we don\u8217\'20\'19t always agree.\par \par \uc2 But he knows what I know: that standing with Ukraine \u8212\'20\'14 and standing up for freedom \u8212\'20\'14 advances our national security. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X67SkDIL6W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/X67SkDIL6W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1629148566835933187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  spoke highly of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s will to fight in his interview with ABC News, he declined to say whether he thought the war would still be raging this time next year.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from his appearance:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHere we are, a year later \u8212\'20\'14 Ukraine is still standing. It remains free. It remains independent. Putin's first objective was to erase Ukraine from the map \u8230\'20\'26 That failed and will never succeed.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @secblinken}}}\uc2  on the one year anniversary of war in Ukraine. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QmvhIPiiZk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QmvhIPiiZk}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SwZiga6cCP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SwZiga6cCP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Good Morning America (@GMA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GMA/status/1629093289008955392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A particular concern for the United States and Kyiv alike is the possibility that China could intervene in the conflict by providing Russia with weapons.\par \par \uc2 American officials have issued strong statements in recent days warning Beijing against getting involved. In an appearance on ABC News this morning, US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  summed up his message to China in three words: \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t do it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re very concerned that they\u8217\'20\'19re thinking about it. Up until now, Chinese companies have provided non-lethal support,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom day one, President Biden warned President Xi not to provide material lethal assistance to Russia for use against Ukraine or to engage in the systematic evasion of sanctions. And the information we have suggests that they\u8217\'20\'19re now actively thinking about it, which is why we\u8217\'20\'19ve been public about warning them not to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The United States\u8217\'20\'19s warning about China\u8217\'20\'19s potential involvement is the latest example of how it has tried to pre-empt Russia and its allies\u8217\'20\'19 war strategy by releasing intelligence shortly after it is gathered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe always have to get the balance right between making sure that we\u8217\'20\'19re protecting the way we get our information and releasing it,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken told ABC. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we thought it was really important to make clear that China\u8217\'20\'19s looking at this. And what they\u8217\'20\'19re hearing not just from us but from many other countries around the world is: Don\u8217\'20\'19t do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking before the global body\u8217\'20\'19s security council, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  argued that the United Nations charter demands Russia withdraw from Ukraine and hand back the territory it seized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistory teaches us that it\u8217\'20\'19s the nature of peace that matters. For peace to be just, it must uphold the principles at the heart of the UN Charter: sovereignty, territorial integrity, independence. For peace to be durable, it must ensure that Russia can\u8217\'20\'19t simply rest rearm and relaunched the war in a few months, or a few years. Any peace that legitimizes Russia\u8217\'20\'19s seizure of land by force will weaken the charter and send a message to would-be the aggressors everywhere that they can invade countries and get away with it,\u8221\'20\'1D the US secretary of state said.\par \par \uc2 He specifically warned against normalizing the types of war crimes the United States accuses Russia of commiting in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can never let the crimes that Russia has committed become our new normal. Bucha is not normal. Mariupol is not normal. Irpin is not normal,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said, referring to cities where Russia is accused of deliberately killing large numbers of civilians. \u8220\'20\'1CBombing schools and hospitals and apartment buildings to rubble is not normal. Stealing Ukrainian children from their families and giving them to people in Russia is not normal. We must not let President Putin\u8217\'20\'19s callous indifference to human life become our own. We must force ourselves to remember that behind every atrocity in this wretched war, in conflicts around the world, is a human being.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state Blinken addresses \uc2 UN\uc2  security council\par \par \uc2 US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  is speaking before the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council on the one-year anniversary of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Follow this blog for the latest updates from his address.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A new poll indicates Americans are growing split over how much longer to provide aid to Ukraine, with the divide occurring along familiar partisan lines.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/official-polls/fox-news-poll-half-say-us-should-support-ukraine-long-as-it-takes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Fox News survey}}}\uc2  finds 50% of respondents argue Washington should support Ukraine for as long as it takes them to win against Russia, while 46% believe there should be some sort of time limit on the support.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are more in favor of sticking with Kyiv, with 66% percent backing support until victory over Russia is achieved. By a 61% margin, Republicans support the idea of a time limit. Independents are divided more closely, with 49% backing a time limit and 45% in favor of long-term support.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has put out a statement expressing strong continued support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Though he\u8217\'20\'19s one of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chief antagonists in Congress, McConnell has generally approved of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s strategy towards Kyiv, and reiterated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.republicanleader.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/mcconnell-on-one-year-anniversary-of-ukraine-escalation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in his statement today}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s part of it:\par \par \uc2 As my fellow leading Republicans and I have explained, it is not an act of charity for the United States and our \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies to help supply the Ukrainian people\u8217\'20\'19s self-defense. It is a direct investment in our own core national interests. America is a world power with worldwide interests. Our security and prosperity are deeply intertwined with a secure and stable Europe. If Putin were given a green light to destabilize Europe, invading and killing at will, the long-term cost to the United States in both dollars and security risks would be astronomically higher than the miniscule fraction of our GDP that we have invested in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense thus far.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The United States hoped its aggressive sanctions regime would crush Russia\u8217\'20\'19s economy and convince president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to rethink his invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 It hasn\u8217\'20\'19t quite turned out that way.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-02-17/putin-s-war-to-lop-190-billion-off-economy-in-delayed-reckoning?cmpid=BBD022423_NEF&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_term=230224&utm_campaign=nef&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2  that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s economy shrunk by 2.5% last year \u8211\'20\'13 far from the 10% drop expected when the US and its allies first announced the economic countermeasures. Meanwhile, Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s central bank projects economic growth could resume this year.\par \par \uc2 That said, the country is on course to lose a lot of money, specifically $190bn in GDP by 2026 compared to the economy\u8217\'20\'19s trajectory before the war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New US penalties target Russian mining sector, sanctions evaders\par \par \uc2 The United States has announced a new battery of sanctions again Russia, targeting its mining sector and dozens of people and companies involved in helping it evade Washington\u8217\'20\'19s trade restrictions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Treasury department}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Ukrainian people continue to valiantly defend their homeland and their freedom, the United States is proud to support Ukraine through economic, security, and humanitarian assistance,\u8221\'20\'1D Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said in announcing the penalties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past year, we have taken actions with a historic coalition of international partners to degrade Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military-industrial complex and reduce the revenues that it uses to fund its war. Our sanctions have had both short-term and long-term impact, seen acutely in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s struggle to replenish its weapons and in its isolated economy. Our actions today with our \uc2 G7\uc2  partners show that we will stand with Ukraine for as long as it takes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The newly sanctioned individuals and companies include \u8220\'20\'1Cfirms that produce or import specialized, high-technology equipment used by Russian defense entities and companies that make advanced materials used in Russian weapons systems,\u8221\'20\'1D Treasury said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Washington crucial to Ukraine war effort \u8212\'20\'14 but Kyiv argues for more\par \par \uc2 Sanctions, weapons and statements: while it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t sent its own troops, the United States has made a robust effort to help Ukraine and penalize Russia ever since Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s troops poured over its borders a year ago today.\par \par \uc2 The aid and intelligence approved by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has proved crucial to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s battlefield success, which has seen it not only fend off Russia\u8217\'20\'19s initial attempt to storm the capital, but also retake ground lost in the war\u8217\'20\'19s early days. On top of that have been public statements of support from Biden and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , who have visited each other capitals even as the war raged.\par \par \uc2 But Ukraine has continued to ask for more sophisticated weapons it argues it needs to sustain the war effort \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/19/us-f-16s-ukraine-un-ambassador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recently advanced fighter jets}}}\uc2 . These negotiations form one of the few public points of tension between Kyiv and its western supporters, but could prove decisive in determining the war\u8217\'20\'19s trajectory.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine war enters second year amid questions of continued US aid\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today marks the first anniversary of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, a grim milestone in a conflict that shows no sign of ending, and in which the United States has played a major role. Aid, particularly of weapons and ammunitions, from Washington and its European allies has proven vital to Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s defense against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s assault, and President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  continues to push for more. He has an ally in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but while they have yet to decisively turn against assisting Ukraine, there are signs Republicans are growing wary of Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s cause. Expect to hear plenty about this dynamic today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden and Zelenskiy will hold a virtual meeting with leaders of \uc2 G7\uc2  countries at 9am eastern time to discuss efforts to aid Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  will speak before the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council at 10am about the war\u8217\'20\'19s anniversary.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold a meeting on reproductive healthcare access at 11 am.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230224ej2o001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
