\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Pro-choice advocates file paperwork for Ohio ballot initiative on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 753 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2023\par 21:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coalition of lawyers, doctors and activists hope to put the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to state voters after toppling of Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Today, reproductive health advocates in Ohio are handing in language to the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, looking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohioansforreproductivefreedom.org/news/press-release/groups-file-reproductive-freedom-constitutional-amendment-paperwork-with-ohio-attorney-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bring a ballot initiative on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to voters in November 2023}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade last summer \u8211\'20\'13 which had secured a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an Ohio ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy immediately came into effect. That ban was then put on hold by an Ohio judge in October 2022, restoring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state up to 22 weeks of pregnancy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acluohio.org/en/press-releases/ohio-lower-court-grant-preliminary-injunction-six-week-abortion-ban-will-remain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 until further notice}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the group bringing the petition, Ohioans United for Reproductive Rights (OPRR), are hoping to put the issue to rest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COhioans are perilously close to losing access to safe, legal, comprehensive reproductive medical care,\u8221\'20\'1D OPRR executive director Dr Lauren Beene said in a virtual press conference today, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThis commonsense amendment ensures that physicians will be able to provide the care our patients need and deserve free from government interference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Once the language has been submitted, the Ohio Ballot Board and attorney general each has ten days to review it. If approved, campaigners will need to collect in excess of 400,000 signatures in order to qualify to be on the ballot. If the ballot language is denied, campaigners \u8211\'20\'13 a coalition of lawyers, doctors and activists from organizations such as Planned Parenthood, the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and Ohio Physicians for Reproductive Rights \u8211\'20\'13 will have to make changes and re-submit it.\par \par \uc2 The ballot could be the seventh such ballot to put the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to voters. In August 2022, voters in Kansas sent shock waves through the country when they rejected a ballot initiative brought by an anti-choice legislature, looking to confirm there was no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protected by the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting 59% to 41%}}}\uc2  in favor of protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the ballot reaffirmed an earlier decision by the Kansas supreme court in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/kansas-court-strikes-down-abortion-method-ban-reaffirming-right-to-abortion-under-state-constitution/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stating \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is indeed protected in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, under the right to autonomy}}}\uc2 . The loss sent a stark warning to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions may not be successful at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 string of similar wins for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  during the 2022 midterms only added to that warning, when ballot initiatives brought in California, Kentucky, Michigan, Montana and Vermont all further secured \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights when put to a popular vote.\par \par \uc2 Since the midterms, legislatures across the country have made moves to blunt the force of citizen-led ballot initiatives in states that allow them. At present, Florida, Missouri, Ohio, Idaho, Oklahoma and North Dakota are all weighing bills that would make it harder for ballot initiatives to be passed.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiohouse.gov/members/brian-stewart/news/stewart-reintroduces-ohio-constitution-protection-amendment-113094"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , a bill has been introduced looking to raise the threshold for ballot proposals to be accepted, from a simple majority to 60% of the vote. It would also require those bringing a petition to collect signatures from all 88 Ohio counties instead of the 44 counties currently required to get a measure on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 That same bill did not garner enough support to get past the house when it was brought in a legislative session just a few months ago, in December 2022. If passed this time, the question of whether to restrict the citizen-led ballot initiative process will also be put to voters in November 2023.\par \par \uc2 Polling suggests that Ohioans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/04/upshot/polling-abortion-states.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support keeping \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  mostly legal in the state}}}\uc2 . Ohio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/religious-landscape-study/state/ohio/views-about-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  tend to be less supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights than independent voters and Democrats, but research on a small sample by Suffolk University in 2022 suggests that most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.suffolk.edu/news-features/news/2022/06/06/15/41/suffolk-poll-shows-ohio-voters-want-abortion-rights-protected"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohioans would vote to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights given the opportunity}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe tremendous and unprecedented level of grassroots support for our effort to constitutionally protect reproductive rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is truly inspiring and demonstrates how necessary this issue is for Ohioans,\u8221\'20\'1D OPRR president Dr Marcela Azevedo said at the press conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are eager to begin collecting the signatures needed to place the amendment on the ballot so Ohioans, rather than government and extremist politicians, have the opportunity to determine the future of reproductive health care in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 21 February 2023. An earlier version said paperwork had been filed for a referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than a ballot initiative.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230221ej2l0038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
