\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a war\u8217\'20\'19: the doctor who wants Americans to get  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills before it\u8217\'20\'19s too late\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,375 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2023\par 15:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rebecca Gomperts has found innovative ways to circumvent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions worldwide \u8211\'20\'13 and a US ruling could make her work even more urgent\par \par \uc2 In the first month of the coronavirus pandemic, when planes from India temporarily stopped flying, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/12/rebecca-gomperts-doctor-defying-laws-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rebecca Gomperts}}}\uc2  faced a problem. A Dutch physician and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist, she had spent the two years prior shipping the pills commonly used to end a pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristone and misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 to people in countries where they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t access them. Now, mifepristone wasn\u8217\'20\'19t available to her any more.\par \par \uc2 Gomperts is a doctor who has gone to extraordinary lengths to circumvent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions around the world, including parking her boat in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/12/rebecca-gomperts-doctor-defying-laws-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 international waters}}}\uc2  outside of countries like Poland to administer abortions. So she pivoted. She trialled misoprostol-only abortions, as that drug was more easily available outside India. The results weren\u8217\'20\'19t ideal, but they were much better than nothing.\par \par \uc2 Her experience has relevance to an upcoming ruling in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/09/abortion-pill-trump-judge-possible-ban-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas lawsuit}}}\uc2  that could have national consequences. There, a judge is considering arguments from a Christian, ultra-conservative legal organization that is suing the Federal Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) over its approval of mifepristone more than two decades ago. If he rules in favor of the plaintiffs, the result will be a mifepristone ban \u8211\'20\'13 not just in Texas or other states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned, but nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The potential for the case to end access to a life-saving drug in the US for the foreseeable future is significant: the Donald Trump-appointed judge, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk}}}\uc2 , previously worked for the \uc2 First Liberty Institute\uc2 , a conservative, Christian organization that brings litigation to promote religious liberty and restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights. As a district judge, he has ruled that teenagers in Texas must seek parental consent before accessing contraception.\par \par \uc2 And so in the meantime, providers and advocates have been scrambling to work out what the country will do if one half of its medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen is no longer available in the US. To answer that question, many have been touting Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1363/psrh.12219"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research on misoprostol-only abortions}}}\uc2 , published earlier this month, suggesting they will be a viable stand-in for the more effective, two-part regimen most commonly used in the US.\par \par \uc2 But while the research is promising, Gomperts is not so sure we should settle for a less effective option.\par \par \uc2 Misoprostol-only abortions are effective 88% of the time, the study found, compared to a 98% success rate for the two-step regimen. They are also more complicated: they are more likely to result in the need for surgical interventions; they bring a risk of foetal abnormalities if the pregnancy is not terminated effectively; they result in more bleeding, cramping and pain; and they come with the potential for very expensive aftercare \u8211\'20\'13 which matters in a privatized system like the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot just say it\u8217\'20\'19s OK. It\u8217\'20\'19s not,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gomperts, striking a tone commensurate with the \u8220\'20\'1Cserene sort of audacity\u8221\'20\'1D that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/abortion-at-sea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been attributed to her}}}\uc2 , when we speak in a phone interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a doctor, you have to give the best treatment that\u8217\'20\'19s available. And we know that the best treatment possible is the two drugs combined,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 If Kacsmaryk bans mifepristone, it will be an attack on women\u8217\'20\'19s health, not just on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gomperts says.\par \par \uc2 There shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be any gatekeepers here. There shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a doctor, a pharmacy, nothing\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Gomperts\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, combined with misoprostol, is the best miscarriage treatment, she explains. Mifepristone is shown to be beneficial for people with breast cancer. It works against myoma, a condition that causes heavy bleeding in women, and endometriosis, a condition where the endometrium is outside of the womb and can cause extreme pain. And it can be used as a birth control pill \u8211\'20\'13 Gomperts is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/zxmvd-mifepristone-a-new-ondemand-contraceptive?utm_campaign=p_lico+share-sheet&utm_medium=copy_link&utm_source=customer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crowdfunding}}}\uc2  for a clinical trial to test mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s safety and effectiveness as a weekly contraceptive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really is a life-saving drug and is relevant to many conditions that women have,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gomperts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be any gatekeepers here. There shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a doctor, a pharmacy, nothing. These medicines have such a high safety profile. They\u8217\'20\'19re so safe, they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be prescribed, they should be available over the counter. That is the goal. That is what we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Of course, Gomperts recognizes that if misoprostol-only abortions are the only option, they should be used \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why she pivoted to them herself in 2020. But she thinks we should reject the premise that it\u8217\'20\'19s all we\u8217\'20\'19ve got \u8211\'20\'13 just because US courts seem to be having a dark-ages moment, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we should roll back the rights we believe ourselves to be entitled to.\par \par \uc2 No matter what Kacsmaryk rules, Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aid Access}}}\uc2 , and others like it will still be shipping mifepristone all over the US. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople should know we will continue to provide medication abortions this way, whatever the ruling is,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Get the medication now\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 conviction, in part, stems from her own experiences: her refusal to accept the status quo, whatever the restrictions. But it also stems from something she began to notice after the supreme court ended the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 Before Roe v Wade was overturned, Gomperts said people in the US who were stymied by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions felt robbed of an entitlement, and angry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were outraged, and they were upset, and they wanted to talk about that,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CThey were saying, \u8216\'20\'18Even though this is my constitutional right, I am not able to access it. That\u8217\'20\'19s wrong\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But after 24 June, the mood changed: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople became much more fearful. They think they are doing something illegal. And that is really damaging. It means that when people need to look for care, they are delayed, because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid. And that is a situation that we see everywhere in the world where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really strictly forbidden,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gomperts.\par \par \uc2 Gomperts is nonplussed by the idea of another ruling that will make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even harder to access in the US. It sounds like for her, the moment for shock has been and gone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so already so appalled by many things that are happening in the US,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gomperts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would feel rather desperate, if I were a US citizen with this supreme court, knowing that everything ends up in this court, which you cannot trust, which is a fundamentalist court, which doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the best interest of the citizens. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t consider human rights as [something] they have to uphold. This court is going to last for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 But she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t suffer from a lack of hope. For all of the obstacles the last three years have presented, she believes the pandemic has also opened up care \u8211\'20\'13 making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication much more widely understood, more readily available and cheaper. Before the pandemic, medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for about 39% of all abortions in the US \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  now, it accounts for more than half}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gomperts is always encouraged by the ways people adapt to keep getting the care they need \u8211\'20\'13 no matter what judgments are handed down.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t wait for the decision. Just get the medication now, get it in your house, get it in your hands\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Gomperts\par \par \uc2 She points to people who have already turned to the internet to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills; people who have travelled out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care; doctors who have referred patients to websites like hers for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are extremely resilient. And also innovative,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 But in the meantime, she wants people to stock up on the drugs currently available to them, fast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t wait for the decision. Just get the medication now, get it in your house, get it in your hands,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re in a war zone, and the war is coming, you also make sure you have enough food in your house. This is how it feels. It really is a war. It\u8217\'20\'19s a war on women,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230221ej2l0028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
