\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Trump judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling could ban  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill across the US\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 February 2023\par 17:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Far-right groups have asked to reverse the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, which has been on the market for decades\par \par \uc2 A Texas judge could soon upend what remains of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the US if he agrees to a request by far-right groups to reverse federal approval of a key drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which accounts for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half}}}\uc2  of pregnancy terminations nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates say the ruling could have a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D impact on the already fragile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care landscape, severely eroded last June by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/scotus-roe-wade-decision-what-happens-next#:~:text=The%20court%20decided%20there%20is,cases%20to%20grant%20more%20rights."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to overturn}}}\uc2  Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In November, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, represented by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a Christian conservative legal advocacy organization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/Alliance-for-Hippocratic-Medicine-v-FDA-2022-11-18-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2  in the northern district of Texas asking Trump-appointed Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk to require the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to reverse its longstanding approval of mifepristone, the first in a two-step \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill regimen. If the group \u8211\'20\'13 which played {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/alliance-defending-freedom-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a key role}}}\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, the supreme court case that ushered in Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise \u8211\'20\'13 is granted a nationwide injunction, as requested, the decision could apply to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday evening, Kacsmaryk filed an order allowing Danco Laboratories, the drug manufacturer, to file briefs defending its \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval. Plaintiffs have until 24 February to respond; a decision in the case could come at any time after that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ruling could be devastating for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrea Miller, president of the National Institute for Reproductive Health. \u8220\'20\'1CCutting off critical access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication \u8211\'20\'13 which is the preferred method for more than half of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients in the country \u8211\'20\'13 would cause significant harm, especially at a time when Dobbs has made it difficult or impossible for many to get care at clinics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/questions-and-answers-mifepristone-medical-termination-pregnancy-through-ten-weeks-gestation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first approved}}}\uc2  the use of mifepristone, which is taken alongside the drug misoprostol during the first 10 weeks of pregnancy, for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in 2000. More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/media/112118/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3.7 million women}}}\uc2  have used the drug since it became available in the US. Mifepristone works by blocking the pregnancy hormone progesterone, which prevents a pregnancy from growing. Taken up to two days later, misoprostol induces cramping and bleeding to empty the uterus.\par \par \uc2 The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/16/health/abortion-pills-fda.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadened access}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in 2021 by allowing patients to receive them by mail through telehealth rather than requiring in-person hospital or clinic visits, a rule change {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/24/medication-abortion-majority-2020-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompted}}}\uc2  by the Covid pandemic. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  widened access further when it announced in January it would allow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/04/abortion-pills-fda-rule-change-pharmacies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certified retail pharmacies}}}\uc2  to dispense mifepristone, known under the brand name Mifeprex. The use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steadily risen}}}\uc2  over time and now comprise at least 53% of abortions in the US, making it the most common choice for pregnancy termination.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed by four physicians and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations including the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine and the American Association of Pro-Life Obstetricians and Gynecologists, claims that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cexceeded its regulatory authority\u8221\'20\'1D by fast-tracking approval of the drug two decades ago. The groups allege that the agency erred in its legal obligations to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect the health, safety, and welfare\u8221\'20\'1D of pregnant women by eliminating necessary safeguards and \u8220\'20\'1Cignoring\u8221\'20\'1D evidence of harm.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2  is entrusted to protect the public from dangerous drugs but it has failed women and girls by approving these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills without the basic levels of protection when evaluating for safety and effectiveness,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erik Baptist, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  senior legal counsel.\par \par \uc2 In response to the suit, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  called the legal request to remove a pharmaceutical drug from the market \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary and unprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D saying that withdrawing access to mifepristone would \u8220\'20\'1Ccause significant harm\u8221\'20\'1D by depriving patients of a safe and effective drug that has been in use for more than 20 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiffs have pointed to no case, and the government has been unable to locate any example, where a court has second-guessed \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s safety and efficacy determination and ordered a widely available \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drug to be removed from the market \u8211\'20\'13 much less an example that includes a two-decade delay,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/file/1563091/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote attorneys}}}\uc2  for the US justice department in a 13 January filing.\par \par \uc2 Greer Donley, associate professor at the University of Pittsburgh Law School and expert in \uc2 FDA\uc2  law, says the suit\u8217\'20\'19s legal argument is rife with \u8220\'20\'1Cfalsehoods and mischaracterizations\u8221\'20\'1D of the regulatory agency\u8217\'20\'19s decision-making. Donley says the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Crigorously\u8221\'20\'1D reviewed mifepristone before approving it, requesting additional clinical trials and restrictions in distribution. She points to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.gao.gov%2Fassets%2Fgao-08-751.pdf&data=05%7C01%7Cdonley%40pitt.edu%7C9e2234dd9a4d4b58331d08db03abe627%7C9ef9f489e0a04eeb87cc3a526112fd0d%7C1%7C0%7C638107809184960306%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&sdata=swEmyEkmo07dZ6nEliqL4gB5aL4DyQuiJAacxPfHLNA%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 55-page audit}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Government Accountability Office\uc2  which found that \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone was consistent with its approval and oversight for other drugs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis drug was certainly not approved in a rush or haphazardly,\u8221\'20\'1D says Donley. \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, many argue the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has actually been largely overprotective and restrictive when it comes to mifepristone, so it\u8217\'20\'19s a bit ironic that these onerous regulations around the drug are being used as evidence of leniency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As one of the most studied drugs in the world, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication \u8211\'20\'13 in use for more than two decades in the US \u8211\'20\'13 is found to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fact-check-medication-abortion-783874945633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe and effective}}}\uc2 , and backed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://searchlf.ama-assn.org/letter/documentDownload?uri=/unstructured/binary/letter/LETTERS/lfdr.zip/2022-6-21-Joint-ACOG-AMA-Letter-to-FDA-re-Mifepristone.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major medical organizations}}}\uc2  including the the \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  and the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 . It holds a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/mifepristone_safety_11-15-22_Updated_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safer track record}}}\uc2  than penicillin, Viagra and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10569383/#:~:text=The%20observed%20incidence%20of%20hospitalization,CI%20%3D%204.1%20to%207.0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tylenol}}}\uc2 . Legal abortions have been found to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22270271/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 times safer}}}\uc2  than childbirth.\par \par \uc2 Removing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an option holds \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying potential consequences\u8221\'20\'1D for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients across the US, says \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , principal policy associate with reproductive health research group the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . The non-invasive method allows patients to terminate a pregnancy in their own homes, especially helpful if travel to clinics is out of reach. Some providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/mifepristone-ban-misoprostol-only-abortions-in-the-us-1850083070"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have signaled}}}\uc2  that if mifepristone is banned, they will offer misoprostol-only abortions, a safe alternative method, but one that can carry more side-effects and a slightly higher failure rate \u8211\'20\'13 misoprostol alone was found in a new study to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1363/psrh.12219"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 88% effective}}}\uc2 , while the pill combination has been shown to have a success rate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/clinical-update/english/recommendations-for-abortion-before-13-weeks-gestation/medical-abortion/mifepristone-and-misoprostol-recommended-regimen/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 98%}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Without access to pills, patients would probably need to undergo procedural \u8211\'20\'13 also known as \u8220\'20\'1Csurgical\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These procedures must be performed in-clinic and necessitate more travel, resources, time, staff and space \u8211\'20\'13 increasingly difficult as overburdened clinics face an influx of displaced patients. Even if the impending ruling takes a more narrow approach than pulling the drug off the market completely \u8211\'20\'13 for example, by blocking medication by mail, or by reinstating the in-person dispensing requirement \u8211\'20\'13 it would still significantly hinder access.\par \par \uc2 The suspension of an \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drug by the judiciary set not only a \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubling precedent\u8221\'20\'1D for other reproductive health care but have \u8220\'20\'1Cserious and broad implications\u8221\'20\'1D for all pharmaceutical drugs approved by the federal agency which would see its authority severely weakened, says Donley.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive health advocates and many legal observers worry that a suit that would be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/01/30/medicalabortions-mifepristone-dobbs-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laughed out of court}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in other circumstances could find a champion in Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a former religious liberties lawyer who has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk-ban-abortion-pill-1234658423/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history of attacking}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and birth control. Appointed to the bench by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2019, Kacsmaryk most recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/12/21/texas-title-x-teens-birth-control/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled against}}}\uc2  a federal program that allows Texas teenagers to access birth control without their parents\u8217\'20\'19 permission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear that this is a very intentional and strategic decision by the plaintiffs to forum-shop for a judge that holds similar radical views,\u8221\'20\'1D says Donley.\par \par \uc2 If Kacsmaryk rules for the plaintiffs and the Biden administration chooses to appeal, it will contend with the fifth circuit court of appeals, one of the most conservative appellate courts in the US. From there, the case could reach the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  lawsuit is part of a multi-front war waged by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists against medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While the federal agency has loosened some restrictions on mifepristone, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still banned in 13 states across the US with 18 states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/state-policy/explore/medication-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carrying laws}}}\uc2  that limit the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs. As they reconvene this year, conservative statehouses across the country are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/state-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ramping up proposals}}}\uc2  to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/11/pharmacies-anti-abortion-pills-00077349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning the mailing of pills}}}\uc2  and making it illegal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/3838126-iowa-republicans-file-legislation-making-it-a-felony-to-manufacture-prescribe-abortion-drug/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distribute, manufacture, or prescribe}}}\uc2 , the medication, says Nash. Extreme measures introduced in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/politics/2023/01/20/on-50th-anniversary-of-roe-vs-wade-americas-abortion-landscape-has-dramatically-changed/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma and Arkansas}}}\uc2  would allow those who self-manage their abortions with pills to be prosecuted. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Health/north-carolina-doctor-sues-abortion-pill-access-test/story?id=96634916"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two lawsuits}}}\uc2  out of North Carolina and West Virginia seek to challenge those states\u8217\'20\'19 restrictions on the pills, arguing that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regulations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication should override state law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COpponents of reproductive freedom set their sights on shutting down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and found success after the fall of Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D says Miller. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, they are turning their attention very intensely \u8211\'20\'13 and very aggressively \u8211\'20\'13 to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their next battleground because they know it still provides a remaining pathway to access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230209ej290018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
