\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The \u8216\'20\'18rogue\u8217\'20\'19 Trump-appointed judge with  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill\u8217\'20\'19s future in his hands\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington \par \uc2 1,502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 February 2023\par 14:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk has amassed a litany of contentious rulings in less than four years\par \par \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge in Texas appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has a tendency to attract strong language. Every Democratic senator opposed his confirmation in 2019, with \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the then minority leader, calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrow-minded\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbigoted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Kacsmaryk has demonstrated a hostility to the LGBTQ [community] bordering on paranoia,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/senate-confirms-trump-judicial-nominee-who-called-homosexuality-disordered/2019/06/19/a56526c4-92d2-11e9-b570-6416efdc0803_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schumer said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Only one Republican senator, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  from Maine, broke party ranks and voted against Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s appointment for life. She also had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/senate-confirms-trump-judicial-nominee-who-called-homosexuality-disordered/2019/06/19/a56526c4-92d2-11e9-b570-6416efdc0803_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 harsh words}}}\uc2 , lamenting that his \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme statements\u8221\'20\'1D on reproductive rights pointed to \u8220\'20\'1Can inability to respect precedent and to apply the law fairly and impartially\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Soon Kacsmaryk, 46, will have the opportunity to prove Collins wrong or \u8211\'20\'13 as his many detractors fear \u8211\'20\'13 all too right. One of his most consequential decisions since joining the federal bench in the northern district of Texas could be delivered by the end of this month , in a case that has the potential to disrupt the lives and futures of millions of American women.\par \par \uc2 Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine v \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) \uc2 is the next frontier in the war against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. In it, a set of ideologically driven conservative Christian groups is inviting Kacsmaryk to impose a nationwide injunction that would in effect ban the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill by nullifying the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s medical approval of one of its key elements, mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Should Trump\u8217\'20\'19s judge side with the plaintiffs, as many reproductive rights experts suspect he will, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill ban would apply across the country. Unlike Dobbs, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  last June that eviscerated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and returned legal control over terminations to individual state legislatures, Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s injunction would render medication abortions unlawful in every state in the union.\par \par \uc2 The stakes are high: the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill now accounts for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half}}}\uc2  of all pregnancy terminations in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA decision to ban mifepristone nationwide would be devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Shaina Goodman\uc2 , director for reproductive health and rights at the \uc2 National Partnership for Women & Families\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a very deliberate, coordinated strategy by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement to attack \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  every which way they can, and they\u8217\'20\'19ve found in Kacsmaryk a judge who has a track record of making decisions based not on law or evidence, but on partisan ideology.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Partisan ideology certainly stands out in Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s background. Before being plucked out by Trump for the federal bench, he worked as deputy general counsel at the \uc2 First Liberty Institute\uc2 , a Christian law firm based in Plano, Texas, which opposes the separation of church and state and propagates anti-LGBTQ legal theories.\par \par \uc2 In his early writings he developed a colourful way of describing the \u8220\'20\'1Csexual revolution\u8221\'20\'1D of the 1960s and 70s. Same-sex relationships were \u8220\'20\'1Cdisordered\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrary to natural law\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncregister.com/news/the-abolition-of-man-and-woman-tpnrdgjq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he opined}}}\uc2 , basing his claims on the Catholic catechism.\par \par \uc2 In 2015, he gave a grotesque caricature of the values of the LGBTQ community. He claimed that a person is seen through the LGBTQ lens as \u8220\'20\'1Can autonomous blog of Silly Putty unconstrained by nature or biology, and that marriage, sexuality, gender identity, and even the unborn child must yield to the erotic desires of liberated adults\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since becoming a federal judge, Kacsmaryk has issued some of the most divisive and contentious decisions in federal jurisprudence. He made his mark by putting a spanner in the works of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy \u8211\'20\'13 not once, but twice.\par \par \uc2 In August 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2021/8/17/22627107/trump-judge-remain-in-mexico-matthew-kacsmaryk-immigration-asylum-joe-biden-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he ruled}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  had to permanently reinstate the widely criticised \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D policy which forced thousands of asylum seekers to stay south of the Mexico-US border while their claims were processed. After the supreme court found last June that the US president did in fact have authority to end the policy, overturning Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision, he confounded the Biden administration a second time \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/regulation/court-battles/3777455-federal-judge-prevents-biden-from-ending-trump-era-remain-in-mexico-policy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordering in December}}}\uc2  that Remain in Mexico must be kept in place while lower courts complete their deliberations.\par \par \uc2 Having shaken up the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approach to immigration, he then turned his spotlight on culture war issues. In October, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lmtonline.com/news/houston-texas/article/Texas-transgender-law-17492400.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down as unlawful}}}\uc2  new guidelines from the Biden administration that protected transgender people from discrimination in the workplace.\par \par \uc2 His ruling, which delighted far-right Republicans in Texas and dismayed LGBTQ advocates, was perhaps unsurprising given Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s earlier characterization of transgender people as suffering from a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/senate-confirms-trump-judicial-nominee-who-called-homosexuality-disordered/2019/06/19/a56526c4-92d2-11e9-b570-6416efdc0803_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mental disorder}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two months after wreaking havoc over transgender protections, Kacsmaryk opened a new front in the battle over reproductive rights: birth control. His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/05/texas-contraception-birth-control-parental-consent-title-x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion in Deanda v Becerra}}}\uc2  requires all under-18s in Texas to seek approval from their parent or guardian before obtaining contraception from federally funded clinics.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Kacsmaryk stuck his oar into another area of fervent ideological disagreement: vaccinations. He agreed to hear a case in which an array of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/2023/1/25/23568436/trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk-press-freedom-antitrust-childrens-health-defense-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-vaxxers and conspiracy theorists}}}\uc2  are suing four of the world\u8217\'20\'19s leading media organisations, including the BBC and Associated Press, for refusing to carry misinformation about vaccines that could put people\u8217\'20\'19s lives at risk.\par \par \uc2 Taken together, Kacsmaryk has amassed an extraordinary litany of contentious rulings in less than four years. For Stephen Vladeck, a professor of constitutional law at the \uc2 University of Texas at Austin\uc2 , the judge\u8217\'20\'19s rapid emergence as a central figure in legal battles across so many different fault lines in American public life is anything but coincidental.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no coincidence that Kacsmaryk has on his docket a higher concentration of hot-button social policy cases\par \par \uc2 Steve Vladeck\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s by design,\u8221\'20\'1D Vladeck told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no coincidence that Judge Kacsmaryk has on his docket a higher concentration of hot-button divisive social policy cases than any other judge in the country \u8211\'20\'13 people are seeking him out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vladeck explained that conservative plaintiffs deciding where to lodge high-profile cases have 94 federal district courts to choose from. Yet so often they select Amarillo, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Probe a bit deeper and it becomes clear why this particular court is so popular among extreme, rightwing litigants. Last September, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.txnd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/orders/3-344.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rules of the court were amended}}}\uc2  so as to require all new civil and criminal cases to be heard by Kacsmaryk \u8211\'20\'13 no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 That means that anyone going judge shopping in Amarillo knows exactly what they are going to get: a Trump-appointed federal judge unafraid to sweep legal precedent aside and replace it with ideological conservative positions.\par \par \uc2 As Vladeck pointed out, there is an added bonus for any rightwing plaintiff coming to Amarillo: what happens to Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s cases if they are appealed, as is almost certainly the case given their contentious nature. Texas is covered by the fifth circuit court of appeals, a panel composed of 16 active judges, 12 of whom were appointed by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of what makes Kacsmaryk especially attractive to conservative litigants is not just his actions as a trial judge, but also that his cases will end up in the fifth circuit which is by far the most conservative in the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Vladeck said.\par \par \uc2 Which brings us back to the pending decision over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk-ban-abortion-pill-1234658423/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rolling Stone}}}\uc2  has noted, the Alliance of Hippocratic Medicine has a mailing address in Tennessee, almost 1,000 miles away from Amarillo.\par \par \uc2 Yet the group has lodged its challenge to the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone with Kacsmaryk. Had the case been brought in any other jurisdiction, it might have struggled even to get a hearing.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone received \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval 22 years ago, and in that time has proved itself to be resoundingly safe and effective. In its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23600981-fda-etc-response-to-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response to the call for a ban}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 FDA\uc2  cites a study of more than 30,000 American women undergoing pregnancy terminations before nine weeks of gestation which found that the efficacy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill was 99.6%.\par \par \uc2 Despite such an overwhelming scientific scorecard, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23600982-main-complaint-on-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative plaintiffs claim}}}\uc2  that a ban would \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect the health, safety and welfare of all Americans by rejecting or limiting the use of dangerous drugs\u8221\'20\'1D. The alliance leans heavily on an obscure 1873 provision known as the Comstock Act which on paper bars materials used in abortions from being sent in the mail \u8211\'20\'13 though the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/sites/default/files/opinions/attachments/2023/01/03/2022-12-23_-_comstock_act_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Department of Justice has shown}}}\uc2  that federal courts have dismissed such a prohibition for at least a century.\par \par \uc2 This titanic clash now falls into the hands of a single \u8220\'20\'1Crogue federal judge\u8221\'20\'1D, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/2022/12/17/23512766/supreme-court-matthew-kacsmaryk-judge-trump-abortion-immigration-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vox has dubbed}}}\uc2  Kacsmaryk. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has an inordinate amount of power to make sweeping, and in this case, devastating impacts on people across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodman said.\par \par \uc2 She added that a contentious Kacsmaryk ruling would fall more heavily on certain people. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen of colour, low-income families, young people, are always \u8211\'20\'13 over and over again \u8211\'20\'13 disproportionately harmed by bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a ban on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be no exception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230210ej2a000gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
