\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden criticized for just one mention of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in State of the Union speech\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo in New York \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par 15:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Activists disappointed with lack of focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in first address since reversal of Roe v Wade in June last year\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden is facing criticism for making only a late, brief mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in his first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-the-union-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address}}}\uc2  since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversal of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  by a conservative-led supreme court last year removed the federal right to the procedure in the US.\par \par \uc2 During Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union speech, Biden used the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newrepublic.com/post/170463/biden-says-abortion-once-first-state-union-since-downfall-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exactly once}}}\uc2 , making remarks about statewide abortions bans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAKitchener/status/1623156278112534530?s=20&t=8B46bY9cyeqKAcOPPtcF6A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost an hour into the speech}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must restore the right that was taken away in Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/byKateSmith/status/1623169601709170690/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Biden}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president and I are doing everything to protect access to reproductive healthcare and safeguard patient safety. But already, more than a dozen states are enforcing extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden also reiterated a promise to veto any national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that might be passed by Congress, although that is unlikely with a Democratic-controlled Senate, despite Republicans having the majority in the House after last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access activists were disappointed at the brevity of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are not pleased with the very brief section of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SOTU?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SOTU}}}\uc2  about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which touted what the admin has already done & called on Congress to restore Roe (won't happen in this Congress). No details/pedges of future admin actions.\u8212\'20\'14 Alice Miranda Ollstein (@AliceOllstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AliceOllstein/status/1623156447801376771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Activists were also disappointed because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was written twice in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.grid.news/story/politics/2023/02/08/full-text-president-bidens-2023-state-of-the-union-address-transcript/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a published draft}}}\uc2  of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese four sentences, and having to be begged to say the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  (once! not twice!) does not meet the moment, and is not reflective of how people showed up in droves to the polls to make their voices heard on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RBraceySherman/status/1623162637201600514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Renee Bracey Sherman, executive director of the nonprofit \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Stories.\par \par \uc2 Others noted that Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s guests for the State of the Union included a Texas patient who almost died after not being able to receive treatment for pregnancy complications due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PatrickSvitek/status/1622963174726152193?s=20&t=8B46bY9cyeqKAcOPPtcF6A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 , which Biden did not make a direction mention of.\par \par \uc2 Others applauded Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Naral Pro-Choice and Planned Parenthood, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AliceOllstein/status/1623168991844868097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since the overturning of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections last June, Biden has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/02/biden-democrats-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged to do more }}}\uc2  to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Biden has passed several executive orders since the fall of Roe v Wade, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an August directive}}}\uc2  for the health and human services department to considers ways to protect people traveling out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Biden pledged last October {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/oct/18/midterms-debates-student-loan-application-biden-abortion-politics-latest?page=with:block-634ecca98f0868508426f408#block-634ecca98f0868508426f408"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to codify}}}\uc2  the rights afforded by the landmark supreme court decision in 1973 if Democrats kept control of the Congress in the midterm elections, but little progress has been made on any legislative protections since the party lost control of the House.\par \par \uc2 At least 14 states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have banned abortions}}}\uc2  since Roe was struck down.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230208ej280028m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
