\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address: key takeaways\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington and Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 1,076 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par 06:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Speech covered China, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the border while challenging Republicans on threats to Medicare and social security\par \par \uc2 In his State of the Union address on Tuesday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  presented a bullish picture of the achievements of his administration and Democrats in Congress since he entered the White House in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The US president also took the battle to Republicans on some issues in what was a widely praised performance as the 2024 race for the White House starts to appear on the horizon.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways from the speech.\par \par \uc2 On China, the \u8216\'20\'18strongest position in decades\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke in a Capitol still reverberating with Republican attempts to capitalise on the affair of the Chinese spy balloon, which was shot down off the Carolinas last Saturday after traversing the country. Rightwingers including the extremist \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/07/marjorie-taylor-greene-state-of-the-union-balloon-stunt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who paraded her own balloon}}}\uc2  through the halls before the speech, say Biden was too slow to take action.\par \par \uc2 Biden rejected that, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we\u8217\'20\'19re in the strongest position in decades to compete with China or anyone else in the world. I am committed to work with China where it can advance American interests and benefit the world. But make no mistake: as we made clear last week, if China threatens our sovereignty, we will act to protect our country. And we did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On threats to social security and Medicare\par \par \uc2 Discussing the looming fight, and possible global crisis, over a US default if the debt ceiling is not raised, and with his opponent in that fight, Kevin McCarthy, sitting behind him, Biden took aim at Republicans who want to cut social security and Medicare as part of (supposedly) balancing the federal budget.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of making the wealthy pay their fair share, some Republicans want Medicare and social security to sunset every five years. That means if Congress doesn\u8217\'20\'19t vote to keep them, those programs will go away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among Republican boos and jeers, Greene was seen and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1623151672745680900"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard to shout}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CLiar!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Biden, engaging almost in call and response, had got Republicans on their feet denying his claim. Which was, it seems, what he wanted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got unanimity,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CApparently it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Expect such footage to resurface in the months before the debt ceiling deadline.\par \par \uc2 On Tyre Nichols and police violence\par \par \uc2 With Republicans holding the House, the prospects for meaningful policing reform are grim. Biden issued an appeal anyway, citing the horrific case of Tyre Nichols, the Black man beaten to death by officers in Memphis, Tennessee, and introducing Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s parents, who were given a standing ovation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CImagine if you lost a child at the hands of the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, also asking the silent chamber to imagine having to give \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/aug/24/police-killings-families-ramarley-graham-terence-crutcher-tamir-rice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the talk}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D which Black and brown parents must give children about how to interact with police to protect themselves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know most cops are good, decent people,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey risk their lives every time they put on that shield. But what happened to Tyre in Memphis happens too often. We have to do better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On guns, an appeal for an assault weapons ban\par \par \uc2 Prospects of gun reform are also grim. But Biden repeated his familiar call to ban assault weapons, mentioning the recent Monterey Park shooting in California. He introduced a survivor, Brandon Tsay, who disarmed the gunman who killed 11 people. Tsay received a standing ovation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBan assault weapons once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe did it before. I led the fight to ban them in 1994 [as a senator from Delaware]. In the 10 years the ban was law, mass shootings went down. After Republicans let it expire, mass shootings tripled. Let\u8217\'20\'19s finish the job and ban assault weapons again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the need to codify \u8216\'20\'18Roe\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must restore the right the supreme court took away last year and codify Roe v Wade to protect every woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: if Congress passes a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, I will veto it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congress is highly unlikely to do that, not least because the court sent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights back to the states. Republicans know the issue is toxic for them at the ballot box and anyway, Democrats hold the Senate. But the ballot box was where Biden was really aiming: the assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is an issue Democrats will ride into 2024.\par \par \uc2 On border matters, more clashes\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, Republicans in the House chamber chanted \u8220\'20\'1Csecure the border\u8221\'20\'1D when Biden spoke about immigration \u8211\'20\'13 including a push for more resources for border protection officers.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1623157275656331265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen to shush the hecklers}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 if not particularly demonstratively. Later, when Biden spoke about the need to secure America\u8217\'20\'19s borders against an influx of the opioid fentanyl, and introduced the parents of a woman killed by the drug, at least one Republican shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s your fault!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Nearly a year after Russia invaded its neighbour, Biden saluted Ukraine and the US effort to support and arm Kyiv, a target of Republican criticism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTogether,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe did what America always does at our best. We led. We united Nato and built a global coalition. We stood against [Vladimir] Putin\u8217\'20\'19s aggression. We stood with the Ukrainian people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Addressing the Ukrainian ambassador, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand with you as long as it takes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On rightwing threats to democracy\par \par \uc2 Biden made reference to the grave threats of the last few years, if not mentioning their chief source, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , by name. He made a point by acknowledging \uc2 Paul Pelosi\uc2 , the husband of the former speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , who was attacked by an extremist in his San Francisco home last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the last few years our democracy has been threatened, attacked and put at risk. \u8230\'20\'26 Here tonight in this chamber is the man who bears the scars of that brutal attack but is as tough and strong and as resilient as they get. My friend, \uc2 Paul Pelosi\uc2 . But such a heinous act never should have happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no place for political violence in America. We have to protect the right to vote, not suppress that fundamental right, respect results of our elections not subvert the will of people. We have to restore trust in our institutions of democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230208ej28000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
