\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Google\uc2  targets low-income US women with ads for anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pregnancy centers, study shows\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 February 2023\par 16:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: research finds ads directing women in two cities to crisis pregnancy centers when they search for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\par \par \uc2 Low-income women in some cities are more likely than their wealthier counterparts to be targeted by \uc2 Google\uc2  ads promoting anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis pregnancy centers when they search for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, researchers at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.techtransparencyproject.org/articles/google-helps-fake-abortion-clinics-target-low-income-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tech Transparency Project have found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The research builds on previous findings detailing how \uc2 Google\uc2  directs users searching for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to so-called crisis centers \u8211\'20\'13 organizations that have been known to pose as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in an attempt to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/15/us-anti-abortion-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steer}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/15/us-anti-abortion-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women away from accessing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The researchers set up test accounts in three cities \u8211\'20\'13 Atlanta, Miami and Phoenix \u8211\'20\'13 for women of three different income groups suggested by \uc2 Google\uc2 : average or lower-income rate, moderately high-income rate and high-income rate. They then entered search terms like \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic near me\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CI want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. In Phoenix, 56% of the search ads shown to the test accounts representing low- to moderate-income women were for crisis centers, compared with 41% of those served to moderately high-income test accounts and 7% to high-income accounts. In Atlanta, 42% of ads shown to the lower-income group were for crisis pregnancy centers, compared with 18% for moderately high-income women and 29% for high-income women.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona and Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned after 15 weeks of pregnancy. In Georgia, it is banned after six weeks, at which point many people do not know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy pointing low-income women to [crisis pregnancy centers] more frequently than higher-income women in states with restrictive laws, \uc2 Google\uc2  may delay these women from finding an actual \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to get a legal and safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D says Katie Paul, the director of the Tech Transparency Project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe time window is critical in some of these states,\u8221\'20\'1D she adds.\par \par \uc2 Lower-income women are the group least likely to be able to travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care because traveling can cost thousands of dollars in lost work, transportation, babysitting and accommodation fees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLower-income women are being targeted, and they\u8217\'20\'19re the ones that are going to suffer the most under these policies,\u8221\'20\'1D Paul says.\par \par \uc2 The results were not the same in all cities. In Miami, researchers saw the inverse result: high-income women were more likely to get ads from crisis centers than lower-income women. The researchers say they cannot be certain why Miami diverged from the other cities but speculate that crisis pregnancy centers might more actively target low-income women in more restrictive states. (While Arizona and Florida both ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks, the former has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/arizona/abortion-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more restrictions}}}\uc2  layered on the 15-week limit.)\par \par \uc2 While pregnancy crisis centers offer pregnant women resources such as diapers and pregnancy testing, they have also been known to employ a number of shady tactics to convince women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep their pregnancies. Those include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/16/georgia-abortion-crisis-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posing as \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics}}}\uc2  online though they do not offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, refusing pregnancy tests for women who say they intend to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/15/us-anti-abortion-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touting widely disputed research about \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care to patients}}}\uc2 . Crisis centers, which go largely unregulated despite offering medical services, have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9189146/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known to target low-income women}}}\uc2  precisely because they find it harder to travel out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Although companies buying ads with \uc2 Google\uc2  can selectively target the groups they want to reach \u8211\'20\'13 including by income \u8211\'20\'13 Paul adds that many users won\u8217\'20\'19t be aware they are being targeted by \uc2 Google\uc2  in this way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Google\uc2  has a large share of influence, particularly in the United States when people are trying to search for authoritative information. And people generally tend to consider \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search engine as an equaliser. They think the results they get are the results that everyone\u8217\'20\'19s going to get. But that\u8217\'20\'19s just not the case,\u8221\'20\'1D Paul says.\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Google\uc2  came under fire after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.techtransparencyproject.org/articles/google-serves-anti-abortion-clinic-ads-violate-its-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Tech Transparency Project investigation}}}\uc2  found the company was serving people with ads for pregnancy crisis centers suggesting they offer abortions even though they do not \u8211\'20\'13 violating the platform\u8217\'20\'19s own rules on misleading advertisements.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has repeatedly been pressed to make changes to its search engine to curtail these issues. In 2022, Senator Mark Warner of Virginia and Representative Elissa Slotkin of Michigan wrote to the company twice, urging it to stop misdirecting users searching for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warner.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/2022/11/following-new-investigation-warner-slotkin-press-google-on-misrepresentation-in-ads-targeted-to-users-searching-for-abortion-services"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to these crisis centers in Google Maps}}}\uc2 . The lawmakers also called on \uc2 Google\uc2  to limit the way crisis centers appear in search results and ads, and to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warner.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/2022/6/warner-slotkin-colleagues-urge-action-on-misleading-search-results-about-abortion-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 add disclaimers clearly indicating whether a search result is an organization}}}\uc2  that provides abortions or not.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  responded by pledging to clearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.ph/yhMyX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 label}}}\uc2  these facilities in the future. But researchers in the study also found a number of ads still being served to users suggesting centers offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care when they do not.\par \par \uc2 In Phoenix, a \uc2 Google\uc2  search by a lower- or average-income test account for \u8220\'20\'1C \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 an organization that provides financial and other forms of support for abortions \u8211\'20\'13 yielded an ad with the text \u8220\'20\'1CFree \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Help \u8211\'20\'13 100% Confidential\u8221\'20\'1D, for a crisis center.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, when the lower- or average-income Atlanta test account searched for \u8220\'20\'1CPlanned Parenthood Atlanta\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Google\uc2  produced a single ad that read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Consultation for Free\u8221\'20\'1D, with an ad linking to a crisis pregnancy center called Health for Her in Atlanta. Although some of the ad results in the Tech Transparency Project\u8217\'20\'19s study included a label stating \u8220\'20\'1CDoes not provide abortions\u8221\'20\'1D, this one, along with several others, did not \u8211\'20\'13 in contravention of \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own labeling rules.\par \par \uc2 Slotkin said she was disappointed to learn the company is still failing to regulate crisis centers on its platform, despite having been in touch with them twice about the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMichigan has roughly 100 pregnancy crisis centers that explicitly do not provide abortions, and these clinics should not be listed among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers,\u8221\'20\'1D Slotkin said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe sent a second letter in November because \uc2 Google\uc2  was still failing to consistently apply disclaimers to misleading ads. Despite our action \u8211\'20\'13 and assurance from \uc2 Google\uc2  that they would only show verified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers when a woman was seeking the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 these findings from TTP [Tech Transparency Project] prove there\u8217\'20\'19s clearly more work that needs to be done,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Warner\u8217\'20\'19s office added: \u8220\'20\'1CAds from \u8216\'20\'18crisis pregnancy centers\u8217\'20\'19 that reference \u8216\'20\'18Free \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Help\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Consultation\u8217\'20\'19 are obviously not in compliance with \uc2 Google\uc2  ads policies that forbid ads \u8216\'20\'18that deceive users by excluding relevant product information or providing misleading information\u8217\'20\'19. I urge \uc2 Google\uc2  to take action to prevent these deceptive advertising practices meant to trick users, especially low-income women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian contacted \uc2 Google\uc2  for comment and on Monday evening an unnamed spokesman sent a response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t allow advertisers to specifically target a \u8216\'20\'18low income\u8217\'20\'19 bracket with ads, and we have strict rules about how location can be used to serve locally relevant ads. It\u8217\'20\'19s important that people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related resources know what services an advertiser actually provides, so we require any organization that wants to target queries related to getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be certified and clearly disclose whether they do or do not offer abortions. Last year, we updated these disclosures to make them more visible for users,\u8221\'20\'1D the response said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230207ej27000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
