\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Surge in complications from unsafe abortions likely post-Roe, doctors warn\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 768 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 February 2023\par 17:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 People in underserved medical communities in states that ban abortions may be more likely to attempt self-managed abortions\par \par \uc2 Top doctors in the US warn that surgeons should be prepared to treat more patients with complications from self-managed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  and forced pregnancy after the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tsaco.bmj.com/content/8/1/e001067"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent opinion piece}}}\uc2  published in journal Trauma Surgery & Acute Care Open, 17 experts from medical centers and universities including the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2 , Duke Medicine and the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  urged surgeons to be prepared to treat medical consequences related to a person\u8217\'20\'19s inability to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the aftermath of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health decision, acute care surgeons face an increased likelihood of seeing patients with complications from both self-managed abortions and forced pregnancy in underserved areas of reproductive and maternity care throughout the USA,\u8221\'20\'1D read the op-ed.\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs v Jackson case eliminated the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights established by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/womens-march-2023-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 1972. While many states still provide access to abortions, many others now generally prohibit the termination of pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Physicians noted that self-managed abortions with pills such as mifepristone are extremely safe and used across the country to help provide access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 But physicians warned that people in underserved medical communities in states that ban abortions may be more likely to attempt a self-managed \u8220\'20\'1Cby ingestion of toxic substances or by self-inflicted physical injury\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDepending on their location and state laws regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, trauma and acute care surgeons may find themselves providing care for people [affected] by the Dobbs ruling who undergo [self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] and suffer injury as a result,\u8221\'20\'1D the op-ed noted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we should strive to prevent such injury by advocating for the protection of access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, surgeons should also prepare to treat resulting complications.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doctors noted that surgeons must act to protect patient privacy and legal safety, especially as conservative states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2023/01/abortion-bans-pregnant-people-prosecution/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have weighed prosecuting}}}\uc2  pregnant people who seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a state that prohibits it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe patient\u8217\'20\'19s legal safety should also be of utmost concern and underscores the significance of knowing your state laws around this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D the op-ed noted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProviders have the ethical duty to protect patient privacy and to not report these complications which implicate self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to law enforcement in states where this is prohibited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Providers also warned that surgeons may have to deal with the medical complications associated with forced pregnancy, especially given higher rates of maternal morbidity and mortality in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAgain, in those states that restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, maternal morbidity, and inevitably mortality, will increase and require physicians from all fields to expand their ability to care for these needs,\u8221\'20\'1D read the op-ed.\par \par \uc2 Physicians warned that the consequences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans will most affect marginalized communities, including people of color and those from lower socioeconomic backgrounds, who are overrepresented in patients seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and are more likely to live in areas where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is restricted.\par \par \uc2 The op-ed urged medical professionals to become educated on how to treat pregnant patients who may face health consequences as a result of not being able to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 22 states }}}\uc2  have taken some action to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, with 12 states banning the procedure from conception.\par \par \uc2 Medical providers in states that have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have stated that they are often delayed in providing life-saving treatment due to bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A recent study from Texas showed that even with high-risk pregnant patients, doctors were forced to wait until some were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cat death\u8217\'20\'19s door\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  before providing pregnancy termination services.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajog.org/action/showPdf?pii=S0002-9378%2822%2900536-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate study }}}\uc2  from Texas found that delays in miscarriage care due to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws resulted in severe health consequences, including admission into an intensive care unit and a hysterectomy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, states have begun enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections amid the continuing battle over reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota on Saturday became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/minnesota-senate-narrowly-backs-right-to-abortion-in-state-law/600247344/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first state to pass}}}\uc2  a bill that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights following the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a crucial first step in establishing rock-solid protections for everyone in Minnesota to make their own decisions about their reproductive destiny,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abena Abraham, campaign director for the advocacy group UnRestrict Minnesota, in a statement, according to the Star Tribune.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 1 February 2023 to clarify that the opinion article was published in the journal Trauma Surgery & Acute Care Open, a BMJ publication.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230131ej1u00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
