\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says in video \u8216\'20\'18anyone in my position not taking the fifth would be an absolute fool\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,914 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 January 2023\par 21:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president repeatedly asserts right against self-incriminationSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfair\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone in my position not taking the fifth would be a fool\u8221\'20\'1D. It was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his finest, or perhaps most exhausting, in video of his summer deposition before the New York attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d947958f086cb243b54001#block-63d947958f086cb243b54001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by CBS News}}}\uc2 . Besides bashing Letitia James and her inquiry \u8211\'20\'13 which alleges he and his children conspired to inflate his net worth in order to get better loan terms \u8211\'20\'13 Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t say much, instead refusing to answer questions more than 400 times. Meanwhile, in Washington, lawmakers have plenty of questions of their own in the ongoing saga of the classified documents discovered in the possession of former White House occupants, with a top Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d94d968f089ec6bac82553#block-63d94d968f089ec6bac82553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding information}}}\uc2  on Trump and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visitors from the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos announced he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d92be28f089ec6bac823ae#block-63d92be28f089ec6bac823ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not serve}}}\uc2  on any House committees, even though Republican speaker Kevin McCarthy said he would be willing to seat him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d91dbd8f089ec6bac8230a#block-63d91dbd8f089ec6bac8230a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will let}}}\uc2  the emergencies declared over Covid-19 expire, but is considering declaring a new crisis to allow Americans to obtain access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d9776f8f0808096a1f070f#block-63d9776f8f0808096a1f070f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will attend}}}\uc2 Tyre Nichols \u8217\'20\'19s funeral in Memphis on Wednesday, her office announced.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor Tim Walz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d971728f08672e3a1ba99e#block-63d971728f08672e3a1ba99e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law}}}\uc2  a measure protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, making the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature the first to enshrine access to the procedure since the end of Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d97ca58f08d9178662b823#block-63d97ca58f08d9178662b823"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid a visit to the US Capitol}}}\uc2  in search of support for Ukraine and perhaps also political relevance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , as he made the rounds of the US Capitol on Tuesday. Photograph: Kevin Dietsch/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , the former British prime minister, has brought his quest for political relevance to Washington, holding talks with Republican members of Congress in an effort to shore up support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Johnson left office last September amid a Trumpian cascade of scandals but, far from fading into retirement, may be hoping that the war with Russia offers a shot at redemption and chance to emulate his hero Winston Churchill as a global statesman.\par \par \uc2 The 58-year-old visited Ukraine earlier this month and, on Tuesday, was seen entering the office of House speaker Kevin McCarthy, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-donald-trump-humanitarian-assistance-congress-c47a255738cd13576aa4d238ec076f4a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruffled feathers last year}}}\uc2  by warning that Republicans will not write a \u8220\'20\'1Cblank check\u8221\'20\'1D for Ukraine if they win back the majority.\par \par \uc2 Reporters also spotted Johnson heading to the office of \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Senate minority leader and staunch supporter of Ukraine who has urged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to act faster, as well as Congressman Jim Banks, a veteran of the Afghanistan war.\par \par \uc2 Cristina Maza, a journalist at the \uc2 National Journal\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CrisLeeMaza/status/1620505125885460480?s=20&t=1g_1lFRB3XA_0eb97KQGzw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that Johnson told her that he is on Capitol Hill to thank Americans for backing Ukraine and called Republican support for Kyiv \u8220\'20\'1Cvery robust\u8221\'20\'1D. The ex-PM also met \uc2 Oksana Markarova\uc2 , the Ukrainian ambassador to the US, and took questions from Ukrainian journalists.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has penned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/01/30/boris-johnson-putin-nato-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an opinion column}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , arguing that years of \u8220\'20\'1Cdiplomatic doublespeak\u8221\'20\'1D about Ukraine joining \uc2 Nato\uc2  ended in disaster. \u8220\'20\'1CUkrainians should be given everything they need to finish this war, as quickly as possible, and we should begin the process of admitting Ukraine to \uc2 NATO\uc2 , and begin it now,\u8221\'20\'1D he writes.\par \par \uc2 The former PM is set to speak at a private Republican club on Tuesday evening and take part in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/event/conversation-with-boris-johnson-sustaining-support-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtual conversation}}}\uc2  about sustaining support to Ukraine with \uc2 the Atlantic Council\uc2  think tank at 11.30am on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a statement from \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2 , attorney for the parents of Tyre Nichols, regarding Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attendance at his funeral tomorrow:\par \par \uc2 This morning, Ms. RowVaughn Wells, Mr. Rodney Wells, and I spoke on the phone with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for over thirty minutes about the tragic loss of Tyre. Vice President Harris and Ms. Wells spoke exclusively, and during this emotional time, the Vice President was able to console Ms. Wells and even help her smile. Tyre\u8217\'20\'19s parents invited Vice President Harris to the funeral tomorrow, and were pleased that she accepted their invitation. Mr. and Mrs. Wells are grateful for Vice President Harris reaching out to them during this heartbreaking time and for her sensitivity on the call.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will travel to Memphis tomorrow to attend Tyre Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s funeral, her office has announced.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke with Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s mother and stepfather after the 29-year-old was beaten by Memphis police following a traffic stop, and died three days later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Minnesota becomes first state to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since Roe overturned\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has signed into law the Protect Reproductive Options (PRO) Act, which creates a \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental right\u8221\'20\'1D to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state\u8217\'20\'19s laws:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, I signed the PRO Act into law.\par \par \uc2 Your reproductive freedom will stay protected in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@GovTimWalz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovTimWalz/status/1620492952496898049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is already protected under a state supreme court ruling, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/gov-tim-walz-to-sign-law-to-strengthen-abortion-rights-in-minnesota/600247932/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minneapolis Star Tribune reports}}}\uc2  Democrats controlling the state legislature passed the PRO Act to guard against the possibility that the precedent gets overturned.\par \par \uc2 With the law, Minnesota has become the first state to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections to its statutes since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last June and allowed states to ban the procedure entirely. Voters elsewhere in the country have approved ballot measures protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in reaction to the ruling from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the wake of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/31/tyre-nichols-death-white-officer-preston-hemphill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tyre Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s death}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with Black lawmakers on Thursday in a bid to revive stalled talks on a federal police reform bill, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr> {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  will meet with members of the Congressional Black Caucus on Thursday to discuss police reform in light of Tyre Nichols' death, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ODalton46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ODalton46}}}\uc2  tells reporters on AF1 en route to NYC\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Seung Min Kim (@seungminkim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/seungminkim/status/1620454985292042243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Spurred by the death of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  in 2020 and the nationwide protests that followed, negotiations over passing some kind of reform measure dragged on for months in 2021, but ultimately proved fruitless. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/01/31/chances-deal-police-reform-quickly-dim/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  that despite the outrage over Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s death following a beating by Memphis police officers \u8211\'20\'13 five of whom have been charged with murder \u8211\'20\'13 the chances of passing such a measure have only worsened.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what the space is for that,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , who is the top Republican on the judiciary committee that would probably consider any such bill.\par \par \uc2 Previous talks were held while Democrats controlled both the House and Senate, and negotiators were trying to find a compromise that could overcome a Republican filibuster in the upper chamber. Now, the GOP controls the House, and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , a Republican who played a part in passing a bill to help police departments implement de-escalation training, doubts such a measure is feasible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s probably less likely to happen now with divided government,\u8221\'20\'1D Cornyn said, according to the Post.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos has elaborated on his decision to recuse himself from the House committees on small business and science, space and technology.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a statement from the New York Republican lawmaker and fabulist:\par \par \uc2 With the ongoing attention surrounding both my personal and campaign financial investigations, I have submitted a request to Speaker McCarthy that I be temporarily recused from my committee assignments until I am cleared. This was a decision that I take very seriously. The business of the 118th Congress must continue without media fanfare. It is important that I primarily focus on serving the constituents of New York\u8217\'20\'19s Third Congressional District and providing federal level representation without distraction.\par \par \uc2 I want to personally thank Speaker McCarthy for meeting with me to discuss the matter and allowing me to take time to properly clear my name before returning to my committees. To my constituents, I remain committed to serving the district, and delivering results for both New York\u8217\'20\'19s Third Congressional District and for the American people.\par \par \uc2 Most of Santos\u8217\'20\'19s constituents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d930038f08d1ba8a8b40e0#block-63d930038f08d1ba8a8b40e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would like him to resign}}}\uc2 , a recent survey said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Far-right commentators who joked or cast doubt about the hammer attack on \uc2 Paul Pelosi\uc2 , husband of former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , are having to eat their words, now that video of assault has been released, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Conservative commentators were forced to backtrack over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/john-oliver-exposes-right-wing-lies-about-paul-pelosi-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  and jokes about the hammer attack on \uc2 Paul Pelosi\uc2 , after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/27/paul-pelosi-attack-video-police-camera"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 release}}}\uc2  of police video and audio last week.\par \par \uc2 One Fox News commentator had to retreat from his claim there was no \u8220\'20\'1Cevidence of a breaking and entering\u8221\'20\'1D when his host pointed out that footage of the attacker breaking into Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s home was playing on screen at the time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGot it,\u8221\'20\'1D Brian Claypool said. \u8220\'20\'1CYeah. OK. Can\u8217\'20\'19t we talk more about what is the DoJ doing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/man-charged-assault-and-attempted-kidnapping-following-breaking-and-entering-pelosi-residence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s attacker, David DePape, with assault and attempted kidnapping. The 42-year-old also faces state charges including attempted murder. He has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7news.com/paul-pelosi-attack-david-depape-not-guilty-plea-state-charges-attempted-murder/12623314/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, 82, was attacked in his San Francisco home in late October, a time when his wife, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , was still speaker of the US House. According to tapes released by the police, the attacker said he was looking for her. She was not present. Her husband suffered a fractured skull and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/03/politics/paul-pelosi-out-of-hospital/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 injuries}}}\uc2  to his hand and arm.\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  condemned the attack.\par \par \uc2 But prominent rightwingers including \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , the Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2  owner \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and Republican members of Congress including Ted Cruz and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  eagerly spread jokes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/11/05/us/politics/pelosi-attack-misinfo-republican-politicians.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misinformation}}}\uc2  and conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/31/paul-pelosi-hammer-attack-police-video-rightwing-pundits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paul Pelosi attack: rightwing pundits backtrack after release of police video}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfair\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone in my position not taking the fifth would be a fool\u8221\'20\'1D. It was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his finest, or perhaps most exhausting, in video of his summer deposition before the New York attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d947958f086cb243b54001#block-63d947958f086cb243b54001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by CBS News}}}\uc2 . Besides bashing Letitia James and her inquiry \u8211\'20\'13 which alleges he and his children conspired to inflate his net worth in order to get better loan terms \u8211\'20\'13 Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t say much, instead refusing to answer questions more than 400 times. In Washington, lawmakers have plenty of questions of their own in the ongoing saga of the classified documents found in the possession of former White House occupants, with a top Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d94d968f089ec6bac82553#block-63d94d968f089ec6bac82553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding information}}}\uc2  on Trump and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visitors from the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 George Santos announced he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d92be28f089ec6bac823ae#block-63d92be28f089ec6bac823ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not serve}}}\uc2  on any House committees, even though Republican speaker Kevin McCarthy said he would be willing to seat him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d91dbd8f089ec6bac8230a#block-63d91dbd8f089ec6bac8230a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will allow}}}\uc2  the emergencies declared over Covid-19 to expire, but is considering declaring a new crisis to allow Americans to obtain access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The fallout from the police killing of Tyre Nichols{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/31/biden-end-covid-emergency-reproductive-health-crisis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-63d929ea8f08d1ba8a8b4086#block-63d929ea8f08d1ba8a8b4086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues}}}\uc2  in Memphis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump: 'Anyone in my position not taking the fifth would be a fool'\par \par \uc2 What does Trump think of those who would answer questions in a deposition, like the one he sat for with New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone in my position not taking the Fifth Amendment would be a fool, an absolute fool,\u8221\'20\'1D he said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-video-deposition-takes-the-fifth-new-york-fraud-probe/?ftag=CNM-00-10aab7e&linkId=199342790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the interview}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on his Truth social network, which stands in for his inactive-but-no-longer-banned \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, the former president was doing his usual thing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrat D.A.\u8217\'20\'19s, Attorney Generals, and Prosecutors are very DANGEROUS to the well being of our Country. Many are deranged and only interested in pleasing the Fake News Media and the Democrat Party. Fair and True Justice means NOTHING in our Country anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  released shortly after CBS News aired video of his deposition today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am being hit by so many DEMOCRAT Prosecutors, LOCAL, STATE, & FEDERAL, all to keep me from \u8220\'20\'1Crunning,\u8221\'20\'1D and all because I am leading by sooo much. The great people of our Country aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to take it. MAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the House oversight committee has sent the director of the Secret Service a letter asking for information on all visitors to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Indiana home since they left office two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin, the ranking member on the Republican-led committee that is playing a major role in investigating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , cited the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s discovery of classified materials at Pence and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s properties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Committee on Oversight and Accountability is investigating former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mishandling of sensitive, highly classified documents,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/sites/democrats.oversight.house.gov/files/2023-01-31%20JBR%20to%20Cheatle-USSS%20re%20Mar-a-Lago%20Visitor%20Logs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in the letter}}}\uc2  to director Kimberly Cheatle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven that the \uc2 U.S. Secret Service\uc2  provided protection for Mr. Trump and Mr. Pence during the time they stored classified materials at their respective residences, the Committee is seeking information from your agency regarding who had access to former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago Club and former Vice President Pence\u8217\'20\'19s personal residence since leaving office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Led by James Comer, Republicans on the oversight committee are investigating Biden over a number of matters, including his improper possession of classified documents. Comer has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/15/biden-documents-discoveries-republicans-pressure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested from the Secret Service}}}\uc2  information regarding visitors to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Delaware residence, where some of his classified documents were found. In a statement, Raskin said he asked Comer to join in his letter about Trump and Pence\u8217\'20\'19s properties, but received no reply.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump refused to answer 400 times in fraud deposition before New York attorney general\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  invoked his fifth amendment right to refuse to answer questions more than 400 times last summer during his deposition in the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s fraud investigation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-video-deposition-takes-the-fifth-new-york-fraud-probe/?ftag=CNM-00-10aab7e&linkId=199342790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The network obtained video of the interview, which starts with the former president accusing attorney general Letitia James of conducting an \u8220\'20\'1Cunfair\u8221\'20\'1D investigation that amounted to a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch hunt\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 familiar words for anyone who has heard Trump talk about the many inquiries he has faced, and is facing.\par \par \uc2 He then states that on the advice of his lawyers, \u8220\'20\'1CI respectfully decline to answer the questions under the rights and privileges afforded to every citizen under the United States constitution. This will be my answer to any further questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An investigator for the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office tells Trump that he can just say \u8220\'20\'1Csame answer\u8221\'20\'1D for all the questions put to him, which Trump does throughout the deposition.\par \par \uc2 Weeks after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s August deposition, James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/trump-new-york-investigation-ivanka-donald-eric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced she was suing}}}\uc2  the former president and three of his children for what she called a fraud scheme of \u8220\'20\'1Cstaggering\u8221\'20\'1D scale in which they falsely inflated his net worth to win more favorable loan terms.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full report and footage of the deposition, from \uc2 CBS\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  searched Biden's former Washington office in November\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents conducted a voluntary search of an office formerly used by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Washington DC after classified materials were discovered there, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/biden-documents-fbi-search-penn-biden-center/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The search of the Penn Biden Center was carried out with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agreement in November of last year, after the secret documents dating from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s time as vice president under Barack Obama were first discovered. The search was not publicly announced, and CBS News cited two sources familiar with the investigation in reporting it.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  earlier this month searched Biden\u8217\'20\'19s home in Delaware, another location where classified materials had been found. That search was also voluntary, and made public by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer the day after it happened.\par \par \uc2 According to CBS News, \u8220\'20\'1CSome documents found at the Penn Biden Center were labeled top secret.\u8221\'20\'1D In total, between 25 and 30 documents marked as classified and dating to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s time as vice president and senator have been found in his possession.\par \par \uc2 The president is not alone in his possession of government secrets without the proper permissions. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was found to have a similar but much larger cache of secret materials at his Mar-a-Lago resort, which he resisted turning over to investigators. His former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  also acknowledged discovering some secret documents at his Indiana home, and turned them over to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . The justice department has appointed special counsels to investigate both Biden and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s possession of the materials.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 But what of George Santos\u8217\'20\'19s staffers?\par \par \uc2 The aides who coordinate lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 office affairs, communications with the press and public and assistance to constituents play a crucial role in Congress. But in Santos\u8217\'20\'19s case, these employees have to reckon with the fact that they will have their name associated with an admitted fabulist.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2023/01/28/santos-staff-hiring-resign-capitol-hill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post took a look}}}\uc2  at who Santos had recruited to work for him, and found that most lacked the deep Capitol Hill experience new lawmakers often come to rely on as they navigate the complex and confusing world of Congress:\par \par \uc2 Santos hired Charles Lovett as his chief of staff. Lovett served as Santos\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager and worked for six months as a field organizer for the Ohio Republican Party, according to LegiStorm. He also served as political director for Ohio Republican Josh Mandel\u8217\'20\'19s unsuccessful primary bid for Senate. He has not worked on the Hill previously. Viswanag Burra, Santos\u8217\'20\'19s operations director, spent less than a year as special operations director for Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R-Fla.) and recently worked as executive secretary for the New York Young Republican Club.\par \par \uc2 His communications director, Naysa Woomer, appears to have the most Hill experience. She worked for three Republican members between 2014 and 2018 before moving to Massachusetts to be the communications director for the state Republican Party and then as a communications specialist for the state Department of Revenue.\par \par \uc2 Rafaello Carone, Santos\u8217\'20\'19s senior legislative assistant, worked for three GOP members, but his stints were short in each office. He spent six months as social media manager for Rep. \uc2 Madison Cawthorn\uc2  (R-N.C.), two months as deputy communications director for Rep. \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2  (R-Fla.) and a month as press secretary for Rep. Paul A. Gosar (R-Ariz.), according to LegiStorm. He also ran a consulting firm that mostly worked for long-shot Republican congressional candidates. Gabrielle Lipsky, who served as Santos\u8217\'20\'19s campaign press secretary, will be his press secretary and office manager. She does not have Hill experience.\par \par \uc2 One Santos aide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/01/30/2023/the-staffers-who-call-george-santos-boss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who spoke anonymously to Semafor}}}\uc2  said they were motivated by a desire to help the people of his district. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just about the constituents of the third congressional district and making sure that they\u8217\'20\'19re actually being represented in Washington D.C. \u8212\'20\'14 whether it\u8217\'20\'19s for federal funding for infrastructure projects down to anything as simple as a flag request,\u8221\'20\'1D the aide said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  got the official word from George Santos\u8217\'20\'19s office about why he won\u8217\'20\'19t serve on committees.\par \par \uc2 The New York Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cis reserving his seats on his assigned committees until he has been properly cleared of both campaign and personal financial investigations,\u8221\'20\'1D his office said in an email.\par \par \uc2 Santos\u8217\'20\'19 trouble isn\u8217\'20\'19t just ethical, but potentially legal. Watchdog groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/10/george-santos-campaign-finance-complaint-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have filed}}}\uc2  complaints about him with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/01/27/santos-doj-investigation-fec/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  the justice department has asked the regulator to hold off on those \u8211\'20\'13 a sign that they may be pursuing their own criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If George Santos were to resign, the person with the most to lose might be Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy, who has a mere four-vote margin of control in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say about \uc2 Santos\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to step down from committee work, according to Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked Speaker McCarthy about Santos\u8217\'20\'19 decision.\par \par \uc2 He told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CI met with George Santos yesterday and I think it was an appropriate decision that until he could clear everything up. He's off committees right now\u8230\'20\'26.We had a discussion and he asked me if he could do that.\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1620443135326445570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Marc Molinaro, one of the New York Republicans who has called on Santos to resign, had stronger words:\par \par \uc2 enltrFreshman Rep. Marc Molinaro (R-NY) tells me re. Santos committee decision: \u8220\'20\'1CThe decision to not serve on committees is in his and our best interest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Adds: \u8220\'20\'1CAs I said, I think he should resign and focus on his defense. But, do welcome this decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1620442272897839110?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But what did Santos have to say? Not much:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen I asked Santos if he\u8217\'20\'19s stepping off his committees he replied first: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry?\u8221\'20\'1D And then when I repeated myself he said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was just after he left the closed House GOP conference meeting room\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1620434315166511104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos may not serve on any committees, but he has insisted he won\u8217\'20\'19t resign from the House. That\u8217\'20\'19s not a popular stance back home.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scri.siena.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Newsday-CD-3-Jan-2023-Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Newsday/Siena College survey}}}\uc2  of voters in his New York district finds that 78% believe he should resign, and 83% view him unfavorably. Those calling for his resignation include 71% of Republicans surveyed and 72% of independents. Perhaps most worryingly for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of keeping his seat should he step down, people who voted for Santos say, by a two-to-one margin, that they would not have supported Santos if they knew he was a liar.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow Santos to sit on committees, 71% say that was a mistake.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos says he will not serve on House committees\par \par \uc2 George Santos, the recently elected House Republican who admitted to lying repeatedly as he campaigned for office, said he will not serve on committees, Punchbowl News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr??BREAKING \u8212\'20\'14 GEORGE SANTOS tells House Republicans he will recuse himself from sitting on committees.\par \par \uc2 Just happened in closed GOP meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1620432993138651138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Santos has faced calls to resign over his many falsehoods, but has said he will not do so. House speaker Kevin McCarthy has declined to call for Santos\u8217\'20\'19 ouster, instead saying the New York lawmakers would be allowed to serve on committees while also referring him for ethics proceedings. Santos was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/17/george-santos-house-committees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  to serve on committees dealing with small businesses and science and technology.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some would go so far as to say police violence is a public health emergency, and on that topic, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  report a seventh Memphis police officer has been taken off the streets over the death of Tyre Nichols:\par \par \uc2 Two more Memphis police officers have been disciplined and three emergency responders fired in connection with the death of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tyre-nichols"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tyre Nichols}}}\uc2 , officials said on Monday. That brings the total number of officers who have been disciplined to seven, including the five Black officers who were fired and charged last week with second-degree murder and other offenses in Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s beating and 10 January death.\par \par \uc2 Officer Preston Hemphill, who is white, was relieved of duty and put on what is known as administrative leave, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/memphis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Memphis}}}\uc2  police major Karen Rudolph said on Monday, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 Later in the day it said another officer had also been relieved, but without naming the person or specifying what role they played in the incident.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/30/congress-police-reform-biden-black-caucus-tyre-nichols-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tyre Nichols\u8217\'20\'19s death: seven officers have been removed from duty, police confirm}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As America comes to grips with the consequences of ending Roe v Wade, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/gloria-oladipo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gloria Oladipo}}}\uc2  reports that experts are warning less access to reproductive healthcare will be felt in doctors offices and emergency rooms nationwide:\par \par \uc2 Top doctors in the US warn that surgeons should be prepared to treat more patients with complications from self-managed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  and forced pregnancy after the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In a recent opinion piece published in the \uc2 BMJ\uc2 , 17 experts from medical centers and universities including the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2 , Duke Medicine and the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  urged surgeons to be prepared to treat medical consequences related to a person\u8217\'20\'19s inability to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the aftermath of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health decision, acute care surgeons face an increased likelihood of seeing patients with complications from both self-managed abortions and forced pregnancy in underserved areas of reproductive and maternity care throughout the USA,\u8221\'20\'1D read the op-ed.\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs v Jackson case eliminated the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights established by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/womens-march-2023-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 1972. While many states still provide access to abortions, many others now generally prohibit the termination of pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Physicians noted that self-managed abortions with pills such as mifepristone are extremely safe and used across the country to help provide access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/30/us-unsafe-abortions-rise-doctors-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Surge in complications from unsafe abortions likely post-Roe, doctors warn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When it comes to Washington and emergencies, it\u8217\'20\'19s out with the old, in with the new.\par \par \uc2 The old, of course, are the national and public health emergencies declared by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to fight Covid-19 as it began its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/15/1-million-us-covid-deaths-effects"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disastrous spread}}}\uc2  across the country in 2020. Republicans were always uneasy with the idea of restricting what Americans could do in a bid to halt transmission of the virus, and the House GOP will today introduce two bills that would end the emergencies. But the Biden White House took some wind out of their sails {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/SAP-H.R.-382-H.J.-Res.-7.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by announcing}}}\uc2  they plan to let both expire on 11 May, while warning that a sudden termination could negatively affect everything from border security to health insurance.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of how or when those emergencies end, we may be getting another one declared soon. Biden is a supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/01/31/biden-public-health-emergency-abortion-dobbs?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2  that his department of health and human services secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  is weighing announcing a public health emergency aimed at ensuring Americans can continue obtaining abortions, even after the supreme court allowed states to ban the procedure entirely last year. Such a declaration could ensure people are able to receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication no matter where they are, but may not hold up in court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House to end Covid emergency, eyes declaring reproductive health crisis\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. It\u8217\'20\'19s been three years since Covid-19 broke out across the United States and the government took extraordinary measures to stop it from spreading. Now, it appears one of those steps is coming to an end, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/SAP-H.R.-382-H.J.-Res.-7.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House announcing}}}\uc2  it will allow the national emergencies declared to fight the pandemic to lapse on 11 May, a statement it made in response to Republican legislation to force their hand on the matter. Much has changed in the country since the anxious early days of Covid-19, including the end of the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/01/31/biden-public-health-emergency-abortion-dobbs?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there are reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is also considering declaring a separate public health emergency aimed at ensuring access to reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we can expect to happen in the world of politics today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s day two of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure blitz, with the president traveling to New York City to promote his 2021 overhaul of the country\u8217\'20\'19s public works, and attend a \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  reception. He was doing much the same in Baltimore yesterday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives convenes at 10am to consider the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s bills to force an end to the Covid-19 national emergencies. The Senate convenes at the same time, where lawmakers will be making speeches and generally getting their ducks in a row to start the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s work.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jan/31/donald-trump-sues-bob-woodward-over-the-trump-tapes-for-50m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  journalist Bob Woodward and his publishers for releasing recordings of their interviews. The former president is seeking just a hair under $50m.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230131ej1v00236\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
