\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden honors Roe v Wade as anti-abortionists rally in Washington \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2023\par 15:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President calls on Congress to protect right to procedureSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This weekend marks the 50th anniversary of the supreme court handing down Roe v Wade, and the first since its conservative justices reversed that ruling last year and allowed states to ban the procedure. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cabe4b8f0835c8bc1c8144#block-63cabe4b8f0835c8bc1c8144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marked the day}}}\uc2  with a proclamation restating his administration\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to protecting reproductive rights, while blocks from the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cac6f18f080b4868cedc7d#block-63cac6f18f080b4868cedc7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists gathered}}}\uc2  for the annual March for Life \u8211\'20\'13 the first since Roe was overturned. The route for their march this year finished near the US Capitol, a signal that swaying legislatures nationwide is the next task for their movement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will next week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cae9f88f080b4868cede2c#block-63cae9f88f080b4868cede2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issue the first opinion of its current term}}}\uc2  after an unusually long period of silence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-63cab03a8f080b4868cedb03#block-63cab03a8f080b4868cedb03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has warned Republicans}}}\uc2  not to cut the popular Social Security or Medicare programs after the party\u8217\'20\'19s leaders vowed to reduce government spending in exchange for raising the debt limit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today marked the halfway point of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first term in office, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63ca9d428f0835c8bc1c7f59#block-63ca9d428f0835c8bc1c7f59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports indicate}}}\uc2  he still intends to seek a second term, with an announcement planned for after the 7 February State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats breathed a big sigh of relief when Virginia senator Tim Kaine{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cab89a8f080b4868cedb82#block-63cab89a8f080b4868cedb82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would seek re-election}}}\uc2 . Had he opted to retire, the party\u8217\'20\'19s quest to hold on to the Senate in the 2024 election could have become more complicated.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s new Democratic administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63caf8908f0835c8bc1c842f#block-63caf8908f0835c8bc1c842f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has paused executions}}}\uc2  and announced a review of the state\u8217\'20\'19s use of capital punishment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This post was edited on 23 January 2023 to clarify that the 50th anniversary of Roe v Wade is 22 January, not 20 January.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host the leaders of Congress at the White House next week, Bloomberg Government reports.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19ll also meet separately with Kevin McCarthy, the Republican House speaker, about raising the debt limit:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: House, Senate Democratic leaders to White House Tuesday to talk about new session w Biden\par \par \uc2 Biden says he'll have a separate discussion w GOP Leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/McCarthy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #McCarthy}}}\uc2  about US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DebtLimit?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DebtLimit}}}\uc2  soon but gives no details\par \par \uc2 US default would be \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented calamity,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nancy Ognanovich (@NOgnanovich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NOgnanovich/status/1616529834179694592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, newly elected Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  has announced a review of the state\u8217\'20\'19s procedures for applying the death penalty, and the attorney general has moved to pause executions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Arizona is going to execute individuals, it should have a system for doing so that is transparent, accountable, and faithful to our Constitution and the rule of law,\u8221\'20\'1D Kris Mayes, the Democratic attorney general elected in November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azag.gov/press-release/arizona-attorney-generals-office-files-motion-withdraw-execution-aaron-brian-gunches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2  that announced the withdrawal of a pending warrant of execution for a death row prisoner.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://azgovernor.gov/office-arizona-governor/news/2023/01/governor-katie-hobbs-unveils-executive-action-improving"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said she had signed an executive order}}}\uc2  creating a Death Penalty Independent Review Commissioner, who is tasked with evaluating \u8220\'20\'1Clethal injection drug and gas chamber chemical procurement process, execution protocols, and staffing considerations including training and experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the \uc2 Arizona Department of Corrections\uc2 , Rehabilitation and Reentry (ADCRR) now under new leadership, it\u8217\'20\'19s time to address the fact that this is a system that needs better oversight on numerous fronts,\u8221\'20\'1D Hobbs said. She noted that Arizona \u8220\'20\'1Chas a history of mismanaged executions that have resulted in serious questions and concerns about ADCRR\u8217\'20\'19s execution protocols and lack of transparency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Looks who\u8217\'20\'19s at the March for Life in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/02/patriot-front-recruits-members-young-pyramid-scheme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white nationalist group the Patriot Front,}}}\uc2  according to two independent photographers documenting the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  event:\par \par \uc2 enltrMembers of patriot front heading out flyers once again at March for life in Washington DC today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fWD5MTHJT3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fWD5MTHJT3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zach D Roberts - Photojournalist (@zdroberts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/zdroberts/status/1616513160319537161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGroups of men in flannel and face masks handing out Patriot Front flyers at March for Life in DC today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lu2hKayMxk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lu2hKayMxk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nathan Howard (@SmileItsNathan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmileItsNathan/status/1616518814950195204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a lengthy reply to Republican House judiciary chair Jim Jordan, the justice department laid out some conditions for its cooperation with the committee, CNN reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: DOJ responds to GOP Rep. Jim Jordan's requests for documents & info related to House Judiciary Committee probes.\par \par \uc2 Makes clear department unlikely to share information about ongoing criminal investigations but will work to accommodate other requests. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mbS2zSpKbZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mbS2zSpKbZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zachary Cohen (@ZcohenCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZcohenCNN/status/1616511883892166661?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s committee is one of several in the House that Republicans are using to launch inquiries into the Biden administration, and it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/media/press-releases/chairman-jim-jordan-puts-biden-administration-officials-notice-about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has already sent several requests}}}\uc2  for documents on various subjects to the White House, justice department and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is well into its 2022-2023 term, but hasn\u8217\'20\'19t released any opinions yet, in what court observers say is an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/supreme-court-waits-and-waits-some-more-to-issue-first-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unprecedented period of silence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s set to change Monday morning, when the justices finally release their first decision, SCOTUSblog reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: The Supreme Court expects to issue one or more opinions on Monday morning. It will be the first opinion-release of the 2022-23 term.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1616513383150518273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 As NBC News points out, there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling which opinions they will release:\par \par \uc2 enltrCourt heard some big cases in the fall but generally its first rulings are in lower-profile cases in which the justices are (mostly) unanimous\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1616511373441175564?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US vice president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  is due to give a speech on Sunday in the Florida state capital of Tallahassee, to mark the 50th anniversary of the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US a constitutional right, with its 1973 decision in the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 It would have been a celebration for those in favor of reproductive rights in America, including personal choice in the matter of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Instead, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is holding its annual rally and march in Washington in an atmosphere of triumph for the anti-choice school because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last June\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  by the now-conservative-dominated supreme court overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  participates in a roundtable discussing women\u8217\'20\'19s issues, rights and empowerment at Sofitel Manila, Philippines, last November. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 That decision in the so-called Dobbs case out of Mississippi ripped up Roe and threw away federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, returning the power to make law on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to individual states.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Harris will make a pro-choice speech and moments ago, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said the veep chose Florida partly because it has tough restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 though less so than its neighboring states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions are not as tough as neighbors,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jean-Pierre, but noted that Florida \u8220\'20\'1Cis considering an even more extreme ban which would be devastating for women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  takes the podium in the west wing of the White House for the daily media briefing. Photograph: Alex Wong/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have been in office for exactly two years today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump withdraws lawsuit against New York attorney general\par \par \uc2 In the wake of a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/trump-and-lawyer-ordered-to-pay-1m-for-bringing-frivolous-lawsuit-against-hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordering }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/trump-and-lawyer-ordered-to-pay-1m-for-bringing-frivolous-lawsuit-against-hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and one of his attorneys to jointly pay nearly $1m in penalties for pursuing a frivolous lawsuit that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/24/trump-hillary-clinton-russia-lawsuit-2016-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/24/trump-hillary-clinton-russia-lawsuit-2016-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton}}}\uc2  and others, the former president today also withdrew his lawsuit against New York Attorney General Letitia James.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/trump-sues-letitia-james-ny-attorney-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case against James}}}\uc2 , in federal court in Florida, had also been before US district court judge Donald Middlebrooks, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Trump withdraws suit against NY State AG Letitia James \u8212\'20\'14 the type of frivolous case that was cited by the judge who last night imposed sanctions of nearly $1 million against Trump and his lawyer Alina Habba\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1616451669264601091?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump sued James in November in response to her lawsuit alleging he and his company mislead banks and others about the value of assets in a practice she dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CThe art of the steal\u8221\'20\'1D [a parody on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s best-selling book about getting rich as a New York real estate mogul, The Art of the Deal.]\par \par \uc2 Trump, a Republican, also sought to prevent James, a Democrat, from having any oversight over the family trust that controls his company.\par \par \uc2 His 35-page complaint rehashed some claims from his previously dismissed lawsuit against James in federal court in New York, irritating Middlebrooks.\par \par \uc2 Middlebrooks wrote in an order in December:\par \par \uc2 This litigation has all the telltale signs of being both vexatious and frivolous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 New York State Attorney General Letitia James speaks during a Martin Luther King Jr. Day event in Harlem National Action Network event last Monday. Photograph: Ron Adar/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Today is the 50th anniversary of the supreme court handing down Roe v Wade, and the first since its conservative justices reversed that ruling last year and allowed states to ban the procedure. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cabe4b8f0835c8bc1c8144#block-63cabe4b8f0835c8bc1c8144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marked the day}}}\uc2  with a proclamation restating his administration\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to protecting reproductive rights, while blocks from the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cac6f18f080b4868cedc7d#block-63cac6f18f080b4868cedc7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists have gathered}}}\uc2  for the annual March for Life \u8211\'20\'13 the first since Roe was overturned. In a sign of the struggle ahead, the route for their march this year will finish near the US Capitol, a signal that legislatures nationwide are now the main battlefields for their movement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-63cab03a8f080b4868cedb03#block-63cab03a8f080b4868cedb03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has warned Republicans}}}\uc2  not to go after the popular Social Security or Medicare programs after the party\u8217\'20\'19s leaders promised to cut government spending in exchange for raising the debt limit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today marks the halfway point of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first term in office, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63ca9d428f0835c8bc1c7f59#block-63ca9d428f0835c8bc1c7f59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports indicate}}}\uc2  he still plans to seek a second term, with an announcement planned for after the 7 February State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats breathed a big sigh of relief when Virginia senator Tim Kaine{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/20/biden-classified-documents-anti-abortion-rally-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-63cab89a8f080b4868cedb82#block-63cab89a8f080b4868cedb82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would seek a third term}}}\uc2 . Had he opted to retire, the party\u8217\'20\'19s quest to hold on to the Senate in the 2024 election could have become more complicated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge: DeSantis broke law by suspending Florida state attorney\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  violated the law when he suspended a Florida state attorney for saying he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t enforce the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive new 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a judge has ruled.\par \par \uc2 But district court judge Robert Hinkle says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the authority to overturn the Republican governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision and reinstate Hillsborough county state attorney Andrew Warren to office.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Warren. Photograph: Octavio Jones/Reuters\par \par \uc2 DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/ron-desantis-suspends-andrew-warren-prosector-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed Warren in August}}}\uc2  after the Democrat said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t enforce the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, or prosecute providers of gender transition treatment for young people. Accusing Warren of following a \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D agenda, the governor said he had put himself \u8220\'20\'1Cabove the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23580631/warren-ruling.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scathing 59-page ruling}}}\uc2  released Friday, Hinkle said it was DeSantis, a likely candidate for the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, who had broken the law.\par \par \uc2 He rejected DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that Warren had a blanket policy of not prosecuting certain cases, and that Warren had every right as a state attorney to \u8220\'20\'1Cexercise prosecutorial discretion at every stage of every case\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 The governor violated the first amendment by considering Mr Warren\u8217\'20\'19s speech on matters of public concern as motivating factors in the decision to suspend him.\par \par \uc2 The governor [also] violated the first amendment by considering Mr Warren\u8217\'20\'19s association with the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 Hinkle conceded that DeSantis would still have removed Warren without the violations, and because they didn\u8217\'20\'19t affect the outcome, he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t provide injunctive relief.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s violation of the Florida state constitution did affect the outcome, Hinkle said. But he noted the 11th amendment prohibited a federal court awarding relief against a state official based only on a violation of state law, and that he had no alternative to dismiss Warren\u8217\'20\'19s request for reinstatement.\par \par \uc2 In an earlier stage of the legal case, Hinkle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/23/ron-desantis-andrew-warren-abortion-ban-lawsuit-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered DeSantis to testify}}}\uc2  in defense of his decision, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wusfnews.wusf.usf.edu/courts-law/2022-11-23/gov-desantis-wont-have-to-testify-at-trial-of-suspended-hillsborough-state-attorney-andrew-warren"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed down in November}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With his legal path to reinstatement now apparently blocked, Warren is expected to lay out his next steps to reporters later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The demise of Roe v Wade was unusual in that Americans knew it was coming weeks in advance.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s because somebody obtained a draft of the decision in the Dobbs case and leaked it to Politico, a highly unusual development for an institution whose inner workings are almost never revealed. Chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  ordered an investigation into the leak, but yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jan/19/us-supreme-court-leaked-dobbs-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court\u8217\'20\'19s marshal said they could not figure out who did it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That hasn\u8217\'20\'19t sat well with some. Republican senator \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2  deployed his trademark colorful language in an interview with Fox News, blaming the leaker for putting a supreme court justice in danger:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations, butthead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (R-LA) message to the leaker of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  draft opinion on overturning Roe v. Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m6XMognn70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m6XMognn70}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1616477844040830976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t name him, but Kennedy is likely referring to \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 ,a conservative who was among the justices voting to overturn Roe. Last summer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/15/brett-kavanaugh-assassination-plot-man-indicted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 26-year-old man was arrested}}}\uc2  for allegedly plotting to assassinate Kavanaugh.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The sentiment among March for Life attendees is a mixture of politics, prayer and poetry, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino reports from the rally:\par \par \uc2 enltrSignage is similar to last years: \u8220\'20\'1CI am the post-roe generation.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CLove them both\u8221\'20\'1D with an image of a pregnant woman.\par \par \uc2 Also spotted some Trump 2024 signage and attire and at least one \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s go Brandon\u8221\'20\'1D flag.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pXD0iUvD8S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pXD0iUvD8S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1616470179805798401?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Dr. Seuss quote is also a popular one in signs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OB2ArfeMBF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OB2ArfeMBF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1616471154675286021?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Irish musician performing at the rally is asking women to pray for the men in the audience who are here standing up for women and children {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sSrHQoLQ3j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sSrHQoLQ3j}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1616474241158742020?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Republicans are welcoming the annual March for Life to Washington DC, including Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrProud of the Kentuckians and all Americans standing up for human dignity at this year\u8217\'20\'19s March for Life. I\u8217\'20\'19m honored to stand together with you today and everyday in solidarity with the most vulnerable in our society.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1616451432915369985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 As well as speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy:\par \par \uc2 enltrI want to welcome everyone who has come to our nation\u8217\'20\'19s Capital today to celebrate a special gift from God: the right to life.\par \par \uc2 Last week, we passed legislation providing medical care for babies born alive during abortions. You now have a Congress that is standing up for life.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1616449303060557828?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 His majority leader Steve Scalise is among the speakers expected at the rally, which is streaming live below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden honors Roe anniversary as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes convene\par \par \uc2 This weekend, 22 January marks the 50th anniversary of the Roe v Wade decision, which protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide until it was overturned by the conservative-dominated supreme court last year. The White House has issued a proclamation honoring the formerly precedent-setting case, and promising to continue fighting for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court got Roe right 50 years ago. It was a balanced decision with broad national consensus that the majority of Americans have continued to support for the last 50 years. And it was a constitutional principle upheld by justices appointed by Democratic and Republican Presidents alike,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wrote in the proclamation, which honors \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerations of advocates who have fought for reproductive freedom, to recognize the countless women whose lives and futures have been saved and shaped by the Roe v. Wade decision, and to march forward with purpose as we work together to restore the right to choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI continue to call on the Congress to pass legislation to make those protections the law of the land once and for all. Until then, I will continue to use my Executive authority to protect women and families from harm in the wake of the Dobbs decision,\u8221\'20\'1D which overturned Roe, the president said.\par \par \uc2 But just blocks from the White House, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates are gathering for the annual March for Life rally, the first since the supreme court ruling in Dobbs vs Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization allowed states to ban the procedure. They\u8217\'20\'19ve changed up their route this year and will finish near the Capitol, a recognition that the latest front in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate is in Congress and state legislatures nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino is on the scene at the rally:\par \par \uc2 enltrAbortion opponents are beginning to gather on the mall before the annual March for Life rally and march, the first since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v Wade. The theme this year is \u8220\'20\'1CNext Steps: Marching Forward into a Post-Roe America.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aQnnE5SLiT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aQnnE5SLiT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1616459953937465350?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Virginia Senator Tim Kaine has announced he will run for another term in 2024, meaning Democrats won\u8217\'20\'19t have to find a new candidate to fill his seat in what is expected to be a very difficult year for the party:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Kaine says he's running for a third term\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marianne LeVine (@marianne_levine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marianne_levine/status/1616455643816415232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Virginia has supported Democrats in recent presidential and Senate elections, but Kaine\u8217\'20\'19s retirement would have created another headache for a party that will have several as they try to maintain control of the Senate in 2024. Several Democratic lawmakers from red states will be up for re-election then, including West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Joe Manchin, Montana\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  and Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , and Republicans only need to win two seats to regain control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re going to be hearing a lot about the debt limit for the next several months, and thus, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  has written a story telling you everything you need to know about the bubbling debate:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  could be headed for a crisis manufactured by a handful of House Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , informed congressional leaders on Thursday that the US has hit its debt ceiling, which limits the amount of money that the government can borrow to pay all of its bills. Yellen urged Congress to work as quickly as possible to raise the debt ceiling and prevent the US from defaulting on any of its financial obligations, which would have catastrophic consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is therefore critical that Congress act in a timely manner to increase or suspend the debt limit,\u8221\'20\'1D Yellen warned in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1188"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  sent last week. \u8220\'20\'1CFailure to meet the government\u8217\'20\'19s obligations would cause irreparable harm to the US economy, the livelihoods of all Americans, and global financial stability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The dire language from the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top economic official underscored the urgency of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s task and appeared to represent an attempt to deter any lawmaker from toying with the idea of a default. Some House Republicans have chosen to do so anyway.\par \par \uc2 Members of the hard-right House Freedom Caucus have already promised to oppose a \u8220\'20\'1Cclean\u8221\'20\'1D debt ceiling increase, meaning a bill that raises the national borrowing limit without any other policy concessions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot raise the debt ceiling,\u8221\'20\'1D the Arizona congressman Andy Biggs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ/status/1615419794362142731"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Tuesday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats have carelessly spent our taxpayer money and devalued our currency. They\u8217\'20\'19ve made their bed, so they must lie in it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/us-debt-ceiling-crisis-house-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US heads for debt-ceiling standoff as House Republicans refuse to budge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump cautions Republicans on debt limit fight\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has weighed in on the battle over raising the debt ceiling, imploring fellow Republicans not to try to change the Social Security or Medicare programs in exchange for agreeing to an increase, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/20/trump-gop-medicare-social-security-debt-ceiling-00078731"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder no circumstances should Republicans vote to cut a single penny from Medicare or Social Security,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a video message.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCut waste, fraud and abuse everywhere that we can find it,\u8221\'20\'1D he continues. \u8220\'20\'1CBut do not cut the benefits our seniors worked for and paid for their entire lives. Save Social Security, don\u8217\'20\'19t destroy it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The video was made by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, and obtained by Politico before its public release.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who control the House of Representatives, are demanding unspecified budget reforms in exchange for agreeing to increase the government\u8217\'20\'19s legal borrowing limit. Washington hit that limit yesterday, but is expected to have enough cash on hand to continue funding government operations until at least June, after which it could default on its debt for the first time in history.\par \par \uc2 The House GOP has been vague on what exactly they want in exchange for an increase, but some lawmakers have called for changing the Social Security retirement benefit or Medicare program, which pays for health care for elderly and disabled people. Both are extremely popular programs, but have become increasing drains on the federal budget.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is usually the feuder-in-chief, but now his former deputies are fighting amongst themselves! Leave it to \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  to tell you why:\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley said the former secretary of state \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jan/18/nikki-haley-plotted-kushner-ivanka-trump-vp-mike-pompeo-new-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claim}}}\uc2  that she plotted to replace \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-president was \u8220\'20\'1Clies and gossip to sell a book\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former United Nations ambassador {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/19/nikki-haley-mike-pompeo-vp-claims-00078669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to Fox News}}}\uc2  on Thursday evening, after the Guardian obtained a copy of Pompeo\u8217\'20\'19s forthcoming memoir, Never Give An Inch, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jan/18/nikki-haley-plotted-kushner-ivanka-trump-vp-mike-pompeo-new-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  his comments about Haley.\par \par \uc2 Haley resigned from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  in October 2018. Before that, Pompeo says, she set up a personal meeting with Trump in the Oval Office without checking with him.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo writes that \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , then Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, thought Haley had in fact been accompanied by \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  as they presented \u8220\'20\'1Ca possible \u8216\'20\'18Haley for vice-president\u8217\'20\'19 option\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo also writes unfavourably of Haley\u8217\'20\'19s performance as \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador and criticises her resignation.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox News, Haley said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know why he said it, but that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly why I stayed out of DC as much as possible, to get away from the drama.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jan/19/nikki-haley-pompeo-lies-and-gossip-to-sell-book-vice-president-plot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley accuses Pompeo of \u8216\'20\'18lies and gossip to sell book\u8217\'20\'19 after vice-president plot claim}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is often in court, both as a plaintiff and defendant, but the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports one of his legal sagas has turned out to have quite an expensive conclusion:\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has ordered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and one of his attorneys to jointly pay nearly $1m in penalties for pursuing a frivolous lawsuit that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/24/trump-hillary-clinton-russia-lawsuit-2016-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused Hillary Clinton, the Democratic National Committee and other perceived enemies}}}\uc2  of the former president of engaging in racketeering and concocting a vast conspiracy against him.\par \par \uc2 The suit was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/trump-hillary-clinton-lawsuit-russia-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed in September}}}\uc2  and Trump was ordered to pay tens of thousands in November after one defendant sought sanctions. The latest order came after a group of the remaining defendants, including Clinton, filed a separate request for sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The end of the lawsuit marks the latest legal setback for Trump as he grapples with an array of civil and criminal investigations, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/18/trump-special-counsel-justice-department-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the probe into his retention of sensitive documents}}}\uc2 , while some of his lawyers are under scrutiny themselves for conduct in those cases.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/trump-and-lawyer-ordered-to-pay-1m-for-bringing-frivolous-lawsuit-against-hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump and lawyer ordered to pay $1m for bringing \u8216\'20\'18frivolous\u8217\'20\'19 lawsuit against Hillary Clinton}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A president in possession of classified documents he should not have. Sound familiar? That\u8217\'20\'19s because both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are facing investigations for potentially breaching government secrecy laws. However there are a number of differences between the cases facing the two men, and the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chris-michael"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Michael}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  have put together a breakdown of the contrasts:\par \par \uc2 The discovery of classified documents in offices used by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s thinktank and in a locked storage unit in a garage near where the president keeps his Corvette may not be a criminal matter, but it does appear to have taken a political toll.\par \par \uc2 With a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/bidens-approval-40-near-lowest-his-presidency-reutersipsos-2023-01-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Reuters/Ipsos poll}}}\uc2  on Thursday finding that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating, which had risen at the end of 2022, was back down to just 40% \u8211\'20\'13 near the lowest level of his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 many Democrats are smacking their foreheads, fearing Biden has done exactly what his expected 2024 opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was under investigation for doing.\par \par \uc2 So much for painting Trump as dangerous, volatile and a threat to national security. Right?\par \par \uc2 But that\u8217\'20\'19s not to say the two cases are the same. The scale of the scandals is hugely lopsided: thousands of documents in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s possession, including many marked top secret, versus an estimated dozen in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/classified-documents-biden-trump-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Trump and two very different classified document scandals, explained}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 By all indications, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will seek a second term in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe spent his entire adult lifetime running for president, and on the third try, he finally got there. Who would give it up under those conditions, who? Almost nobody,\u8221\'20\'1D veteran political analyst \uc2 Larry Sabato{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/09/joe-biden-2024-race-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  earlier this month, in a comment that encapsulates much of the reason the 80-year-old is expected to run again, despite being the oldest president to serve.\par \par \uc2 But the announcement will likely be made under a cloud of scandal, though it\u8217\'20\'19s to be seen how much voters will care. The classified documents discovery is being taken seriously in Washington, with the justice department appointing a special prosecutor to look into whether Biden did wrong. But beyond that, people in his administration say much of the furor is \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18DC elite\u8217\'20\'19 making \u8216\'20\'18DC noise,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/01/19/politics/joe-biden-2024-classified-documents/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported yesterday}}}\uc2 , and the president still plans to announce his bid for a second term sometime after the 7 February State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With 'no regrets' about classified documents, Biden marks two years in office, hints at 2024\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today marks the halfway point of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first term as president. Will he seek a second? He has yet to officially decide, but all signs continue to point to yes. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest one: the White House is circulating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000185-cd58-de44-a7bf-ed5f61aa0000&nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a document}}}\uc2 , obtained by Politico, recounting all of what they say are his accomplishments over the past 24 months. But in recent days, Biden has found himself personally entangled in a growing scandal over classified documents from his time as vice-president that were found at his home and former residence. Considering the justice department is going after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for doing something similar, albeit in much greater quantities and with much less transparency, the affair seems to present a threat to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. Yesterday, Biden shrugged it off. \u8220\'20\'1CI think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to find there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing there. I have no regrets,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied, when a reporter asked about the documents. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no there there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what we can expect today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  March of Life is holding its annual rally in Washington DC, the first since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. This year, the marchers will conclude not at the high court, but near the Capitol, in a sign of how campaign\u8217\'20\'19s focus has shifted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden welcomes a bipartisan groups of mayors to the White House at 2pm eastern time, before heading to Delaware for the weekend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Kaine is expected to announce whether he will seek a third term today, according to Punchbowl News. A retirement by the Virginia Democrat would give Republicans another opportunity to flip a seat and take control of the chamber in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230120ej1k00209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
