\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March draws thousands across US after Roe v Wade overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor in Washington \par \uc2 799 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 January 2023\par 15:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Protesters mark 50 years since landmark decision that protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide\par \par \uc2 Thousands of protesters gathered across the United States to protest the end of the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 marching on the the 50th anniversary of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  supreme court decision that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a constitutional right in 1973, but which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 At more than 200 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March events in 46 states, demonstrators condemned the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which leaves it up to individual states to decide whether to protect, ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Since last year\u8217\'20\'19s startling decision from the conservative-dominated bench, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been banned or severely restricted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2023/01/six-months-post-roe-24-us-states-have-banned-abortion-or-are-likely-do-so-roundup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 states, after the ruling on 24 June.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFifty years after the anniversary of Roe v Wade, a radical rightwing movement hijacked our courts and eliminated federal protections for abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Carmona, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organization, who orchestrated the nationwide events.\par \par \uc2 Carmona added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut as the fight turns to the states, they are going to learn that the overwhelming majority of Americans in all states support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and women will fight to protect our rights and our lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protests included thousands gathered at the Freedom Plaza steps in Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 Activists from Harriet\u8217\'20\'19s Wildest Dreams, a police-abolitionist group wearing colorful bomber jackets, led the march in Washington, with chants such as: \u8220\'20\'1CNot the church, not the state, the people must decide their fate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They led a thick crowd of protesters who filled downtown streets, marching from Freedom Plaza to the White House, holding banners that read \u8220\'20\'1Cforced vasectomies: they prevent abortions and they\u8217\'20\'19re reversible!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmore women die from misogyny than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Celeste Hidalgo, 4o, attended the march with her daughter, Raven Hidalgo, 18. It was Raven\u8217\'20\'19s first marching experience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because it\u8217\'20\'19s unfair men are taking away our rights over our own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to male-dominated courts and legislatures.\par \par \uc2 Saskia Lodder, 68, held a sign that read: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been marching 50 years to keep politics and religion out of women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D She said she had been devastated on the day the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overturned. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a nurse. No man in a suit or black robe should be able to make these deeply personal decisions on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s behalf,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In Madison, Wisconsin, designated as Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s main event, thousands of protesters flooded the streets, with signs that read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmy body, my soul, my life, my choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended last summer, Wisconsin has been operating under a near-total ban written in the 1800s. Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2 , and governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , are fighting the ban in court. Prior to last June\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision, abortions were legal in Wisconsin until 20 weeks into the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March organizers chose Wisconsin to highlight the state\u8217\'20\'19s forthcoming state supreme court election, which could be pivotal, and mobilize protesters and activists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe upcoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/partisan-battle-over-balance-power-wisconsin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court election}}}\uc2  in Wisconsin this spring will determine the balance of power on the [state] court, and the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the State,\u8221\'20\'1D organizers said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are taking the fight to the states. From Wisconsin, to Nebraska, to Georgia, to Arizona and Texas, women and our allies are defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights where they still stand, and working to put measures on the ballot to regain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in places where politicians are putting their agendas over the will of the people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The events follow the annual anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/20/march-for-life-anti-abortion-roe-v-wade-fall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March for Life demonstration}}}\uc2 , which took place on Friday in Washington DC, where thousands of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists turned up to celebrate the movement\u8217\'20\'19s success.\par \par \uc2 To mark the 50th anniversary of the landmark Roe v Wade ruling, the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , delivered a speech in Tallahassee, Florida, another state with tight restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will get tighter if state Republicans have their way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince our founding, we have been on a march forward \u8230\'20\'26 to secure freedom and liberty for all. This fight will not be inevitable, this will not just happen \u8211\'20\'13 it takes steadfast determination and dedication. So today, we are fighting back,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 With Republicans controlling the House of Representatives, there is little hope of federal legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally.\par \par \uc2 But Harris added: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden has issued a presidential memorandum. Members of our cabinet and our administration are now directed to identify barriers to [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] access and recommend actions to make sure that doctors can legally prescribe, doctors can dispense and women can secure safe and effective medication,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230122ej1m002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
