\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s marches take place across country on 50th anniversary of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 1,878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2023\par 21:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 200 events in 46 states protest supreme court decision that struck down the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in US\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 4.30pm in Washington DC. We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog now, but you can read the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s story on the women\u8217\'20\'19s march and reproductive rights issue today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/womens-march-2023-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Although smaller compared to previous years, this year\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s March still saw thousands take to the streets. Many showed up with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd9e278f080b4868ceed2b#block-63cd9e278f080b4868ceed2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 creative signs}}}\uc2  in passionate protest for reproductive freedoms.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona, the executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd97268f08475f7d94d21d#block-63cd97268f08475f7d94d21d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addressed}}}\uc2  crowds in Madison, Wisconsin, which has been chosen by march organizers as this year\u8217\'20\'19s rallying base. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be distracted by the drama in DC. Instead we are sending a clear message to elected leaders and to our base \u8211\'20\'13 we are going to where the fight is, and that is at the state level,\u8221\'20\'1D organizers said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd90328f0835c8bc1c91b3#block-63cd90328f0835c8bc1c91b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  Congress on Sunday to pass legislation that codifies reproductive rights offered by Roe. \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear: a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose is non-negotiable. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t stopped fighting to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 and I never will. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for Congress to pass legislation codifying the protections of Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Washington DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd7dfc8f080b4868ceec54#block-63cd7dfc8f080b4868ceec54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizers}}}\uc2  from the Black-led abolitionist group Harriet\u8217\'20\'19s Wildest Dreams drowned out the sound of counter-protesters, chanting \u8220\'20\'1CHey hey, ho ho, these racist bitches have got to go.\u8221\'20\'1D Speaking to the Guardian, 18-year old protestor Raven Hidalgo said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unfair men are taking away our rights over our own bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd7e848f08475f7d94d17a#block-63cd7e848f08475f7d94d17a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 address}}}\uc2  at Tallahassee, Florida, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reaffirmed the fight for reproductive rights across the country and announced a presidential memorandum issued by Biden. \u8220\'20\'1C Today, we are fighting back. I am pleased to announce that President Biden has issued a presidential memorandum. Members of our cabinet and our administration are now directed to identify barriers to access and recommend actions to make sure that doctors can legally prescribe, doctors can dispense and women can secure safe and effective medication,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A small counter-protest of less than a dozen people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/22/us-womens-marches-50th-anniversary-roe-v-wade-live?page=with:block-63cd7c748f080b4868ceec38#block-63cd7c748f080b4868ceec38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  stood}}}\uc2  outside Freedom Plaza steps in DC at noon today, chanting racist and sexist chants about slavery as thousands descended upon DC to march on the 50th anniversary of Roe being signed into law, half a year after the constitutional right was dismantled. Jessica Nowell, 19, from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students For Life, told the Guardian that she was upset by the counter-protest which she did not believe reflected the movement. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe with the pro-choicers but this behavior is disgusting and it\u8217\'20\'19s not the gospel. God loves us all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up our live coverage of this year\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s March. Thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Passionate signs and pins have been popping up all across the country as thousands of people took to the streets to demonstrate their opposition towards the removal of federal protections of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Scenes from outside the White House in Washington. Photograph: Bryan Olin Dozier/NurPhoto/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona, the executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, addressed crowds in Madison, Wisconsin, on Sunday as thousands descended upon the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital to demonstrate for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProud to be in Madison today fighting to let every politician know \u8211\'20\'13 if you come for our freedom, our families, or our futures, we\u8217\'20\'19re coming for you,\u8221\'20\'1D Carmona said.\par \par \uc2 enltrProud to be in Madison today fighting to let every politician know \u8212\'20\'14 if you come for our freedom, our families, or our futures, we're coming for you. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UGXARrYQ2p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UGXARrYQ2p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona (@RachCarmona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RachCarmona/status/1617251255394476032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Organizers of the annual Women\u8217\'20\'19s March chose Madison as this year\u8217\'20\'19s rallying base, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensmarch.com/BTR-March-on-Madison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be distracted by the drama in DC. Instead we are sending a clear message to elected leaders and to our base \u8211\'20\'13 we are going to where the fight is, and that is at the state level. We\u8217\'20\'19ll start in Wisconsin, where an upcoming supreme court election this spring will determine the balance of power on the State\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court and the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Wisconsin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  urged Congress on Sunday to pass legislation that codifies reproductive rights protections offered by Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday should\u8217\'20\'19ve been the 50th Anniversary of Roe v Wade. Instead, Maga Republican officials are waging a war on women\u8217\'20\'19s right to make their own healthcare decisions. But this fight isn\u8217\'20\'19t over,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1617180530281168896?s=20&t=q_4GtDa3qcw6YWfnHo3ymg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear: a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose is non-negotiable. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t stopped fighting to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 and I never will. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for Congress to pass legislation codifying the protections of Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access during a \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  event at the Howard Theatre in October 2022. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The march formally ended around 1pm with a bulk of the crowd dispersing, but protestors stayed on with megaphones and bright banners, marching downtown towards the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Takira Walker, 19, attended with a group of students from \uc2 Howard University\uc2  as part of a group called Revolt Incorporated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of us here are religious and don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we believe it should be a choice to access safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walker, who hopes to become an OB-GYN.\par \par \uc2 Takira Walker, 19, stands with a sign at the women's march, on the 50th anniversary of Roe vs Wade. Photograph: Poppy Noor\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Organizers from the Black-led abolitionist group Harriet\u8217\'20\'19s Wildest Dreams drowned out the sound of counter protestors, chanting \u8220\'20\'1CHey hey, ho ho, these racist bitches have got to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Celeste Hidalgo, 40, attended the march in Washington DC with her daughter Raven Hidalgo, 18. It was Raven\u8217\'20\'19s first march.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unfair men are taking away our rights over our own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D said 18-year-old Raven.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Hidalgo, 40, and her daughter Raven Hidalgo, 18, at the women\u8217\'20\'19s march. Photograph: Poppy Noor\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In her address at Tallahassee, Florida, vice -president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reaffirmed the fight for reproductive rights across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince our founding, we have been on a march forward to fully realize our promise. To complete the unfinished work. To secure freedom and liberty for all. This fight will not be inevitable. This will not just happen. It takes steadfast determination and dedication,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo today, we are fighting back. I am pleased to announce that President Biden has issued a presidential memorandum. Members of our cabinet and our administration are now directed to identify barriers to access and recommend actions to make sure that doctors can legally prescribe, doctors can dispense and women can secure safe and effective medication,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  delivers remarks to commemorate the 50th Anniversary of Roe v Wade in Tallahassee, Florida. Photograph: ABACA/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Around 12 .30pm, protestors headed to the White House, amidst chants of \u8220\'20\'1COur bodies, our choice,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are under attack what do we do? Stand up fight back!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Around 12.45pm, protestors assembled outside the White House to a backing track of Bob Marley and chants of \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that we will win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protestors stand outside the White House in DC for the women\u8217\'20\'19s march, on the 50th anniversary of Roe vs Wade. Photograph: Poppy Noor\par \par \uc2 Saskia Lodder, 68, held a sign that read: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been marching 50+ years to keep politics and religion out of women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare \u8230\'20\'26 Now I march for our granddaughters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said she was devastated on the day the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overturned. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a nurse. No man in a suit or black robe should be able to make these deeply personal decisions on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s behalf,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Saskia Lodder, 68, stands outside the White House for the women\u8217\'20\'19s march. Photograph: Poppy Noor\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A small counter protest of less than a dozen people stood outside Freedom Plaza steps in D C at noon today, chanting racist and sexist chants about slavery as thousands descended upon D C to march on the 50th anniversary of Roe being signed into law, half a year after the constitutional right was dismantled.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Nowell, 19, from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students For Life says she was upset by the counter protest which she did not believe reflected the movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe with the pro-choicers but this behavior is disgusting and it\u8217\'20\'19s not the gospel. God loves us all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Women's marches take place 50 years since Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Hello Guardian live blog readers, we are currently covering several developing news events and this blog is going to keep you appraised on the women\u8217\'20\'19s march now underway in Washington, DC, and some other places in the US.\par \par \uc2 And US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is speaking in Tallahassee, Florida, in a major speech to mark what would have been the 50th anniversary of the Roe v Wade decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 1973 that afforded the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade was struck down last June by a now conservative-dominated supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At more than 200 Women\u8217\'20\'19s March events in 46 states, demonstrators are lamenting the supremecourt\u8217\'20\'19s decision that now leaves it to individual states to decide on whether to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal for themselves. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since been banned or severely restricted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2023/01/six-months-post-roe-24-us-states-have-banned-abortion-or-are-likely-do-so-roundup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 states since the ruling on 24 June.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Protests included hundreds gathered at the Freedom Plaza steps in Washington, DC, ahead of the march.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Madison, Wisconsin, where a key event is taking place, thousands of protestors are flooding the streets surrounding the state Capitol, with signs that read \u8220\'20\'1Cbans off our bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cour blood is on your hands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is talking now in Florida on the ongoing battle for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230122ej1m00233\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
