\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 McCarthy may be speaker, but Trump is the real leader of House Republicans\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,733 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 January 2023\par 16:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 After Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for speaker narrowly won, what sway will the former president hold over Congress\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority?\par \par \uc2 Like an exhausted marathon runner, Kevin McCarthy had just about staggered across the finish line. But even at 2.11am, with tempers frayed and eyes bleary, the newly elected speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  wanted to single out one person for praise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do want to especially thank President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/video/2023/01/07/speaker_mccarthy_i_especially_want_to_thank_president_trump_do_not_doubt_his_influence.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McCarthy told reporters}}}\uc2  after prevailing in the longest election for speaker since before the civil war. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think anyone should doubt his influence. He was with me from the beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The gushing tribute obscured the complexity of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s intervention in the election for speaker \u8211\'20\'13 and what sway he might hold over the narrow Republican majority in the new Congress.\par \par \uc2 The week that followed brought a series of extremist actions and appointments that appear designed to resonate with his rightwing base. But whether House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 agenda will ultimately complement or conflict with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential election campaign remains uncertain.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/07/kevin-mccarthy-republican-house-speaker-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election as speaker}}}\uc2  took four gruelling days, 15 roll call votes and concessions that he might come to regret. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement appeared impotent for much of that time, even among some of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s champions in Congress. As he made calls in the dying hours of Friday night, a memorable photo showed Congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  attempting to give her phone, with \u8220\'20\'1CDT\u8221\'20\'1D on the line, to colleague \uc2 Matt Rosendale\uc2 , only for him to wave it away.\par \par \uc2 But in the end, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-urges-house-republicans-back-mccarthy-speaker-2023-01-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s man won}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a sign that he remains important if not decisive. McCarthy duly felt obliged to heap praise on the kingmaker. He also made a somewhat optimistic claim: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the great part: because it took this long, now we learned how to govern.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was immediately put to the test. On Monday evening, Republicans passed legislation to cut funding that was intended to bolster the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/09/us/politics/house-republicans-irs-funding.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a party-line vote}}}\uc2 . The speaker proclaimed: \u8220\'20\'1CPromises made. Promises kept.\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats called it a deficit-raising windfall for wealthy tax cheats at the expense of the majority that has no chance of passing in a Senate they still control.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/09/house-republicans-defang-ethics-office-investigating-members"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formed a panel}}}\uc2  to tackle what they perceive as rampant abuse of power in the federal government, not least by law enforcement agencies investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn the 2020 election results and handling and storing of presidential records at his Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida.\par \par \uc2 The subcommittee focusing on \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/01/11/republican-federal-law-enforcement-weaponization?utm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the weaponization of the federal government}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D falls under the judiciary committee, headed by Congressman Jim Jordan of Ohio, who has repeatedly said Trump should become president again. It will have access to classified information, a privilege usually reserved for the intelligence committees in the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Its \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestigate the investigators\u8221\'20\'1D mandate was doubtless music to the ears of Trump, who has spent years airing grievances at rallies about a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy that led to the Russia investigation and two impeachments. Democrat \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , a prominent member of the now dissolved January 6 committee, called the new panel an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection protection team\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Republicans targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Their majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/new-abortion-restrictions-bills-republicans-house-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a resolution}}}\uc2  to condemn attacks on anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities, including crisis pregnancy centers, and a separate bill that would impose new penalties if a doctor refused to care for an infant born alive after an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempt. Neither is expected pass the Democratic-led Senate.\par \par \uc2 The moves were condemned by liberals but did not go as far as some conservatives would have liked \u8211\'20\'13 a tacit acknowledgment that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become politically awkward for Republicans since last year\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision that overturned Roe v Wade after half a century. Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/trump-blames-abortion-issue-for-gops-poor-2022-midterms-results-2023-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  hardliners}}}\uc2  for Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 disappointing midterm elections results.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/staff/larry-j-sabato/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Sabato}}}\uc2 , director of the Center for Politics at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWould you start with that, if you were in their position, having just lost a midterm election effectively because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue? What was that doing there in the first place? Forty-eight hours of the actual Congress and this unorganized? Just amazing. There must be a stupidity chemical in the Washington water system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McCarthy also spent the week fending off questions over calls for fabulist New York congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/12/george-santos-republican-party-calls-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Santos}}}\uc2  to resign and the deal he struck with the House Freedom Caucus during his epic election battle. Like the Tea Party before it, the House Freedom Caucus is fixated on small government and less spending. Media reports suggest that it intends to seek cuts to entitlement programs such as social security and Medicare as well as to defense and law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 It is all part of an \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme Maga Republican agenda\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democrats.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/majority-leader-schumer-statement-on-house-gops-extreme-first-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last week Republicans have given a free pass to wealthy tax cheats, empaneled a committee to undermine and threaten law enforcement, undercut women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, and put forward a draconian budget plan that will lead to cuts to Medicare and social security and defunding the police.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There was a further statement of intent in House committees. Despite claiming to have embraced diversity and inclusion, Republicans named fewer women as committee chairs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/house-republicans-more-mike-women-committee-chairs-2023-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than men named Mike}}}\uc2 . The new chairs also have records that suggest they are ready to push Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D agenda.\par \par \uc2 Jordan, leading the judiciary panel, has amplified Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D that the 2020 election was stolen and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/26/us/republicans-jan-6-subpoenas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to comply with a subpoena}}}\uc2  issued by the January 6 committee over his communications with the former president.\par \par \uc2 The new chair of the oversight committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/8814/cosponsors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 James Comer}}}\uc2 , has co-sponsored a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that could have imprisoned doctors, amplified false claims of voter fraud in the 2020 election and called attempts to investigate the January 6 insurrection a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical stunt\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ca big show\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cillegitimate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jason Smith, chair of the ways and means committee, has supported cutting social security and Medicare, voted to overturn the 2020 election and described the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jasonsmith.house.gov/newsroom/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=3730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as a \u8220\'20\'1Csham\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that was \u8220\'20\'1Cdesigned to attack President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Jodey Arrington\uc2 , chair of the budget committee, has adopted similar positions.\par \par \uc2 Mark Green, chair of the homeland security committee, has introduced legislation to build a border wall and called for the homeland security secretary, Alejandro Mayorkas, to resign. He has also asserted that being \u8220\'20\'1Ctransgender is a disease\u8221\'20\'1D and said America must \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a stand on the indoctrination of Islam in our public schools\u8221\'20\'1D. Green identifies as a creationist and has argued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2017/05/01/politics/kfile-trump-army-secretary-pick-theory-of-evolution/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against the theory of evolution}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At first glance, it has the makings of a Trump caucus ready to do its master\u8217\'20\'19s bidding and aid his run for the White House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WalshFreedom?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Walsh}}}\uc2 , a former Republican congressman, said: \u8220\'20\'1CMost of what they\u8217\'20\'19re going to focus on is a bunch of revenge stuff for Trump, for how they believe Trump was treated, and a lot of this culture war bullshit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m convinced that a big part of what all these investigations involve is a lot of these guys believe the 2020 election was stolen from Trump: the \uc2 FBI\uc2  did it, the justice department did it. Trump and the Republicans declared war on the \uc2 FBI\uc2  some years ago so they\u8217\'20\'19re going to go after them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That McCarthy credited Trump with helping him secure the gavel \u8220\'20\'1Ctells you exactly still where Trump stands in the party\u8221\'20\'1D, Walsh added. \u8220\'20\'1CMcCarthy said that publicly, which is why Trump is still the king of the GOP hill unless something happens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was McCarthy who initially condemned Trump over the January 6 assault on democracy only to then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow-show/maddowblog/why-it-matters-mccarthy-went-mar-lago-kiss-ring-n1256137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make a pilgrimage to Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  a few weeks later and signal that all was forgiven. Now that Trump has backed McCarthy for speaker, despite significant opposition from his own base, he might expect the California Republican to repay the favour in 2024.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eppc.org/author/henry_olsen/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Henry Olsen}}}\uc2 , a senior fellow at the Ethics and Public Policy Center in Washington, has doubts. \u8220\'20\'1CMcCarthy is going to go where the winds blow,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CTo begin with, as a speaker he has to recognise where everyone in his conference is so he could very easily tell Trump at least during the early part of 2023, \u8216\'20\'18Look, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got a five-vote majority. I\u8217\'20\'19ve got people who love you, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got people who hate you, you know I love you but I\u8217\'20\'19ve got to keep this group together.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe may not like that but, if McCarthy did anything other than that in the initial jousting phases of the primary, McCarthy would be a poor political strategist. And McCarthy may lack certain attributes necessary to be a speaker but reading the room is not something he lacks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are other icebergs on the horizon. Congress faces an agenda of must-pass bills to fund the government, resupply a military depleted by decades of war and support for Ukraine, authorise farming programmes and raise the nation\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit to avert a disastrous federal default. In this context, an obsessive Republican pursuit of dead-on-arrival bills and Biden investigations could backfire on Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/experts/elaine-kamarck/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elaine Kamarck}}}\uc2 , a senior fellow at the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  thinktank in Washington, said: \u8220\'20\'1CBetween opposition within their party, between the Senate and the presidency, they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to win anything. What it\u8217\'20\'19s going to do is be a constant reminder to people of the extremes of the far right and Trump is so firmly associated with them. Substantively they\u8217\'20\'19re alike but stylistically they\u8217\'20\'19re alike as well. It\u8217\'20\'19s bad for him. It paints him into a real corner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kamarck, who served in \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House, added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that was amazing about his presidency was that, unlike any other president before him, he did not ever seek to expand his base. He was purely and simply happy with his factional base. The demographics of his factional base are that they\u8217\'20\'19re old so every year that he relies on that base gets more and more problematic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s simply weak. And he\u8217\'20\'19s going to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/12/donald-trump-us-midterms-republicans-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challengers for the 2024 Republican nomination}}}\uc2  which will make him look weaker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230116ej1g001tc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
