\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 South Carolina supreme court rules six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban unconstitutional\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 443 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 January 2023\par 23:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Decision means state\u8217\'20\'19s ban with exceptions for rape and incest will be immediately and permanently struck down\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina supreme court has ruled that the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unconstitutional, under the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 The 3-2 decision will mean the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with exceptions for rape and incest will be immediately and permanently struck down. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain legal in South Carolina up until 22 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that the decision to terminate a pregnancy rests upon the utmost personal and private considerations imaginable, and implicates a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice Kaye Hearn wrote in her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fwww.plannedparenthood.org%252Fuploads%252Ffiler_public%252F5e%252Ffc%252F5efcd6bb-9378-40a0-b9c2-66baf84cbf5b%252Fop_28127_-_planned_parenthood_v_state.pdf%26data%3D05%257C01%257CTYakupitiyage%2540reprorights.org%257Cf265a44ff01b4f27607908daef3f1a3c%257Ce5451579057a46829656b9548f94b665%257C0%257C0%257C638085351566995224%257CUnknown%257CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%253D%257C3000%257C%257C%257C%26sdata%3D8nQKM66w2h5uF0rSWGtwlXduyc%252F58%252FdFYpBLXdTWnpk%253D%26reserved%3D0&source=gmail&ust=1673024813284000&usg=AOvVaw3p7av6O5iyIFv-IDOyxkkg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile this right is not absolute, and must be balanced against the state\u8217\'20\'19s interest in protecting unborn life, this Act \u8211\'20\'13 which severely limits \u8211\'20\'13 and in many instances completely forecloses \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is an unreasonable restriction on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy and is therefore unconstitutional,\u8221\'20\'1D the decision read.\par \par \uc2 The law was written in 2021, before the federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was dismantled by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , and came into effect three days after that decision, on 27 June 2022.\par \par \uc2 The judgment also casts doubt on whether any future plans by the legislature to bring a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be considered unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision means that the right to make deeply personal healthcare decisions will remain protected in South Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 an immense victory for South Carolinians and the entire region,\u8221\'20\'1D stated \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights, one of the litigating groups in the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that lawmakers will double down on their relentless efforts to restrict essential healthcare, but we will continue to use every tool at our disposal to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the country once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D said Northup.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a monumental victory in the movement to protect legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the south,\u8221\'20\'1D Jenny Black, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, added. Planned Parenthood were the lead litigators in the case.\par \par \uc2 During legal arguments in October, justices had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/politics/articles/2022-10-19/south-carolina-supreme-court-takes-up-states-abortion-ban#:~:text=The%20hearing%20marked%20the%20latest,that%20endanger%20the%20patient%27s%20life."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debated whether the six-week ban }}}\uc2  allowed individuals to practice their rights to make informed medical decisions.\par \par \uc2 In the decision today, Chief Justice Donald Beatty ruled that the time frame was not reasonable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix weeks is, quite simply, not a reasonable period of time \u8230\'20\'26 and therefore the act violates our constitution\u8217\'20\'19s prohibition against unreasonable invasions of privacy,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the conclusion.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 5 January 2023 to correct a pronoun error in referring to Justice Kaye Hearn.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230116ej1f00262\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
