\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 House\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority gets to work with two  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  measures \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,406 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 January 2023\par 13:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 House to vote on medical protections for \u8216\'20\'18babies that survive an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18attacks on pro-life\u8217\'20\'19 groups and churchesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the House are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bec1338f08a62e1a2e22eb#block-63bec1338f08a62e1a2e22eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to pass two measures}}}\uc2  concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  later this afternoon, one a resolution condemning violence against opponents of the procedure, the other a bill meant to protect the life of babies who survive abortions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bf1baa8f085fda3e65ce92#block-63bf1baa8f085fda3e65ce92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats oppose both}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63beed698f085fda3e65ccd6#block-63beed698f085fda3e65ccd6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP officials in New York}}}\uc2  have called on George Santos to resign from Congress after he admitted to lying about his qualifications, but he says he\u8217\'20\'19s not going anywhere.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Domestic flights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/11/us-flights-disrupted-after-faa-alert-system-outage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resumed}}}\uc2  across the United States after all departures were briefly halted this morning by a systems failure at the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Republican investigator in the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bed7d28f085fda3e65cb97#block-63bed7d28f085fda3e65cb97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded}}}\uc2  documents from the Treasury related to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and other members of the president\u8217\'20\'19s family. He also wants testimony from three former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives involved in the platform\u8217\'20\'19s temporary banning of the New York Post after it reported on the discovery of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s laptop.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bee9468f08a62e1a2e2538#block-63bee9468f08a62e1a2e2538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried their best}}}\uc2  to get voters riled up over gas cookstoves.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s aides {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bf1e558f08fa7950d4c0c3#block-63bf1e558f08fa7950d4c0c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found more classified documents}}}\uc2  at a location he once used, though further details are scarce.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor is unlikely to be able to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bf0b0f8f085fda3e65ce37#block-63bf0b0f8f085fda3e65ce37"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats flipped a state Senate seat}}}\uc2  in a special election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More classified documents found in location used by Biden\par \par \uc2 Another batch of classified documents has turned up at a location used by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that is separate from the Washington DC office where the first cache was discovered in November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-aides-find-second-batch-classified-documents-new-location-rcna65371"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president has faced scrutiny ever since reports emerged this week that approximately 10 papers bearing government classification markings and dating to his time as vice-president were found at an office once used by Biden. According to NBC, the latest cache was found by aides to the president, though details of the documents\u8217\'20\'19 content and how many were found were not available.\par \par \uc2 NBC reports the documents were discovered after the president ordered a search for any other classified documents that may have been taken from the White House when he departed in January 2017 at the end of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At 4 pm, the House is scheduled to vote on a GOP-proposed resolution and bill concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But first, the Democrats will try to attach an amendment to the Born-Alive \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Survivors Protection Act, which is meant to protect babies who survive the procedure. The proposed amendment would \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibit government restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D according to Democratic whip Katherine Clark \u8217\'20\'19s office. \u8220\'20\'1CThis would include any limits to providers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to prescribe certain drugs, offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling services via telemedicine, or provide emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services when a delay would risk the health of the mother.\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans are certain to vote this proposal down.\par \par \uc2 The chamber will then consider both the born-alive act and the resolution condemning violence against anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups. Clark\u8217\'20\'19s office is encouraging Democrats to vote against both, saying the resolution does not contain \u8220\'20\'1Cany acknowledgment of violent attacks on providers or facilities that offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D and the born alive bill \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessarily restates current law requiring a doctor to provide the same standard of medical care for an infant born during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure as they would for any other infant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have the numbers to pass both, but at this stage, the effort is more about signaling priorities to GOP voters than changing the law. When the born-alive act arrives in the Senate, it is unlikely to be considered by its Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The calls for George Santos to resign have spread from county level Republicans to the state party, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrINBOX: NY state GOP backs call for Rep. George Santos' resignation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fIr0uSzDJX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fIr0uSzDJX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1613262163853905920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  was asked at her daily briefing about the classified documents discovered at an office formerly used by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and she said\u8230\'20\'26 not much.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith was in the White House briefing room to experience the illuminating exchange up close:\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre on Biden's classified documents: "He was surprised to find any records were there. He doesn't know what's in them... As he said, his team is cooperating fully with the review... We are committed to doing the right thing."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1613258391115411458?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJean-Pierre: "This is under review by the Department of Justice. I'm not going to go beyond what the president shared yesterday."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1613258683076706304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Reporters are wont to press, and press they did, at which point it grew a little heated:\par \par \uc2 enltrEd O'Keefe of CBS News notes that Biden acknowledged that he would make mistakes and ask for help fixing them. Jean-Pierre replies: "We don't need to have this kind of confrontation. Ask your question... You don't need to be contentious here with me, Ed."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1613260403571830785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if Biden is looking into whether there might be more classified documents elsewhere, Jean-Pierre replies: "I'm just not going to speak to this. I'm going to let the process continue."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1613260859111006208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has joined \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the club of current or former American presidents who may be in trouble over classified documents. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, the two men are not facing identical peril:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s retention of documents marked classified at his Mar-a-Lago resort has aggravating factors that might support his criminal prosecution unlike the discovery of some documents also marked classified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/09/us-justice-department-investigating-documents-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stored at Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s former institute}}}\uc2  from his time as vice-president, legal experts said.\par \par \uc2 The US justice department has clear criteria for prosecuting people who intentionally mishandle highly sensitive government documents, and the facts of the Trump documents case appear to satisfy more elements than in the Biden documents case.\par \par \uc2 Broadly, the Department of Justice has typically pursued prosecutions when cases have involved a combination of four factors: wilful mishandling of classified information, vast quantities of classified information to support an inference of misconduct, disloyalty to the United States and obstruction.\par \par \uc2 The criminal investigation into Trump touches on at least two of those elements \u8211\'20\'13 obstruction, where a person conceals documents with an intent to impede a government agency, and the volume of classified materials at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 unlike the Biden case, which appears to touch on none.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/trump-biden-classified-documents-serious-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In the case of the classified documents, it\u8217\'20\'19s more serious for Trump than Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While they may have momentum in the US House, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups continue to lose ground at the state level, with a special election in Virginia bringing the latest setback for their movement.\par \par \uc2 Last night, Democrat Aaron Rouse claimed victory in the race for a vacant seat in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s state Senate, which, if confirmed, would expand the party\u8217\'20\'19s margins in the chamber. It would also mean Republican governor Glenn Youngkin would not have the votes he needs to pass a proposed ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wusa9.com/article/news/local/virginia/governor-youngkin-abortion-ban-proposal-fires-up-opposing-virginia-democrats/65-a35be9f9-8cbe-4e36-8740-b87ac09df25c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he unveiled last month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have faired well at ballot boxes ever since the supreme court last year overturned Roe v Wade. In the November midterms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/abortion-midterm-elections-republicans-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters rejected new limits on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  or expanded access in every state where it was on the ballot}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier this morning in the Capitol, George Santos kept it to the point with a quick \u8220\'20\'1CI will not,\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if he would resign.\par \par \uc2 He was a bit more loquacious on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this afternoon:\par \par \uc2 enltrI was elected to serve the people of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY03?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY03}}}\uc2  not the party & politicians, I remain committed to doing that and regret to hear that local officials refuse to work with my office to deliver results to keep our community safe and lower the cost of living.\par \par \uc2 I will NOT resign!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Santos (@Santos4Congress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Santos4Congress/status/1613234542650982400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republican: party is 'tone deaf' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the introduction of two anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures in the newly Republican-controlled House, one House Republican said her party was \u8220\'20\'1Ctone deaf\u8221\'20\'1D on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace, of South Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/republican-house-will-vote-bills-curtail-abortion-immigration-rcna64944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC on Tuesday}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been tone deaf on this issue since the time that Roe was overturned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, was overturned by the ruling in Dobbs v Jackson which the conservative-dominated supreme court handed down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last June}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Extensive evidence, including Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 disappointing performance in the midterm elections in November, suggests the ruling was drastically out of step with public support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which runs around 60%}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe buried our heads in the sand,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t have any policy alternatives. We were not compassionate to both sides of the aisle on this argument.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mace also told NBC her party was \u8220\'20\'1Cpaying lip service to the pro-life movement\u8221\'20\'1D and said anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures introduced in this Congress were \u8220\'20\'1Cnever going to pass the Senate. It\u8217\'20\'19s never going to get to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk to be signed into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to make a difference and reduce the number of abortions with a Democrat-controlled Senate, the No1 issue we should be working on is access to birth control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some pertinent lunchtime reading from our columnist Jill Filipovic, as House Republicans seek to advance their agenda in the chamber they newly control\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The Republican party didn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly start 2023 hot out of the gate.\par \par \uc2 Despite a new House majority, the Republican members of Congress spent their first few days in office in an embarrassing protracted squabble over the speakership.\par \par \uc2 Representative Kevin McCarthy of California, who has spent the last few years assisting members of the extremist conspiracy-mongering Trumpian Republican radicals in their rise to power, found himself predictably on the receiving end of the extremist conspiracy-mongers, who wanted one of their own in charge as well as a series of rule changes. After largely capitulating to his party\u8217\'20\'19s lunatic fringe, McCarthy squeaked through on the 15th vote.\par \par \uc2 Now, he holds the gavel, but it\u8217\'20\'19s clear he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t hold his party\u8217\'20\'19s confidence, and that he\u8217\'20\'19s not a leader in any meaningful sense of the word. If he can\u8217\'20\'19t even get his troops lined up to vote for him, how is he going to get his clearly out-of-control party in line to support even tougher votes?\par \par \uc2 Which raises the question of what the party can reasonably accomplish in the House this term.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jan/11/republicans-congress-house-of-representatives-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Expect the Republican House to be just like the speaker debacle: pure chaos}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some good news for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.economist.com/president-joe-biden-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling by the Economist}}}\uc2  and \uc2 YouGov\uc2 , his approval rating is net positive, his best such rating since July 2021:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden's net job approval is now positive in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheEconomist?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheEconomist}}}\uc2  's polling with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YouGovAmerica?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @YouGovAmerica}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IVjBfI5OAY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IVjBfI5OAY}}}\par \par \uc2 - This includes a +2 reading (47% approve to 45% disapprove) in this week's poll\par \par \uc2 - 45% approve of his handling of the economy\par \par \uc2 - Biden's best numbers since July 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5ASvKye83h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5ASvKye83h}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 G. Elliott Morris (@gelliottmorris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gelliottmorris/status/1613191175531274242?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 More from the Economist and \uc2 YouGov\uc2 , under the title \u8220\'20\'1CWeekly Insight\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Two years on from the mob attack at the US Capitol on 6 January 2021, a new poll from the Economist and \uc2 YouGov\uc2  finds that most Americans still disapprove of the insurrectionists who stormed the building. The poll finds that 64% of adults disapprove of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Trump supporters taking over the Capitol building\u8221\'20\'1D on January 6, including 52% who say they \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D disapprove. Meanwhile 20% of adults \u8211\'20\'13 mostly respondents who also said they voted for Mr Trump in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 say they approve. By 45% to 37%, a plurality of adults believe Mr Trump urged his supporters to engage in violence that day.\par \par \uc2 So that\u8217\'20\'19s reassuring. Ish.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the House are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bec1338f08a62e1a2e22eb#block-63bec1338f08a62e1a2e22eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to pass two measures}}}\uc2  concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this afternoon, one a resolution condemning violence against opponents of the procedure, the other a bill meant to protect the life of babies who survive abortions. Democrats oppose both. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63beed698f085fda3e65ccd6#block-63beed698f085fda3e65ccd6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP officials in New York}}}\uc2  have called on George Santos to resign from Congress after he admitted to lying about his qualifications, but he says he\u8217\'20\'19s not going anywhere.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today thus far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Domestic flights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jan/11/us-flights-disrupted-after-faa-alert-system-outage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are resuming}}}\uc2  across the United States after all departures were briefly halted this morning by a systems failure at the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Republican investigator in the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bed7d28f085fda3e65cb97#block-63bed7d28f085fda3e65cb97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is demanding}}}\uc2  documents from the Treasury related to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and other members of the president\u8217\'20\'19s family. He also wants testimony from three former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives involved in the platform\u8217\'20\'19s temporary banning of the New York Post after it reported on the discovery of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s laptop.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jan/11/house-republicans-abortion-rights-committees-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-63bee9468f08a62e1a2e2538#block-63bee9468f08a62e1a2e2538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying their best}}}\uc2  to get voters riled up over gas cookstoves.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s newly elected congressman Anthony D\u8217\'20\'19Esposito becoming the first Republican lawmaker to call for George Santos\u8217\'20\'19s resignation:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Anthony D'Esposito (R-NY) becomes the first GOP member of Congress to call on Rep. George Santos (R-NY) to resign from the House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VArdpuwLor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VArdpuwLor}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1613221703911604228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Like \uc2 Santos\uc2 , D\u8217\'20\'19Esposito is a Republican who represents a Democratic-leaning suburban New York City district.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Joseph Cairo, chair of the Republican party in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Nassau county, calling for George Santos\u8217\'20\'19 resignation:\par \par \uc2 enltrNassau County Republican Chair Joseph Cairo calls for Rep. George Santos\u8217\'20\'19 (R-NY) \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate\u8221\'20\'1D resignation:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not welcome here at Republican headquarters \u8230\'20\'26 He\u8217\'20\'19s disgraced the House of Representatives, and we do not consider him one of our Congress people.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fgK4t1lzC0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fgK4t1lzC0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1613218867073126400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Santos\u8217\'20\'19s congressional district includes part of the county in suburban New York City, and his victory in last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election flipped it from Democratic to Republican representation.\par \par \uc2 ABC News caught up with Santos at the Capitol, who said he has no plans to step down:\par \par \uc2 enltr??Rep. George Santos tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelvscott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rachelvscott}}}\uc2  and me he will NOT resign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vBMvotq3Y0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vBMvotq3Y0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lalee Ibssa (@LaleeIbssa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaleeIbssa/status/1613218633341145094?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no shortage of business on the House\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, but several Republicans are doing all they can to make the gas cookstove kerfuffle last.\par \par \uc2 Consider this, from Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s Mark Alford :\par \par \uc2 qmeltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ePzSGT9woQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ePzSGT9woQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Alford ???????????????????? (@markalfordkc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/markalfordkc/status/1613008003510460417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2 , the former White House doctor to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is promoting a website\u8230\'20\'26:\par \par \uc2 enltrIf gas stoves were really a health hazard, would \u8220\'20\'1Cdoctor\u8221\'20\'1D Jill Biden be using one?? I think not. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2DQMkP2ZIy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2DQMkP2ZIy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QSH3A72Ifj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QSH3A72Ifj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2  (@RonnyJacksonTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonnyJacksonTX/status/1613181014372921345?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 ... and employing the all-caps approach:\par \par \uc2 enltr187 MILLION Americans have gas stoves in their homes, and it will cost a FORTUNE to replace them. There's no "science" behind this. It's just another excuse Biden is trying to use to put MORE GOVERNMENT in your lives. HANDS OFF OUR STOVES!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2DQMkP2ZIy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2DQMkP2ZIy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xPxM5KwbKa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xPxM5KwbKa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2  (@RonnyJacksonTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonnyJacksonTX/status/1613200620223332358?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Venture to certain corners of conservative media today and you\u8217\'20\'19ll find lots of discussion of gas stoves. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alaina-demopoulos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaina Demopoulos}}}\uc2  explains why:\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration announced it was considering regulating \u8211\'20\'13 or banning \u8211\'20\'13 gas stoves, Richard Trumka of the US consumer product safety commission (\uc2 CPSC\uc2 ) offered some words of clarity: \u8220\'20\'1CTo be clear, \uc2 CPSC\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t coming for anyone\u8217\'20\'19s gas stoves,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumkaCPSC/status/1612553459462721536?s=20&t=VXGFfTjhDWU8YoMLL6FgpA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou will have to pry my gas stove from my cold dead hands,\u8221\'20\'1D replied Matt Walsh, the rightwing political podcaster and Daily Wire columnist.\par \par \uc2 Despite Trumka\u8217\'20\'19s words of assurance, and the fact that no regulation or ban has been put in place or announced as a course of action, conservative figures are trying to turn gas stoves into the next culture war.\par \par \uc2 Gas stoves have become a hot-button issue in the first weeks of 2022, as new research reveals that the appliances emit toxic chemicals and carcinogens, even while turned off. The report found that 12.7% of cases of childhood asthma in the US are due to the presence of gas stoves.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/republicans-culture-war-gas-stoves-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans turn up the heat on a new culture war target: gas stoves}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York Republicans to call for Santos resignation\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Nassau county will later today call on George Santos to resign after he admitted to lying about his qualifications in his campaign for Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/01/11/local-n-y-gop-leaders-to-call-on-george-santos-to-resign-00077450"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement will be made by the county\u8217\'20\'19s GOP chair Joe Cairo along with other party officials. According to Politico, it is intended to mitigate the damage Santos did to the party\u8217\'20\'19s standing in New York\u8217\'20\'19s third congressional district, which leans Democratic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Facts First USA, a group recently set up by Democrats to counter the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s investigations against the Biden administration, has hit back on House oversight committee chair James Comer\u8217\'20\'19s request for documents related to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CComer\u8217\'20\'19s latest letter is yet another rehashed conspiracy theory about a Biden family member that has already been thoroughly debunked by fact checkers,\u8221\'20\'1D Facts First USA president David Brock said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe interesting news here is that if Comer continues to move forward with this tinfoil hat hearing it is really bad news for the people in his Congressional district, where, \u8216\'20\'18over 62,000 reports were filed between 2014 and 2022, averaging one filing for every 12 people in the district,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said, citing reporting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americanindependent.com/james-comer-biden-family-suspicious-banking-false-claim/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the American Independent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House GOP requests \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  documents, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  execs testimony\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are making good on their promises to investigate the Biden administration and other perceived opponents, with the oversight committee chair James Comer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/release/comer-announces-new-actions-in-biden-family-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today requesting}}}\uc2  the Treasury turn over documents related to the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , as well as calling for testimony from three former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives.\par \par \uc2 Comer sent Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/2023-01-11-Treasury.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  requesting \u8220\'20\'1Csuspicious activity reports\u8221\'20\'1D related to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and other members of the president\u8217\'20\'19s family, and their businesses. Suspicious activity reports are submitted to Treasury by banks that suspect a customer may be engaged in unlawful or dangerous business.\par \par \uc2 He is also calling former executives \uc2 Vijaya Gadde\uc2 , James Baker, and \uc2 Yoel Roth\uc2  to testify on the week of 6 February before the committee about \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision in 2020 to briefly ban the New York Post\u8217\'20\'19s account after it published reporting about a laptop belonging to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the past two years, the Biden Administration and Big Tech worked overtime to hide information about the Biden family\u8217\'20\'19s suspicious business schemes and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s involvement. Now that Democrats no longer have one-party rule in Washington, oversight and accountability are coming,\u8221\'20\'1D Comer said in announcing the requests.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 George Santos, the Republican congressman who admitted to lying about his qualifications, will not be serving on any major committees, House speaker Kevin McCarthy told CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D Speaker McCarthy told me when asked whether he expects Rep. George Santos to serve on any of the key committees that are being populated today\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1613191545678708737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans are today appointing members to some of the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s most influential committees: appropriations, ways and means, financial services and energy and commerce. Santos may be banned from those panels, but the House Republican leadership hasn\u8217\'20\'19t announced any other sanctions against him, though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/george-santos-democrats-goldman-torres-hand-deliver-ethics-complaint"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19s in plenty of hot water nonetheless}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic chair of the Senate commerce committee \uc2 Maria Cantwell\uc2  has pledged to investigate the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s computer outage today that caused flights to be briefly grounded nationwide:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe number one priority is safety. As the Committee prepares for \uc2 FAA\uc2  reauthorization legislation, we will be looking into what caused this outage and how redundancy plays a role in preventing future outages. The public needs a resilient air transportation system.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 Maria Cantwell\uc2  (@SenatorCantwell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorCantwell/status/1613180843626725378?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Texas, some cities are moving to become havens for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a state where the procedure is otherwise banned, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Campaigners in San Antonio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , on Tuesday delivered more than 38,000 signatures to the city clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office, petitioning for a May vote that would decriminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the city.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas has been banned since August 2022, following the supreme court decision to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last summer.\par \par \uc2 The campaigners hope to pass what they are calling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://act4sa.org/tuesday-san-antonio-justice-charter-coalition-submits-35000-signatures-for-may-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Antonio Justice Charter}}}\uc2  , which would also end criminalization for low-level marijuana possession, and put limits on police use of no-knock warrants and chokeholds.\par \par \uc2 San Antonio, Austin and Waco \u8211\'20\'13 all in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 already passed resolutions to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/democratic-cities-texas-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 de-prioritize the investigation of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  crimes}}}\uc2  through their city councils in 2022, at the same time as a string of progressive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/14/progressive-prosecutors-refuse-abortion-bans-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 district attorneys across the country}}}\uc2  vowed to resist state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that came into effect when the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended in June.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/texas-abortion-san-antonio-ballot-measure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Antonio campaigners bid for ballot measure to buck Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Alabama, the state\u8217\'20\'19s top prosecutor has reacted to the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/04/abortion-pills-fda-rule-change-pharmacies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expansion of access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  by warning that women who take the medication could be prosecuted under a law meant to protect children from methamphetamine fumes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPromoting the remote prescription and administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills endangers both women and unborn children,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican attorney general \uc2 Steve Marshall{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2023/01/women-can-be-prosecuted-for-taking-abortion-pills-says-alabama-attorney-general.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement to Al.com}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CElective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills \u8211\'20\'13 is illegal in Alabama. Nothing about the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s guidance changes that. Anyone who remotely prescribes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in Alabama does so at their own peril: I will vigorously enforce Alabama law to protect unborn life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s governor in 2019 signed the Human Life Protection Act, which bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except to protect the life of the mother. It only went into effect last year, when the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. But the law allows for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to be punished, not recipients, which is why Marshall is threatening to use the state\u8217\'20\'19s chemical endangerment law against women who end their pregnancies medically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Human Life Protection Act targets \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, exempting women \u8216\'20\'18upon whom an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is performed or attempted to be performed\u8217\'20\'19 from liability under the law,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marshall, who has also threatened to prosecute veterans affair doctors who perform abortions in cases of incest or rape. \u8220\'20\'1CIt does not provide an across-the-board exemption from all criminal laws, including the chemical-endangerment law \u8211\'20\'13 which the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  has affirmed and reaffirmed protects unborn children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The first days of a new Congress are typically when the party in charge lays out its priority, and today, it\u8217\'20\'19s the turn of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes.\par \par \uc2 The two measures the Republican-led House will consider don\u8217\'20\'19t amount to the sort of draconian laws some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes would like to see passed, and supporters of the procedure fear. They are not, for instance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the nationwide \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  proposed last year.\par \par \uc2 Rather, they target more niche aspects and consequences of the procedure. One is a resolution condemning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/11/pro-choice-militants-pregnancy-crisis-centers-attacks-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks on churches, groups and facilities that work against \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The other is the Born-Alive \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Survivors Protection Act, which is intended to protect the rights of babies born after surviving an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocate argue their rights are already secured by a 2002 law, and just last November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/11/10/1134833151/montana-midterms-results-born-alive-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters in Montana rejected}}}\uc2  a similar measure that was on their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are telling their members to vote against both measures.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes have their moment as House GOP gets to work\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. House Republicans will today introduce two measures concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one being a bill that \u8220\'20\'1Csecures medical protections for babies that survive an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, and the other a resolution condemning \u8220\'20\'1Cattacks on pro-life facilities, groups, and churches\u8221\'20\'1D. That the party opposes the procedure is no surprise, but they still have to tread carefully. After all, it was outrage to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last year allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely that led to the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s underperformance in the midterms. The House will convene at 12pm eastern time, with votes on these two bills expected at 4pm.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 All domestic flight departures are paused until 9am eastern time due to a system failure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.faa.gov/newsroom/faa-notams-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Federal Aviation Administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters at 2pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House panel charged with determining which lawmakers sit on committees will meet at 10am today to continue filling out the ranks of key bodies, such as financial services, energy and commerce, ways and means and appropriations.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230112ej1c001br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
