\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Friend of Satan: how Lucien Greaves and his Satanic Temple are fighting the religious right\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 2,301 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2023\par 09:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 They have protested against a homophobic church and opposed prayer in classrooms. Now this minority religion is defending the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 A statue of Baphomet \u8211\'20\'13 a pagan idol used in popular culture as a representation of the devil, with the head, horns and feet of a goat, the torso of a man and the wings of an angel \u8211\'20\'13 is the centrepiece of the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Salem, Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 More than 8ft (2.4 metres) tall, jet black and altogether unnerving, Baphomet serves as a reminder of what brought the Satanic Temple to fame. In 2013, the group, which is acknowledged as a religion by the \uc2 US government\uc2 , responded to the installation of a Ten Commandments monument on the grounds of the Oklahoma state capitol building \u8211\'20\'13 seemingly a flagrant abuse of the US constitution\u8217\'20\'19s separation of church and state \u8211\'20\'13 by demanding that its own Baphomet statue also be positioned in the grounds. According to the first amendment, which protects freedom of religion, public spaces should be open to all religions or none, it argued.\par \par \uc2 It turned out that Republican politicians did not want a big statue of a goat-headed pagan deity on capitol grounds. Amid lawsuits, the Oklahoma supreme court eventually ordered that the Ten Commandments monument should be removed.\par \par \uc2 The tactic, with its wry and anarchic undertones, is typical of the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s battle against the religious right in the US. In the decade since the spat over the statue, the Temple has tackled prayer in classrooms, religious holiday displays and the distribution of Bibles in schools.\par \par \uc2 Now, it is taking on another fundamental issue: the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court#:~:text=US%20supreme%20court%20overturns%20abortion%20rights%2C%20upending%20Roe%20v%20Wade,-This%20article%20is&text=The%20supreme%20court%20has%20ruled,fracture%20reproductive%20rights%20in%20America."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last June opened the door for more than half of US states to effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or restrict access to it, horrifying supporters of reproductive rights. The Satanic Temple \u8211\'20\'13 and many other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/22/opinion/abortion-religion-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observers}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 believe the decision of the supreme court was made on the basis of religion: specifically the extreme form of Christianity that has come to dominate Republican politics in the US.\par \par \uc2 The Temple has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thesatanictemple.com/blogs/the-satanic-temple-tenets/there-are-seven-fundamental-tenets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cseven fundamental tenets\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , one of which states: \u8220\'20\'1COne\u8217\'20\'19s body is inviolable, subject to one\u8217\'20\'19s own will alone.\u8221\'20\'1D This, it believes, offers a way around these draconian new laws. It is arguing that its members are exempt from bans or restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to their right to a \u8220\'20\'1CSatanic Temple religious \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ritual\u8221\'20\'1D, more of which later. With lawsuits already filed in Indiana, Idaho, Texas and Missouri, the Satanic Temple is about to find out whether US courts agree.\par \par \uc2 Legal battles are long-running, expensive and frustrating for people desperate for immediate change. But Lucien Greaves, who co-founded the Satanic Temple in 2012, points to the success the Republican party has had in overturning Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 a decision brought before the court through decades of lobbying and legislating.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI get messages from people denigrating us for taking legal action to assert our rights, saying: \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t change the system from within the system,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I keep asking them: \u8216\'20\'18What the fuck do you think you just saw happen? That\u8217\'20\'19s what they just did.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tall, slim, pale and dressed in black, Greaves is a fitting frontman for a group that is regularly demonised by its Christian opponents. A leather strap wrapped around his wrist, his thin blond ponytail tied up with black bands, he could be in one of the heavy metal bands that terrified neurotic parents in the 1980s and 90s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to play the long game,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says. \u8220\'20\'1CThey spent generations doing this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Satanists don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in Satan in a literal, demonic sense, Greaves explains, but rather as a symbol of rebellion and opposition to authoritarianism. According to the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s website: \u8220\'20\'1CTo embrace the name Satan is to embrace rational inquiry removed from supernaturalism and archaic tradition-based superstitions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Satanic Temple held its first public activity in January 2013, and a decade on it has more than 700,000 members, with congregations in 24 states and six countries, including the UK, Germany and Finland.\par \par \uc2 The organisation is recognised by the \uc2 US Internal Revenue Service\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cchurch or a convention or association of churches\u8221\'20\'1D and, as such, it is able to highlight, and attempt to tackle, the disparity in how Christianity is treated compared with other religious groups in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we have a minority religious theocratic movement, so entrenched in politics and getting away with whatever they want,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says. \u8220\'20\'1CNow they\u8217\'20\'19ve got the courts on their side and everything \u8211\'20\'13 and they don\u8217\'20\'19t need to bend to the will of the majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He is speaking to the Guardian at the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters, a three-storey former funeral parlour ringed by neatly trimmed lawns and topiary. The building is not hard to spot. In a residential area where most of the traditional, clapboard homes are cream or white, it is painted black.\par \par \uc2 The interior matches the gothic exterior. The walls are covered with dark, velvety wallpaper, and daylight is shut out by floor-length crimson curtains. Baphomet lurks in one room, ready to be summoned once more. A gift shop sells \u8220\'20\'1CFriend of Satan\u8221\'20\'1D mugs, \u8220\'20\'1CHail Satan\u8221\'20\'1D T-shirts, and \u8220\'20\'1CSatanic Temple official hot sauce\u8221\'20\'1D, which comes in four flavours and costs $12 (\u163\'00\'A310) a bottle. Upstairs, a chandelier-lit throne room features grand mahogany chairs flanked by Norse helmets. The space is also available as a wedding venue, and newlyweds can spend the night in a vampiric-looking bedroom suite.\par \par \uc2 Greaves, who uses a pseudonym as a result of threats, somewhat reluctantly became the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson in 2013, the year after it was founded. The organisation quickly became known for its anarchic activities. That same year, it praised the governor of Florida for having signed a bill allowing students to lead prayer at school assemblies. The decision, the Temple said, was exciting \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause now our Satanic children could pray to Satan in school\u8221\'20\'1D. Faced with the threat of litigation from civil rights organisations, it is unclear if any school districts ever took up the student-led prayer option.\par \par \uc2 That same year, the group held a mocking \u8220\'20\'1Cpink mass\u8221\'20\'1D to protest against the notoriously homophobic Westboro Baptist Church, and specifically its founder, Fred Phelps. The mass featured two men kissing over the grave of Phelps\u8217\'20\'19 mother.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, in response to hundreds of schools hosting after-class Bible study groups (mostly promoted by the Good News Club, a weekly Christian programme for children), the group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/nation/la-na-satanic-after-school-20160928-snap-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it would offer its own after-school Satan clubs. The clubs, which are \u8220\'20\'1Cdesigned to promote intellectual and emotional development\u8221\'20\'1D, are still around: last year there was much purse-clutching when a school in Ohio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://local12.com/news/local/satan-after-school-club-inspired-by-satan-to-start-at-local-elementary-school-cincinnati-lebanon-donovan-ohio-kentucky-indiana-local-12-wkrc-tristate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave the go-ahead}}}\uc2  for an After School Satan club.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, though, the Temple has moved beyond physical stunts, and into the courtroom, spending hundreds of thousands of dollars on legal efforts to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, ensure the right to free speech and protect children from abuse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s getting really frustrating now with the overturn of Roe v Wade, when people are still treating us not like we\u8217\'20\'19re a minority religion \u8211\'20\'13 which we are \u8211\'20\'13 but more like, we\u8217\'20\'19re just this kind of clever tactic that may or may not work,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat gets to be really tedious, because I think people aren\u8217\'20\'19t terribly invested in the outcomes of the Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits. And it shows that they don\u8217\'20\'19t understand that the outcomes of what the Satanic Temple is doing have ramifications for everybody: all minority religious organisations, all different types of viewpoint positions that might be outside the Christian nationalist perspective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In recent years, Republicans have ushered in a wave of discriminatory, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/15/christian-nationalist-religious-right-legislation-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-Christian legislation}}}\uc2  in states across the country. Conservatives have targeted LGBTQ+ people, in particular, with efforts to prevent transgender people using certain bathrooms, and to prevent LGBTQ+ couples from adopting children. Many of these bills are lifted from model legislation drafted by Christian lobbying organisations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jun/04/project-blitz-the-legislative-assault-by-christian-nationalists-to-reshape-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under an effort known as \u8220\'20\'1CProject Blitz\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is this religious crusade that ultimately resulted in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 6-3 conservative majority overturning Roe v Wade, with its Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization ruling, which held that the constitution of the United States does not confer a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That is where the Satanic Temple is hoping to find some leeway. It has insisted that its members do have a religious right to receive abortions, as part of its \u8220\'20\'1CSatanic \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ritual\u8221\'20\'1D. The Temple\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thesatanictemple.com/pages/about-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental tenet\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cone\u8217\'20\'19s body is inviolable, subject to one\u8217\'20\'19s own will alone\u8221\'20\'1D is a position that contradicts people being denied the right to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 During {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0428/0465/files/Abortion_Ritual_Procedure_061322.pdf?v=1657724339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ritual}}}\uc2 , the person having the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks at their reflection, before taking deep breaths and reciting two of the seven tenets. Once the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is complete, the person must recite the \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal affirmation\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CBy my body, my blood, by my will, it is done.\u8221\'20\'1D The ritual is conceived to serve an \u8220\'20\'1Caffirmative function of assuring membership that their decision is their own\u8221\'20\'1D, the group says, while also offering a kind of counselling effect.\par \par \uc2 Once someone determines they want to undergo the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ritual, the Satanic Temple believes that the state has no right to intervene in what is essentially a religious practice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStates are passing laws premised on this idea that foetal tissue has personhood, or is a unique and distinct human life. We don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with that position. We believe it\u8217\'20\'19s a religious position, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t believe states have any right to put any impositions on us,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Opinion polls}}}\uc2 , and results such as last August\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas }}}\uc2  ballot \u8211\'20\'13 in which a majority voted in favour of keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in the state \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  that most Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, and the Roe v Wade decision sparked protests across the country. This might have buoyed those involved, but Greaves \u8211\'20\'13 speaking in a personal capacity, rather than on behalf of the Satanic Temple \u8211\'20\'13 thinks it is unlikely to change the opinions of rightwing politicians and courts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not going to wave signs now and shame the Republicans into acting rationally,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 The documentary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.hailsatanfilm.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hail Satan?}}}\uc2 , released in 2019, helped increase the Temple\u8217\'20\'19s popularity and membership, but exposure has also brought problems.\par \par \uc2 In June, the Satanic Temple headquarters was subject to an arson attack. A man wearing a T-shirt that read \u8220\'20\'1CGod\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.masslive.com/police-fire/2022/06/satanic-temple-fire-daniel-lucey-who-police-said-acknowledged-that-setting-temple-on-fire-was-a-hate-crime-pleads-not-guilty.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked up to the front porch}}}\uc2 , poured an unknown accelerant over it, then set it on fire. The Satanic Temple\u8217\'20\'19s door cam recorded the whole thing. A man was arrested the same night, and has been charged with arson, destruction of a place of worship and civil rights violation charges. If he was genuinely trying to burn down the building, it was a lamentable effort, but the incident was a reminder of the risks the Satanic Temple faces. As the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s visible figurehead, Greaves is particularly \u8211\'20\'13 and literally \u8211\'20\'13 in the line of fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI honestly felt like I was committing suicide at the point where I was being the public face of satanism, because I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen people\u8217\'20\'19s lives totally ruined on accusations of satanism,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Greaves recently came to the attention of the Sovereign Citizens, a loose group of Americans who do not believe they are under the jurisdiction of the federal government, and are not subject to US law. According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/extremist-files/ideology/sovereign-citizens-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center}}}\uc2 , the movement is \u8220\'20\'1Crooted in racism and antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csome sovereign citizens have turned to violence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In late 2021, Greaves received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUnXhj20gbs&t=905s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a message}}}\uc2  from the group that informed him he was to be deported from the US.\par \par \uc2 After finding a Zoom link for a Sovereign Citizens assembly meeting, Greaves gatecrashed it, and managed to derail the meeting almost immediately by taking on a chairman role and calling it to order. \u8220\'20\'1CI suppose you\u8217\'20\'19re all wondering why I gathered you here today,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves said, before being told to \u8220\'20\'1CShut your damn mouth,\u8221\'20\'1D by a Sovereign Citizen.\par \par \uc2 Greaves was eventually ejected from the meeting, which bore all the professionalism of a parish council get-together. Soon after, he says, a $100,000 bounty was placed on his head. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americanheraldnews.com/?p=8670"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A notice on the American Herald news site}}}\uc2  stated Greaves was wanted \u8220\'20\'1Cdead or alive\u8221\'20\'1D, and called him \u8220\'20\'1Ca domestic and international terrorist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 People who post death threats in plain sight could seem like harmless cranks, but Greaves points out that plenty of violence has been committed in the name of quackery: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to distinguish what is more and less serious unless somebody actually comes in and does something.\u8221\'20\'1D If a person does attack him, Greaves says: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be someone this dumb.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He is forced to take precautions nowadays. Last year he moved \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cvery secretly\u8221\'20\'1D, he says \u8211\'20\'13 and he tries to keep personal details as personal as possible. But he and his fellow satanists are undeterred. The Satanic Temple will keep chipping away at the inroads the Christian right have made. This religion, one of the most curious churches in a country full of them, is in it for the long haul.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot of work to do to bring shit back to a reasonable level. And we\u8217\'20\'19re not close to that right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Greaves says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to take many years to undo the damage that has been done. But that\u8217\'20\'19s the opposite of an excuse to give up. There\u8217\'20\'19s no excuse to not be engaged right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230105ej1500001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
