\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Plan B morning-after contraceptive is not  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill, US to specify\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 485 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulators to change packaging labels to make clear pill will not work if person is already pregnant\par \par \uc2 The US food and drug administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) has announced it will change packaging labels for the emergency contraceptive Plan B to specify that it is not an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 According to many anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, any form of disruption to an egg is considered an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said on Friday it would remove all references on packaging that claims the pill might prevent a fertilized egg implanting in the womb.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlan B One-Step will not work if a person is already pregnant, meaning it will not affect an existing pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/plan-b-one-step-15-mg-levonorgestrel-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CPlan B One-Step prevents pregnancy by acting on ovulation, which occurs well before implantation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvidence does not support that the drug affects implantation or maintenance of a pregnancy after implantation, therefore it does not terminate a pregnancy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The over-the-counter drug can be used after sex to prevent pregnancy. According to \uc2 FDA\uc2  recommendations, Plan B should be taken as soon as possible within 72 hours of unprotected sex or contraceptive failure.\par \par \uc2 The medication, which comes in the form of one tablet, contains a higher dose of the synthetic hormone levonorgestrel than birth control pills and works in a similar way by stopping or delaying the release of an egg from the ovary.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  update on Friday, the agency is making the label changes at the request of the manufacturer of Plan B and after \u8220\'20\'1Ccareful consideration of \u8230\'20\'26 additional scientific evidence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 FDA\uc2  determined the current science supports a conclusion that Plan B One-Step works by inhibiting or delaying ovulation and the mid-cycle hormonal changes,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence also supports the conclusion that there is no direct effect on fertilization or implantation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a 2021 survey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/wr/mm7004a7.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2 , 24.3% of women aged 22 to 49 indicated they had used emergency contraception.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the supreme court decision to overturn Roe v Wade earlier this year, thereby removing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , numerous pharmacies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jun/28/emergency-contraception-pills-pharmacies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  set limits on the number of emergency contraception pills consumers could buy.\par \par \uc2 Access to the emergency contraceptive remains severely limited in several conservative states.\par \par \uc2 Despite the Republican governor of Texas, Greg Abbott, saying rape victims can take Plan B, the pill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/09/03/emergency-contraception-access-rape-victim-abbott/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  remains unavailable for some of the poorest Texans, especially as it can sell for up to $50 (\u163\'00\'A341).\par \par \uc2 In Idaho, public universities have warned employees against guiding students on how to obtain emergency contraception, as they could be charged with a felony.\par \par \uc2 Under the state No Public Funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act, university staffers and school-based health clinics are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-legislature-idaho-birth-control-bd238c572da10d812ef5ba93f1860fc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prohibited}}}\uc2  from dispensing or telling students where to get emergency contraception, except in instances of rape.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14001m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
