\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DeSantis appoints judge who denied  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to girl over school grades\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jared Smith, who issued controversial ruling in January, named to new court of appeal by Florida governor\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has appointed a judge who was previously ousted over a controversial ruling where he denied a teenager an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , citing her school grades.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://flgov.com/2022/12/20/governor-ron-desantis-makes-three-judicial-appointments-6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed}}}\uc2  Jared Smith to the newly established sixth district court of appeal, an appointment which will begin on 1 January 2023. Smith previously served as a judge on the Hillsborough county court until he was ousted in August after his decision on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related case.\par \par \uc2 In January, Smith had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.2dca.org/content/download/823307/opinion/220051_DC13_01182022_130002_i.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that a 17-year-old teenager was unfit to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as he questioned her \u8220\'20\'1Coverall intelligence\u8221\'20\'1D. According to Florida law, both parental notification and consent is required in order for a minor to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the teenager\u8217\'20\'19s case, she had asked the court to waive the requirement.\par \par \uc2 Under Florida\u8217\'20\'19s law, the requirement can be waived if the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0300-0399/0390/Sections/0390.01114.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finds}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cby clear and convincing evidence, that the minor is sufficiently mature to decide whether to terminate her pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 However, in Smith\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, he cited the teenager\u8217\'20\'19s grades as a factor in his decision that denied her the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAddressing her \u8216\'20\'18overall intelligence\u8217\'20\'19 \u8230\'20\'26 the court found her intelligence to be less than average because \u8216\'20\'18[w]hile she claimed that her grades were \u8216\'20\'18Bs\u8217\'20\'19 during her testimony, her GPA is currently 2.0. Clearly, a \u8216\'20\'18B\u8217\'20\'19 average would not equate to a 2.0 GPA,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his ruling.\par \par \uc2 Smith also went on to question the teenager\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cemotional development and stability, and ability to accept responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis court has long recognized that the trial court\u8217\'20\'19s findings \u8230\'20\'26 may support a determination that the minor did not prove that she was sufficiently mature to decide whether to terminate her pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 An appeals court eventually overturned the ruling. In August, Smith lost his re-election bid against Nancy Jacobs, a Tampa criminal defense and family law attorney. According to the Hill, Jacobs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/3615274-judge-who-denied-florida-teen-an-abortion-citing-grades-loses-reelection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  approximately 51.9% of the votes, surpassing Smith by about 3.7 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is a rising star in the Republican party, especially after his strong performance in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, which was in stark contrast to the Republican party showing overall. He has emerged as a powerful rival to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and is widely expected to challenge the former US president in the Republican 2024 presidential nomination race.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s appointment of Smith comes a week after the Florida supreme court tossed out challenges to the eligibility of six appeals court candidates, including Smith. The challenges argued that the candidates live outside the jurisdiction of the fifth and six district court of appeals, the Tampa Bay Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2022/12/15/florida-supreme-court-rejects-challenges-beltran-other-judicial-candidates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled that the residency requirement would only apply once the judges are appointed, not during the nomination process of the candidates.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej140019k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
