\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The year in patriarchy: a dancing PM, an \u8216\'20\'18inclusive\u8217\'20\'19 M&M, and lots of protests\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,249 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 2022 saw a stunning reverse on reproductive rights in the US but there were also victories for women \u8211\'20\'13 and the plain bizarre\par \par \uc2 The year in patriarchy 2022\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s start on a positive note, eh? Because there were a few victories. 2022 was a crummy year in many respects for women but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t all bad. In terms of reproductive rights, for example, Colombia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/02/colombia-decriminalization-abortion-triumph-human-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decriminalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and India\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court extended access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indias-top-court-gives-all-women-right-abortion-2022-09-29/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to unmarried women}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A lot of women also became heads of states which would have been a great thing had those women not had very regressive politics. In Hungary, Katalin Nov\u225\'00\'E1k, a close ally of the truly terrible prime minister, \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/10/orban-loyalist-katalin-novak-elected-hungary-first-female-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 country\u8217\'20\'19s first female president}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 not so much feminist pioneer as fascist puppet. Meanwhile, in Italy, far-right Giorgia Meloni was sworn in as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/22/far-right-leader-giorgia-meloni-sworn-in-as-italys-prime-minister"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 country\u8217\'20\'19s first female prime minister}}}\uc2 . In terms of somewhat more positive \u8220\'20\'1Cfirsts\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ketanji-brown-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2  became the first black woman to sit on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the good and the bad there was a lot of inanity. Wife guys {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/01/ned-fulmer-try-guys-wife-guys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were declared}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cover\u8221\'20\'1D after a major wife guy scandal; Elon Musk (definitely not a wife guy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jul/06/elon-musk-twins-children-shivon-zilis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impregnated}}}\uc2  half the world; Pete Davidson kept up his reputation as the most eligible man in the heterosexual universe.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a long year. To help you look back, I\u8217\'20\'19ve put together 12 memorable moments from the year in patriarchy.\par \par \uc2 1 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In June six unelected supreme court justices issued a decision that ended nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/25/abortion-war-against-women-in-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50 years of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in the US.}}}\uc2  Numerous Republican-led states had been preparing for Roe v Wade to be overturned with trigger laws immediately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/the-guardian-view-on-overturning-roe-v-wade-anti-abortionists-reign-supreme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions}}}\uc2  in these states. Horror stories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/us-abortion-bans-states-after-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quickly followed}}}\uc2 . One of the worst: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/16/rightwing-rape-abortion-10-year-old-worse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year-old rape victim}}}\uc2  had to travel to a different state to get a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . First, the right denied the story and then the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/indiana-investigates-abortion-doctor-10-year-old-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana state attorney general}}}\uc2  investigated the doctor who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the little girl. Among all the horror, however, there was some hope. Kansas put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to a vote and people in the conservative state overwhelmingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . A few months later voters came out to support reproductive rights in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/nov/09/abortion-rights-american-voters-democrats-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections}}}\uc2 . The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it became clear, do not match the average American\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 2 Finland\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister was made to apologize for dancing\par \par \uc2 Sanna Marin\uc2  was also forced to take a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/19/finlands-pm-sanna-marin-takes-drug-test-after-videos-show-her-drinking-and-dancing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drug test}}}\uc2  (she passed) by a bunch of people who were outraged that a young woman was having fun. As we all know the world\u8217\'20\'19s male leaders are a pious lot who are completely scandal-free.\par \par \uc2 3 The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  drastically restricted women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in Afghanistan\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s rights were a major justification for the US war in Afghanistan. It was pretty obvious that was all spin at the time but it\u8217\'20\'19s still maddening to see how women in Afghanistan have been abandoned by their supposed saviours. What on earth were those two decades of war for? The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  spent 2022 doing their best to erase women from public life and keep them captive in their homes. Afghan women have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/20/taliban-ban-afghan-women-university-education"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned from higher education}}}\uc2  and most teenage girls have been banned from secondary school education.\par \par \uc2 4 Andrew Tate was publicly humiliated by Greta Thunberg\par \par \uc2 Dubbed the \u8220\'20\'1Cking of toxic masculinity\u8221\'20\'1D, Tate is a violent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/aug/06/andrew-tate-violent-misogynistic-world-of-tiktok-new-star"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misogynist with millions of followers}}}\uc2 . The kickboxer turned influencer\u8217\'20\'19s TikTok videos have been watched billions of times and he has reportedly helped to radicalize a lot of young, resentful men. Just as 2022 was about to end, Tate, 35, was catapulted to new heights of fame when he tried to troll Thunberg, 19, about his enormous emissions. She very succinctly put him in his place. The Romanian police then added to his humiliation by raiding Tate\u8217\'20\'19s villa in Romania and detaining him on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/30/andrew-tate-detained-in-romania-on-organised-and-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organised crime and rape charges}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 5 The green M&M character swapped her heels for sensible shoes\par \par \uc2 This was to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jan/26/mms-have-had-a-progressive-makeover-could-this-be-feminisms-sweetest-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promote \u8220\'20\'1Cinclusivity\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  or something like that. Rightwing commentators lost their minds, as they always do, while the rest of us said \u8220\'20\'1Cerm \u8230\'20\'26 what? Did we really ask for this?\u8221\'20\'1D Still it represented a small win for fem&minism. (Yes I\u8217\'20\'19ve made that joke before, but in honour of Greta Thunberg I\u8217\'20\'19m doing some recycling.)\par \par \uc2 6 Russians were accused of using rape as a \u8216\'20\'18military strategy\u8217\'20\'19 in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 As war correspondent Christina Lamb has written, rape is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/15/rape-weapon-ukraine-war-crime-sexual-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the cheapest weapon known to man}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Sexual assault has long been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/03/all-wars-are-like-this-used-as-a-weapon-of-war-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a weapon of war}}}\uc2  and the invasion of Ukraine is, tragically, no exception. In June Ukraine held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/23/ukraine-to-begin-first-trial-of-russian-soldier-charged-with-rape-mikhail-romanov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preliminary hearing}}}\uc2  in its first trial of a Russian soldier charged with rape, the first of what will presumably be many cases.\par \par \uc2 7 There were historic women-led protests across Iran\par \par \uc2 There have been widespread protests across Iran since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2022/oct/31/mapping-irans-unrest-how-mahsa-aminis-death-led-to-nationwide-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death in custody of Mahsa Amini back in September}}}\uc2 . The protests were met with violence and death sentences: at least 100 Iranians arrested during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/28/dozens-of-iran-protesters-facing-charges-punishable-by-death-rights-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests face charges punishable by death}}}\uc2 . Iran has now been booted off the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/14/iran-likely-to-be-ousted-from-un-womens-body-bloody-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN commission on the status of women}}}\uc2  for obvious reasons.\par \par \uc2 8 Prince Andrew settled a \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 -related sexual assault case in the US\par \par \uc2 But let\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/feb/15/prince-andrew-and-virginia-giuffre-reach-settlement-in-principle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not talk about that, eh?}}}\uc2  The fact that the Duke of York paid off a woman who accused him of sexual assault isn\u8217\'20\'19t the real scandal here. The fact that one of the most senior members of the royal family was palling around with Epstein isn\u8217\'20\'19t the real scandal here. The real scandal, as we well know, is Meghan Markle\u8217\'20\'19s very existence!\par \par \uc2 9 Shireen Abu Akleh was killed and nobody has faced any consequences for it\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/17/shireen-abu-aqleh-was-a-lifeline-for-palestinians-and-her-killing-has-shaken-us-to-the-core"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iconic}}}\uc2  Palestinian-American journalist was killed by what the \uc2 UN\uc2  described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cseemingly well-aimed\u8221\'20\'1D bullet fired by Israeli forces in May. The Biden administration announced there would be an \u8220\'20\'1Cinquiry\u8221\'20\'1D into the matter but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/04/shireen-abu-akleh-documentary-faultlines-israel-biden-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 absolutely nothing has happened}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 10 The world was glued to the Johnny Depp-Amber Heard defamation trial\par \par \uc2 The televised trial was described as an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/01/amber-heard-johnny-depp-trial-metoo-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 orgy of misogyny}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just about Depp and Heard, it was about how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dazeddigital.com/life-culture/article/56244/1/johnny-depp-amber-heard-trial-women-female-solidarity-myth-misogyny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 online propaganda works}}}\uc2  ; it was about victim-blaming; it was about what it takes for a woman to be believed; it was about what happens when women speak up.\par \par \uc2 11 France went berserk over burkinis\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s highest administrative court, which presumably has quite a lot on its plate, spent a portion of the summer deliberating on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/21/french-obsessed-burkini-france-women-long-sleeves-swim-islamophobia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acceptable swimwear for women}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 12 \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  turned on her father and shunned politics\par \par \uc2 Only a few years ago Ivanka reportedly wanted to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/jan/07/ivanka-trump-wants-to-be-the-first-female-us-president-perhaps-she-already-is-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first female US president.}}}\uc2  In 2022, however, she tried to get as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/15/ivanka-trump-donald-trump-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far away}}}\uc2  from politics as possible and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/ivanka-trump-election-not-stolen-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distance herself from her dad}}}\uc2 . She spent much of the year hiding out at the beach. While that sounds lovely, the world of Superficial Self-Serving Women\u8217\'20\'19s Empowerment has lost a real icon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a response of up to 300 words by email to be considered for publication in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/letters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letters}}}\uc2  section, please {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com?body=Please%20include%20your%20name,%20full%20postal%20address%20and%20phone%20number%20underneath%20your%20letter.%20Letters%20are%20usually%20published%20with%20the%20author’s%20name%20and%20city/town/village.%20The%20rest%20of%20the%20information%20is%20for%20verification%20only%20and%20to%20contact%20you%20if%20your%20letter%20is%20used."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej140013y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
