\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Our favorite data stories: how Guardian US visualized 2022\b0\par\par\uc2 Aliya Uteuova, Andrew Witherspoon and Alvin Chang \par \uc2 806 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 From neighborhood heatmaps to banana diagrams, the visuals we used to tell this year\u8217\'20\'19s stories\par \par \uc2 In 2022, the Guardian US visuals team used data to tell stories ranging from the effects of our warming planet to voter disenfranchisement and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  deserts. When our reporting led us to a point too complex for words we crafted data graphics to simplify and inform. Below are nine stories that represent our best work of the year.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/food/ng-interactive/2022/apr/14/climate-crisis-food-systems-not-ready-biodiversity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Our food system isn\u8217\'20\'19t ready for the climate crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s farms lack biodiversity \u8211\'20\'13 they produce only a handful of varieties of bananas, avocados, coffee and other foods. This monoculture leaves crops vulnerable to floods, droughts and disease. Starting with bananas, we visualized how the increasing lack of diversity among the foods we eat can lead to crop loss and malnutrition.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alvin-chang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Chang}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/new-york-heat-deaths-map-inequality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The wealth divide linked to 370 heat deaths in New York each year}}}\par \par \uc2 A groundbreaking study by citizen scientists surveyed the temperature of New York City streets, using data to define the boundaries of climate inequality. Neighborhoods in the Bronx with little tree cover were on average 8F (4.5C) hotter than the wealthier and more canopied Upper West Side. We created a heatmap to highlight the areas most affected by dangerous heat.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/aliya-uteuova"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aliya Uteuova}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jan/25/nashville-tennessee-gerrymandering-congress-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A masterclass in election-rigging: how Republicans \u8216\'20\'18dismembered\u8217\'20\'19 a Democratic stronghold}}}\par \par \uc2 Every 10 years congressional redistricting brings a focus on gerrymandering, the process of manipulating political boundaries to benefit a party. Using demographic and voting data we created a series of stories to help readers understand how this intentionally confusing process disenfranchises voters. This story visualizes how Democratic-leaning Nashville, Tennessee, was dismantled into three Republican-favored districts.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/10/us-summer-temperatures-rising-climate-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not your imagination, US summers are hotter than ever before}}}\par \par \uc2 The US experienced a historic heatwave this summer. An alarming trend shows average temperatures have increased by at least 2F since 1970. Using a spike map of major American cities we focused on the almost-universal warming trend, with the highest spikes in the west and south-west.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/aliya-uteuova"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aliya Uteuova}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/nov/20/amazon-warehouse-new-york-brooklyn-red-hook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Are Amazon delivery hubs making neighborhoods less healthy and more dangerous?}}}\par \par \uc2 Last-mile warehouses are springing up across the US, enabling the instant gratification of online deliveries. Working with Consumer Reports and local citizen scientists, we collected and visualized air quality and traffic sensor data to track the effect of these warehouses on the Red Hook neighborhood of New York City.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/aliya-uteuova"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aliya Uteuova}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/abortion-laws-by-state-map-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  deserts: America\u8217\'20\'19s new geography of access to care \u8211\'20\'13 mapped}}}\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services became much more uneven for women across the nation. Some already had sparse access, but with entire states expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  we wanted to visually contextualize how far women would have to travel. Using sensitive clinic location data we mapped the distance from each US county to the nearest available clinic and charted the average increase in distance for each state.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alvin-chang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Chang}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/13/how-covid-shook-the-us-charts-graphs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Covid shook the US: eight charts that capture the last two years}}}\par \par \uc2 As the global Covid-19 pandemic reached its second year, we wanted to step back and take a look at the larger picture. Two years of data allowed for more complete conclusions about the regional peaks and valleys of caseloads, the racial disparities in death rates, and plateaued vaccine adoption.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/20/syngenta-weedkiller-pesticide-parkinsons-disease-paraquat-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret files suggest chemical giant feared weedkiller\u8217\'20\'19s link to Parkinson\u8217\'20\'19s disease}}}\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  analyzed hundreds of internal documents that revealed the chemical giant \uc2 Syngenta\uc2  was aware their weedkiller Paraquat could lead to Parkinson\u8217\'20\'19s disease. To show the pervasiveness of the weedkiller, we mapped the chemical\u8217\'20\'19s agricultural use in the US over time.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/aliya-uteuova"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aliya Uteuova}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/feb/05/americans-above-average-temperature-increase-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A third of Americans are already facing above-average warming}}}\par \par \uc2 As the world comes dangerously close to the 1.5C (2.7F) post-industrial warming threshold set in the Paris agreement, we wanted to explore the crisis at a more local level. We mapped temperatures of US counties in 48 states, finding at least 499 counties that have already reached 1.5C. To show the populations most affected we made a stacked bar chart sized by each state\u8217\'20\'19s population and colored by temperature increase.\par \par \uc2 Data visualization:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\par \par \uc2 For more data visuals, read some of the prolific work from our UK colleagues this year. They\u8217\'20\'19ve covered the impact of the war in Ukraine on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/ng-interactive/2022/jun/09/the-black-sea-blockade-mapping-the-impact-of-war-in-ukraine-on-the-worlds-food-supply-interactive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 world\u8217\'20\'19s food supply}}}\uc2 , a timeline of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2022/jan/14/how-no-10s-alleged-parties-took-place-as-uk-covid-death-toll-rose-interactive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid in the UK}}}\uc2 , and the money {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/ng-interactive/2022/dec/01/down-the-drain-how-billions-of-pounds-are-sucked-out-of-englands-water-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 behind England\u8217\'20\'19s water system}}}\uc2 . See all of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/interactive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s interactives here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej140010n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
