\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Women with restricted  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access may face higher suicide risk \u8211\'20\'13 study\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 618 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Research shows anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws may have affected suicide rates among reproductive-aged women from 1974 to 2016\par \par \uc2 Women with restricted access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last 40 years may have faced a higher risk of suicide, according to new research from the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction laws may have influenced suicide rates among reproductive-aged women from 1974 to 2016, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamapsychiatry/fullarticle/2799597?guestAccessKey=9ac07a88-f8d6-40c4-b074-8b1a0311faf0&utm_source=For_The_Media&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=ftm_links&utm_content=tfl&utm_term=122822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study released Wednesday}}}\uc2  in Jama Psychiatry.\par \par \uc2 Previously, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/research/ongoing/turnaway-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Turnaway Study}}}\uc2  conducted by the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2  found that women are more likely to suffer anxiety and loss of self-esteem in the short term after being denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and are less likely to have aspirational life plans for the coming year.\par \par \uc2 However, according to the researchers behind Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s study, this study is the first of its kind to test whether access to reproductive care is directly associated with suicide.\par \par \uc2 According to the study in Jama, 21 states implemented at least one targeted regulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers law from 1974 to 2016. Trap laws are measures that regulate where abortions may be provided and performed. Major medical organizations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/18/18-1323/124091/20191202145531124_18-1323%2018-1460%20tsac%20American%20College%20of%20Obstetricians%20and%20Gynecologists%20et%20al.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oppose}}}\uc2  Trap laws and have called them clandestine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/issues/abortion/types-attacks/trap-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempts}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/12/02/784312265/major-medical-legal-groups-oppose-louisiana-abortion-law-before-u-s-supreme-cour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limit}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access via costly and medically unnecessary requirements.\par \par \uc2 Some Trap law regulations include minimum measurements for room size and corridor width, which, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/evidence-you-can-use/targeted-regulation-abortion-providers-trap-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cmay necessitate relocation or costly changes to a clinic\u8217\'20\'19s physical layout and structure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy imposing regulations that sound technical and bureaucratic to a casual observer, [Trap laws] avoid the kind of widespread public scrutiny that the flurry of bans passed in 2019 provoked. Typically cloaked in the language of healthcare, the regulations they impose on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are costly and, in many cases, impossible to comply with,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/news/reproductive-freedom/trap-laws-are-the-threat-to-abortion-rights-you-dont-know-about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said a report from}}}\uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since 1970, states have enacted more than 1,300 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, including limitations on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks. \u8220\'20\'1CEnforcement of a Trap law was associated with a 5.81% higher annual rate of suicide than in pre-enforcement years,\u8221\'20\'1D Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s study {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamapsychiatry/fullarticle/2799597?guestAccessKey=9ac07a88-f8d6-40c4-b074-8b1a0311faf0&utm_source=For_The_Media&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=ftm_links&utm_content=tfl&utm_term=122822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmong reproductive-aged women, the weighted average annual-state level suicide rate when no Trap laws were enforced was 5.5 for every 100,000 deaths. We found that the enforcement of a Trap law was related to higher suicide rates among reproductive-aged women \u8230\'20\'26 but not to suicide rates among women of post-reproductive age,\u8221\'20\'1D the study added.\par \par \uc2 According to researchers behind the study, the findings are significant for several reasons, especially as suicide currently represents the second and third leading cause of death among reproductive-aged women 20 to 24 and 25 to 34 respectively.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClinicians should be cognizant of the additional stresses that restricted access to reproductive care engenders as it pertains to clinical care and suicide prevention for women of reproductive age,\u8221\'20\'1D the study said.\par \par \uc2 The findings also inform \u8220\'20\'1Cethical considerations surrounding access to abortions and reproductive care more broadly\u8221\'20\'1D, it added, especially given the overturn of Roe v Wade earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Researchers also say that the findings \u8220\'20\'1Ccontribute to a \u8216\'20\'18multi-level\u8217\'20\'19 approach for suicide prevention that relies on integrating individual- and population-level factors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the US, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://suicidepreventionlifeline.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Suicide Prevention Lifeline}}}\uc2  is at 800-273-8255 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://suicidepreventionlifeline.org/chat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 online chat is also available}}}\uc2 . You can also text HOME to 741741 to connect with a crisis text line counselor. In the UK and Ireland, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.samaritans.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samaritans}}}\uc2  can be contacted on freephone 116 123, or email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jo@samaritans.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jo@samaritans.org}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jo@samaritans.ie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jo@samaritans.ie}}}\uc2 . In Australia, the crisis support service {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lifeline.org.au/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lifeline}}}\uc2  is 13 11 14. Other international helplines can be found at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.befrienders.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 befrienders.org}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14000zo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
