\par\par \uc2 Music\par \b \uc2 Aerosmith\u8217\'20\'19s Steven Tyler sued for 1970s sexual battery and assault of minor\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett \par \uc2 1,067 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Suit alleges \u8216\'20\'18various acts of criminal sexual conduct\u8217\'20\'19 were committed against teenager by singer over three-year period\par \par \uc2 A woman who says she had a sexual relationship with Aerosmith frontman Steven Tyler when she was 16 is suing him in California, under a state law that has temporarily extended the statute of limitations for adults to take legal action on sexual abuse they suffered as children.\par \par \uc2 Julia Holcomb Misley, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2021/sep/13/look-away-review-horrifying-stories-of-abuse-at-the-hands-of-male-rock-stars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  spoken out publicly for years}}}\uc2  about Tyler\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of her as a teenager, filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.andersonadvocates.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/Julia-Misley-Holcomb-vs.-Defendant-Doe-1_Does-2-Through-50.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  in Los Angeles on Tuesday alleging sexual battery, sexual assault and intentional infliction of distress during a three-year period in the 1970s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I know that I am not the only one who suffered abuse in the music industry, I feel it is time for me to take this stand,\u8221\'20\'1D Misley, now 65, said in a statement. She said the goal of her lawsuit was to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake the music industry safer, expose the predators in it, and expose those forces in the industry that have both enabled and created a culture of permissiveness and self-protection of themselves and the celebrity offenders among them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While the lawsuit does not name Tyler, referring to him only as \u8220\'20\'1CDoe 1\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Cwell-known musician and rock star\u8221\'20\'1D, the complaint quotes directly from Tyler\u8217\'20\'19s 2011 memoir, Does the Noise in My Head Bother You?, in which the rock star describes his sexual relationship with a 16-year-old girl he picked up after a show in 1973, including convincing her parents to give him legal custody of her, \u8220\'20\'1Cso I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get arrested if I took her out of state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I feel it is time for me to take this stand\par \par \uc2 Julia Holcomb Misley\par \par \uc2 However, Misley\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers named Tyler in a press release about the case. Representatives for the singer did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In the lawsuit, Misley says that the rock star met her after a concert in Portland in 1973, when she had just turned 16, and that he took her back to a hotel, where she told him her age and described her troubled family background. The musician \u8220\'20\'1Cperformed various acts of criminal sexual conduct\u8221\'20\'1D, and then sent her home in a taxi, according to the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 He soon followed up to offer her a ticket to another show, saying \u8220\'20\'1Che would buy the plane ticket so that she could travel separately from him since she was a minor and could not travel with [him] across state lines\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He would go on to use his power and influence as a prominent rock star to \u8220\'20\'1Cgroom, manipulate, exploit, [and] sexually assault\u8221\'20\'1D the teenager \u8220\'20\'1Cover the course of three years in numerous states across the country\u8221\'20\'1D, including in California, the lawsuit alleges.\par \par \uc2 After her sophomore year in high school, the lawsuit alleges, the rock star brought the teenager to stay with him in Boston, then convinced her not to return home to school, but travel with him on the road instead. He convinced her mother to allow him to become her legal guardian, \u8220\'20\'1Cpromising he would enroll her in school\u8221\'20\'1D and provide her with better support than her mother could, but in fact, only \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinued to travel with, assault and provide alcohol and drugs\u8221\'20\'1D to her.\par \par \uc2 When Misley became pregnant, in 1975, the rock star was now \u8220\'20\'1Cboth the father of Plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s unborn child and her legal guardian\u8221\'20\'1D, the suit alleges, and he told her not to seek appropriate prenatal care, worried \u8220\'20\'1Che would get in trouble\u8221\'20\'1D with doctors.\par \par \uc2 Later, after she was trapped inside a burning apartment and suffered from smoke inhalation, he coerced her to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing her years of distress, the lawsuit alleges.\par \par \uc2 Misley\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with Tyler was well documented: \u8220\'20\'1CJulia Holcomb\u8221\'20\'1D was named in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/aerosmith-hard-rocks-down-and-dirty-heroes-99418/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 1976 Rolling Stone profile of the rock star}}}\uc2 , in which she was portrayed as a girlfriend who was constantly in his company. The two had been photographed together, and Misley was interviewed about her interactions with Tyler in a 2021 documentary, Look Away, which focused on the abuse of young women in the music industry during the 70s and 80s.\par \par \uc2 Tyler\u8217\'20\'19s 2011 memoir devotes several pages to his upbeat and sexually graphic recollections of a three-year relationship with an anonymous teenage \u8220\'20\'1Cgroupie\u8221\'20\'1D he compares to Kate Hudson\u8217\'20\'19s character in the film Almost Famous, writing that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cso in love I almost took a teen bride\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith my bad self being twenty-six and she barely old enough to drive and sexy as hell, I just fell madly in love with her,\u8221\'20\'1D Tyler wrote.\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1CJulia Halcomb\u8221\'20\'1D is named in his book\u8217\'20\'19s acknowledgments. In Misley\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, she accuses the rock star of inflicting additional emotional distress on her through the \u8220\'20\'1Cinvoluntary infamy\u8221\'20\'1D of being described in graphic terms in his memoirs, which created additional trauma, and deep feelings of shame, humiliation and fear in her.\par \par \uc2 Misley \u8220\'20\'1Cwas in line at a grocery store and saw a picture of herself on a tabloid that referred to her as DEFENDANT DOE 1\u8217\'20\'19s teen lover. The caption under Plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s photo read, \u8216\'20\'18She was 15 when they fell in love. He\u8217\'20\'19s described her as having \u8220\'20\'1Cmore legs than a bucket of chicken,\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit alleges. The same tabloid story included explicit details of her coerced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Misley has since become an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocate in the US, speaking and writing about her experience with Tyler in the context of campaigns to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JHC4d_LTExU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 Tucker Carlson}}}\uc2  and a long written piece on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lifesitenews.com/news/the-light-of-the-world-the-steve-tyler-and-julia-holcomb-story/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  advocacy site}}}\uc2 . Her lawsuit and statements emphasised the importance of her Catholic faith, and said that she believed safety inside the Catholic church had been improved because of legal efforts to tackle the sexual abuse of children within the church.\par \par \uc2 Misley\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit was filed just days before the end of a three-year window, created by a 2019 California law, that gave adult survivors a chance to file lawsuits about child sexual abuse that occurred decades ago.\par \par \uc2 The impending deadline has resulted in a flood of new lawsuits, including more than 2,000 against the Catholic church, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2022-12-28/child-sex-abuse-lawsuits-california-deadline-ab218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej14000xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
