\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump blaming  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  for midterms flop shows \u8216\'20\'18ship is sinking\u8217\'20\'19, insider says\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 647 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 January 2023\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president says \u8216\'20\'18it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t my fault\u8217\'20\'19 Republicans fared poorly in 2022 but political wisdom of citing key rightwing issue questioned\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent comments about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a political issue show the former president has lost his ability to read Republican voters, a veteran Trump campaign insider said.\par \par \uc2 In messages seen by the Guardian, the operative said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has no political skills left. His team is a joke. The ship is sinking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump kicked off his latest scrap with his own party on his Truth Social platform on Sunday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/trump-says-abortion-issue-not-he-is-to-blame-for-gop-1849942969"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t my fault that the Republicans didn\u8217\'20\'19t live up to expectations in the midterms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, most observers suggest Trump\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to admit defeat in 2020 and endorsement of backers of his election fraud lie contributed to Republican disappointments in November, including barely scraping a House majority, failing to take the Senate and losing key races in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was the \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue\u8217\'20\'19, poorly handled by many Republicans, especially those that firmly insisted on no exceptions, even in the case of rape, incest, or life of the mother, that lost large numbers of voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In this instance, most observers would agree. It is generally held that Dobbs v Jackson, the supreme court ruling handed down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in June}}}\uc2  which ended federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, had a tangible effect at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 Trump also complained that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople that pushed so hard, for decades, against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , got their wish from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  and just plain disappeared, not to be seen again\u8221\'20\'1D, and said the Republican leader in the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , had been \u8220\'20\'1Cstupid\u8221\'20\'1D in how he spent campaign cash.\par \par \uc2 The comments prompted criticism from the political right.\par \par \uc2 The Fox News contributor Ben Domenech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bdomenech/status/1609672882749313025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Chard to express how many false things Trump says in this one \u8216\'20\'18truth\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He listed stringently anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans who won, contested Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that candidates supported no-exception bans and said Trump should have spent his own money to boost candidates such as Kari Lake, the election denier defeated for governor in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to a 2024 primary in which Trump is the only declared candidate but has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/why-desantis-is-a-major-threat-to-trumps-reelection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slipped in polling}}}\uc2 , in part due to legal exposure for election subversion and his business affairs, Domenech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bdomenech/status/1609672882749313025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CTrump betraying the pro-life cause on Dobbs has been telegraphed for a long time and is a huge opening to bash him in the 2024 stakes which I expect several candidates to seize.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFinally, think how stupid it is for Trump to run left on the pro-life issue. This is the biggest win of his presidency. Huge vested goodwill from pro-lifers. And what does he do? Call them quislings and say they\u8217\'20\'19re too radical! Very dumb.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three hardline conservatives to the court which ended \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But his own views have long been questioned and even in 2016, in his successful run for the White House, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/mar/31/donald-trump-abortion-remarks-biggest-campaign-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled}}}\uc2  to follow a consistent line.\par \par \uc2 Back then, Trump was asked \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/apr/02/donald-trump-marueen-dowd-interview-abortion-past-partners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by a New York Times reporter}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 if \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen he was a swinging bachelor in Manhattan, was he ever involved with anyone who had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CSuch an interesting question. So what\u8217\'20\'19s your next question?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Six years later, the messages from the veteran operative about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remarks pointed to a widening perception that the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 candidacy is in danger of falling apart a year before the primary.\par \par \uc2 Last month, after New York Magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/27/trump-olivia-nuzzi-profile-sunset-boulevard-norma-desmond-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 portrayed}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Csad, lonely, thirsty, broken, basically pretend run for re-election\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump disputed the reporting and called the reporter, Olivia Nuzzi, \u8220\'20\'1Ca shaky and unattractive wack job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Trump insider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/27/trump-olivia-nuzzi-profile-sunset-boulevard-norma-desmond-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Nuzzi\u8217\'20\'19s piece contained \u8220\'20\'1Csome accurate stuff\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230104ej140004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
