\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  tells of \u8216\'20\'18proud\u8217\'20\'19 record as speaker in likely final press conference \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,530 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2022\par 21:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Outgoing House speaker praises \u8216\'20\'18remarkable\u8217\'20\'19 Joe BidenSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing our politics blog now. Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 So far there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign of a deal in the Senate over a stopgap funding agreement that would keep the government running. The House passed the measure last night.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  praised \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as she reflected on their legislative accomplishments during her time a House speaker. Pelosi, who steps down next month, gave what could be her last press conference in the job.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  indicated he was ready to sign the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, a Texas-style \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat ban\u8221\'20\'1D that outlaws the procedure as soon as a fetal heartbeat is detected, usually around the sixth week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House voted 233-191 to allow Puerto Rico to hold a vote on becoming the 51st state, a largely symbolic measure because the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/8393"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico Status Act}}}\uc2  is unlikely to get a hearing in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he\u8217\'20\'19ll be heading to sub-Saharan Africa soon. He was speaking at the conclusion of a summit with African leaders in which he pledged hundreds of millions of dollars for infrastructure, technology and free elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden says she\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Call in\u8221\'20\'1D on her husband running again for the presidency in 2024, according to a report from CNN that says her position is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/15/politics/jill-biden-2024-campaign/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \u8220\'20\'1Ctidal shift\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  from her reluctant feelings of just three months ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two conspirators convicted of terrorism last month in a plot to kidnap Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  were sentenced to prison sentences of 12 and 10 years respectively. A third convict is yet to be sentenced.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The state department has announced a new round of sanctions against a number of Russian oligarchs, government officials and their families for enabling president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 DeSantis back 'heartbeat' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban for Florida\par \par \uc2 An extreme \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban looks to be coming to Florida after Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  announced his willingness Thursday to sign such a law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m willing to sign great life legislation. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ve always said I would do,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said at a press conference in Fort Lauderdale, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridapolitics.com/archives/576545-gov-desantis-ready-to-sign-abortion-heartbeat-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Florida Phoenix}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Amy Beth Bennett/AP\par \par \uc2 A heartbeat ban outlaws an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the presence of a fetal heartbeat is detected, usually around the sixth week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 A version of the law, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took effect in Texas in 2021}}}\uc2  after the Supreme Court, which had yet to overturn federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, declined to block it.\par \par \uc2 Rightwinger DeSantis is seen as a likely contender for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024, and leads in several recent polls of party members.\par \par \uc2 Despite passing a raft of culture war legislation during his first term of office, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/florida-abortion-ban-restored-15-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , DeSantis largely avoided the issue during campaigning ahead of his landslide reelection as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor last month.\par \par \uc2 The Republican supermajority in the Florida legislature means Democrats would be unable to block any new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Free-spirited Arizona senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  raised eyebrows last week when she announced she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/09/kyrsten-sinema-independent-days-after-democrats-secure-senate-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaving the Democratic party}}}\uc2  to sit as an independent. Now, it seems, she\u8217\'20\'19s also become an independent trader.\par \par \uc2 An extraordinary article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2022/12/kyrsten-sinema-facebook-marketplace-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published Thursday by Slate}}}\uc2  outs the enigmatic Sinema as a prolific seller of goods, especially shoes and clothes, on Facebook Marketplace, enough to rise to the level of a \u8220\'20\'1Cside hustle\u8221\'20\'1D, the magazine says.\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 . Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Reporter Christina Cauterucci said she exchanged \uc2 Facebook\uc2  messages with the politician over the potential purchase of a pair of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/1237190187048816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worn-only-once Badgley Mischka}}}\uc2  heels ($65, \u8220\'20\'1Cin perfect condition\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 Digging deeper, she found also for sale: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/1537381906704214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $215 cycling ensemble}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/477505990791607"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $25 trucker hat}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/1186188778618521/?hoisted=false&ref=product_details&referral_code=undefined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $150 stainless steel watch}}}\uc2  with a silicone strap.\par \par \uc2 Within the past six weeks, Cauterucci says, Sinema has \u8220\'20\'1Coffloaded\u8221\'20\'1D a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/993522768274194/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $150 fitness tracker ring}}}\uc2 , an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/5802244029836555/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $80 cycling jersey}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/664026508498819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $500 bicycle travel case}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Longer ago, there were listings on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral dozen personal items\u8221\'20\'1D, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/165645355484176"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $100 pair of sunglasses}}}\uc2  (\u8220\'20\'1CJust too big for my tiny head!!\u8221\'20\'1D), two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/846946849282759/?hoisted=false&ref=product_details&referral_code=undefined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $50 puffer jackets}}}\uc2 , three {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/3430086810415029/?hoisted=false&ref=product_details&referral_code=undefined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $75 pairs of high-heeled boots}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/groups/TriGirlsGotGear/posts/1703691253330124/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $75 cycling bib}}}\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/1358156204683874/?hoisted=false&ref=product_details&referral_code=undefined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $60 Lululemon raincoat}}}\uc2 , several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/493413002103985/?hoisted=false&ref=product_details&referral_code=undefined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mesh tanks}}}\uc2  at $55 a pop ($20 off the current {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bettydesigns.com/collections/tops-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retail price}}}\uc2  ), and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/marketplace/item/778317662877527"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple bikinis}}}\uc2 , priced between $60 and $70, that ranged from \u8220\'20\'1Cnever worn\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cin great condition\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Slate is cautious and won\u8217\'20\'19t state outright that it\u8217\'20\'19s definitely Sinema who\u8217\'20\'19s been selling off her worldly goods.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWould a sitting senator respond within seconds on a weekday morning to a message about her used heels?\u8221\'20\'1D Cauterucci wonders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWould it be worth her time to photograph a pair of old shoes, write a sales listing, field inquiries from potential buyers, and arrange pickup logistics \u8211\'20\'13 all for just $65?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But as if to answer its own questions, Slate points out that it\u8217\'20\'19s Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s name on the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Marketplace listing, it\u8217\'20\'19s her in the profile photo, the seller\u8217\'20\'19s biography says she lives in Phoenix, and she shares one mutual \uc2 Facebook\uc2  friend with the reporter who works for the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 The clincher, perhaps: The 4.5in, rhinestone-studded stilettoes \u8220\'20\'1Clook as if they would fit pretty well in Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s wardrobe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s possible we\u8217\'20\'19ll never know. According to Slate, Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s staff would not confirm or deny the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Marketplace account was hers, and did not respond to fact-checking queries.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video clip from \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s final press conference, definitely, maybe, as House speaker.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the media on Thursday morning, Pelosi looked back on some of the main policy accomplishments that took place under her tenure, and praised presidents \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for getting them done.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis may be the last time I see you in this way,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 She said she was particularly proud of the passage of the Affordable Care Act under Obama, which she said brought healthcare to tens of millions previously denied, and this week\u8217\'20\'19s signing of the same-sex Respect for Marriage Act.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, a Democrat from California, became speaker in 2007. She will retire next month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s travails as he seeks to become House speaker when Republicans take over the majority in January are well documented, no more so than in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/12/14/house-republicans-mccarthy-speaker-00074006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this latest take by Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The California congressman has been scrambling to attract the 218 votes he needs to take the gavel, and making some pretty unsavory promises to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/nov/17/donald-trump-kevin-mccarthy-republicans-house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightwing extremists in his party}}}\uc2  to get there, if accounts are to be believed.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Politico drills down on the fragile political game behind McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s maneuvering, the pledges he has had to make, and particularly something called the \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate the chair\u8221\'20\'1D, a potentially hazardous procedure in which any House member would be able to force a vote on deposing a sitting speaker.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s horse trading going on between the pro and anti-McCarthy camps among House Republicans over setting a threshold of votes that would be needed for such a motion in exchange for support.\par \par \uc2 One of McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s fears is that Democrats could use a motion to vacate in retaliation for his threats to remove prominent opposition congress members Adam Schiff, \uc2 Eric Swalwell\uc2  and \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  from committees.\par \par \uc2 Politico likens the haggling to an episode of the TV gameshow The Price is Right. You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/12/14/house-republicans-mccarthy-speaker-00074006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 read their report here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House approves Puerto Rico statehood act\par \par \uc2 In what was largely a symbolic gesture, the House has voted to allow Puerto Rico to decide whether it wants to pursue becoming the 51st state.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/8393"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico Status Act}}}\uc2  passed 233-191 in the chamber, requiring the US territory to hold a vote of its residents on three options, statehood, independence or sovereignty in free association with the US.\par \par \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 But with little to no time left on the Senate calendar, the measure, hailed by outgoing Democratic House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , is unlikely to be heard there, sounding its death knell in this current Congress at least.\par \par \uc2 Statehood for Puerto Rico was supported by the Biden administration. 16 Republicans voted for the bill in a free vote.\par \par \uc2 A joint statement from bipartisan negotiators of the act said: \u8220\'20\'1CMany of us disagree on what that future should look like, but we all accept that the decision must belong to the people of Puerto Rico and to them alone. The Puerto Rico Status Act will grant them that choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/20/puerto-rico-statehood-independent-free-association-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Statehood or independence? Puerto Rico\u8217\'20\'19s status at forefront of political debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2 , the Republican governor of Massachusetts who will soon step down after choosing not to run for a third term \u8211\'20\'13 or for president or any other office as a GOP candidate despite (or perhaps because of) leading a Democratic-dominated state for so long \u8211\'20\'13 will be the next president of the \uc2 NCAA\uc2 , the largest governing body in US college sports.\par \par \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2 . Photograph: Barry Chin/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 NCAA\uc2  is confronting complex and significant challenges but I am excited to get to work as the awesome opportunity college athletics provides to so many students is more than worth the challenge,\u8221\'20\'1D Baker said on Thursday, about the job he will start in March, replacing \uc2 Mark Emmert\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd for the fans that faithfully fill stadiums, stands and gyms from coast to coast, I am eager to ensure the competitions we all love to follow are there for generations to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the Associated Press has it, the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  has recently been \u8220\'20\'1Cbattered by losses in court and attacks by politicians\u8221\'20\'1D and is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing through a sweeping reform, trying to decentralize the way college sports is run\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCollege sports leaders, including Emmert, have repeatedly asked for help from Congress to regulate name, image and likeness compensation since the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  lifted its ban in 2021 on athletes being paid endorsers. Now the association will be led by a politician for the first time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baker, the AP says, \u8220\'20\'1Cgraduated from Harvard, where he played on the junior varsity basketball team. That\u8217\'20\'19s the extent of his personal experience in college sports\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Linda Livingstone\uc2 , president of Baylor in Texas and chair of the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  board, said Baker had \u8220\'20\'1Cshown a remarkable ability to bridge divides and build bipartisan consensus, taking on complex challenges in innovative and effective ways. These skills and perspective will be invaluable as we work with policymakers to build a sustainable model for the future of college athletics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Futher reading:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/sep/22/andrew-cooper-from-college-star-to-activist-the-ncaa-does-not-exist-to-protect-athletes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Cooper, from college star to activist: \u8216\'20\'18The NCAA does not exist to protect athletes\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In something close to a policy announcement \u8211\'20\'13 a scarce feature of a 2024 presidential run that has so far featured little of anything, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/14/desantis-trump-2024-republican-presidential-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly polling success}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has promised to stop government \u8220\'20\'1Cimpeding the lawful speech of American citizens\u8221\'20\'1D, should he retake the White House.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 In a video shared with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/12/15/trump-vows-to-ban-feds-from-id-ing-domestic-misinformation-if-elected/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Post}}}\uc2  (a Murdoch-owned tabloid though not the source of support it used to be), the former president said: \u8220\'20\'1CI will sign an executive order banning any federal department or agency from colluding with any organization, business or person to censor, limit, categorize or impede the lawful speech of American citizens. I will then ban federal money from being used to label domestic speech as mis- or disinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the Post put it:\par \par \uc2 The 76-year-old Trump made the pledge as part of a broader \u8216\'20\'18free speech\u8217\'20\'19 platform \u8230\'20\'26 vowing also to impose a seven-year ban on former \uc2 FBI\uc2  and CIA workers handling private-sector US consumer records.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would fire bureaucrats deemed to have engaged in censorship, \u8220\'20\'1Cdirectly or indirectly, whether they are the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the DOJ, no matter who they are\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf any US university is discovered to have engaged in censorship activities or election interferences in the past, such as flagging social media content for removal of blacklisting, those universities should lose federal research dollars and federal student loan support for a period of five years, and maybe more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Free speech, or a particular rightwing version of it, is of course the much-discussed topic of the day at \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , where the site\u8217\'20\'19s new owner, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , is dedicated to the concept to the extent of reinstating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s account \u8211\'20\'13 though Trump has not yet returned to tweeting.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/13/techscape-twitter-files-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TechScape: I read Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Twitter Files\u8217\'20\'19 so you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump, the Post reports, thinks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/13/techscape-twitter-files-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this month\u8217\'20\'19s }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/13/techscape-twitter-files-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Twitter Files\u8217\'20\'19}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/13/techscape-twitter-files-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  releases}}}\uc2  have \u8220\'20\'1Cconfirmed that a sinister group of Deep State bureaucrats, Silicon Valley tyrants, leftwing activists, and depraved corporate news media have been conspiring to manipulate and silence the American People.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe censorship cartel must be dismantled and destroyed \u8211\'20\'13 and it must happen immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/15/trump-mocked-superhero-digital-card-collection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Losing the plot\u8217\'20\'19: Trump mocked after announcing superhero card collection}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve reached lunchtime on a busy day in US politics, which includes ongoing discussions in the Senate on approving a short-term funding measure to keep the government open for at least another week.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re hoping to learn more this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Also happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has been speaking of her \u8220\'20\'1Cpride\u8221\'20\'1D in a number of legislative achievements during what could be her final press conference as House speaker. She paid tribute to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden says he\u8217\'20\'19ll be heading to sub-Saharan Africa soon on the first visit there of his presidency. He was speaking at the conclusion of a summit with African leaders in which he pledged hundreds of millions of dollars for infrastructure, technology and free elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two conspirators convicted of terrorism last month in a plot to kidnap Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  were sentenced to prison sentences of 12 and 10 years respectively. A third convict is yet to be sentenced.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden says she\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Call in\u8221\'20\'1D on her husband running again for the presidency in 2024, according to a report from CNN that says her position is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/15/politics/jill-biden-2024-campaign/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \u8220\'20\'1Ctidal shift\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  from her reluctant feelings of just three months ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The state department has announced a new round of sanctions against a number of Russian oligarchs, government officials and their families for enabling president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden announces Africa visit\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon visit sub-Saharan Africa, he announced on Thursday. It came at the conclusion of a three-day summit with African leaders in which he announced hundreds of millions of dollars in investment in the continent for infrastructure, technology initiatives and supporting free elections.\par \par \uc2 A day earlier, the president said he was \u8220\'20\'1Call in\u8221\'20\'1D on strengthening US relations with African countries, which was why he had sent many of his top advisers there, including secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , treasury secretary Janet Yellin and commerce secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  listens as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addresses the US-Africa summit leaders session on Thursday. Photograph: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to seeing you in your home countries,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the leaders of 49 African countries on Thursday about what will be the first visit there of his presidency other than a brief stopover in Egypt last month, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 He did state which countries he will visit or when the trip will happen.\par \par \uc2 Biden on Thursday pledged $165m in US funding to support peaceful, credible elections in Africa next year as his administration looked to underscore the importance of fair voting in countries where it sometimes has been blighted by violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pelosi 'proud' of achievements as Speaker\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has given what she suggests will be her final press conference as House speaker, telling reporters this is \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe the last time I see you in this way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s been reflecting on some of the successes of her tenure, and paying tribute to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  for most of them, from the passing of the Affordable Care Act to this week\u8217\'20\'19s signing of the same-sex {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/13/biden-signs-law-protecting-same-sex-interracial-marriages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Respect for Marriage Act}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D to have her signature below Biden\u8217\'20\'19s on that law:\par \par \uc2 He has been a remarkable president. He has a record that is so outstanding, and for such a short period of time as well.\par \par \uc2 People compare him to Lyndon Johnson, to \uc2 Franklin Roosevelt\uc2 , but I\u8217\'20\'19d remind you all that Roosevelt had 319 Democrats in the House, President Biden 222, whatever it is, and even fewer now.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  gives what might be her last press conference as speaker on Thursday. Photograph: Win McNamee/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 She went on to list many of the items of legislation she was most proud of, under Biden\u8217\'20\'19s leadership:\par \par \uc2 Passing the American rescue plan, getting vaccines at arms, money in pockets, children back to school and people safely back to work, the bipartisan infrastructure law, building roads, bridges, ports and water systems\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Bringing people together, not projects that divide communities but bringing people together, and this such a source of pride, putting justice and equity front and center.\par \par \uc2 Of her regrets, the inability to pass comprehensive gun reform saddened her, she said. Speaking one day after the 10th anniversary of the Sandy Hook shooting that killed 20 elementary school children and six adults, she said:\par \par \uc2 We won\u8217\'20\'19t relent until the job is done, until we can have background checks, and have banned assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi doesn\u8217\'20\'19t leave office until early next month, and didn\u8217\'20\'19t rule out speaking with the media again, particularly if there\u8217\'20\'19s a resolution to threat of a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The speaker says she\u8217\'20\'19s optimistic that a \u8220\'20\'1Cbipartisan, bicameral\u8221\'20\'1D omnibus spending deal will pass next week to keep the government funded for a year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Whitmer kidnap plot conspirators sentenced\par \par \uc2 Two men who forged an early alliance with the leader of a plot to kidnap Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  were sentenced Thursday to lengthy prison terms for assisting him before the \uc2 FBI\uc2  broke up the scheme in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Pete Musico was given a minimum term of 12 years and his son-in-law Joe Morrison got 10 years, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 A third person, Paul Bellar, was awaiting his sentence at the same hearing in Jackson county.\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 . Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 They were convicted in October of providing material support for a terrorist act, which carries a maximum term of 20 years, and two other crimes.\par \par \uc2 Musico, 45, Morrison, 28, and Bellar, 24, were members of a paramilitary group known as the Wolverine Watchmen.\par \par \uc2 Musico and Morrison will be eligible for parole after serving their minimum sentences. The maximum they can held in prison would be 42 years under state law.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/gretchen-whitmer-michigan-governor-kidnap-plit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Militia group trio found guilty of aiding plot to kidnap Michigan governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There are \u8220\'20\'1Cbig announcements\u8221\'20\'1D, and others are not so big. The internet was having fun on Thursday with this latest one from former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a man who never knowingly undersells any potential money-making venture.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest wheeze, which he trailed heavily on his failing Truth Social network over the last 24 hours, casts himself as the superhero central figure in a new \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://collecttrumpcards.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 digital trading card collection}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For only $99, customers can acquire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/nfts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-fungible tokens}}}\uc2  (NFTs) of Trump dressed in a variety of \u8220\'20\'1Chero\u8221\'20\'1D outfits, including a shiny red bodysuit and cape; as an astronaut; a racing car driver and football player, and so on.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust when you thought this grifter couldn't humiliate himself any more than he already has, there's this. THIS is what the big announcement was. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/npsjPNYpBA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/npsjPNYpBA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Kiriakou (@JohnKiriakou) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnKiriakou/status/1603422816015097860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump is adamant they will sell out \u8220\'20\'1CI believe very quickly\u8221\'20\'1D, and offers those who pay the chance to win one of several prizes, including dinner with him in Miami; lunch at his Florida resort Mar-a-Lago; a round of golf with the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/mar/31/trump-golf-cheats-new-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 world\u8217\'20\'19s worst cheat}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D; signed photographs etc.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, the internet was quick to react, with a series of tweets raging from incredulity to outright mocking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust when you thought this grifter couldn\u8217\'20\'19t humiliate himself any more than he already has, there\u8217\'20\'19s this,\u8221\'20\'1D says author and CIA whistleblower John Kiriakou.\par \par \uc2 enltrNow that my beautiful NFT apes are all worthless, I need a new place to invest my money. These Trump trading cards may be just what the doctor ordered. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tojlGEHkER"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tojlGEHkER}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark R. Yzaguirre (@markyzaguirre) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/markyzaguirre/status/1603431007042117633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump's "major announcement" turns out to be a series of $99 NFTs that are ugly even by the usual NFT standards. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/f6r80q2PgB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/f6r80q2PgB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Will Sommer (@willsommer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/willsommer/status/1603422514511740928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 itltrHAHAAHAHAHAAHAHAHAHAHAHAAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHHHHHHHHHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAHHAHAHAHHHAHAHAH {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MajorAnnouncement?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MajorAnnouncement}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MIiEnF0kEg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MIiEnF0kEg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6JPjimoMcw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6JPjimoMcw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lesley Abravanel ?? (@lesleyabravanel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lesleyabravanel/status/1603423857511112704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltri am going to acquire this \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  NFT because it is the everyday looking version of him that we all know and love {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zVnAS3H6xk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zVnAS3H6xk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Binder (@MattBinder) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MattBinder/status/1603422642610266113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The state department has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/furthering-the-united-states-effort-to-hold-russia-to-account-for-its-war-against-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiled a new round of sanctions}}}\uc2  against Russian oligarchs and others it says are enabling the country\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  in his war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 They include \uc2 Vladimir Olegovich Potanin\uc2 , a former deputy prime minister of the Russian federation and Potanin\u8217\'20\'19s wife Ekaterina Viktorovna Potanina and their two adult children.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the United States is taking sweeping actions against major actors in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s financial sector, governors in Russia, and proxy authorities installed in Ukraine by the Kremlin. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SvHTaz8S1t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SvHTaz8S1t}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  (@SecBlinken) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken/status/1603418796919758849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Also on the list are five directors of Russian railways, and about 40 members of the Russian government and certain family members, both in Russia and installed by the Kremlin as \u8220\'20\'1Cproxy authorities\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is committed to working alongside our allies and partners to further impose severe consequences on President Putin and his enablers for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s unconscionable war against Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the state department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/furthering-the-united-states-effort-to-hold-russia-to-account-for-its-war-against-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in the statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/04/meet-the-oligarchs-sanctions-russian-billionaires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meet the oligarchs: the Russian billionaires whose jets, yachts and mansions are now in the crosshairs}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More migrants may be released into the US to pursue immigration cases when Trump-era asylum restrictions end next week, the homeland security department is warning, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Texas congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  says customs and border protection officials told him as many as 50,000 migrants could be waiting at the US southern border for the scheduled 21 December termination of the policy.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/16/title-42-immigration-judge-orders-biden-administration-trump-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered the ending on that date of Title 42}}}\uc2 , under which migrants have been denied rights to seek asylum more than 2.5m times on grounds of preventing spread of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2 . Photograph: Veronica Cardenas/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The AP has reviewed a homeland security document dated Tuesday that says the department is reporting faster processing for migrants in custody on the border, more temporary detention tents, staffing surges and increased criminal prosecutions of smugglers.\par \par \uc2 But the seven-page document included no major structural changes amid unusually large numbers of migrants entering the country, and more expected when Title 42 ends.\par \par \uc2 Cuellar, who has clashed with the Biden administration over immigration, said in an interview that authorities plan to admit those seeking asylum who go through ports of entry, but return to Mexico those who cross illegally between official crossings.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/16/title-42-immigration-judge-orders-biden-administration-trump-rule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Title 42: judge orders Biden to lift Trump-era immigration rule}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  will shortly host one of her final press conferences as Speaker.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the House honored its long-serving, first woman Speaker with the unveiling of a portrait, an oil-on-canvas by artist Ron Sherr of the California Democrat wielding the gavel for the first time, in January 2007.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the House unveiled its portrait of \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the first woman to serve as Speaker of the House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HouseCollection?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HouseCollection}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l1TR6fCQfS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/l1TR6fCQfS}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Wpl3GGOm4y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Wpl3GGOm4y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 U.S. House History (@USHouseHistory) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USHouseHistory/status/1603157776221765632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the end of the road for the bust in the US Capitol of a supreme court judge who wrote a slavery ruling that helped pave the pathway to the civil war. Martin Pengelly reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  voted on Wednesday to remove from the Capitol a bust of Roger Taney, the supreme court justice who in 1857 wrote the Dred Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/dred-scott-v-sandford"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2 , justifying slavery and denying that Black people had rights any \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite man was bound to respect\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If the new measure is signed into law by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the bust will be removed from outside the old supreme court chamber and replaced by a bust of Thurgood Marshall, the first Black justice.\par \par \uc2 The measure that passed the House by voice vote was reduced from one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/powerpost/congress-confederates-statues-house/2021/06/29/304f7960-d8db-11eb-9bbb-37c30dcf9363_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which would also}}}\uc2  have removed statues of Confederates who fought the civil war to protect slavery and which was re-introduced in the aftermath of the Capitol riot of 6 January 2021, when Trump supporters carried Confederate flags into the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2 . Photograph: US House Of Representatives/Reuters\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2 , a House Democrat from California, said she would have preferred to remove Confederate statuary too, but to remove the Taney bust was literally about \u8220\'20\'1Cwho we put on a pedestal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States Capitol is a beacon of democracy, freedom and equality,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lofgren, a member of the January 6 committee. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat and who we choose to honor in this building should represent our values. Chief Justice Taney \u8230\'20\'26 does not meet the standard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Dred Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/dred-scott-v-sandford"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2  concerned an enslaved man who lived in Illinois and the Louisiana territory, where slavery was forbidden, then with his wife sued for freedom when taken back to Missouri, a state where slavery was legal.\par \par \uc2 The court ruled 7-2 for Scott\u8217\'20\'19s enslaver, John Sandford, an army surgeon.\par \par \uc2 Taney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/dred-scott-v-sandford"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  that Black people \u8220\'20\'1Chad for more than a century before been regarded as beings of an inferior order, and altogether unfit to associate with the white race, either in social or political relations; and so far inferior, that they had no rights which the white man was bound to respect; and that the negro might justly and lawfully be reduced to slavery for his benefit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/15/house-votes-remove-bust-roger-taney-dred-scott-us-capitol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House votes to remove bust of judge who wrote Dred Scott decision defending slavery}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Report: First lady 'all in' on new Biden presidential run\par \par \uc2 In what CNN is calling \u8220\'20\'1Ca tidal shift\u8221\'20\'1D, Jill Biden has reportedly reversed her opinion about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  running again for the White House and is now \u8220\'20\'1Call in\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The network {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/15/politics/jill-biden-2024-campaign/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a report}}}\uc2  Thursday citing anonymous sources in the East Wing who say that after reluctance just three months ago, the first lady \u8220\'20\'1Chas begun to say the quiet part out loud\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Friends, CNN says, have \u8220\'20\'1Cnoticed a change\u8221\'20\'1D in Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s demeanor since Democrats performed better in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms than expected, and has developed new enthusiasm for remaining in the White House, even though a flurry of recent events have left her \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jill and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the US-African leaders summit in the White House on Wednesday. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is 80, and the first lady is 71.\par \par \uc2 The Bidens will discuss the issue \u8220\'20\'1Cover the holidays\u8221\'20\'1D, the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/10/joe-biden-2024-president-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said last month}}}\uc2 , telling reporters \u8220\'20\'1Cwatch me\u8221\'20\'1D at a press conference following the midterms when asked if he would be a candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think everybody wants me to run, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have discussions about it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at the time, indicating that he would sit down with his family over the holiday period and announce his decision \u8220\'20\'1Cearly next year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If he does run and win, Biden would be 82 when sworn in for his second term, and be the oldest president in history. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2022/12/13/2024-campaigns-trump-biden-00073548"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that it\u8217\'20\'19s been a touchy subject for the president. \u8220\'20\'1CYou think I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how fucking old I am?\u8221\'20\'1D he reportedly said to one ally earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Voters, however, appear to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/12/14/politics/biden-trump-2024-poll/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 little appetite}}}\uc2  for a rematch between Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the presidency in 2024, a poll released Wednesday found.\par \par \uc2 Roughly six in 10 Republicans, and the same margin in the Democratic party, don\u8217\'20\'19t want their respective 2020 nominees to run again, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23460217/cnn-poll-americans-have-little-appetite-for-biden-trump-rematch-in-2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN poll conducted by SSRS}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Shelby: Government funding negotiations 'only $25bn apart'\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been barely two months since the Senate last {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/29/us-supreme-court-biden-republicans-democrats-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6335e8b98f0883d28b584a83#block-6335e8b98f0883d28b584a83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a short-term spending fix}}}\uc2  to avert a government shutdown, yet here we are again today.\par \par \uc2 Senators will on Thursday take up what has become something of a regular fixture in US politics as they discuss a one-week spending bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-kevin-mccarthy-government-and-politics-1e238f6b65ffb8ac0490dfaf13229edb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by the House on Wednesday}}}\uc2  to keep the government funded until 23 December.\par \par \uc2 And, as always, bipartisan politics are playing a role, even though Republican Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has indicated he\u8217\'20\'19s open to a long-term deal that many of his colleagues in the House have opposed.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic majority leader, has his eyes on an appropriations package of roughly $1.7tn to fund an entire year, and a one-week extension before Friday\u8217\'20\'19s deadline would avoid a partial government closure and provide breathing space for a compromise.\par \par \uc2 Richard Shelby\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, \uc2 Richard Shelby\uc2 , the Republican senator for Alabama leading the negotiations, says the two sides are only about $25bn apart overall, and had agreed over an $858bn spend on defense.\par \par \uc2 McConnell said Wednesday night:\par \par \uc2 If a truly bipartisan full-year bill without poison pills is ready for final Senate passage by late next week, I\u8217\'20\'19ll support it for our armed forces.\par \par \uc2 Otherwise, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be passing a short-term continuing resolution into the new year.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, Republicans in the House want to stamp their own mark on things, given they take over control of the chamber in early January.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, the Republican House minority leader vying for the Speaker\u8217\'20\'19s gavel, points out that the two senators leading the negotiations, Shelby and Democrat \uc2 Patrick Leahy\uc2  of Vermont, are retiring and won\u8217\'20\'19t still be around to be answerable for their work.\par \par \uc2 And No 2 House Republican Steve Scalise opposes the $1.7tn proposal saying it\u8217\'20\'19s a sign \u8220\'20\'1CCongress failed to do its job\u8221\'20\'1D, even though, according to the AP, many Republican senators feel that blocking a long-term deal would reflect badly on the party.\par \par \uc2 But for today at least, it\u8217\'20\'19s all about a short-term fix. Hopefully the picture will become clearer as the day moves on.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning politics blog readers. The early order of business in the Senate today is finding a way to keep the government funded, if only for a week.\par \par \uc2 Senators will take up the one-week spending bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-kevin-mccarthy-government-and-politics-1e238f6b65ffb8ac0490dfaf13229edb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by the House on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , a short-term fix that, if also passed in the upper chamber, would avert a shutdown and keep the government machine ticking until 23 December.\par \par \uc2 It would also give Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  breathing space to work on a $1.7tn fiscal year package, but Republicans are not happy about it. A clearer picture could emerge today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is scheduled to give one of her final press conferences as House speaker at 10.45am.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting \uc2 African Union\uc2  leaders in Washington DC to discuss US political and business ties with the continent. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if he will talk to the press.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House convenes shortly to discuss collective bargaining rights to Veterans\u8217\'20\'19 Association health care workers. Statehood for Puerto Rico is also up for discussion.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Survivors of mass shootings in Uvalde, Texas; and Newtown, Connecticut will testify at a morning hearing of the House subcommittee on crime, terrorism and homeland security.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020221215eicf0020j\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 atleast5(abortion)\cell \pa